{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789085504095,"sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-ba73ca2a750e903b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-12ee85/review-plan.yaml"},"output":"<path>/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-12ee85/review-plan.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: review_plan:\n2:   id: REVIEW-PLAN-BATCH-12ee85\n3:   recorded_at: '2026-09-10'\n4:   goal_id: GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f\n5:   question_id: RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5\n6:   batch_id: BATCH-12ee85\n7:   experiment_id: EXP-ECDLP-6ac801\n8:   hypothesis_id: H-ECDLP-37dc01\n9:   written_by: coordinator-ecdlp-20260910\n10:   authority: 'Opened under the standing user authorization of 2026-09-06 and the approved v3 chain: EXP-ECDLP-6ac801\n11:     v3 approved by the independent gate DEC-20260907-b4f2a9 (gate task TASK-20260907-e17c05), which names\n12:     as its RANK 1 exactly this round''s subject matter: dispatch and then review Stage A'''' (the blind\n13:     re-derivation seal, executed and snapshotted under BATCH-4433c1) and the Stage B'''' production grid\n14:     (50 runs, 200 cells, snapshot 9e6396c35e). No run and no reading of this round existed when this plan\n15:     was written.'\n16:   claim_under_review: 'Two independent measurement packages, both observations only. (1) Stage A'''':\n17:     the blind re-derivation seal of TASK-20260907-7afa98 (seal.json hash set + UTC stamp declared before\n18:     any non-packet read; reading_attestation.json; instrument.py, run_full.py, cells.jsonl, summary.json,\n19:     run.log), per-cell k_25 verdicts and bootstrap CIs over the full (N, a) grid: a=1/16 G3-FEASIBLE at\n20:     both scales (25/25, margin +0.0187/+0.0216), a=1/8 borderline (N=2^20 k_25=16, margin +0.0043 CI [-0.0002,+0.0087]\n21:     straddling zero; N=2^24 k_25=20, margin +0.0081 CI [+0.0050,+0.0115]), a=3/16 and a=1/4 G3-INFEASIBLE\n22:     at both scales with CIs excluding zero. (2) Stage B'''': the production grid RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-v3-n20-s01..25\n23:     and RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-v3-n24-s01..25 (kind stageBpp_exact_ceiling_v3, exact-basin closed form, zero\n24:     re-selected arms), each run covering the four-value a-grid {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4} at T=256, T_sel=128,\n25:     T4=64, T8=32, r=2, 25 seeds per scale = 200 cells, snapshot-archived at commit 9e6396c35e (receipt\n26:     backfilled 718af27fae). NEITHER package interprets; both record. The comparison of the two packages,\n27:     and every reading of the crossing bracket''s robustness and N-dependence at the borderline cell a=1/8,\n28:     are THE WORK OF THIS REVIEW ROUND and are unselected in the records under review.'\n29:   coordinator_prior: 'Written before any reviewer runs, on the opening Coordinator''s own independent\n30:     recomputation (NOT on the producers'' code): I recomputed the margin identity margin == exact_top_T_sel_share\n31:     - static_T_r2_exact_coverage on ALL 200 production cells and it holds exactly (200/200); I recomputed\n32:     per-(N,a) mean margins and margin>=0 counts from the production summaries (a=1/16: +0.0168 k=24/25\n33:     at 2^20, +0.0202 k=25/25 at 2^24; a=1/8: +0.0069 k=17/25 at 2^20, +0.0102 k=24/25 at 2^24; a=3/16:\n34:     -0.0086 k=8/25 at 2^20, -0.0054 k=5/25 at 2^24; a=1/4: -0.0228 k=2/25 at 2^20, -0.0185 k=0/25 at 2^24;\n35:     max residual fraction 0.0232). (1) J1 blind re-derivation: I EXPECT the derived values at the eight\n36:     frozen cells to agree with the PRODUCTION grid on the definition-exact fields (accounting_identity_holds\n37:     true, residual_fraction, cap convention, rho_ORACLE) and to agree with BOTH implementations only QUALITATIVELY\n38:     on seed-dependent fields (sign of margin, verdict family), because three implementations (blind instrument,\n39:     Stage A'''' instrument, production exact-basin closed form) need not agree bit-wise on walk-dependent\n40:     quantities; per-seed margin magnitudes are expected to differ between implementations at the same\n41:     cell and that difference is EXPECTED, not a defect. The live risk I name: if quantity.md''s seed/walk\n42:     convention underdetermines a field, the honest blind report records the ambiguity rather than resolving\n43:     it, and the ambiguity localizes to the packet''s statement -- that would be a finding about the definition,\n44:     carried to the composed decision. (2) J2 integrity: I EXPECT the Stage A'''' seal hashes to match\n45:     the committed files byte for byte, both snapshot receipts to verify (Stage A'''' via the c3f20c receipt\n46:     commits d144025225/ab711b0662; Stage B'''' via 9e6396c35e + backfill 718af27fae), the margin identity\n47:     to hold on all 200 cells (I verified it myself), and the accounting identity sum_d b(d) + cycle_mass\n48:     + capped_mass == N to hold exactly per cell. (3) J2 conformance: I EXPECT params (T=256, T_sel=128,\n49:     T4=64, T8=32, r=2, 25 seeds, 4-value grid, both scales) to match v3''s stage plan and the bootstrap\n50:     CIs to reproduce from the recorded bootstrap seeds (bootstrap_B 10000, log2(N) convention). (4) The\n51:     comparison headline I EXPECT: the crossing bracket is corroborated as BETWEEN a=1/16 and a=3/16 with\n52:     a=1/8 the live borderline cell, stable in location across N in {2^20, 2^24}, with a visible N-dependence\n53:     AT a=1/8 only (leaning-infeasible/straddled at 2^20, feasible with CI excluding zero at 2^24) -- the\n54:     robustness and N-dependence reading v3''s rewritten objective exists to measure. (5) Expected disposition:\n55:     EV-ECDLP-5035ed records the two-implementation corroboration at the tested scope (ceiling-level, exact-basin,\n56:     N in {2^20, 2^24}, 25 seeds); NO hypothesis-status promotion on any clause of H-ECDLP-37dc01 in this\n57:     round (DEC-20260907-b4f2a9 RANK 3 makes any promotion a further decision on THIS round''s reviewed\n58:     evidence; the goal head independently forbids any promotion beyond ceiling-feasibility before an ONLINE\n59:     arm exists -- zero have); the composed DEC-20260910-34e654 records the robustness reading and names\n60:     the RANK-2 online-RESEL-L lane as successor. If the reviewers break a joint this prior expected to\n61:     hold, the composition follows the reports, not this prior.'\n62:   joints:\n63:   - joint: J1_blind_rederivation_and_cross_implementation\n64:     assigned_to: TASK-20260910-19bd7b\n65:     attack_plan: 'TWO PHASES, FREEZE ENFORCED. Phase 1 (blind): read ONLY blind-input.yaml and the four\n66:       packet files (experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/derivation-packet/PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3/{MANIFEST.yaml,quantity.md,deliverables.md,prohibitions.md});\n67:       implement the quantity from the definition from scratch; derive every listed field at the eight\n68:       frozen cells; write and freeze the report in your own task directory; STOP. Phase 2 (comparison,\n69:       only after the Coordinator commits the frozen report): read Stage A'''' cells.jsonl/summary.json\n70:       and the Stage B'''' summaries for the same cells; compare per field into EXACT / QUALITATIVE / DISAGREES\n71:       / UNDERDETERMINED, recording for every walk-dependent disagreement whether it is explained by seed-convention\n72:       or method difference (exact-basin closed form vs simulated walk) or is a genuine discrepancy against\n73:       the definition. Report per cell: derived values, per-field comparison verdicts against BOTH implementations,\n74:       and any packet ambiguity encountered, verbatim.'\n75:     breaking_artifact: A definition-exact field (accounting identity, residual_fraction, cap, rho_ORACLE)\n76:       that disagrees with BOTH recorded implementations at any frozen cell; a frozen-cell derivation that\n77:       cannot proceed because quantity.md underdetermines it; a sign/verdict-family disagreement between\n78:       your derivation and BOTH implementations at the same cell. Each localizes the defect to the packet's\n79:       statement or to one of two named implementations.\n80:   - joint: J2_record_integrity_conformance_and_comparison_recompute\n81:     assigned_to: TASK-20260910-c8cb36\n82:     attack_plan: 'Hash-verify the Stage A'''' package against its own seal.json (recompute sha256 of instrument.py,\n83:       run_full.py, cells.jsonl, summary.json, reading_attestation.json, run.log; verify the seal''s declared\n84:       hash set matches and the seal statement''s ordering claim is auditable from the transcript/journal\n85:       if present). Verify the Stage A'''' snapshot receipt (archives/TASK-20260907-c3f20c/snapshot_commit_receipt.json\n86:       against commits d144025225 and ab711b0662) and the Stage B'''' snapshot (9e6396c35e with backfill\n87:       718af27fae) -- every bound path hash recomputed from the committed bytes. Recompute from the production\n88:       summaries: margin identity on all 200 cells; the accounting identity sum_d b(d) + cycle_mass + capped_mass\n89:       == N exactly per cell; residual_fraction == (cycle_mass + capped_mass)/N; cov_static_shuf presence;\n90:       then per-(N,a) mean margins, margin>=0 counts, and bootstrap CI REPRODUCTION from the recorded bootstrap\n91:       seeds (B=10000, log2(N) convention) compared against Stage A'''' summary.json''s CIs. Verify parameters\n92:       against the v3 contract''s stage plan (read specification.v3.yaml stage sections and the amendment):\n93:       T=256/T_sel=128/T4=64/T8=32/r=2, 25 seeds, 4-value grid, both scales, kind stageBpp_exact_ceiling_v3.\n94:       Adjudicate whether the production instrument''s exact-basin method is what v3''s stage plan specifies\n95:       for Stage B'''' (contract-conformant) and whether anything in either package claims more than observations.'\n96:     breaking_artifact: Any seal/receipt hash mismatch; any failed identity on any cell; a CI that fails\n97:       to reproduce from the recorded seed; a parameter or method divergence from v3's stage plan; an interpretation\n98:       claim inside a package that declares itself observations-only.\n99:   - joint: J3_interpretation_and_proves_too_much\n100:     assigned_to: TASK-20260910-59d885\n101:     attack_plan: 'Read the frozen J1 report, then both packages, then attack the candidate readings with\n102:       the declared proves-too-much objects (below), plus your own: exact algebra on the cap convention\n103:       and the exact-basin closed form (is ''exact ceiling'' exact by construction or by computation?);\n104:       the straddled-CI cell''s epistemic status; whether the two-scale comparison supports any N-extrapolation\n105:       beyond 2^24; whether ''robustness of the crossing bracket'' is even well-defined when one bracket\n106:       edge (a=1/8 at 2^20) is underpowered. Record per object the exact step where each candidate inference\n107:       breaks or survives.'\n108:     breaking_artifact: Per-object outcomes with the named broken step; any scoped reading that survives\n109:       an object where its conclusion is known false is the finding.\n110:   blindness:\n111:     mutual: true\n112:     lifted_for: []\n113:     rationale: null\n114:     note: 'J1 (TASK-20260910-19bd7b) is blind until its phase-1 freeze: it reads only blind-input.yaml\n115:       and the four packet files; its frozen report becomes readable by J2/J3 owners only AFTER the Coordinator\n116:       commits it, and must appear in their sources_read. The J2 owner (TASK-20260910-c8cb36) and the J3\n117:       owner (TASK-20260910-59d885) may not read each other''s reports at any point. All three are independent\n118:       sessions that authored none of the reviewed artifacts.'\n119:   proves_too_much:\n120:     objects:\n121:     - The inference 'a=1/8 at N=2^24 with margin CI [+0.0050,+0.0115] is a confirmed feasible operating\n122:       point for an online RESEL-L arm' tested against the goal head's own standing record that ZERO online\n123:       arms have ever been run and that ceiling results are SILENT on whether the online lower-bracket\n124:       mechanism reaches the ceiling at any achievable batch size U (DEC-20260907-b4f2a9 RANK 2/3; DEC-20260907-de6b71)\n125:       -- a ceiling-to-online jump that still goes through proves too much.\n126:     - The inference 'a=1/8 at N=2^20 is G3-INFEASIBLE' tested against that cell's own recorded CI [-0.0002,+0.0087]\n127:       straddling zero and k_25=16/25 -- a strict-infeasibility reading that survives a straddled CI proves\n128:       too much; symmetrically, the inference 'the straddle means the cell is really feasible' tested against\n129:       the same numbers proves too much in the permissive direction.\n130:     - The inference 'the margin identity holding exactly on all 200 cells validates the walk-based estimator'\n131:       tested against the recorded method difference (Stage B'' is an exact-basin closed form with zero\n132:       re-selected arms; the walk-based fields it reports are computed within that closed form) -- an inference\n133:       that reads identity-of-identity as inter-method agreement, or that reads ANY per-seed margin agreement\n134:       between independently seeded implementations as required, breaks.\n135:     - The inference 'the crossing bracket is N-stable' tested against the recorded a=1/8 verdict flip\n136:       between scales (k_25=16 straddled at 2^20 vs k_25=20 CI-excluding-zero at 2^24, corroborated by\n137:       the production k>=0 counts 17 vs 24) -- an N-stability claim that still goes through proves too\n138:       much; conversely an inference 'the bracket moves with N' tested against a=1/16 and a=3/16 verdict\n139:       stability at both scales breaks.\n140:     failure_signature: An inference that still goes through where its conclusion is known false, or that\n141:       voids or validates what the recorded numbers and the frozen contract text do not, is wrong somewhere\n142:       nobody has read closely enough yet.\n143:     assigned_to: TASK-20260910-59d885\n144:   blind_rederivation:\n145:     required: true\n146:     quantity: 'Per-cell derivation, from the derivation packet''s definition ALONE, of every field blind-input.yaml\n147:       lists at the eight frozen cells: share_top_Tsel, cov_static, margin, share_top_T, share_top_Tover4,\n148:       share_top_Tover8, rho_ORACLE, n_dps, cycle_mass, capped_mass, cap, capped_walks, residual_fraction,\n149:       accounting_identity_holds (exact integer), min_basin_size, n_tied_at_Tth_weight, and the three null\n150:       margins (oracle-rand-uniform, oracle-rand-sizebiased, randsel) plus cov_static_shuf. The packet''s\n151:       cap convention, seed conventions and walk construction govern; exact integer/rational arithmetic\n152:       for every exact field.'\n153:     parameters: coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-12ee85/blind-input.yaml\n154:     blind_from:\n155:     - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml\n156:     - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml\n157:     - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.yaml\n158:     - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/\n159:     - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/source/\n160:     - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/runs/\n161:     - coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-4433c1/reviews/TASK-20260907-7afa98/\n162:     - coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-12ee85/review-plan.yaml\n163:     - coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-12ee85/dispatch_queue.json\n164:     - coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-12ee85/reviews/TASK-20260910-c8cb36\n165:     - coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-12ee85/reviews/TASK-20260910-59d885\n166:     - ledger/decisions/\n167:     - ledger/evidence/\n168:     - ledger/hypotheses/H-ECDLP-37dc01.yaml\n169:     phases: Phase 1 blind derivation and freeze; phase 2 comparison against Stage A'' cells.jsonl/summary.json\n170:       and the Stage B'' production summaries, per-field verdicts EXACT / QUALITATIVE / DISAGREES / UNDERDETERMINED\n171:       with the reason for every non-EXACT verdict.\n172:     post_freeze_reads:\n173:     - coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-4433c1/reviews/TASK-20260907-7afa98/cells.jsonl\n174:     - coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-4433c1/reviews/TASK-20260907-7afa98/summary.json\n175:     - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/runs/ (the v3 run summaries for the frozen cells)\n176:   reviewer_independence:\n177:     sessions_must_not_be:\n178:     - TASK-20260907-058c69 (v3 authoring)\n179:     - TASK-20260907-6077f2 (v3 snapshot)\n180:     - TASK-20260907-9c0626 (prior gate)\n181:     - TASK-20260907-7cce3e (post-gate fixes)\n182:     - TASK-20260907-e17c05 (approving gate)\n183:     - TASK-20260907-7afa98 (Stage A'' producer)\n184:     - TASK-20260907-c20638 (Stage B'' snapshot)\n185:     note: Each reviewer is a fresh api_direct session with no prior role in this lineage; runtime provenance\n186:       recorded per run receipt.\n\n(End of file - total 186 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"review_plan:\n  id: REVIEW-PLAN-BATCH-12ee85\n  recorded_at: '2026-09-10'\n  goal_id: GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f\n  question_id: RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5\n  batch_id: BATCH-12ee85\n  experiment_id: EXP-ECDLP-6ac801\n  hypothesis_id: H-ECDLP-37dc01\n  written_by: coordinator-ecdlp-20260910\n  authority: 'Opened under the standing user authorization of 2026-09-06 and the approved v3 chain: EXP-ECDLP-6ac801\n    v3 approved by the independent gate DEC-20260907-b4f2a9 (gate task TASK-20260907-e17c05), which names\n    as its RANK 1 exactly this round''s subject matter: dispatch and then review Stage A'''' (the blind\n    re-derivation seal, executed and snapshotted under BATCH-4433c1) and the Stage B'''' production grid\n    (50 runs, 200 cells, snapshot 9e6396c35e). No run and no reading of this round existed when this plan\n    was written.'\n  claim_under_review: 'Two independent measurement packages, both observations only. (1) Stage A'''':\n    the blind re-derivation seal of TASK-20260907-7afa98 (seal.json hash set + UTC stamp declared before\n    any non-packet read; reading_attestation.json; instrument.py, run_full.py, cells.jsonl, summary.json,\n    run.log), per-cell k_25 verdicts and bootstrap CIs over the full (N, a) grid: a=1/16 G3-FEASIBLE at\n    both scales (25/25, margin +0.0187/+0.0216), a=1/8 borderline (N=2^20 k_25=16, margin +0.0043 CI [-0.0002,+0.0087]","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-12ee85/review-plan.yaml","text":"review_plan:\n  id: REVIEW-PLAN-BATCH-12ee85\n  recorded_at: '2026-09-10'\n  goal_id: GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f\n  question_id: RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5\n  batch_id: BATCH-12ee85\n  experiment_id: EXP-ECDLP-6ac801\n  hypothesis_id: H-ECDLP-37dc01\n  written_by: coordinator-ecdlp-20260910\n  authority: 'Opened under the standing user authorization of 2026-09-06 and the approved v3 chain: EXP-ECDLP-6ac801\n    v3 approved by the independent gate DEC-20260907-b4f2a9 (gate task TASK-20260907-e17c05), which names\n    as its RANK 1 exactly this round''s subject matter: dispatch and then review Stage A'''' (the blind\n    re-derivation seal, executed and snapshotted under BATCH-4433c1) and the Stage B'''' production grid\n    (50 runs, 200 cells, snapshot 9e6396c35e). No run and no reading of this round existed when this plan\n    was written.'\n  claim_under_review: 'Two independent measurement packages, both observations only. (1) Stage A'''':\n    the blind re-derivation seal of TASK-20260907-7afa98 (seal.json hash set + UTC stamp declared before\n    any non-packet read; reading_attestation.json; instrument.py, run_full.py, cells.jsonl, summary.json,\n    run.log), per-cell k_25 verdicts and bootstrap CIs over the full (N, a) grid: a=1/16 G3-FEASIBLE at\n    both scales (25/25, margin +0.0187/+0.0216), a=1/8 borderline (N=2^20 k_25=16, margin +0.0043 CI [-0.0002,+0.0087]\n    straddling zero; N=2^24 k_25=20, margin +0.0081 CI [+0.0050,+0.0115]), a=3/16 and a=1/4 G3-INFEASIBLE\n    at both scales with CIs excluding zero. (2) Stage B'''': the production grid RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-v3-n20-s01..25\n    and RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-v3-n24-s01..25 (kind stageBpp_exact_ceiling_v3, exact-basin closed form, zero\n    re-selected arms), each run covering the four-value a-grid {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4} at T=256, T_sel=128,\n    T4=64, T8=32, r=2, 25 seeds per scale = 200 cells, snapshot-archived at commit 9e6396c35e (receipt\n    backfilled 718af27fae). NEITHER package interprets; both record. The comparison of the two packages,\n    and every reading of the crossing bracket''s robustness and N-dependence at the borderline cell a=1/8,\n    are THE WORK OF THIS REVIEW ROUND and are unselected in the records under review.'\n  coordinator_prior: 'Written before any reviewer runs, on the opening Coordinator''s own independent\n    recomputation (NOT on the producers'' code): I recomputed the margin identity margin == exact_top_T_sel_share\n    - static_T_r2_exact_coverage on ALL 200 production cells and it holds exactly (200/200); I recomputed\n    per-(N,a) mean margins and margin>=0 counts from the production summaries (a=1/16: +0.0168 k=24/25\n    at 2^20, +0.0202 k=25/25 at 2^24; a=1/8: +0.0069 k=17/25 at 2^20, +0.0102 k=24/25 at 2^24; a=3/16:\n    -0.0086 k=8/25 at 2^20, -0.0054 k=5/25 at 2^24; a=1/4: -0.0228 k=2/25 at 2^20, -0.0185 k=0/25 at 2^24;\n    max residual fraction 0.0232). (1) J1 blind re-derivation: I EXPECT the derived values at the eight\n    frozen cells to agree with the PRODUCTION grid on the definition-exact fields (accounting_identity_holds\n    true, residual_fraction, cap convention, rho_ORACLE) and to agree with BOTH implementations only QUALITATIVELY\n    on seed-dependent fields (sign of margin, verdict family), because three implementations (blind instrument,\n    Stage A'''' instrument, production exact-basin closed form) need not agree bit-wise on walk-dependent\n    quantities; per-seed margin magnitudes are expected to differ between implementations at the same\n    cell and that difference is EXPECTED, not a defect. The live risk I name: if quantity.md''s seed/walk\n    convention underdetermines a field, the honest blind report records the ambiguity rather than resolving\n    it, and the ambiguity localizes to the packet''s statement -- that would be a finding about the definition,\n    carried to the composed decision. (2) J2 integrity: I EXPECT the Stage A'''' seal hashes to match\n    the committed files byte for byte, both snapshot receipts to verify (Stage A'''' via the c3f20c receipt\n    commits d144025225/ab711b0662; Stage B'''' via 9e6396c35e + backfill 718af27fae), the margin identity\n    to hold on all 200 cells (I verified it myself), and the accounting identity sum_d b(d) + cycle_mass\n    + capped_mass == N to hold exactly per cell. (3) J2 conformance: I EXPECT params (T=256, T_sel=128,\n    T4=64, T8=32, r=2, 25 seeds, 4-value grid, both scales) to match v3''s stage plan and the bootstrap\n    CIs to reproduce from the recorded bootstrap seeds (bootstrap_B 10000, log2(N) convention). (4) The\n    comparison headline I EXPECT: the crossing bracket is corroborated as BETWEEN a=1/16 and a=3/16 with\n    a=1/8 the live borderline cell, stable in location across N in {2^20, 2^24}, with a visible N-dependence\n    AT a=1/8 only (leaning-infeasible/straddled at 2^20, feasible with CI excluding zero at 2^24) -- the\n    robustness and N-dependence reading v3''s rewritten objective exists to measure. (5) Expected disposition:\n    EV-ECDLP-5035ed records the two-implementation corroboration at the tested scope (ceiling-level, exact-basin,\n    N in {2^20, 2^24}, 25 seeds); NO hypothesis-status promotion on any clause of H-ECDLP-37dc01 in this\n    round (DEC-20260907-b4f2a9 RANK 3 makes any promotion a further decision on THIS round''s reviewed\n    evidence; the goal head independently forbids any promotion beyond ceiling-feasibility before an ONLINE\n    arm exists -- zero have); the composed DEC-20260910-34e654 records the robustness reading and names\n    the RANK-2 online-RESEL-L lane as successor. If the reviewers break a joint this prior expected to\n    hold, the composition follows the reports, not this prior.'\n  joints:\n  - joint: J1_blind_rederivation_and_cross_implementation\n    assigned_to: TASK-20260910-19bd7b\n    attack_plan: 'TWO PHASES, FREEZE ENFORCED. Phase 1 (blind): read ONLY blind-input.yaml and the four\n      packet files (experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/derivation-packet/PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3/{MANIFEST.yaml,quantity.md,deliverables.md,prohibitions.md});\n      implement the quantity from the definition from scratch; derive every listed field at the eight\n      frozen cells; write and freeze the report in your own task directory; STOP. Phase 2 (comparison,\n      only after the Coordinator commits the frozen report): read Stage A'''' cells.jsonl/summary.json\n      and the Stage B'''' summaries for the same cells; compare per field into EXACT / QUALITATIVE / DISAGREES\n      / UNDERDETERMINED, recording for every walk-dependent disagreement whether it is explained by seed-convention\n      or method difference (exact-basin closed form vs simulated walk) or is a genuine discrepancy against\n      the definition. Report per cell: derived values, per-field comparison verdicts against BOTH implementations,\n      and any packet ambiguity encountered, verbatim.'\n    breaking_artifact: A definition-exact field (accounting identity, residual_fraction, cap, rho_ORACLE)\n      that disagrees with BOTH recorded implementations at any frozen cell; a frozen-cell derivation that\n      cannot proceed because quantity.md underdetermines it; a sign/verdict-family disagreement between\n      your derivation and BOTH implementations at the same cell. Each localizes the defect to the packet's\n      statement or to one of two named implementations.\n  - joint: J2_record_integrity_conformance_and_comparison_recompute\n    assigned_to: TASK-20260910-c8cb36\n    attack_plan: 'Hash-verify the Stage A'''' package against its own seal.json (recompute sha256 of instrument.py,\n      run_full.py, cells.jsonl, summary.json, reading_attestation.json, run.log; verify the seal''s declared\n      hash set matches and the seal statement''s ordering claim is auditable from the transcript/journal\n      if present). Verify the Stage A'''' snapshot receipt (archives/TASK-20260907-c3f20c/snapshot_commit_receipt.json\n      against commits d144025225 and ab711b0662) and the Stage B'''' snapshot (9e6396c35e with backfill\n      718af27fae) -- every bound path hash recomputed from the committed bytes. Recompute from the production\n      summaries: margin identity on all 200 cells; the accounting identity sum_d b(d) + cycle_mass + capped_mass\n      == N exactly per cell; residual_fraction == (cycle_mass + capped_mass)/N; cov_static_shuf presence;\n      then per-(N,a) mean margins, margin>=0 counts, and bootstrap CI REPRODUCTION from the recorded bootstrap\n      seeds (B=10000, log2(N) convention) compared against Stage A'''' summary.json''s CIs. Verify parameters\n      against the v3 contract''s stage plan (read specification.v3.yaml stage sections and the amendment):\n      T=256/T_sel=128/T4=64/T8=32/r=2, 25 seeds, 4-value grid, both scales, kind stageBpp_exact_ceiling_v3.\n      Adjudicate whether the production instrument''s exact-basin method is what v3''s stage plan specifies\n      for Stage B'''' (contract-conformant) and whether anything in either package claims more than observations.'\n    breaking_artifact: Any seal/receipt hash mismatch; any failed identity on any cell; a CI that fails\n      to reproduce from the recorded seed; a parameter or method divergence from v3's stage plan; an interpretation\n      claim inside a package that declares itself observations-only.\n  - joint: J3_interpretation_and_proves_too_much\n    assigned_to: TASK-20260910-59d885\n    attack_plan: 'Read the frozen J1 report, then both packages, then attack the candidate readings with\n      the declared proves-too-much objects (below), plus your own: exact algebra on the cap convention\n      and the exact-basin closed form (is ''exact ceiling'' exact by construction or by computation?);\n      the straddled-CI cell''s epistemic status; whether the two-scale comparison supports any N-extrapolation\n      beyond 2^24; whether ''robustness of the crossing bracket'' is even well-defined when one bracket\n      edge (a=1/8 at 2^20) is underpowered. Record per object the exact step where each candidate inference\n      breaks or survives.'\n    breaking_artifact: Per-object outcomes with the named broken step; any scoped reading that survives\n      an object where its conclusion is known false is the finding.\n  blindness:\n    mutual: true\n    lifted_for: []\n    rationale: null\n    note: 'J1 (TASK-20260910-19bd7b) is blind until its phase-1 freeze: it reads only blind-input.yaml\n      and the four packet files; its frozen report becomes readable by J2/J3 owners only AFTER the Coordinator\n      commits it, and must appear in their sources_read. The J2 owner (TASK-20260910-c8cb36) and the J3\n      owner (TASK-20260910-59d885) may not read each other''s reports at any point. All three are independent\n      sessions that authored none of the reviewed artifacts.'\n  proves_too_much:\n    objects:\n    - The inference 'a=1/8 at N=2^24 with margin CI [+0.0050,+0.0115] is a confirmed feasible operating\n      point for an online RESEL-L arm' tested against the goal head's own standing record that ZERO online\n      arms have ever been run and that ceiling results are SILENT on whether the online lower-bracket\n      mechanism reaches the ceiling at any achievable batch size U (DEC-20260907-b4f2a9 RANK 2/3; DEC-20260907-de6b71)\n      -- a ceiling-to-online jump that still goes through proves too much.\n    - The inference 'a=1/8 at N=2^20 is G3-INFEASIBLE' tested against that cell's own recorded CI [-0.0002,+0.0087]\n      straddling zero and k_25=16/25 -- a strict-infeasibility reading that survives a straddled CI proves\n      too much; symmetrically, the inference 'the straddle means the cell is really feasible' tested against\n      the same numbers proves too much in the permissive direction.\n    - The inference 'the margin identity holding exactly on all 200 cells validates the walk-based estimator'\n      tested against the recorded method difference (Stage B'' is an exact-basin closed form with zero\n      re-selected arms; the walk-based fields it reports are computed within that closed form) -- an inference\n      that reads identity-of-identity as inter-method agreement, or that reads ANY per-seed margin agreement\n      between independently seeded implementations as required, breaks.\n    - The inference 'the crossing bracket is N-stable' tested against the recorded a=1/8 verdict flip\n      between scales (k_25=16 straddled at 2^20 vs k_25=20 CI-excluding-zero at 2^24, corroborated by\n      the production k>=0 counts 17 vs 24) -- an N-stability claim that still goes through proves too\n      much; conversely an inference 'the bracket moves with N' tested against a=1/16 and a=3/16 verdict\n      stability at both scales breaks.\n    failure_signature: An inference that still goes through where its conclusion is known false, or that\n      voids or validates what the recorded numbers and the frozen contract text do not, is wrong somewhere\n      nobody has read closely enough yet.\n    assigned_to: TASK-20260910-59d885\n  blind_rederivation:\n    required: true\n    quantity: 'Per-cell derivation, from the derivation packet''s definition ALONE, of every field blind-input.yaml\n      lists at the eight frozen cells: share_top_Tsel, cov_static, margin, share_top_T, share_top_Tover4,\n      share_top_Tover8, rho_ORACLE, n_dps, cycle_mass, capped_mass, cap, capped_walks, residual_fraction,\n      accounting_identity_holds (exact integer), min_basin_size, n_tied_at_Tth_weight, and the three null\n      margins (oracle-rand-uniform, oracle-rand-sizebiased, randsel) plus cov_static_shuf. The packet''s\n      cap convention, seed conventions and walk construction govern; exact integer/rational arithmetic\n      for every exact field.'\n    parameters: coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-12ee85/blind-input.yaml\n    blind_from:\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.yaml\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/source/\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/runs/\n    - coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-4433c1/reviews/TASK-20260907-7afa98/\n    - coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-12ee85/review-plan.yaml\n    - coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-12ee85/dispatch_queue.json\n    - coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-12ee85/reviews/TASK-20260910-c8cb36\n    - coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-12ee85/reviews/TASK-20260910-59d885\n    - ledger/decisions/\n    - ledger/evidence/\n    - ledger/hypotheses/H-ECDLP-37dc01.yaml\n    phases: Phase 1 blind derivation and freeze; phase 2 comparison against Stage A'' cells.jsonl/summary.json\n      and the Stage B'' production summaries, per-field verdicts EXACT / QUALITATIVE / DISAGREES / UNDERDETERMINED\n      with the reason for every non-EXACT verdict.\n    post_freeze_reads:\n    - coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-4433c1/reviews/TASK-20260907-7afa98/cells.jsonl\n    - coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-4433c1/reviews/TASK-20260907-7afa98/summary.json\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/runs/ (the v3 run summaries for the frozen cells)\n  reviewer_independence:\n    sessions_must_not_be:\n    - TASK-20260907-058c69 (v3 authoring)\n    - TASK-20260907-6077f2 (v3 snapshot)\n    - TASK-20260907-9c0626 (prior gate)\n    - TASK-20260907-7cce3e (post-gate fixes)\n    - TASK-20260907-e17c05 (approving gate)\n    - TASK-20260907-7afa98 (Stage A'' producer)\n    - TASK-20260907-c20638 (Stage B'' snapshot)\n    note: Each reviewer is a fresh api_direct session with no prior role in this lineage; runtime provenance\n      recorded per run receipt.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":186,"totalLines":186,"truncated":false}},"title":"coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-12ee85/review-plan.yaml","time":{"start":1789085504079,"end":1789085504091}},"id":"prt_08dce4d4d001XxfUnQuFwj6jgo","sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","messageID":"msg_08dcbb348001f3YJDMARqUfjDT"}}
