{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789085754087,"sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-999770607659c385","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-12ee85/blind-input.yaml"},"output":"<path>/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-12ee85/blind-input.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Blind input for J1 (TASK-20260910-19bd7b), BATCH-12ee85.\n2: # Authored by the opening Coordinator BEFORE any reviewer ran.\n3: # The J1 owner reads THIS file plus exactly the four packet files at\n4: # experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/derivation-packet/PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3/\n5: # (MANIFEST.yaml, quantity.md, deliverables.md, prohibitions.md) until the\n6: # two-phase freeze in the review plan. NOTHING else in the repository.\n7: \n8: blind_input:\n9:   id: BLIND-INPUT-BATCH-12ee85\n10:   for_task: TASK-20260910-19bd7b\n11:   statement: >\n12:     Derive, from the derivation packet's definition of the quantity ALONE\n13:     (quantity.md is the definition; deliverables.md names the fields), the\n14:     per-cell values listed below for the frozen cells. Your own\n15:     implementation, any language, any libraries. Do not look for any\n16:     existing implementation; the packet's prohibitions.md governs. Freeze\n17:     everything first (phase 1); the comparison phase (phase 2) is named in\n18:     the review plan and runs only after the Coordinator commits your\n19:     frozen report.\n20: \n21:   frozen_cells:\n22:     # (N, a, seed) triples; parameters per the packet's grid definition.\n23:     - {N: 1048576, a: '1/8',   seed: 1}\n24:     - {N: 1048576, a: '1/8',   seed: 7}\n25:     - {N: 1048576, a: '1/8',   seed: 13}\n26:     - {N: 16777216, a: '1/8',  seed: 3}\n27:     - {N: 16777216, a: '1/8',  seed: 11}\n28:     - {N: 16777216, a: '1/8',  seed: 25}\n29:     - {N: 1048576, a: '1/16',  seed: 5}\n30:     - {N: 16777216, a: '1/16', seed: 17}\n31: \n32:   derived_fields_per_cell:\n33:     - share_top_Tsel\n34:     - cov_static\n35:     - margin          # per the packet's definition of margin\n36:     - share_top_T\n37:     - share_top_Tover4\n38:     - share_top_Tover8\n39:     - rho_ORACLE\n40:     - n_dps\n41:     - cycle_mass\n42:     - capped_mass\n43:     - cap             # per the packet's cap convention\n44:     - capped_walks\n45:     - residual_fraction\n46:     - accounting_identity_holds   # sum_d b(d) + cycle_mass + capped_mass == N, exactly\n47:     - min_basin_size\n48:     - n_tied_at_Tth_weight\n49:     - margin_null_oracle_rand_uniform\n50:     - margin_null_oracle_rand_sizebiased\n51:     - margin_null_randsel\n52:     - cov_static_shuf\n53: \n54:   derivation_requirements:\n55:     - Exact integer/rational arithmetic wherever the definition is exact;\n56:       any float use must be disclosed per value with the exact source of\n57:       rounding. The accounting identity check must be exact integer.\n58:     - State your seed convention for every pseudo-random choice, taken\n59:       from the packet's own definition; if the packet underdetermines a\n60:       choice your derivation needs, record the ambiguity AS the result\n61:       for that field rather than resolving it silently.\n62:     - Record per cell the wall time and the exact command.\n63: \n64:   output: >\n65:     Write your frozen report to your own task directory\n66:     (reviews/TASK-20260910-19bd7b/blind-rederivation.yaml) as phase 1 and\n67:     STOP; the review plan defines what phase 2 may read and compare.\n\n(End of file - total 67 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Blind input for J1 (TASK-20260910-19bd7b), BATCH-12ee85.\n# Authored by the opening Coordinator BEFORE any reviewer ran.\n# The J1 owner reads THIS file plus exactly the four packet files at\n# experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/derivation-packet/PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3/\n# (MANIFEST.yaml, quantity.md, deliverables.md, prohibitions.md) until the\n# two-phase freeze in the review plan. NOTHING else in the repository.\n\nblind_input:\n  id: BLIND-INPUT-BATCH-12ee85\n  for_task: TASK-20260910-19bd7b\n  statement: >\n    Derive, from the derivation packet's definition of the quantity ALONE\n    (quantity.md is the definition; deliverables.md names the fields), the\n    per-cell values listed below for the frozen cells. Your own\n    implementation, any language, any libraries. Do not look for any\n    existing implementation; the packet's prohibitions.md governs. Freeze\n    everything first (phase 1); the comparison phase (phase 2) is named in\n    the review plan and runs only after the Coordinator commits your\n    frozen report.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-12ee85/blind-input.yaml","text":"# Blind input for J1 (TASK-20260910-19bd7b), BATCH-12ee85.\n# Authored by the opening Coordinator BEFORE any reviewer ran.\n# The J1 owner reads THIS file plus exactly the four packet files at\n# experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/derivation-packet/PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3/\n# (MANIFEST.yaml, quantity.md, deliverables.md, prohibitions.md) until the\n# two-phase freeze in the review plan. NOTHING else in the repository.\n\nblind_input:\n  id: BLIND-INPUT-BATCH-12ee85\n  for_task: TASK-20260910-19bd7b\n  statement: >\n    Derive, from the derivation packet's definition of the quantity ALONE\n    (quantity.md is the definition; deliverables.md names the fields), the\n    per-cell values listed below for the frozen cells. Your own\n    implementation, any language, any libraries. Do not look for any\n    existing implementation; the packet's prohibitions.md governs. Freeze\n    everything first (phase 1); the comparison phase (phase 2) is named in\n    the review plan and runs only after the Coordinator commits your\n    frozen report.\n\n  frozen_cells:\n    # (N, a, seed) triples; parameters per the packet's grid definition.\n    - {N: 1048576, a: '1/8',   seed: 1}\n    - {N: 1048576, a: '1/8',   seed: 7}\n    - {N: 1048576, a: '1/8',   seed: 13}\n    - {N: 16777216, a: '1/8',  seed: 3}\n    - {N: 16777216, a: '1/8',  seed: 11}\n    - {N: 16777216, a: '1/8',  seed: 25}\n    - {N: 1048576, a: '1/16',  seed: 5}\n    - {N: 16777216, a: '1/16', seed: 17}\n\n  derived_fields_per_cell:\n    - share_top_Tsel\n    - cov_static\n    - margin          # per the packet's definition of margin\n    - share_top_T\n    - share_top_Tover4\n    - share_top_Tover8\n    - rho_ORACLE\n    - n_dps\n    - cycle_mass\n    - capped_mass\n    - cap             # per the packet's cap convention\n    - capped_walks\n    - residual_fraction\n    - accounting_identity_holds   # sum_d b(d) + cycle_mass + capped_mass == N, exactly\n    - min_basin_size\n    - n_tied_at_Tth_weight\n    - margin_null_oracle_rand_uniform\n    - margin_null_oracle_rand_sizebiased\n    - margin_null_randsel\n    - cov_static_shuf\n\n  derivation_requirements:\n    - Exact integer/rational arithmetic wherever the definition is exact;\n      any float use must be disclosed per value with the exact source of\n      rounding. The accounting identity check must be exact integer.\n    - State your seed convention for every pseudo-random choice, taken\n      from the packet's own definition; if the packet underdetermines a\n      choice your derivation needs, record the ambiguity AS the result\n      for that field rather than resolving it silently.\n    - Record per cell the wall time and the exact command.\n\n  output: >\n    Write your frozen report to your own task directory\n    (reviews/TASK-20260910-19bd7b/blind-rederivation.yaml) as phase 1 and\n    STOP; the review plan defines what phase 2 may read and compare.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":67,"totalLines":67,"truncated":false}},"title":"coordination/goals/GOAL