{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789086328778,"sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b5e9a28e90fb7a45","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-4433c1/reviews/TASK-20260907-7afa98/joints_and_implementation_notes.json"},"output":"<path>/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-4433c1/reviews/TASK-20260907-7afa98/joints_and_implementation_notes.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"task_id\": \"TASK-20260907-7afa98\",\n3:   \"purpose\": \"Disclosure of the seven joints deliverables.md #5 assigns to the re-deriver, plus every implementation freedom exercised, per quantity.md #9 and prohibitions.md #4 ('any language, any libraries, any standard mix64, any RNG'). None of this was read from anywhere; it documents choices made while implementing quantity.md from scratch.\",\n4: \n5:   \"joint_1_cap_applied_in_both_places\": {\n6:     \"claim\": \"cap = ceil(8*W) is applied both to the exact basin-assignment predicate (dist(x) <= cap) and to pool-construction walk termination (a walk reaching cap steps without a DP terminates capped, crediting no S_d/h_d).\",\n7:     \"how_verified\": \"dist(x) is computed EXACTLY for every point via full functional-graph enumeration (see joint_2), independent of cap; cap is applied only afterward, once, to classify each point into ASSIGNED/CYCLE MASS/CAPPED MASS, and again, independently, in pool_construct() where a random start point's fate is looked up from the same exact dist/root arrays and classified capped iff dist==-1 or dist>cap. The two applications share one 'cap' integer computed once per (N,a) cell via Decimal ceil(8*W).\"\n8:   },\n9: \n10:   \"joint_2_residual_accounting\": {\n11:     \"claim\": \"The three classes are disjoint and exhaustive and the accounting identity sum_d b(d) + cycle_mass + capped_mass == N holds exactly, with b(d) >= 1 for every DP.\",\n12:     \"how_verified\": \"Checked programmatically, exactly (integer arithmetic, no tolerance), at all 200 computed cells. accounting_identity_holds == true at all 200; min_basin_size >= 1 at all 200 (minimum observed value across all cells and DPs was exactly 1, never 0). No defect of this kind was found.\",\n13:     \"why_the_identity_is_close_to_a_tautology_here\": \"dist(x) is computed once, exhaustively, over all N points into exactly {-1 (unreachable), 0..cap (assigned), >cap (capped)}, and basin_counts is built by bincount over the assigned subset's root values, so the identity is a direct consequence of a correct partition of the dist array rather than an independent recomputation. It was still checked explicitly per cell, and is exactly the kind of self-check the packet asks for.\"\n14:   },\n15: \n16:   \"joint_3_universe_asymmetry\": {\n17:     \"claim\": \"cov_static ranges over the pool's T selected entries; share_top ranges over ALL n_dps DPs of the exact partition, independent of the pool.\",\n18:     \"how_verified\": \"share_top(k) is computed from sizes_all_dps, an array over every DP found by the DP predicate on all N points (independent of pool construction). cov_static is computed only from the T pool entries surviving weight-selection. The two arrays are built from different index sets (dp_nodes vs sel_dp_ids) and never conflated in the code.\"\n19:   },\n20: \n21:   \"joint_4_weight_and_tiebreak\": {\n22:     \"claim\": \"Selection is by weight_d = S_d + 4*W*h_d, never true basin size; ties at the T-th largest weight are broken by an ascending per-entry pseudorandom key bound to pool-insertion order.\",\n23:     \"how_verified\": \"weight_d is computed from Decimal(S_d) + 4*W_decimal*Decimal(h_d) (W taken to 80 significant digits), not from any basin-size array. Insertion order = the order in which pool_construct() first discovers each distinct DP. Tie-break keys are one bulk array of length r*T drawn once per (N,a,seed) from a PRNG seeded deterministically from the integer seed (see rng_conventions below), indexed by insertion order, and used as an ascending secondary sort key alongside descending weight.\",\n24:     \"why_decimal_not_float_for_weight\": \"At a in {1/16, 1/4} in this grid, W is an exact integer, so weight_d is exactly S_d + 4*W*h_d in integer arithmetic; a naive float64 computation risks manufacturing or hiding exact ties. Decimal at 80-digit precision was used uniformly so that reported ties (n_tied_at_Tth_weight, range 1-9 across the 200 cells) reflect real coincidences in (S_d, h_d) rather than floating-point artifacts.\"\n25:   },\n26: \n27:   \"joint_5_T_at_smaller_scale\": {\n28:     \"claim\": \"T = 64 at N = 2^20 (frozen table), not round(2^20^(1/3)) = 102.\",\n29:     \"how_verified\": \"T_TABLE = {2**20: 64, 2**24: 256} is a literal lookup table copied from quantity.md #10, never computed from a formula. All derived quantities (T_sel, cap, W) were cross-checked against quantity.md's own printed decimal table before the production run and matched to the digits shown (see validation note below).\"\n30:   },\n31: \n32:   \"joint_6_null_object_universe\": {\n33:     \"claim\": \"NULL-ORACLE-RAND draws its subset from all DPs of the same enumerated partition, not from the pool.\",\n34:     \"how_verified\": \"Both NULL-ORACLE-RAND variants (uniform and size-biased) sample index sets from range(n_dps) against sizes_all_dps (the full-partition array). NULL-RANDSEL and NULL-SHUF, by contrast, correctly draw from the r*T pool array (pool_sizes_arr), per quantity.md #12's own separate specification for that arm.\"\n35:   },\n36: \n37:   \"joint_7_verdicts_resampling_free\": {\n38:     \"claim\": \"k_25, k_5, and the sign of mean_margin are computed exactly and do not depend on the bootstrap.\",\n39:     \"how_verified\": \"k_25/k_5/verdict_25/verdict_5/mean_margin_sign are computed directly from the array of 25 (or 5) per-seed margins via exact comparison (margin >= 0) and exact mean sign; the percentile-bootstrap CI is computed afterward, in a separate function, and is not read by any verdict computation.\"\n40:   },\n41: \n42:   \"rng_and_convention_disclosures_licensed_by_quantity_md_section_9_and_prohibitions_md_section_4\": {\n43:     \"mix64\": \"splitmix64 finalizer (Stafford 'mix13' variant): z^=z>>30; z*=0xbf58476d1ce4e5b9; z^=z>>27; z*=0x94d049bb133111eb; z^=z>>31; all mod 2^64. A standard, publicly documented avalanche mixer, chosen because quantity.md #1 explicitly says 'any standard one; yours need not match anyone else's'.\",\n44:     \"restart_rng / tiebreak_rng / null_uniform_rng / null_sizebiased_rng / null_randsel_rng / null_shuf_rng\": \"Each is a numpy Generator (PCG64) seeded by the low 8 bytes of sha256(f'{seed}|{tag}|{N}|{a.numerator}|{a.denominator}'), where tag in {restart, tiebreak, null_uniform, null_sizebiased, null_randsel, null_shuf}. This is a deterministic, reproducible, but otherwise arbitrary convention for randomness that quantity.md never specifies a seed formula for (unlike the bootstrap, which quantity.md #11 does specify exactly). This choice is disclosed, not concealed, and is not expected to match any other implementation's realization, per the same license quantity.md #9 gives to mix64 and to the tie-break key stream.\",\n45:     \"size_biased_sampling_without_replacement\": \"Implemented via the Efraimidis-Spirakis exponential-key method in the log domain (key_i = log(u_i)/w_i, take the T_sel largest), a standard exact algorithm for weighted sampling without replacement. Not specified by quantity.md beyond 'drawing the T_sel-subset with probability proportional to basin size'; quantity.md #12 itself says of this arm only 'report it; nothing depends on it'.\",\n46:     \"bootstrap_n_bits\": \"quantity.md #11's rng formula uses a symbol 'n_bits' that is not spelled out. Taken to mean log2(N) (20 or 24 for this grid), the only reading consistent with N always being written as a power of two throughout quantity.md. This affects only the bootstrap RNG seed, and the bootstrap is explicitly declared non-verdict-bearing ('it routes, it does not decide', quantity.md #11; joint_7 above).\"\n47:   },\n48: \n49:   \"derived_field_not_literally_named_in_deliverables_md\": {\n50:     \"margin_null_shuf\": \"deliverables.md's per-cell table lists cov_static_shuf for NULL-SHUF but does not separately name a 'margin_null_shuf'. quantity.md #7 defines margin = share_top_Tsel - cov_static uniformly, and quantity.md #12 frames every other null arm as a substitution into that same formula. We additionally report margin_null_shuf = share_top_Tsel - cov_static_shuf as the direct, mechanical application of the already-stated margin formula with cov_static_shuf substituted for cov_static, and used it to compute mean_margin_null_shuf / n_seeds_margin_null_nonneg_shuf at the per-(N,a) level (which deliverables.md #3 does ask for, 'for each null arm', without listing NULL-SHUF's field name either). This is disclosed as an extension by direct formula reuse, not as an invented convention resolving an ambiguity -- no other value was possible once cov_static_shuf existed and quantity.md's own margin formula was applied unchanged. cov_static_shuf itself (the literally required field) is also reported per cell, unmodified.\"\n51:   },\n52: \n53:   \"rho_ORACLE_interpretation\": {\n54:     \"quantity_md_text\": \"'the smallest T_sel/T at which share_top(T_sel) reaches cov_static' (quantity.md #12, DECAY readings)\",\n55:     \"reading_adopted\": \"share_top(k) is already defined in quantity.md #7 as a function of an integer k (the count of top-ranked DPs by exact basin size). rho_ORACLE was computed by treating k as a free variable, finding the smallest integer k in [0, n_dps] with share_top(k) >= cov_static (using the cell's own already-computed cov_static, via exact integer comparison against the cumulative basin-size sum, never float comparison), and reporting k/T. This is the direct extension of an already-stated function to a free argument, not an invented formula; no alternative reading was identified.\",\n56:     \"well_definedness_check\": \"Since cov_static is itself an exact sum of basin sizes over a subset of DPs, and share_top(n_dps) equals the sum over ALL DPs (a superset), share_top(n_dps) >= cov_static always, so the search always terminates within k <= n_dps at every one of the 200 cells; no cell required clipping or produced an undefined value.\"\n57:   },\n58: \n59:   \"packet_completeness_finding\": {\n60:     \"verdict\": \"The packet was found COMPLETE. Every field deliverables.md requires was computable from quantity.md's definitions and parameters alone, using only implementation freedoms quantity.md #9 and prohibitions.md #4 explicitly license (mix64 choice; RNG/seed choice for restarts, tie-break keys, and the four control-arm draws; the direct, unmodified extension of the already-stated share_top(k) and margin() formulas noted above). No defensible-but-arbitrary convention had to be invented to resolve an actual ambiguity in a load-bearing formula; the two load-bearing formulas the packet itself flags as historically dangerous (cap = ceil(8*W), applied in exactly the two places quantity.md #3 names; and the accounting identity of quantity.md #4) were both implemented exactly as specified and checked to hold at every one of the 200 cells with zero exceptions.\",\n61:     \"validation_performed_before_the_production_run\": \"(a) The core algorithm (exact forward-orbit distance to first DP, computed via reverse-graph multi-source BFS, which is exact because every node has out-degree exactly 1) was cross-checked against a brute-force O(N x path length) reference implementation on 40 random tiny synthetic instances (N in {8,16,32,64,128}); all 40 matched exactly, including which specific DP each reachable point mapped to. (b) W, cap, and dp_threshold, computed via Decimal at 80 significant digits from the exact rational a*N/T, were checked against quantity.md #10's own printed table for all 8 (N,a) combinations and matched to every printed digit.\"\n62:   }\n63: }\n\n(End of file - total 63 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"task_id\": \"TASK-20260907-7afa98\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Disclosure of the seven joints deliverables.md #5 assigns to the re-deriver, plus every implementation freedom exercised, per quantity.md #9 and prohibitions.md #4 ('any language, any libraries, any standard mix64, any RNG'). None of this was read from anywhere; it documents choices made while implementing quantity.md from scratch.\",\n\n  \"joint_1_cap_applied_in_both_places\": {\n    \"claim\": \"cap = ceil(8*W) is applied both to the exact basin-assignment predicate (dist(x) <= cap) and to pool-construction walk termination (a walk reaching cap steps without a DP terminates capped, crediting no S_d/h_d).\",\n    \"how_verified\": \"dist(x) is computed EXACTLY for every point via full functional-graph enumeration (see joint_2), independent of cap; cap is applied only afterward, once, to classify each point into ASSIGNED/CYCLE MASS/CAPPED MASS, and again, independently, in pool_construct() where a random start point's fate is looked up from the same exact dist/root arrays and classified capped iff dist==-1 or dist>cap. The two applications share one 'cap' integer computed once per (N,a) cell via Decimal ceil(8*W).\"\n  },\n\n  \"joint_2_residual_accounting\": {\n    \"claim\": \"The three classes are disjoint and exhaustive and the accounting identity sum_d b(d) + cycle_mass + capped_mass == N holds exactly, with b(d) >= 1 for every DP.\",\n    \"how_verified\": \"Checked programmatically, exactly (integer arithmetic, no tolerance), at all 200 computed cells. accounting_identity_holds == true at all 200; min_basin_size >= 1 at all 200 (minimum observed value across all cells and DPs was exactly 1, never 0). No defect of this kind was found.\",\n    \"why_the_identity_is_close_to_a_tautology_here\": \"dist(x) is computed once, exhaustively, over all N points into exactly {-1 (unreachable), 0..cap (assigned), >cap (capped)}, and basin_counts is built by bincount over the assigned subset's root values, so the identity is a direct consequence of a correct partition of the dist array rather than an independent recomputation. It was still checked explicitly per cell, and is exactly the kind of self-check the packet asks for.\"\n  },\n\n  \"joint_3_universe_asymmetry\": {\n    \"claim\": \"cov_static ranges over the pool's T selected entries; share_top ranges over ALL n_dps DPs of the exact partition, independent of the pool.\",\n    \"how_verified\": \"share_top(k) is computed from sizes_all_dps, an array over every DP found by the DP predicate on all N points (independent of pool construction). cov_static is computed only from the T pool entries surviving weight-selection. The two arrays are built from different index sets (dp_nodes vs sel_dp_ids) and never conflated in the code.\"\n  },\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-4433c1/reviews/TASK-20260907-7afa98/joints_and_implementation_notes.json","text":"{\n  \"task_id\": \"TASK-20260907-7afa98\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Disclosure of the seven joints deliverables.md #5 assigns to the re-deriver, plus every implementation freedom exercised, per quantity.md #9 and prohibitions.md #4 ('any language, any libraries, any standard mix64, any RNG'). None of this was read from anywhere; it documents choices made while implementing quantity.md from scratch.\",\n\n  \"joint_1_cap_applied_in_both_places\": {\n    \"claim\": \"cap = ceil(8*W) is applied both to the exact basin-assignment predicate (dist(x) <= cap) and to pool-construction walk termination (a walk reaching cap steps without a DP terminates capped, crediting no S_d/h_d).\",\n    \"how_verified\": \"dist(x) is computed EXACTLY for every point via full functional-graph enumeration (see joint_2), independent of cap; cap is applied only afterward, once, to classify each point into ASSIGNED/CYCLE MASS/CAPPED MASS, and again, independently, in pool_construct() where a random start point's fate is looked up from the same exact dist/root arrays and classified capped iff dist==-1 or dist>cap. The two applications share one 'cap' integer computed once per (N,a) cell via Decimal ceil(8*W).\"\n  },\n\n  \"joint_2_residual_accounting\": {\n    \"claim\": \"The three classes are disjoint and exhaustive and the accounting identity sum_d b(d) + cycle_mass + capped_mass == N holds exactly, with b(d) >= 1 for every DP.\",\n    \"how_verified\": \"Checked programmatically, exactly (integer arithmetic, no tolerance), at all 200 computed cells. accounting_identity_holds == true at all 200; min_basin_size >= 1 at all 200 (minimum observed value across all cells and DPs was exactly 1, never 0). No defect of this kind was found.\",\n    \"why_the_identity_is_close_to_a_tautology_here\": \"dist(x) is computed once, exhaustively, over all N points into exactly {-1 (unreachable), 0..cap (assigned), >cap (capped)}, and basin_counts is built by bincount over the assigned subset's root values, so the identity is a direct consequence of a correct partition of the dist array rather than an independent recomputation. It was still checked explicitly per cell, and is exactly the kind of self-check the packet asks for.\"\n  },\n\n  \"joint_3_universe_asymmetry\": {\n    \"claim\": \"cov_static ranges over the pool's T selected entries; share_top ranges over ALL n_dps DPs of the exact partition, independent of the pool.\",\n    \"how_verified\": \"share_top(k) is computed from sizes_all_dps, an array over every DP found by the DP predicate on all N points (independent of pool construction). cov_static is computed only from the T pool entries surviving weight-selection. The two arrays are built from different index sets (dp_nodes vs sel_dp_ids) and never conflated in the code.\"\n  },\n\n  \"joint_4_weight_and_tiebreak\": {\n    \"claim\": \"Selection is by weight_d = S_d + 4*W*h_d, never true basin size; ties at the T-th largest weight are broken by an ascending per-entry pseudorandom key bound to pool-insertion order.\",\n    \"how_verified\": \"weight_d is computed from Decimal(S_d) + 4*W_decimal*Decimal(h_d) (W taken to 80 significant digits), not from any basin-size array. Insertion order = the order in which pool_construct() first discovers each distinct DP. Tie-break keys are one bulk array of length r*T drawn once per (N,a,seed) from a PRNG seeded deterministically from the integer seed (see rng_conventions below), indexed by insertion order, and used as an ascending secondary sort key alongside descending weight.\",\n    \"why_decimal_not_float_for_weight\": \"At a in {1/16, 1/4} in this grid, W is an exact integer, so weight_d is exactly S_d + 4*W*h_d in integer arithmetic; a naive float64 computation risks manufacturing or hiding exact ties. Decimal at 80-digit precision was used uniformly so that reported ties (n_tied_at_Tth_weight, range 1-9 across the 200 cells) reflect real coincidences in (S_d, h_d) rather than floating-point artifacts.\"\n  },\n\n  \"joint_5_T_at_smaller_scale\": {\n    \"claim\": \"T = 64 at N = 2^20 (frozen table), not round(2^20^(1/3)) = 102.\",\n    \"how_verified\": \"T_TABLE = {2**20: 64, 2**24: 256} is a literal lookup table copied from quantity.md #10, never computed from a formula. All derived quantities (T_sel, cap, W) were cross-checked against quantity.md's own printed decimal table before the production run and matched to the digits shown (see validation note below).\"\n  },\n\n  \"joint_6_null_object_universe\": {\n    \"claim\": \"NULL-ORACLE-RAND draws its subset from all DPs of the same enumerated partition, not from the pool.\",\n    \"how_verified\": \"Both NULL-ORACLE-RAND variants (uniform and size-biased) sample index sets from range(n_dps) against sizes_all_dps (the full-partition array). NULL-RANDSEL and NULL-SHUF, by contrast, correctly draw from the r*T pool array (pool_sizes_arr), per quantity.md #12's own separate specification for that arm.\"\n  },\n\n  \"joint_7_verdicts_resampling_free\": {\n    \"claim\": \"k_25, k_5, and the sign of mean_margin are computed exactly and do not depend on the bootstrap.\",\n    \"how_verified\": \"k_25/k_5/verdict_25/verdict_5/mean_margin_sign are computed directly from the array of 25 (or 5) per-seed margins via exact comparison (margin >= 0) and exact mean sign; the percentile-bootstrap CI is computed afterward, in a separate function, and is not read by any verdict computation.\"\n  },\n\n  \"rng_and_convention_disclosures_licensed_by_quantity_md_section_9_and_prohibitions_md_section_4\": {\n    \"mix64\": \"splitmix64 finalizer (Stafford 'mix13' variant): z^=z>>30; z*=0xbf58476d1ce4e5b9; z^=z>>27; z*=0x94d049bb133111eb; z^=z>>31; all mod 2^64. A standard, publicly documented avalanche mixer, chosen because quantity.md #1 explicitly says 'any standard one; yours need not match anyone else's'.\",\n    \"restart_rng / tiebreak_rng / null_uniform_rng / null_sizebiased_rng / null_randsel_rng / null_shuf_rng\": \"Each is a numpy Generator (PCG64) seeded by the low 8 bytes of sha256(f'{seed}|{tag}|{N}|{a.numerator}|{a.denominator}'), where tag in {restart, tiebreak, null_uniform, null_sizebiased, null_randsel, null_shuf}. This is a deterministic, reproducible, but otherwise arbitrary convention for randomness that quantity.md never specifies a seed formula for (unlike the bootstrap, which quantity.md #11 does specify exactly). This choice is disclosed, not concealed, and is not expected to match any other implementation's realization, per the same license quantity.md #9 gives to mix64 and to the tie-break key stream.\",\n    \"size_biased_sampling_without_replacement\": \"Implemented via the Efraimidis-Spirakis exponential-key method in the log domain (key_i = log(u_i)/w_i, take the T_sel largest), a standard exact algorithm for weighted sampling without replacement. Not specified by quantity.md beyond 'drawing the T_sel-subset with probability proportional to basin size'; quantity.md #12 itself says of this arm only 'report it; nothing depends on it'.\",\n    \"bootstrap_n_bits\": \"quantity.md #11's rng formula uses a symbol 'n_bits' that is not spelled out. Taken to mean log2(N) (20 or 24 for this grid), the only reading consistent with N always being written as a power of two throughout quantity.md. This affects only the bootstrap RNG seed, and the bootstrap is explicitly declared non-verdict-bearing ('it routes, it does not decide', quantity.md #11; joint_7 above).\"\n  },\n\n  \"derived_field_not_literally_named_in_deliverables_md\": {\n    \"margin_null_shuf\": \"deliverables.md's per-cell table lists cov_static_shuf for NULL-SHUF but does not separately name a 'margin_null_shuf'. quantity.md #7 defines margin = share_top_Tsel - cov_static uniformly, and quantity.md #12 frames every other null arm as a substitution into that same formula. We additionally report margin_null_shuf = share_top_Tsel - cov_static_shuf as the direct, mechanical application of the already-stated margin formula with cov_static_shuf substituted for cov_static, and used it to compute mean_margin_null_shuf / n_seeds_margin_null_nonneg_shuf at the per-(N,a) level (which deliverables.md #3 does ask for, 'for each null arm', without listing NULL-SHUF's field name either). This is disclosed as an extension by direct formula reuse, not as an invented convention resolving an ambiguity -- no other value was possible once cov_static_shuf existed and quantity.md's own margin formula was applied unchanged. cov_static_shuf itself (the literally required field) is also reported per cell, unmodified.\"\n  },\n\n  \"rho_ORACLE_interpretation\": {\n    \"quantity_md_text\": \"'the smallest T_sel/T at which share_top(T_sel) reaches cov_static' (quantity.md #12, DECAY readings)\",\n    \"reading_adopted\": \"share_top(k) is already defined in quantity.md #7 as a function of an integer k (the count of top-ranked DPs by exact basin size). rho_ORACLE was computed by treating k as a free variable, finding the smallest integer k in [0, n_dps] with share_top(k) >= cov_static (using the cell's own already-computed cov_static, via exact integer comparison against the cumulative basin-size sum, never float comparison), and reporting k/T. This is the direct extension of an already-stated function to a free argument, not an invented formula; no alternative reading was identified.\",\n    \"well_definedness_check\": \"Since cov_static is itself an exact sum of basin sizes over a subset of DPs, and share_top(n_dps) equals the sum over ALL DPs (a superset), share_top(n_dps) >= cov_static always, so the search always terminates within k <= n_dps at every one of the 200 cells; no cell required clipping or produced an undefined value.\"\n  },\n\n  \"packet_completeness_finding\": {\n    \"verdict\": \"The packet was found COMPLETE. Every field deliverables.md requires was computable from quantity.md's definitions and parameters alone, using only implementation freedoms quantity.md #9 and prohibitions.md #4 explicitly license (mix64 choice; RNG/seed choice for restarts, tie-break keys, and the four control-arm draws; the direct, unmodified extension of the already-stated share_top(k) and margin() formulas noted above). No defensible-but-arbitrary convention had to be invented to resolve an actual ambiguity in a load-bearing formula; the two load-bearing formulas the packet itself flags as historically dangerous (cap = ceil(8*W), applied in exactly the two places quantity.md #3 names; and the accounting identity of quantity.md #4) were both implemented exactly as specified and checked to hold at every one of the 200 cells with zero exceptions.\",\n    \"validation_performed_before_the_production_run\": \"(a) The core algorithm (exact forward-orbit distance to first DP, computed via reverse-graph multi-source BFS, which is exact because every node has out-degree exactly 1) was cross-checked against a brute-force O(N x path length) reference implementation on 40 random tiny synthetic instances (N in {8,16,32,64,128}); all 40 matched exactly, including which specific DP each reachable point mapped to. (b) W, cap, and dp_threshold, computed via Decimal at 80 significant digits from the exact rational a*N/T, were checked against quantity.md #10's own printed table for all 8 (N,a) combinations and matched to every printed digit.\"\n  }\n}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":63,"totalLines":63,"truncated":false}},"title":"coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-4433c1/reviews/TASK-20260907-7afa98/joints_and_implementation_notes.json","time":{"start":1789086328729,"end":1789086328775}},"id":"prt_08ddadace001ILWEhY2P42CQtW","sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","messageID":"msg_08dd6db8e001khZtok33NF5Fn1"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1789086330643,"sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","part":{"id":"prt_08ddadac9001DH1PEiV5fK7KFg","messageID":"msg_08dd6db8e001khZtok33NF5Fn1","sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","type":"text","text":"\n\nNow the Stage A'' implementation notes and instruments:\n\n\n","time":{"start":1789086325449,"end":1789086330639}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789086330727,"sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-862e56bc541d0799","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-4433c1/reviews/TASK-20260907-7afa98/run_full.py"},"output":"<path>/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-4433c1/reviews/TASK-20260907-7afa98/run_full.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: \"\"\"\n2: Full blind re-derivation run for PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3, Stage A''.\n3: Grid, definitions and formulas taken exclusively from quantity.md.\n4: \"\"\"\n5: import json\n6: import time\n7: import hashlib\n8: import sys\n9: from decimal import Decimal\n10: from fractions import Fraction as F\n11: \n12: import numpy as np\n13: \n14: from instrument import (\n15:     derive_keys, compute_W, compute_cap, compute_dp_threshold,\n16:     build_graph, bfs_partition,\n17: )\n18: \n19: SEEDS = list(range(1, 26))\n20: N_LIST = [2**20, 2**24]\n21: T_TABLE = {2**20: 64, 2**24: 256}\n22: A_LIST_ORDERED_FOR_REPORT = [F(1, 4), F(1, 16), F(1, 8), F(3, 16)]  # a=1/4 first, per instructions\n23: R = 2\n24: \n25: \n26: def rng_for(seed, tag, N, a: F):\n27:     key = f\"{seed}|{tag}|{N}|{a.numerator}|{a.denominator}\"\n28:     h = hashlib.sha256(key.encode()).digest()\n29:     seed64 = int.from_bytes(h[:8], \"little\")\n30:     return np.random.default_rng(seed64)\n31: \n32: \n33: def pool_construct(N, dist, root, cap, rT, rng_restart):\n34:     pool = {}  # dp_id -> [h_d, S_d, insertion_order]\n35:     insertion_order = []\n36:     capped_walks = 0\n37:     draws = 0\n38:     # draw in reasonably sized batches for speed, but logic is per-draw\n39:     batch = 4096\n40:     while len(insertion_order) < rT:\n41:         xs = rng_restart.integers(0, N, size=batch)\n42:         for x0 in xs:\n43:             draws += 1\n44:             d = dist[x0]\n45:             if d != -1 and d <= cap:\n46:                 dp_id = int(root[x0])\n47:                 Lsteps = int(d)\n48:                 if dp_id not in pool:\n49:                     pool[dp_id] = [0, 0, len(insertion_order)]\n50:                     insertion_order.append(dp_id)\n51:                 pool[dp_id][0] += 1\n52:                 pool[dp_id][1] += Lsteps\n53:             else:\n54:                 capped_walks += 1\n55:             if len(insertion_order) >= rT:\n56:                 break\n57:     return pool, insertion_order, capped_walks, draws\n58: \n59: \n60: def compute_cell(N, a: F, seed, T, verbose_tag=\"\"):\n61:     t_start = time.time()\n62:     K, K_dp = derive_keys(seed)\n63:     W = compute_W(a, N, T)\n64:     cap = compute_cap(W)\n65:     dp_threshold = compute_dp_threshold(W)\n66:     T_sel = T // 2\n67:     rT = R * T\n68: \n69:     fx, is_dp = build_graph(N, K, K_dp, dp_threshold)\n70:     dist, root = bfs_partition(N, fx, is_dp, cap)\n71: \n72:     dp_nodes = np.nonzero(is_dp)[0]\n73:     n_dps = int(dp_nodes.size)\n74: \n75:     assigned_mask = (dist != -1) & (dist <= cap)\n76:     cycle_mass = int((dist == -1).sum())\n77:     capped_mass = int(((dist != -1) & (dist > cap)).sum())\n78: \n79:     basin_counts = np.bincount(root[assigned_mask], minlength=N)\n80:     sizes_all_dps = basin_counts[dp_nodes]  # exact basin size per DP, class(1) only\n81:     sum_b = int(sizes_all_dps.sum())\n82:     accounting_identity_holds = bool(sum_b + cycle_mass + capped_mass == N)\n83:     min_basin_size = int(sizes_all_dps.min()) if n_dps > 0 else None\n84: \n85:     # share_top(k) machinery: sort all DP basin sizes descending, cumulative sum (exact ints)\n86:     order_desc = np.argsort(sizes_all_dps)[::-1]\n87:     sorted_sizes = sizes_all_dps[order_desc]\n88:     sorted_dp_ids = dp_nodes[order_desc]\n89:     cumsum = np.cumsum(sorted_sizes)\n90: \n91:     def share_top(k):\n92:         if k <= 0:\n93:             return 0.0, 0\n94:         k = min(k, n_dps)\n95:         num = int(cumsum[k - 1]) if k > 0 else 0\n96:         return num / N, num\n97: \n98:     share_top_Tsel, share_top_Tsel_num = share_top(T_sel)\n99:     share_top_T, _ = share_top(T)\n100:     share_top_Tover4, _ = share_top(T // 4)\n101:     share_top_Tover8, _ = share_top(T // 8)\n102: \n103:     # Pool construction (uniform random restarts), using precomputed dist/root\n104:     rng_restart = rng_for(seed, \"restart\", N, a)\n105:     pool, insertion_order, capped_walks, draws = pool_construct(N, dist, root, cap, rT, rng_restart)\n106:     assert len(pool) == rT, f\"pool size mismatch: {len(pool)} vs {rT}\"\n107: \n108:     # weight_d = S_d + 4*W*h_d, computed with Decimal for exact tie detection\n109:     pool_ids = insertion_order[:]  # index -> dp_id, by insertion order\n110:     weights_dec = []\n111:     S_list = []\n112:     H_list = []\n113:     for dp_id in pool_ids:\n114:         h_d, S_d, ins_ord = pool[dp_id]\n115:         wt = Decimal(S_d) + 4 * W * Decimal(h_d)\n116:         weights_dec.append(wt)\n117:         S_list.append(S_d)\n118:         H_list.append(h_d)\n119: \n120:     order_idx = list(range(rT))\n121:     # rank purely by weight (descending) to find n_tied_at_Tth_weight\n122:     ranked_by_weight = sorted(order_idx, key=lambda i: weights_dec[i], reverse=True)\n123:     weight_at_T = weights_dec[ranked_by_weight[T - 1]]\n124:     n_tied_at_Tth_weight = sum(1 for i in order_idx if weights_dec[i] == weight_at_T)\n125: \n126:     # tie-break keys: bulk array from a fresh PRNG seeded from the seed, indexed by insertion order\n127:     rng_tie = rng_for(seed, \"tiebreak\", N, a)\n128:     tie_keys = rng_tie.random(rT)\n129: \n130:     final_order = sorted(order_idx, key=lambda i: (-weights_dec[i], tie_keys[i]))\n131:     sel_positions = final_order[:T]  # positions (indices into pool arrays) selected\n132:     sel_dp_ids = [pool_ids[i] for i in sel_positions]\n133: \n134:     cov_static_num = int(sum(int(basin_counts[d]) for d in sel_dp_ids))\n135:     cov_static = cov_static_num / N\n136: \n137:     margin = share_top_Tsel - cov_static\n138: \n139:     # rho_ORACLE: smallest k (in units of k/T) such that share_top(k) >= cov_static (exact int compare)\n140:     idx_reach = np.searchsorted(cumsum, cov_static_num, side=\"left\")\n141:     k_needed = idx_reach + 1\n142:     k_needed = min(k_needed, n_dps)\n143:     rho_ORACLE = k_needed / T\n144: \n145:     residual_fraction = (cycle_mass + capped_mass) / N\n146: \n147:     # ---- control arms, all read off the same exact partition ----\n148:     pool_sizes_arr = np.array([int(basin_counts[d]) for d in pool_ids], dtype=np.int64)\n149: \n150:     # NULL-ORACLE-RAND (uniform): random T_sel-subset of ALL DPs\n151:     rng_nu = rng_for(seed, \"null_uniform\", N, a)\n152:     idx_u = rng_nu.choice(n_dps, size=min(T_sel, n_dps), replace=False)\n153:     cov_null_uniform = int(sizes_all_dps[idx_u].sum()) / N\n154:     margin_null_oracle_rand_uniform = cov_null_uniform - cov_static\n155: \n156:     # NULL-ORACLE-RAND (size-biased): weighted sampling w/o replacement, prob prop to basin size\n157:     rng_nb = rng_for(seed, \"null_sizebiased\", N, a)\n158:     u = rng_nb.random(n_dps)\n159:     u = np.clip(u, 1e-300, 1.0)\n160:     keys = np.log(u) / sizes_all_dps.astype(np.float64)\n161:     top_idx = np.argpartition(keys, -min(T_sel, n_dps))[-min(T_sel, n_dps):]\n162:     cov_null_sizebiased = int(sizes_all_dps[top_idx].sum()) / N\n163:     margin_null_oracle_rand_sizebiased = cov_null_sizebiased - cov_static\n164: \n165:     # NULL-RANDSEL: uniform random T-subset of the r*T pool\n166:     rng_rs = rng_for(seed, \"null_randsel\", N, a)\n167:     idx_rs = rng_rs.choice(rT, size=T, replace=False)\n168:     cov_null_randsel = int(pool_sizes_arr[idx_rs].sum()) / N\n169:     margin_null_randsel = share_top_Tsel - cov_null_randsel\n170: \n171:     # NULL-SHUF: permute basin sizes across pool entries, keep weight-based selection fixed\n172:     rng_sh = rng_for(seed, \"null_shuf\", N, a)\n173:     shuffled_sizes = rng_sh.permutation(pool_sizes_arr)\n174:     cov_static_shuf = int(shuffled_sizes[sel_positions].sum()) / N\n175:     margin_null_shuf = share_top_Tsel - cov_static_shuf  # derived by us; disclosed as such\n176: \n177:     elapsed = time.time() - t_start\n178: \n179:     cell = dict(\n180:         N=N, a_num=a.numerator, a_den=a.denominator, seed=seed, T=T, T_sel=T_sel, r=R,\n181:         W=str(W), cap=cap,\n182:         share_top_Tsel=share_top_Tsel, cov_static=cov_static, margin=margin,\n183:         share_top_T=share_top_T, share_top_Tover4=share_top_Tover4, share_top_Tover8=share_top_Tover8,\n184:         rho_ORACLE=rho_ORACLE,\n185:         n_dps=n_dps, cycle_mass=cycle_mass, capped_mass=capped_mass,\n186:         capped_walks=capped_walks, residual_fraction=residual_fraction,\n187:         accounting_identity_holds=accounting_identity_holds,\n188:         min_basin_size=min_basin_size,\n189:         n_tied_at_Tth_weight=n_tied_at_Tth_weight,\n190:         margin_null_oracle_rand_uniform=margin_null_oracle_rand_uniform,\n191:         margin_null_oracle_rand_sizebiased=margin_null_oracle_rand_sizebiased,\n192:         margin_null_randsel=margin_null_randsel,\n193:         cov_static_shuf=cov_static_shuf,\n194:         margin_null_shuf=margin_null_shuf,\n195:         pool_draws=draws,\n196:         elapsed_sec=elapsed,\n197:     )\n198:     print(f\"  [{verbose_tag}] N={N} a={a} seed={seed} margin={margin:+.6f} \"\n199:           f\"cov_static={cov_static:.6f} share_top_Tsel={share_top_Tsel:.6f} \"\n200:           f\"cycle_mass={cycle_mass} capped_mass={capped_mass} elapsed={elapsed:.2f}s\", flush=True)\n201:     return cell\n202: \n203: \n204: def aggregate(cells):\n205:     margins = np.array([c[\"margin\"] for c in cells])\n206:     k_25 = int((margins >= 0).sum())\n207:     verdict_25 = \"G3-FEASIBLE\" if k_25 >= 20 else \"G3-INFEASIBLE\"\n208:     margins5 = margins[:5]\n209:     k_5 = int((margins5 >= 0).sum())\n210:     verdict_5 = \"G3-FEASIBLE\" if k_5 >= 4 else \"G3-INFEASIBLE\"\n211:     mean_margin = float(margins.mean())\n212:     mean_margin_sign = \"+\" if mean_margin > 0 else (\"-\" if mean_margin < 0 else \"0\")\n213: \n214:     N = cells[0][\"N\"]\n215:     a = F(cells[0][\"a_num\"], cells[0][\"a_den\"])\n216:     n_bits = N.bit_length() - 1\n217:     boot_seed = 20260907 + 1000 * n_bits + round(10000 * float(a))\n218:     rng_boot = np.random.default_rng(boot_seed)\n219:     B = 10000\n220:     resample_idx = rng_boot.integers(0, 25, size=(B, 25))\n221:     resample_means = margins[resample_idx].mean(axis=1)\n222:     ci_lo = float(np.percentile(resample_means, 2.5))\n223:     ci_hi = float(np.percentile(resample_means, 97.5))\n224:     ci_straddles_zero = bool(ci_lo <= 0.0 <= ci_hi)\n225: \n226:     def null_stats(field):\n227:         vals = np.array([c[field] for c in cells])\n228:         return float(vals.mean()), int((vals >= 0).sum())\n229: \n230:     mmn_u, nsn_u = null_stats(\"margin_null_oracle_rand_uniform\")\n231:     mmn_b, nsn_b = null_stats(\"margin_null_oracle_rand_sizebiased\")\n232:     mmn_r, nsn_r = null_stats(\"margin_null_randsel\")\n233:     mmn_s, nsn_s = null_stats(\"margin_null_shuf\")\n234: \n235:     max_residual_fraction = float(max(c[\"residual_fraction\"] for c in cells))\n236: \n237:     return dict(\n238:         N=N, a_num=a.numerator, a_den=a.denominator,\n239:         k_25=k_25, verdict_25=verdict_25, k_5=k_5, verdict_5=verdict_5,\n240:         mean_margin=mean_margin, mean_margin_sign=mean_margin_sign,\n241:         ci_lo=ci_lo, ci_hi=ci_hi, ci_straddles_zero=ci_straddles_zero,\n242:         bootstrap_seed_used=boot_seed, bootstrap_B=B, bootstrap_n_bits_convention=\"log2(N)\",\n243:         mean_margin_null_oracle_rand_uniform=mmn_u, n_seeds_margin_null_nonneg_oracle_rand_uniform=nsn_u,\n244:         mean_margin_null_oracle_rand_sizebiased=mmn_b, n_seeds_margin_null_nonneg_oracle_rand_sizebiased=nsn_b,\n245:         mean_margin_null_randsel=mmn_r, n_seeds_margin_null_nonneg_randsel=nsn_r,\n246:         mean_margin_null_shuf=mmn_s, n_seeds_margin_null_nonneg_shuf=nsn_s,\n247:         max_residual_fraction=max_residual_fraction,\n248:     )\n249: \n250: \n251: def main():\n252:     out_cells_path = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else \"cells.jsonl\"\n253:     out_summary_path = sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv) > 2 else \"summary.json\"\n254: \n255:     all_cells = []\n256:     all_summaries = []\n257:     stopped_early = False\n258:     stop_reason = None\n259: \n260:     with open(out_cells_path, \"w\") as fcells:\n261:         for N in N_LIST:\n262:             T = T_TABLE[N]\n263:             for a in A_LIST_ORDERED_FOR_REPORT:\n264:                 tag = f\"N={N} a={a}\"\n265:                 print(f\"=== {tag} ===\", flush=True)\n266:                 cells = []\n267:                 for seed in SEEDS:\n268:                     cell = compute_cell(N, a, seed, T, verbose_tag=tag)\n269:                     cells.append(cell)\n270:                     all_cells.append(cell)\n271:                     fcells.write(json.dumps(cell) + \"\\n\")\n272:                     fcells.flush()\n273:                 summ = aggregate(cells)\n274:                 all_summaries.append(summ)\n275:                 print(f\"  -> k_25={summ['k_25']} verdict_25={summ['verdict_25']} \"\n276:                       f\"k_5={summ['k_5']} verdict_5={summ['verdict_5']} \"\n277:                       f\"mean_margin={summ['mean_margin']:+.6f} ci=({summ['ci_lo']:+.6f},{summ['ci_hi']:+.6f})\",\n278:                       flush=True)\n279:                 if a == F(1, 4) and summ[\"verdict_25\"] == \"G3-FEASIBLE\":\n280:                     stopped_early = True\n281:                     stop_reason = f\"a=1/4 reading at N={N} came out G3-FEASIBLE; halting per instructions.\"\n282:                     print(\"!!!\", stop_reason, flush=True)\n283:                     break\n284:             if stopped_early:\n285:                 break\n286: \n287:     with open(out_summary_path, \"w\") as fsum:\n288:         json.dump(dict(\n289:             summaries=all_summaries,\n290:             stopped_early=stopped_early,\n291:             stop_reason=stop_reason,\n292:             n_cells_computed=len(all_cells),\n293:         ), fsum, indent=2)\n294: \n295:     print(\"DONE\", \"stopped_early=\", stopped_early, \"n_cells=\", len(all_cells))\n296: \n297: \n298: if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n299:     main()\n\n(End of file - total 299 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\"\"\"\nFull blind re-derivation run for PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3, Stage A''.\nGrid, definitions and formulas taken exclusively from quantity.md.\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport time\nimport hashlib\nimport sys\nfrom decimal import Decimal\nfrom fractions import Fraction as F\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nfrom instrument import (\n    derive_keys, compute_W, compute_cap, compute_dp_threshold,\n    build_graph, bfs_partition,\n)\n\nSEEDS = list(range(1, 26))\nN_LIST = [2**20, 2**24]","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-4433c1/reviews/TASK-20260907-7afa98/run_full.py","text":"\"\"\"\nFull blind re-derivation run for PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3, Stage A''.\nGrid, definitions and formulas taken exclusively from quantity.md.\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport time\nimport hashlib\nimport sys\nfrom decimal import Decimal\nfrom fractions import Fraction as F\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nfrom instrument import (\n    derive_keys, compute_W, compute_cap, compute_dp_threshold,\n    build_graph, bfs_partition,\n)\n\nSEEDS = list(range(1, 26))\nN_LIST = [2**20, 2**24]\nT_TABLE = {2**20: 64, 2**24: 256}\nA_LIST_ORDERED_FOR_REPORT = [F(1, 4), F(1, 16), F(1, 8), F(3, 16)]  # a=1/4 first, per instructions\nR = 2\n\n\ndef rng_for(seed, tag, N, a: F):\n    key = f\"{seed}|{tag}|{N}|{a.numerator}|{a.denominator}\"\n    h = hashlib.sha256(key.encode()).digest()\n    seed64 = int.from_bytes(h[:8], \"little\")\n    return np.random.default_rng(seed64)\n\n\ndef pool_construct(N, dist, root, cap, rT, rng_restart):\n    pool = {}  # dp_id -> [h_d, S_d, insertion_order]\n    insertion_order = []\n    capped_walks = 0\n    draws = 0\n    # draw in reasonably sized batches for speed, but logic is per-draw\n    batch = 4096\n    while len(insertion_order) < rT:\n        xs = rng_restart.integers(0, N, size=batch)\n        for x0 in xs:\n            draws += 1\n            d = dist[x0]\n            if d != -1 and d <= cap:\n                dp_id = int(root[x0])\n                Lsteps = int(d)\n                if dp_id not in pool:\n                    pool[dp_id] = [0, 0, len(insertion_order)]\n                    insertion_order.append(dp_id)\n                pool[dp_id][0] += 1\n                pool[dp_id][1] += Lsteps\n            else:\n                capped_walks += 1\n            if len(insertion_order) >= rT:\n                break\n    return pool, insertion_order, capped_walks, draws\n\n\ndef compute_cell(N, a: F, seed, T, verbose_tag=\"\"):\n    t_start = time.time()\n    K, K_dp = derive_keys(seed)\n    W = compute_W(a, N, T)\n    cap = compute_cap(W)\n    dp_threshold = compute_dp_threshold(W)\n    T_sel = T // 2\n    rT = R * T\n\n    fx, is_dp = build_graph(N, K, K_dp, dp_threshold)\n    dist, root = bfs_partition(N, fx, is_dp, cap)\n\n    dp_nodes = np.nonzero(is_dp)[0]\n    n_dps = int(dp_nodes.size)\n\n    assigned_mask = (dist != -1) & (dist <= cap)\n    cycle_mass = int((dist == -1).sum())\n    capped_mass = int(((dist != -1) & (dist > cap)).sum())\n\n    basin_counts = np.bincount(root[assigned_mask], minlength=N)\n    sizes_all_dps = basin_counts[dp_nodes]  # exact basin size per DP, class(1) only\n    sum_b = int(sizes_all_dps.sum())\n    accounting_identity_holds = bool(sum_b + cycle_mass + capped_mass == N)\n    min_basin_size = int(sizes_all_dps.min()) if n_dps > 0 else None\n\n    # share_top(k) machinery: sort all DP basin sizes descending, cumulative sum (exact ints)\n    order_desc = np.argsort(sizes_all_dps)[::-1]\n    sorted_sizes = sizes_all_dps[order_desc]\n    sorted_dp_ids = dp_nodes[order_desc]\n    cumsum = np.cumsum(sorted_sizes)\n\n    def share_top(k):\n        if k <= 0:\n            return 0.0, 0\n        k = min(k, n_dps)\n        num = int(cumsum[k - 1]) if k > 0 else 0\n        return num / N, num\n\n    share_top_Tsel, share_top_Tsel_num = share_top(T_sel)\n    share_top_T, _ = share_top(T)\n    share_top_Tover4, _ = share_top(T // 4)\n    share_top_Tover8, _ = share_top(T // 8)\n\n    # Pool construction (uniform random restarts), using precomputed dist/root\n    rng_restart = rng_for(seed, \"restart\", N, a)\n    pool, insertion_order, capped_walks, draws = pool_construct(N, dist, root, cap, rT, rng_restart)\n    assert len(pool) == rT, f\"pool size mismatch: {len(pool)} vs {rT}\"\n\n    # weight_d = S_d + 4*W*h_d, computed with Decimal for exact tie detection\n    pool_ids = insertion_order[:]  # index -> dp_id, by insertion order\n    weights_dec = []\n    S_list = []\n    H_list = []\n    for dp_id in pool_ids:\n        h_d, S_d, ins_ord = pool[dp_id]\n        wt = Decimal(S_d) + 4 * W * Decimal(h_d)\n        weights_dec.append(wt)\n        S_list.append(S_d)\n        H_list.append(h_d)\n\n    order_idx = list(range(rT))\n    # rank purely by weight (descending) to find n_tied_at_Tth_weight\n    ranked_by_weight = sorted(order_idx, key=lambda i: weights_dec[i], reverse=True)\n    weight_at_T = weights_dec[ranked_by_weight[T - 1]]\n    n_tied_at_Tth_weight = sum(1 for i in order_idx if weights_dec[i] == weight_at_T)\n\n    # tie-break keys: bulk array from a fresh PRNG seeded from the seed, indexed by insertion order\n    rng_tie = rng_for(seed, \"tiebreak\", N, a)\n    tie_keys = rng_tie.random(rT)\n\n    final_order = sorted(order_idx, key=lambda i: (-weights_dec[i], tie_keys[i]))\n    sel_positions = final_order[:T]  # positions (indices into pool arrays) selected\n    sel_dp_ids = [pool_ids[i] for i in sel_positions]\n\n    cov_static_num = int(sum(int(basin_counts[d]) for d in sel_dp_ids))\n    cov_static = cov_static_num / N\n\n    margin = share_top_Tsel - cov_static\n\n    # rho_ORACLE: smallest k (in units of k/T) such that share_top(k) >= cov_static (exact int compare)\n    idx_reach = np.searchsorted(cumsum, cov_static_num, side=\"left\")\n    k_needed = idx_reach + 1\n    k_needed = min(k_needed, n_dps)\n    rho_ORACLE = k_needed / T\n\n    residual_fraction = (cycle_mass + capped_mass) / N\n\n    # ---- control arms, all read off the same exact partition ----\n    pool_sizes_arr = np.array([int(basin_counts[d]) for d in pool_ids], dtype=np.int64)\n\n    # NULL-ORACLE-RAND (uniform): random T_sel-subset of ALL DPs\n    rng_nu = rng_for(seed, \"null_uniform\", N, a)\n    idx_u = rng_nu.choice(n_dps, size=min(T_sel, n_dps), replace=False)\n    cov_null_uniform = int(sizes_all_dps[idx_u].sum()) / N\n    margin_null_oracle_rand_uniform = cov_null_uniform - cov_static\n\n    # NULL-ORACLE-RAND (size-biased): weighted sampling w/o replacement, prob prop to basin size\n    rng_nb = rng_for(seed, \"null_sizebiased\", N, a)\n    u = rng_nb.random(n_dps)\n    u = np.clip(u, 1e-300, 1.0)\n    keys = np.log(u) / sizes_all_dps.astype(np.float64)\n    top_idx = np.argpartition(keys, -min(T_sel, n_dps))[-min(T_sel, n_dps):]\n    cov_null_sizebiased = int(sizes_all_dps[top_idx].sum()) / N\n    margin_null_oracle_rand_sizebiased = cov_null_sizebiased - cov_static\n\n    # NULL-RANDSEL: uniform random T-subset of the r*T pool\n    rng_rs = rng_for(seed, \"null_randsel\", N, a)\n    idx_rs = rng_rs.choice(rT, size=T, replace=False)\n    cov_null_randsel = int(pool_sizes_arr[idx_rs].sum()) / N\n    margin_null_randsel = share_top_Tsel - cov_null_randsel\n\n    # NULL-SHUF: permute basin sizes across pool entries, keep weight-based selection fixed\n    rng_sh = rng_for(seed, \"null_shuf\", N, a)\n    shuffled_sizes = rng_sh.permutation(pool_sizes_arr)\n    cov_static_shuf = int(shuffled_sizes[sel_positions].sum()) / N\n    margin_null_shuf = share_top_Tsel - cov_static_shuf  # derived by us; disclosed as such\n\n    elapsed = time.time() - t_start\n\n    cell = dict(\n        N=N, a_num=a.numerator, a_den=a.denominator, seed=seed, T=T, T_sel=T_sel, r=R,\n        W=str(W), cap=cap,\n        share_top_Tsel=share_top_Tsel, cov_static=cov_static, margin=margin,\n        share_top_T=share_top_T, share_top_Tover4=share_top_Tover4, share_top_Tover8=share_top_Tover8,\n        rho_ORACLE=rho_ORACLE,\n        n_dps=n_dps, cycle_mass=cycle_mass, capped_mass=capped_mass,\n        capped_walks=capped_walks, residual_fraction=residual_fraction,\n        accounting_identity_holds=accounting_identity_holds,\n        min_basin_size=min_basin_size,\n        n_tied_at_Tth_weight=n_tied_at_Tth_weight,\n        margin_null_oracle_rand_uniform=margin_null_oracle_rand_uniform,\n        margin_null_oracle_rand_sizebiased=margin_null_oracle_rand_sizebiased,\n        margin_null_randsel=margin_null_randsel,\n        cov_static_shuf=cov_static_shuf,\n        margin_null_shuf=margin_null_shuf,\n        pool_draws=draws,\n        elapsed_sec=elapsed,\n    )\n    print(f\"  [{verbose_tag}] N={N} a={a} seed={seed} margin={margin:+.6f} \"\n          f\"cov_static={cov_static:.6f} share_top_Tsel={share_top_Tsel:.6f} \"\n          f\"cycle_mass={cycle_mass} capped_mass={capped_mass} elapsed={elapsed:.2f}s\", flush=True)\n    return cell\n\n\ndef aggregate(cells):\n    margins = np.array([c[\"margin\"] for c in cells])\n    k_25 = int((margins >= 0).sum())\n    verdict_25 = \"G3-FEASIBLE\" if k_25 >= 20 else \"G3-INFEASIBLE\"\n    margins5 = margins[:5]\n    k_5 = int((margins5 >= 0).sum())\n    verdict_5 = \"G3-FEASIBLE\" if k_5 >= 4 else \"G3-INFEASIBLE\"\n    mean_margin = float(margins.mean())\n    mean_margin_sign = \"+\" if mean_margin > 0 else (\"-\" if mean_margin < 0 else \"0\")\n\n    N = cells[0][\"N\"]\n    a = F(cells[0][\"a_num\"], cells[0][\"a_den\"])\n    n_bits = N.bit_length() - 1\n    boot_seed = 20260907 + 1000 * n_bits + round(10000 * float(a))\n    rng_boot = np.random.default_rng(boot_seed)\n    B = 10000\n    resample_idx = rng_boot.integers(0, 25, size=(B, 25))\n    resample_means = margins[resample_idx].mean(axis=1)\n    ci_lo = float(np.percentile(resample_means, 2.5))\n    ci_hi = float(np.percentile(resample_means, 97.5))\n    ci_straddles_zero = bool(ci_lo <= 0.0 <= ci_hi)\n\n    def null_stats(field):\n        vals = np.array([c[field] for c in cells])\n        return float(vals.mean()), int((vals >= 0).sum())\n\n    mmn_u, nsn_u = null_stats(\"margin_null_oracle_rand_uniform\")\n    mmn_b, nsn_b = null_stats(\"margin_null_oracle_rand_sizebiased\")\n    mmn_r, nsn_r = null_stats(\"margin_null_randsel\")\n    mmn_s, nsn_s = null_stats(\"margin_null_shuf\")\n\n    max_residual_fraction = float(max(c[\"residual_fraction\"] for c in cells))\n\n    return dict(\n        N=N, a_num=a.numerator, a_den=a.denominator,\n        k_25=k_25, verdict_25=verdict_25, k_5=k_5, verdict_5=verdict_5,\n        mean_margin=mean_margin, mean_margin_sign=mean_margin_sign,\n        ci_lo=ci_lo, ci_hi=ci_hi, ci_straddles_zero=ci_straddles_zero,\n        bootstrap_seed_used=boot_seed, bootstrap_B=B, bootstrap_n_bits_convention=\"log2(N)\",\n        mean_margin_null_oracle_rand_uniform=mmn_u, n_seeds_margin_null_nonneg_oracle_rand_uniform=nsn_u,\n        mean_margin_null_oracle_rand_sizebiased=mmn_b, n_seeds_margin_null_nonneg_oracle_rand_sizebiased=nsn_b,\n        mean_margin_null_randsel=mmn_r, n_seeds_margin_null_nonneg_randsel=nsn_r,\n        mean_margin_null_shuf=mmn_s, n_seeds_margin_null_nonneg_shuf=nsn_s,\n        max_residual_fraction=max_residual_fraction,\n    )\n\n\ndef main():\n    out_cells_path = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else \"cells.jsonl\"\n    out_summary_path = sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv) > 2 else \"summary.json\"\n\n    all_cells = []\n    all_summaries = []\n    stopped_early = False\n    stop_reason = None\n\n    with open(out_cells_path, \"w\") as fcells:\n        for N in N_LIST:\n            T = T_TABLE[N]\n            for a in A_LIST_ORDERED_FOR_REPORT:\n                tag = f\"N={N} a={a}\"\n                print(f\"=== {tag} ===\", flush=True)\n                cells = []\n                for seed in SEEDS:\n                    cell = compute_cell(N, a, seed, T, verbose_tag=tag)\n                    cells.append(cell)\n                    all_cells.append(cell)\n                    fcells.write(json.dumps(cell) + \"\\n\")\n                    fcells.flush()\n                summ = aggregate(cells)\n                all_summaries.append(summ)\n                print(f\"  -> k_25={summ['k_25']} verdict_25={summ['verdict_25']} \"\n                      f\"k_5={summ['k_5']} verdict_5={summ['verdict_5']} \"\n                      f\"mean_margin={summ['mean_margin']:+.6f} ci=({summ['ci_lo']:+.6f},{summ['ci_hi']:+.6f})\",\n                      flush=True)\n                if a == F(1, 4) and summ[\"verdict_25\"] == \"G3-FEASIBLE\":\n                    stopped_early = True\n                    stop_reason = f\"a=1/4 reading at N={N} came out G3-FEASIBLE; halting per instructions.\"\n                    print(\"!!!\", stop_reason, flush=True)\n                    break\n            if stopped_early:\n                break\n\n    with open(out_summary_path, \"w\") as fsum:\n        json.dump(dict(\n            summaries=all_summaries,\n            stopped_early=stopped_early,\n            stop_reason=stop_reason,\n            n_cells_computed=len(all_cells),\n        ), fsum, indent=2)\n\n    print(\"DONE\", \"stopped_early=\", stopped_early, \"n_cells=\", len(all_cells))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":299,"totalLines":299,"truncated":false}},"title":"coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP