{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789086801478,"sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-ad96f65dfe59b534","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml"},"output":"<path>/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: experiment:\n2:   id: EXP-ECDLP-6ac801\n3:   id_allocation_provenance: >-\n4:     UNCHANGED by this v3 amendment: no new experiment identifier is minted;\n5:     this is the same EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 record, amended additively per\n6:     `protocol_amendment` below. v1's and v2's own id_allocation_provenance\n7:     notes stand at their own paths and are not restated here.\n8:   hypothesis_id: H-ECDLP-37dc01\n9:   question_id: RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5\n10:   goal_id: null\n11:   goal_id_note: >-\n12:     UNCHANGED from v2, verbatim in substance: RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5 and\n13:     H-ECDLP-37dc01 are themselves unbound to a GOAL record. This v3 amendment\n14:     was authored under GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f (batch BATCH-48ef8b), which is a\n15:     COORDINATION binding of the authoring lane and is NOT written into this\n16:     field: the hypothesis-to-goal binding is not this contract's to create.\n17:   derived_from_decision: DEC-20260906-bcc097\n18:   derived_from_decision_note: >-\n19:     UNCHANGED from v2. This v3 amendment's own triggering decisions are named\n20:     separately in `protocol_amendment` below, and do not replace v1's\n21:     derivation.\n22:   derived_from_idea: null\n23: \n24:   version: 3\n25:   status: approved\n26:   approved_by: coordinator\n27:   frozen: true\n28:   execution_authorized: true\n29:   gate_fields_note: >-\n30:     SUPERSEDED IN EFFECT BY `approval_note` BELOW, PRESERVED VERBATIM FOR\n31:     HISTORY (this sentence added by the approving gate; nothing above it in\n32:     this note is edited): this paragraph originally read \"DELIBERATE AND\n33:     BINDING. This v3 contract is NOT approved, NOT frozen and NOT authorized\n34:     for execution...\" That was true from authoring (TASK-20260907-058c69,\n35:     BATCH-48ef8b) through two prior independent-gate cycles\n36:     (DEC-20260907-4e34c5 on the v1-to-v2 predecessor draft; DEC-20260907-2c4beb\n37:     `revise` on this exact v2-to-v3-r2 revision) until the approval recorded in\n38:     `approval_note`. The original text, UNCHANGED below this sentence:\n39:     DELIBERATE AND BINDING. This v3 contract is NOT approved, NOT frozen and\n40:     NOT authorized for execution. It was authored by TASK-20260907-058c69\n41:     (coordinator, BATCH-48ef8b), and that session may not gate it: authorship\n42:     is not approval. Until an INDEPENDENT approval gate -- a coordinator\n43:     session that authored none of these artifacts -- records a committed\n44:     decision, no run under this v3 contract is evidence, by this contract's\n45:     own first `invalidation_rules` entry (carried verbatim from v2) and by the\n46:     appended v3 entry that names the gate-outcome record explicitly. The\n47:     approved v2 contract at experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml\n48:     remains in force, unedited and byte-identical, and this record changes\n49:     nothing about it or about the runs executed under v1.\n50:   approval_note: >-\n51:     APPROVED by an INDEPENDENT approval-gate coordinator session (gate task\n52:     TASK-20260907-e17c05, decision DEC-20260907-b4f2a9) that authored none of\n53:     specification.v3.yaml, amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml, the v3_r2_addendum, the\n54:     derivation-packet files, DEC-20260907-2c4beb, or TASK-20260907-7cce3e's\n55:     fixes. This approval rests on TASK-20260907-7cce3e (the post-gate fix\n56:     batch) discharging, correctly and completely, all four required fixes\n57:     named by DEC-20260907-2c4beb / amendments/v2_to_v3.gate-outcome.yaml\n58:     `required_fixes` -- independently re-verified by this gate, not accepted\n59:     on the fix task's own say-so. See DEC-20260907-b4f2a9 for the full,\n60:     per-defect independent re-verification (including its own explicit\n61:     disclosure of this gate session's tool limits: it has no Bash/shell, so\n62:     fix (4)'s sha256/script re-run was corroborated by source-code reading and\n63:     cross-reference against the separately committed\n64:     experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/archives/TASK-20260907-7cce3e/fix-receipt.json,\n65:     not by this session independently re-executing sha256sum or the script\n66:     itself). Approving this contract text does not re-open D1/D2/D3 (sound,\n67:     per both prior gates), does not predetermine any cell's verdict at\n68:     a in {1/16, 1/8, 3/16}, and does not move H-ECDLP-37dc01's status. It\n69:     authorizes dispatch of Stage A'' (the blind re-derivation under the\n70:     derivation packet) and, once sealed, Stage B/C's own execution under this\n71:     contract's stage plan -- nothing under v3 was evidence before this\n72:     record, and nothing here itself IS evidence: no run has occurred.\n73: \n74:   protocol_amendment:\n75:     version: 3\n76:     supersedes: 2\n77:     from_version: 2\n78:     to_version: 3\n79:     amendment_record: experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml\n80:     amendment_id: PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3\n81:     amends_which_document: >-\n82:       THE APPROVED ONE. The identifier PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v1-to-v2 names TWO\n83:       records (identifier collision IC-1, disposed of by DEC-20260907-b6bcf4\n84:       and NOT reopened here). This v3 amends the APPROVED, FROZEN v2 at\n85:       experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml with its amendment at\n86:       experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/v1_to_v2.yaml. It does NOT amend\n87:       the refused sidecar draft at\n88:       experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/{specification.v2.BATCH-e9fd22-proposed.yaml,\n89:       amendments/v1_to_v2.BATCH-e9fd22-proposed.yaml}, whose status\n90:       `revision_required` is unchanged by this record. See\n91:       `amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml` `amends` for the full disposition and the\n92:       sha256 of every file this amendment must not touch.\n93:     triggering_decisions:\n94:       - 'DEC-20260907-b6bcf4 (the lane close and rerank: RANK 1 = author this amendment; the compatibility read CR-1 and its four binding conditions; CR-1a)'\n95:       - 'DEC-20260907-4e34c5 (the approval gate refusal that identified D1, D2, D3 as blocking and D4-D7 as non-blocking, and TF-1)'\n96:     triggering_reports:\n97:       - coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-e9fd22/tasks/TASK-20260907-f65c6e/approval_review.yaml\n98:     amended_by: coordinator\n99:     amended_at: '2026-09-07'\n100:     amended_at_note: >-\n101:       This role holds no independent clock; the date is the runtime-supplied\n102:       calendar date, per the same disclosure every prior record in this lane\n103:       carries. The commit time is authoritative.\n104:     prior_frozen_path: experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml\n105:     prior_frozen_sha256: a989f8c2aea27ef79997b401ca475f74f87b45fc5f5762ab7ddf385878c9891c\n106:     prior_frozen_sha256_provenance: >-\n107:       COMPUTED by this authoring session with `sha256sum` over the committed\n108:       bytes at that path, not reused from any receipt and not estimated. It\n109:       DIFFERS from the hash recorded for the same literal path by\n110:       TASK-20260907-4ce154's snapshot receipt, because that receipt hashed\n111:       BATCH-e9fd22's own draft, which occupied this path when that snapshot\n112:       was taken and was later moved to the sidecar path by commit 465c01cba.\n113:       Both hashes are correct for their own bytes at their own commit; the\n114:       difference is the concrete residual cost of IC-1 and is disclosed here\n115:       so no reader mistakes it for a defect. See `amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml`\n116:       `additivity_check` for the full four-file check.\n117:     authority_to_change: >-\n118:       THE APPROVED CONTRACT'S OWN `invalidation_rules` ITEM 7, verbatim: \"Any\n119:       post-hoc change to the a-grid, N, r, T_sel, or the G3-style feasibility\n120:       criterion beyond what THIS versioned contract states: requires a further\n121:       versioned protocol_amendment; runs already executed are never\n122:       re-scored.\" This IS that further versioned protocol_amendment. Its\n123:       binding condition holds: RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-001..006 are never re-scored\n124:       under this contract and enter it in exactly ONE role, as the REFERENCE\n125:       of control (h). The one wide-scope item item 7 does not name is the SEED\n126:       COUNT; the authority used for that is control (e)'s own stated\n127:       rationale, argued a fortiori in control (g), and it is recorded as the\n128:       weaker warrant it is rather than assimilated to item 7. See\n129:       `amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml` `authority_to_change` for the full argument\n130:       and the fallback if a gate rejects it.\n131:     reason: >-\n132:       An independent approval gate (TASK-20260907-f65c6e, DEC-20260907-4e34c5)\n133:       REFUSED a proposed wide-scope v1-to-v2 draft on three blocking defects.\n134:       Two of the three are live IN THE APPROVED v2 as well, not only in the\n135:       refused draft, and that is why this amendment exists rather than a\n136:       narrower one.\n137:         D2 (THE REASON THIS OUTRANKS EVERYTHING ELSE): the strings `cap`,\n138:       `CAP_MULT`, `cycle_mass` and `capped_mass` appear ZERO times in the\n139:       approved v2. That contract is `execution_authorized: true` and requires\n140:       a freshly sealed blind re-derivation of the a = 1/8 cell, so a\n141:       from-scratch re-deriver working from its text alone MUST INVENT A CAP\n142:       CONVENTION -- and production's cap = ceil(8*W) truncates every walk and\n143:       every basin. Worse, the refused draft asserted the basin partition is\n144:       exhaustive (sum_d b(d) = N) while production leaves DP-free-cycle mass\n145:       and beyond-cap mass unassigned. This is the same class of gap that\n146:       produced the original a = 1/8 blind-versus-production disagreement,\n147:       relocated from the selection weight to the cap. v3 states the cap as a\n148:       formula in the measured quantities and replaces the false identity with\n149:       an exact accounting.\n150:         D3: the Coordinator's directional prior sat in plain text on the\n151:       re-deriver's own required reading path, and neither leaking path was on\n152:       any blind list. v3 replaces the DENYLIST MECHANISM with an enumerated,\n153:       hashed, self-contained ALLOWLIST (`blind_rederivation.v3_derivation_packet`),\n154:       because a blind discipline a fresh re-deriver cannot obey from the text\n155:       it is given is not a blind discipline.\n156:         D1: T must be 64 at N = 2^20 per the frozen T_OF_NBITS table, not the\n157:       102 that round(2^20^(1/3)) gives. Against the approved v2 this is a\n158:       BLANK TO FILL, not a value to contradict: v2 states nothing at N = 2^20.\n159:         Four non-blocking defects D4 (tie-break key unspecified), D5 (verdicts\n160:       resting on an underspecified bootstrap), D6 (a = 1/16 contamination left\n161:       to a review joint) and D7 (a null object of the wrong shape) are folded\n162:       in at the same time. See `amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml` for the worked\n163:       discharge of each.\n164:     what_changes_summary: >-\n165:       ADDITIVE THROUGHOUT. Nine appended `definitions` keys (the cap\n166:       convention and its residual accounting; the DP predicate's floor and\n167:       independent key; the tie-break key stream; T/T_sel at the second scale;\n168:       the W/cap table at all eight cells; the 25-seed set; the interval\n169:       estimator; the fresh label SU; the a = 1/16 independence ruling). Two\n170:       appended `blind_rederivation` sub-keys (`v3_derivation_packet`,\n171:       `v3_rerequirement_stage_a_dprime`) with all eight v1 fields and v2's own\n172:       `v2_rerequirement_a_1_8` retained byte-identically. Eight appended\n173:       `controls` items (g)-(n) with (a)-(f) byte-identical. Appended\n174:       stopping_rules, invalidation_rules, required_artifacts, interpretation,\n175:       tail_checks and distinguishable_outcomes entries, with every v1/v2 entry\n176:       retained verbatim. Separate additive keys carrying the v3 grid\n177:       (`independent_variables_v3`), the v3 metrics\n178:       (`metrics.primary_v3_additions`), the v3 replication\n179:       (`replication_v3`), the SU routing (`success_criterion_v3_additions`)\n180:       and the v3 falsification additions. Two ADVISORY budget numbers raised\n181:       (maximum_runs 8 -> 30, total_cpu_hours 1 -> 6); the two MACHINE\n182:       PROTECTION numbers unchanged (maximum_memory_gb 8, maximum_workers 1).\n183:       One field is deliberately NOT restated verbatim and the deviation is\n184:       declared: `preregistered_prediction`, for leak-discipline reasons given\n185:       in that field. Nothing in v1, in the approved v2, in either sidecar, or\n186:       under experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/runs/ is edited by one byte.\n187:     binding: >-\n188:       This amendment AUTHORIZES NOTHING. It does not authorize a run, a\n189:       re-seal, a review round, or a hypothesis-status movement, and it\n190:       approves neither itself nor this contract -- see `gate_fields_note`\n191:       above and `invalidation_rules`' appended v3 entry. It asserts no\n192:       research finding: no measurement, timing, margin, pass-count, interval\n193:       or verdict originates in it. What it produces is a contract text whose\n194:       quantities a from-scratch re-deriver can derive without inventing a\n195:       convention. Whether the corrected cap convention could change any\n196:       cell's verdict is UNMEASURED, and the direction of any induced\n197:       difference is unpredictable from the contract; nothing here is evidence\n198:       for or against G3 feasibility at any a.\n199: \n200:   status_history_note: >-\n201:     v1's gate fields at specification.yaml and v2's gate fields at\n202:     specification.v2.yaml are UNCHANGED and remain in force for their own\n203:     content: v1's for the already-executed Stage B/C runs\n204:     (RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-001..006, never re-scored), v2's for the explicit weight\n205:     formula and the scoped a = 1/8 re-seal requirement. This v3 record's own\n206:     gate fields are `proposed` / null / false / false and govern ONLY the new,\n207:     additive content introduced by this amendment. H-ECDLP-37dc01's status is\n208:     NOT moved by this record and carries no new `status_history` entry: there\n209:     is no evidence to add one for.\n210: \n211:   approval_note: >-\n212:     NOT APPROVED, AND NOT SELF-APPROVABLE. This differs deliberately from v1's\n213:     and v2's own approval pattern, and the difference is the point.\n214:       v1 and v2 were each authored and gated inside one lane under the\n215:     standing research-budget authorization, then presented to the user for\n216:     confirmation. v3 is NOT: an independent approval gate refused this\n217:     contract's predecessor draft (DEC-20260907-4e34c5) precisely because\n218:     contract text and implementation had drifted, and DEC-20260907-b6bcf4\n219:     `limitations` records explicitly that a fresh v3 gate must REPEAT the\n220:     contract-versus-implementation comparison rather than inherit it -- in\n221:     particular against the APPROVED v2's text, which no gate has yet done.\n222:       So the gate for this contract is a SEPARATE TASK IN A FRESH SESSION that\n223:     authored none of these artifacts, and it records its outcome in its own\n224:     additive record at\n225:     experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/v2_to_v3.gate-outcome.yaml -- NOT\n226:     by editing this file. Two reasons, one mechanical and one substantive: the\n227:     dispatcher permits exactly one owning task per artifact path\n228:     (tools/research_dispatch.py `validate_queue`), and BATCH-e9fd22's gate\n229:     wrote its outcome into the object it gated, which had to be reverted by\n230:     another session afterwards (PD-1, DEC-20260907-4e34c5). A gate outcome in\n231:     its own record leaves the gated bytes exactly as archived.\n232:       The standing research-budget authorization (CLAUDE.md \"Research budgets:\n233:     progress first\") removes the need for repeated USER budget approval. It\n234:     does not remove the need for an INDEPENDENT SCIENTIFIC GATE, and this\n235:     record does not treat it as though it did.\n236: \n237:   designed_by: coordinator\n238:   designed_at: '2026-09-07'\n239:   designed_at_note: >-\n240:     This role holds no independent clock; the date is the runtime-supplied\n241:     calendar date, per the same disclosure every prior record in this lane\n242:     carries.\n243: \n244:   title: >-\n245:     THE STAGE-0 T/2 DISCREPANCY, RE-CHECKED AT SCALE AND BLIND: does the\n246:     ORIGINAL clause (C1) claim -- a re-selected table with T_sel = T/2\n247:     reaching the static full-T table's steady-state ceiling -- become\n248:     G3-feasible at a SMALLER a than H-ECDLP-37dc01's stated test_boundary\n249:     (a in {1/4, 1/2}) names, specifically a in {1/16, 1/8}, and where does\n250:     the crossing between a = 1/8 and a = 3/16 fall, when re-measured at\n251:     N = 2^24 exact basins (one scale up from the v2 Stage 0 a-scan's\n252:     N = 2^20) under a FROZEN, mandatory blind re-derivation rather than a\n253:     second read of the same executor table that produced the discrepancy?\n254:   title_v3_scope_note: >-\n255:     The title above is v1's, retained verbatim. v3 adds a SECOND SCALE\n256:     (N = 2^20, the scale at which the original discrepancy was found), widens\n257:     the seed set from 5 to 25, and gates every verdict on a from-scratch\n258:     re-derivation whose readable inputs are an enumerated packet rather than a\n259:     prohibition list. The question is unchanged; what changes is the\n260:     derivability of its quantities and the power of its controls.\n261: \n262:   context: >-\n263:     UNCHANGED from v1/v2 in substance and retained by reference rather than\n264:     restated, so that no sentence of it drifts: see\n265:     experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml `context` (itself\n266:     byte-identical to v1's), which records how DEC-20260906-bcc097's closing\n267:     of BATCH-f3a30a surfaced the Stage 0 a-scan reading, how the orchestrating\n268:     session confirmed it by a second arithmetic route, and why\n269:     DEC-20260906-bcc097 RANK 1 required an independent from-scratch\n270:     re-derivation rather than a third read of the same table.\n271:   context_v3_addition: >-\n272:     WHAT HAS HAPPENED SINCE v2 WAS APPROVED, and why this contract exists.\n273:       (1) v1's Stage B/C executed and completed (RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-001..006,\n274:     6/6 completed_valid). v2 was approved to state the selection weight\n275:     formula explicitly and to require a fresh, sealed a = 1/8 re-derivation\n276:     under it.\n277:       (2) A wide-scope draft amendment was then authored in a separate lane\n278:     (BATCH-e9fd22) and submitted to an INDEPENDENT approval gate, which\n279:     REFUSED it (TASK-20260907-f65c6e, DEC-20260907-4e34c5) on three blocking\n280:     defects and recorded four more as non-blocking. The gate ALSO did\n281:     something more valuable than refuse: it reproduced all three primary\n282:     quantities at all 20 committed cells from the pinned instrument to a worst\n283:     absolute deviation of 0.000e+00 (TF-1), which is what makes this\n284:     contract's reproduction control achievable rather than aspirational.\n285:       (3) That lane closed (DEC-20260907-b6bcf4) and its rerank set RANK 1 to\n286:     exactly this record, under a compatibility read CR-1 with four binding\n287:     conditions, discharging D2 first, then D3, then D1.\n288:       (4) THE FINDING THAT MAKES THIS URGENT RATHER THAN TIDY (CR-1a): D2 is\n289:     live in the APPROVED v2, not merely in the refused draft. The approved\n290:     contract is execution_authorized and demands a blind re-derivation whose\n291:     central object -- the exact basin partition -- it truncates at a cap it\n292:     never mentions. Any re-derivation sealed against that text is sealed\n293:     against a convention its author had to guess.\n294: \n295:   hypothesis_test_boundary_note: >-\n296:     UNCHANGED from v1/v2: H-ECDLP-37dc01's own `statement` and\n297:     `test_boundary.parameters` scope `a` to {1/4, 1/2} ONLY, so testing at\n298:     a in {1/16, 1/8, 3/16} is OUTSIDE that stated boundary, and that widening\n299:     was disclosed additively on H-ECDLP-37dc01 itself\n300:     (`test_boundary.boundary_amendments`, 2026-09-07) rather than smuggled in.\n301:     See experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml\n302:     `hypothesis_test_boundary_note` for the full text, retained by reference\n303:     so no sentence drifts.\n304:   hypothesis_test_boundary_note_v3_addition: >-\n305:     v3 ADDS A SECOND N (2^20) BESIDE THE EXISTING N = 2^24, and that is a\n306:     FURTHER scope disclosure of the same kind. It is NOT a further widening of\n307:     the hypothesis's `a` boundary -- the a_grid is unchanged at\n308:     {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4} -- and it requires no edit to H-ECDLP-37dc01,\n309:     because N = 2^20 is where the Stage 0 discrepancy this lineage\n310:     investigates was originally read, and the already-recorded boundary\n311:     amendment covers the a-range at issue. NO HYPOTHESIS FIELD IS TOUCHED BY\n312:     THIS CONTRACT. This contract holds no authority to move\n313:     H-ECDLP-37dc01's status and does not; it stays `analyzed`.\n314: \n315:   objective: >-\n316:     UNCHANGED from v1/v2 for the N = 2^24 arm, retained by reference: see\n317:     experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml `objective`. v1's Stage\n318:     B/C already discharged that objective at all four a-values, and those runs\n319:     are not re-run and not re-scored by this contract.\n320:   objective_v3: >-\n321:     v3's OWN OBJECTIVE, stated in full because it is what the executor and the\n322:     re-deriver are held to.\n323:       For each a in {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4}, at BOTH N = 2^20 (T = 64,\n324:     T_sel = 32) and N = 2^24 (T = 256, T_sel = 128), r = 2, over 25\n325:     pre-registered seeds (1..25), compute per (N, a, seed): the exact\n326:     top-T_sel basin share, the STATIC(T)_{r=2} exact coverage, their\n327:     difference (the G3-style margin), and the four accounting quantities the\n328:     cap convention makes necessary (cycle_mass, capped_mass, capped_walks, and\n329:     the residual fraction). Apply the v2 G3-style feasibility criterion,\n330:     verbatim, to determine at each (N, a) whether T_sel = T/2 is G3-feasible.\n331:       Do this INDEPENDENTLY TWICE: once as STAGE A'' (a from-scratch blind\n332:     re-derivation whose entire permitted reading before its seal is the\n333:     enumerated derivation packet), and once as STAGE B''/C'' (production,\n334:     reusing the commit-pinned instrument). Then compare, per (N, a), on the\n335:     PASS-COUNT and the SIGN OF THE MEAN MARGIN -- two resampling-free\n336:     integers-and-signs quantities -- never on an interval endpoint.\n337:       Run every declared control, each of which has a state of the world in\n338:     which it fires on a correct implementation. Report the a = 1/4 cell FIRST,\n339:     because it is this batch's known-false object.\n340:       NOTHING ABOUT THIS OBJECTIVE PREDICTS AN OUTCOME. The contract states no\n341:     expected verdict, pass-count, margin or crossing bracket at a = 1/16,\n342:     a = 1/8 or a = 3/16 at either N; see `preregistered_prediction` for where\n343:     the Coordinator's expectation is recorded and why it is not here.\n344: \n345:   definitions: # v2 AMENDMENT NOTE, RETAINED: every key from \"N\" down to and\n346:                # including \"STATIC(T)_r pool-selection weight formula (v2\n347:                # amendment item 1...)\" is reproduced BYTE-IDENTICALLY from the\n348:                # APPROVED experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml\n349:                # `definitions`. v3 AMENDMENT NOTE: NINE new keys are APPENDED\n350:                # after them, each marked \"(v3 amendment item k, ADDITIVE)\".\n351:                # No existing wording is touched. Where a v3 key ADDS a value\n352:                # at a scale v2 left blank, it says so explicitly and leaves\n353:                # every v2 number in force.\n354:     N: \"order of the group (or size of the set for the generic instrument); fixed at 2^24 = 16777216 for this contract (one scale up from the v2 Stage 0 a-scan's N = 2^20)\"\n355:     T: \"nominal table size N^{1/3} rounded = 256 at N = 2^24\"\n356:     T_sel: \"number of entries STORED (the advice); FIXED at T/2 = 128 for this contract (the ORIGINAL clause (C1) value, not the v2 grid's 0.65T/0.75T)\"\n357:     W: \"expected walk length between DPs, W = sqrt(a N / T); theta = 1/W\"\n358:     a: \"T W^2 / N; a_grid = {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4} for this contract (see `hypothesis_test_boundary_note`)\"\n359:     r: \"precomputation pool ratio; FIXED at r = 2 for this contract (the value at which the original discrepancy was found; matches the operating point found feasible)\"\n360:     exact top-T_sel basin share: >-\n361:       the exact fraction of the N points whose walk terminates, under the\n362:       exact (non-sampled) basin partition of the DP-truncated functional\n363:       graph, in one of the T_sel largest basins by size -- computed by full\n364:       enumeration, not walked online, exactly as v1/v2's `exact_basins`\n365:       procedure and Stage 0's own a-scan compute it.\n366:     STATIC(T)_r exact coverage: >-\n367:       the exact fraction of the N points covered by the T basins selected\n368:       by the published Bernstein-Lange weight from an r T-distinct-DP\n369:       precomputation pool at ratio r, read exactly (not sampled) from the\n370:       same basin partition -- v1/v2's own STATIC(T) arm's exact-coverage\n371:       reading.\n372:     \"G3-style feasibility criterion (this contract's operative rule, IDENTICAL IN FORM to experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/specification.v2.yaml `inputs.g3_gate_procedure`, reused verbatim to prevent the exact definitional/units mismatch that is this contract's own outcome (b))\": >-\n373:       at a given a, T_sel = T/2 is G3-FEASIBLE iff exact top-T_sel basin\n374:       share >= STATIC(T)_r exact coverage in >= 4 of the 5 seeds; otherwise\n375:       G3-INFEASIBLE (equivalently, per-seed rho_ORACLE = the smallest\n376:       T_sel/T at which the exact share equals STATIC(T)'s coverage; T/2 is\n377:       feasible at a seed iff rho_ORACLE < 0.5 at that seed -- the SAME\n378:       arithmetic the orchestrating session's second, independent\n379:       confirmation used on EV-ECDLP-f6b3f5).\n380:     crossing point: >-\n381:       the (open) interval between the largest a at which T_sel = T/2 is\n382:       G3-feasible and the smallest a at which it is not, as bracketed by\n383:       this contract's own a_grid; this contract locates the crossing to\n384:       within the grid's own resolution (between 1/8 and 3/16, per the\n385:       Stage 0 N = 2^20 reading) and does NOT interpolate a point estimate\n386:       beyond that bracket (a finer grid is out of scope; see `out_of_scope`).\n387:     seed: \"walk-key seed for the generic instrument; 5 seeds per a, matching Stage 0's and v2's own seed count.\"\n388:     \"STATIC(T)_r pool-selection weight formula (v2 amendment item 1, ADDITIVE -- resolves the underspecification named by protocol_amendment.reason and by TASK-20260907-80e198 validation_report.yaml `a_1_8_disagreement_root_cause`)\": >-\n389:       \"STATIC(T)_r exact coverage\" above names \"the published\n390:       Bernstein-Lange weight\" but v1's own text never stated the formula --\n391:       a genuine gap in the frozen contract, not a physics disagreement (see\n392:       `protocol_amendment.reason`). The formula, stated explicitly and\n393:       completely for the first time in this contract by this amendment, IS:\n394: \n395:         weight_d = S_d + 4 * W * h_d\n396: \n397:       where, for each distinguished point (DP) d collected into the r*T\n398:       precomputation pool during pool generation (uniform random restarts,\n399:       batched, every walk charged):\n400:         - \"d\" is one DP entry in the r*T-distinct-DP pool (an index into the\n401:           pool, not a group element by itself beyond its DP identity).\n402:         - \"S_d\" is the SUM, over every pool-construction walk that\n403:           terminated at DP d, of that walk's GENERATING-WALK LENGTH (the\n404:           number of steps from that walk's own start/restart point to its\n405:           termination at d). A DP hit by three separate walks of lengths\n406:           L1, L2, L3 has S_d = L1 + L2 + L3.\n407:         - \"h_d\" is the HIT COUNT of DP d: the number of distinct\n408:           pool-construction walks that terminated at d (h_d = 3 in the\n409:           example above).\n410:         - \"W\" is `definitions.W` above (the expected walk length between\n411:           DPs, W = sqrt(a N / T)), the SAME W used everywhere else in this\n412:           contract; the constant multiplier on the h_d term is exactly 4\n413:           (not 4W^2, not W/4 -- the literal coefficient is \"4 * W\").\n414:       The T pool entries with the T LARGEST values of weight_d (ties broken\n415:       by an arbitrary but fixed key, per the tie-break discipline already\n416:       used by the reused instrument) are SELECTED into STATIC(T)_r's table;\n417:       \"STATIC(T)_r exact coverage\" is then read, exactly (not sampled), as\n418:       the true exact-basin coverage of that SELECTED set -- the selection\n419:       is by the realistic estimator weight_d above, never by the selected\n420:       entries' own true exact basin size (an oracle selection is a\n421:       DIFFERENT, NOT-STATIC(T)_r, and objectively worse-performing-for-the-\n422:       table-builder quantity; see `protocol_amendment.reason` for the\n423:       demonstrated numerical effect of conflating the two).\n424:       SOURCE / PRIOR ART: this is the published Bernstein-Lange\n425:       selection-weight formula for a distinguished-point precomputation\n426:       pool (the \"published Bernstein-Lange weight\" `STATIC(T)_r exact\n427:       coverage` above already names), and it is ALREADY IMPLEMENTED,\n428:       unchanged, by this contract's own reused Stage B instrument: class\n429:       `Pool`, method `weights`, in\n430:       experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/source_v2/instrument.py, lines 445-446\n431:       (verified by direct read of that file at this amendment's authoring\n432:       time): `def weights(self, W: float) -> np.ndarray: return\n433:       np.asarray(self.S, dtype=np.float64) + 4.0 * W *\n434:       np.asarray(self.h, dtype=np.float64)`, where `self.S` and `self.h`\n435:       are accumulated per-DP exactly as `S_d`/`h_d` are defined above (see\n436:       `Pool.add_or_credit`/`Pool.credit_index` in the same file, which\n437:       accumulate `self.S[j] += length` and `self.h[j] += count` per\n438:       pool-construction walk credited to pool index j). This formula\n439:       GOVERNS, and always has governed, Stage B/C's already-executed\n440:       production runs (RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-001..006); this amendment adds NO\n441:       new computation to Stage B/C and does not re-run it. It exists solely\n442:       so that any FUTURE independent from-scratch (blind) re-derivation of\n443:       STATIC(T)_r under this contract has the same formula available that\n444:       production has always used, closing the gap that produced\n445:       TASK-20260907-80e198's a = 1/8 sealed disagreement.\n446: \n447:     \"WALK CAP (v3 amendment item 1, ADDITIVE -- discharges blocking defect D2 of DEC-20260907-4e34c5; THE MOST LOAD-BEARING ADDITION IN THIS AMENDMENT)\": >-\n448:       THE PROBLEM THIS CLOSES. Every quantity in this contract is read off a\n449:       basin partition that production TRUNCATES at a walk cap. The strings\n450:       `cap`, `CAP_MULT`, `cycle_mass` and `capped_mass` appear ZERO times in\n451:       the approved v2 (and zero times in v1), so a from-scratch re-deriver\n452:       had to invent the convention. The independent gate that refused this\n453:       contract's predecessor draft found exactly this, and called it the same\n454:       class of gap as the one that produced the original a = 1/8 sealed\n455:       disagreement -- relocated from the selection weight to the cap.\n456: \n457:       THE CONVENTION, AS A FORMULA IN THE MEASURED QUANTITIES:\n458: \n459:         cap(N, a) = ceil( 8 * W(N, a) ),   W(N, a) = sqrt( a * N / T(N) )\n460: \n461:       with T(N) the frozen table T(2^20) = 64, T(2^24) = 256, T(2^30) = 1024\n462:       (see `T (v3 amendment item 4...)` below).\n463: \n464:       WHAT `cap` IS, EXACTLY. A COUNT OF WALK STEPS (group operations); a\n465:       non-negative integer; the LEAST INTEGER >= 8*W. It is NOT 8*W\n466:       truncated, NOT round(8*W), and NOT a distance in any other unit. The\n467:       multiplier is exactly 8. In production the float64 value of 8*W is\n468:       passed through math.ceil and then int(...).\n469: \n470:       READ OFF THE PRODUCTION IMPLEMENTATION, NOT PARAPHRASED FROM A\n471:       DECISION RECORD. The three governing lines, verbatim, from\n472:       experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/source_v2/instrument.py -- the\n473:       commit-pinned instrument this contract's own `instrument` field names\n474:       and Stage B imports:\n475:         line 31: `CAP_MULT = 8                                  # cap = 8W`\n476:         line 75: `self.W = math.sqrt(self.a * self.N / self.T)`\n477:         line 77: `self.cap = int(math.ceil(CAP_MULT * self.W))`\n478: \n479:       WHERE THE CAP BITES -- BOTH PLACES, BOTH BINDING:\n480:         (i) THE EXACT BASIN PARTITION. `exact_basins` assigns a point to a\n481:         basin only if its distance to its first DP is <= cap; see\n482:         `EXACT-BASIN RESIDUAL MASS ACCOUNTING (v3 amendment item 2...)`\n483:         below for the exact three-class partition and the accounting\n484:         identity that replaces the false claim that the partition is\n485:         exhaustive.\n486:         (ii) POOL CONSTRUCTION. `walk_to_dp` (instrument.py lines 126-151)\n487:         stops at the cap: its loop condition is\n488:         `while active.size and steps < P.cap` (line 141), it returns\n489:         terminal = -1 for a capped walk, and it charges\n490:         `length[active] = P.cap` to the survivors (line 150).\n491:         `generate_pools` (lines 243-289) then charges EVERY walk's length to\n492:         the precomputation cost (`P_cost += L`, line 268) but credits ONLY\n493:         the terminating ones: a capped walk (t < 0) increments a\n494:         `capped_walks` counter and contributes NOTHING to any S_d or h_d,\n495:         while a terminating walk credits `S[j] += L` and `h[j] += 1` at its\n496:         DP's pool index.\n497:         CONSEQUENCE, STATED BECAUSE IT IS EXACTLY WHAT A RE-DERIVER WOULD\n498:         GET WRONG: a pool-construction walk that reaches the cap is charged\n499:         its `cap` steps and credits NO S_d and NO h_d. A reading that\n500:         instead credits a capped walk to the DP it would eventually have\n501:         reached computes a different weight_d, hence a different\n502:         STATIC(T)_{r} selection, hence a different exact coverage. Both\n503:         readings MUST report `capped_walks` per cell so this is checkable\n504:         rather than invisible.\n505: \n506:       A CONSEQUENCE OF THE FORMULA, NOT A MEASUREMENT: because cap grows\n507:       like sqrt(a*N/T) while the walk-length distribution has mean W, the\n508:       cap sits at 8 mean walk lengths. This contract makes NO claim about\n509:       how much mass that leaves unassigned at any cell; that is a measured\n510:       quantity of this batch, required per cell of both readings, and is\n511:       reported, never predicted.\n512: \n513:     \"EXACT-BASIN RESIDUAL MASS ACCOUNTING (v3 amendment item 2, ADDITIVE -- the second half of D2's discharge; replaces a FALSE identity with an exact one)\": >-\n514:       THE FALSE STATEMENT, NAMED SO IT CANNOT PROPAGATE. The refused sidecar\n515:       draft (experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.BATCH-e9fd22-proposed.yaml,\n516:       lines 92 and 169) asserts that the basin partition is exhaustive:\n517:       \"sum over all d of b(d) = N\". THAT IS FALSE of the object production\n518:       computes, and it is stated here explicitly -- rather than merely\n519:       omitted -- because a reader arriving from that draft will have seen it\n520:       and must be told which way it was resolved. THE APPROVED v2 IS SILENT\n521:       on the question, so v3 retracts no approved sentence; it fills a\n522:       silence and corrects a draft.\n523: \n524:       THE THREE DISJOINT, EXHAUSTIVE CLASSES. For each of the N points x let\n525:       dist(x) be the number of walk steps from x to the first distinguished\n526:       point on its forward orbit, and reach(x) the predicate that such a DP\n527:       exists at all. `exact_basins` (instrument.py lines 194-215) computes\n528:       dist by pointer doubling with DPs made absorbing, saturates dist at\n529:       sat = 2^n_bits for points with no DP on their orbit, and then\n530:       partitions the N points into:\n531:         (1) ASSIGNED:     reach(x) AND dist(x) <= cap.\n532:                           line 209: `ok = reach & (dist <= P.cap)`\n533:         (2) CYCLE MASS:   NOT reach(x) -- a DP-free cycle, or a tail feeding\n534:                           one.\n535:                           line 210: `cycle_mass = int((~reach).sum())`\n536:         (3) CAPPED MASS:  reach(x) AND dist(x) > cap.\n537:                           line 211: `capped_mass = int((reach & ~ok).sum())`\n538:       BASIN SIZES ARE COUNTED OVER CLASS (1) ALONE. Lines 212-213:\n539:       `idx = np.searchsorted(dps, nxt[ok]...)` then\n540:       `size = np.bincount(idx, minlength=len(dps))`. So sum_d b(d) is\n541:       exactly the cardinality of class (1).\n542: \n543:       WHERE THE RESIDUAL GOES: NOWHERE. It is not assigned to any basin, not\n544:       redistributed, and not silently discarded -- it is REPORTED, as the two\n545:       named integer fields `Basins.cycle_mass` and `Basins.capped_mass`\n546:       (declared at instrument.py lines 164-165 with the comments \"points that\n547:       never reach a DP (DP-free cycle and its tails)\" and \"points whose first\n548:       DP lies beyond the cap\"). A point on a DP-free cycle, a point in a tail\n549:       feeding such a cycle, and a point whose first DP lies beyond the cap\n550:       all belong to NO basin.\n551: \n552:       THE TRUE RELATION, WHICH REPLACES THE FALSE IDENTITY:\n553: \n554:         sum over all DPs d of b(d)  =  N - cycle_mass - capped_mass\n555: \n556:       equivalently, as an exact accounting identity every reading must\n557:       satisfy in integer arithmetic with ZERO tolerance:\n558: \n559:         sum_d b(d)  +  cycle_mass  +  capped_mass  =  N\n560: \n561:       This is an identity of the object `exact_basins` computes, NOT an\n562:       empirical claim: classes (1), (2), (3) are disjoint and exhaustive over\n563:       the N points by construction. Because it cannot fail on a correct\n564:       implementation it is carried as a STRUCTURAL SELF-CHECK (control item\n565:       (n)) and NOT as a control -- see that item for why the distinction is\n566:       load-bearing here.\n567: \n568:       A COROLLARY WORTH STATING BECAUSE IT CATCHES A REAL DEFECT CLASS: every\n569:       DP lies in its own basin, so b(d) >= 1 for every DP d. At a DP,\n570:       dist = 0 (line 202, `dist = (~dp).astype(np.int32)`) and 0 <= cap, so\n571:       every DP is in class (1) and is counted into its own bincount bucket. A\n572:       reading that produces b(d) = 0 for some DP has a defect.\n573: \n574:       DERIVED QUANTITY, REQUIRED PER CELL OF BOTH READINGS:\n575:         residual_fraction = (cycle_mass + capped_mass) / N\n576:       reported alongside cycle_mass, capped_mass and capped_walks. This\n577:       contract states NO expected value for it at any cell.\n578: \n579:     \"DP PREDICATE AND ITS INDEPENDENT KEY (v3 amendment item 3, ADDITIVE -- so no second convention has to be invented either)\": >-\n580:       The approved v2's `instrument` field names the DP predicate in words\n581:       (\"DP predicate hash64(x) < floor(2^64 / W) with an independent key\").\n582:       v3 states it as a formula, for the same reason it states the cap: a\n583:       re-deriver must not have to guess a rounding or a key derivation.\n584:         theta = 1/W  (instrument.py line 76: `self.theta = 1.0 / self.W`)\n585:         dp_threshold = floor( 2^64 / W )  -- instrument.py line 83:\n586:           `self.dp_threshold = int(math.floor((1 << 64) / self.W))`\n587:         the predicate is  mix64( x XOR K_dp ) < dp_threshold\n588:         with the DP key derived independently of the walk key:\n589:           K_dp = mix64( K XOR 0xD1B54A32D192ED03 )   (instrument.py line 82)\n590:           K    = mix64( 0x9E3779B97F4A7C15 + seed )  (instrument.py line 84)\n591:       FLOOR, not round and not ceil. The DP key is derived from the walk key\n592:       by a fixed XOR-then-mix, so the marking is independent of the step\n593:       function while remaining a deterministic function of the seed. A\n594:       re-deriver implementing its own mix function will produce a DIFFERENT\n595:       concrete instance at the same seed; that is expected and is not a\n596:       defect, because agreement is judged on pass-counts and signs over 25\n597:       seeds, never on per-seed coincidence.\n598: \n599:     \"T (v3 amendment item 4, ADDITIVE -- discharges blocking defect D1; FILLS A BLANK, CONTRADICTS NO APPROVED VALUE)\": >-\n600:       v2's `definitions.T` above reads \"nominal table size N^{1/3} rounded =\n601:       256 at N = 2^24\" and states NOTHING at N = 2^20. That value stays in\n602:       force, byte-identical, and this key adds the second scale.\n603:         T(2^20) = 64      T(2^24) = 256      T(2^30) = 1024\n604:       THE FROZEN SOURCE, quoted verbatim from\n605:       experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/specification.v2.yaml line 223:\n606:         \"T: nominal table size N^{1/3} rounded, i.e. 64 at 2^20, 256 at 2^24,\n607:          1024 at 2^30\"\n608:       CORROBORATED BY THE COMMIT-PINNED INSTRUMENT, verbatim from\n609:       instrument.py line 29:\n610:         `T_OF_NBITS = {20: 64, 24: 256, 30: 1024}      # T = N^{1/3} rounded, as frozen`\n611:       and line 74: `self.T = T_OF_NBITS[self.n_bits]`.\n612:       T = 64 AT N = 2^20, NOT 102. The refused sidecar draft stated 102, and\n613:       the arithmetic of its stated rule is right -- round(2^20^(1/3)) = 102 --\n614:       which is exactly why the value must be pinned to the TABLE rather than\n615:       to the rule. THE PINNED INSTRUMENT HAS NO CODE PATH TO 102: T is a\n616:       dictionary lookup keyed on n_bits, with no fallback and no\n617:       round(N**(1/3)) expression anywhere in the file. At 2^24 and 2^30 the\n618:       table and round(N^{1/3}) coincide; 2^20 is the one scale where they\n619:       diverge, and 2^20 is the scale v3 adds. A reading that uses 102 at\n620:       N = 2^20 is invalid under this contract (see `invalidation_rules`).\n621: \n622:     \"T_sel (v3 amendment item 5, ADDITIVE -- follows T; v2's N = 2^24 value unchanged)\": >-\n623:       v2's `definitions.T_sel` above reads \"FIXED at T/2 = 128 for this\n624:       contract\" and stays in force, byte-identical, at N = 2^24. v3 adds:\n625:         T_sel = T/2  at every scale, hence\n626:         T_sel(2^20) = 32       T_sel(2^24) = 128   (v2's value, unchanged)\n627:       T_sel = T/2 remains THE ORIGINAL clause (C1) value and the only stored\n628:       size any verdict is read at. The DECAY-TSEL control additionally READS\n629:       T/4 and T/8 -- at N = 2^20 that is 16 and 8, at N = 2^24 that is 64 and\n630:       32 -- and those readings gate nothing except through control (l)'s own\n631:       stated clauses.\n632: \n633:     \"W AND cap AT EVERY CELL OF THIS CONTRACT'S GRID (v3 amendment item 6, ADDITIVE -- DERIVED FROM THE FORMULAS ABOVE, MEASURED FROM NOTHING)\": >-\n634:       Tabulated so that no reader, gate or re-deriver has to recompute eight\n635:       square roots to check a manifest. EVERY ROW IS A CONSEQUENCE OF\n636:       W = sqrt(a*N/T) AND cap = ceil(8*W) WITH T FROM THE FROZEN TABLE. No\n637:       row is read off any run, and no row is a result.\n638: \n639:         N = 2^20, T = 64:\n640:           a = 1/16 -> W = 32                 -> cap = 256\n641:           a = 1/8  -> W = 45.254833996...    -> cap = 363\n642:           a = 3/16 -> W = 55.425625842...    -> cap = 444\n643:           a = 1/4  -> W = 64                 -> cap = 512\n644: \n645:         N = 2^24, T = 256:\n646:           a = 1/16 -> W = 64                 -> cap = 512\n647:           a = 1/8  -> W = 90.509667992...    -> cap = 725\n648:           a = 3/16 -> W = 110.851251684...   -> cap = 887\n649:           a = 1/4  -> W = 128                -> cap = 1024\n650: \n651:       The BINDING definition is the formula, never the printed decimal:\n652:       W is used at float64 precision and cap is the integer above. A reading\n653:       whose cap differs from the value in this table at any cell has either\n654:       used a different T or a different multiplier, and is invalid under this\n655:       contract (see `invalidation_rules`).\n656: \n657:     \"SEED SET (v3 amendment item 7, ADDITIVE -- 25 pre-registered seeds; v2's 5-seed field unchanged and retained as a subgroup)\": >-\n658:       v2's `definitions.seed` above (\"5 seeds per a, matching Stage 0's and\n659:       v2's own seed count\") stays in force byte-identically and now describes\n660:       a NAMED SUBGROUP rather than the whole set. v3 pre-registers:\n661:         SEEDS = {1, 2, ..., 25}, the same 25 integers at every (N, a) cell,\n662:         in both readings, and in every control arm.\n663:         SEEDS_V1COMPARABLE = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}, a distinguished SUBGROUP of the\n664:         above, which is the seed set control (h) reproduces against and the\n665:         only seed set whose reading is directly comparable to the committed\n666:         v1 cells.\n667:       FIXED BEFORE EXECUTION, and fixed as a LIST rather than a count, so\n668:       that \"25 seeds\" cannot be satisfied by 25 seeds of someone's choosing\n669:       after seeing five of them. The 25-seed reading and the 5-seed subgroup\n670:       reading are reported SEPARATELY and are NEVER composited into one\n671:       number (control (g)).\n672:       Seed streams are the v1 construction, unchanged: the walk key, the DP\n673:       key, the target/phi/null/tie-break streams are all derived from the\n674:       integer seed exactly as instrument.py's `Params.__post_init__` derives\n675:       them (lines 84-91), so seeds 6..25 are the same KIND of object as seeds\n676:       1..5 and add power without changing the instrument.\n677: \n678:     \"INTERVAL ESTIMATOR (v3 amendment item 8, ADDITIVE -- discharges non-blocking defect D5; ROUTES ONLY, GATES NOTHING)\": >-\n679:       WHAT IT IS NOT FOR, FIRST, BECAUSE THAT IS THE DEFECT BEING CLOSED.\n680:       NO VERDICT, NO CONTROL CLAUSE AND NO AGREEMENT TEST IN THIS CONTRACT\n681:       DEPENDS ON A BOOTSTRAP. G3-FEASIBLE and G3-INFEASIBLE are functions of\n682:       the integer pass-count k alone. Blind-versus-production agreement is\n683:       judged on (k, sign of mean margin) alone. Both are exact and\n684:       resampling-free, so two independent implementations compute them\n685:       identically or differ for a reason about the quantity.\n686: \n687:       WHAT IT IS FOR: routing a cell to the fresh label SU (CONFIRMED\n688:       UNRESOLVED) -- see `SU ... (v3 amendment item 9...)` below -- which is\n689:       not a feasibility verdict and supports no hypothesis movement in either\n690:       direction.\n691: \n692:       THE PRIMARY ESTIMATOR, SPECIFIED TO THE CALL:\n693:         method:      PERCENTILE bootstrap (not BCa, not basic, not studentised)\n694:         statistic:   the MEAN over seeds of the per-seed margin at that\n695:                      (N, a) cell\n696:         resample:    i.i.d. with replacement over the 25 per-seed margins,\n697:                      preserving cell membership; seeds are the resampling\n698:                      unit\n699:         B:           10000 resamples\n700:         rng:         numpy.random.default_rng(20260907 + 1000*n_bits +\n701:                      round(10000*a)), constructed FRESH per cell so a cell's\n702:                      interval does not depend on the order cells were\n703:                      processed in\n704:         endpoints:   the 2.5th and 97.5th percentiles of the B resample\n705:                      means, via numpy.percentile(..., method='linear')\n706:                      (numpy's default), stated explicitly because\n707:                      percentile-method choice is a real source of\n708:                      implementation divergence\n709:       BCa IS REPORTED BESIDE IT AS CONTEXT ONLY, with its own variant and\n710:       parameters recorded by whoever computes it, and NO RULE OF THIS\n711:       CONTRACT DEPENDS ON IT. Two implementations that disagree on BCa\n712:       disagree about nothing this contract decides.\n713: \n714:       WHY THIS IS STRONGER THAN PINNING A BCa VARIANT, and what it costs.\n715:       Pinning the variant would make the interval reproducible for two\n716:       implementations sharing a library and still not for two that do not,\n717:       and it would leave a verdict resting on machinery whose failure mode is\n718:       invisible at a near-zero cell. Removing the interval from every verdict\n719:       removes the failure mode instead of documenting it. THE COST, STATED:\n720:       this contract buys no interval-based confidence statement about\n721:       feasibility, and a cell whose interval straddles zero is routed to SU\n722:       rather than called either way. That is the honest reading, and it is\n723:       why SU exists.\n724:       A ROUTING DIFFERENCE BETWEEN THE TWO READINGS is reported as INTERVAL-\n725:       METHOD SENSITIVITY, never as S3 DISAGREEMENT.\n726: \n727:     \"SU -- THE FRESH LABEL FOR THE INTERVAL-ROUTED OUTCOME (v3 amendment item 9, ADDITIVE -- S1/S2/S3 keep the approved v2's meanings; NO 'S4' EXISTS IN THIS CONTRACT)\": >-\n728:       THE LABEL: SU (CONFIRMED UNRESOLVED).\n729:       WHY A FRESH LABEL AND NOT S3. The approved v2's S3 means DISAGREEMENT\n730:       between the blind and production readings. The refused sidecar draft\n731:       re-used \"S3\" for CONFIRMED UNRESOLVED and put DISAGREEMENT at \"S4\" --\n732:       a label collision under one experiment identifier, where one label\n733:       would denote two different outcomes depending on which document a\n734:       reader had open. This experiment has already paid for one collision at\n735:       the amendment identifier (IC-1); a second, at the outcome labels, is\n736:       not a disclosed cost but a pattern. So: S1, S2 and S3 keep the approved\n737:       v2's meanings VERBATIM (see `success_criterion`, reproduced\n738:       byte-identically below), and the interval-routed outcome is SU. NO\n739:       OUTCOME OF THIS CONTRACT IS LABELLED S4: the string occurs only in this\n740:       key's own name, in the sentence above describing the refused draft's\n741:       labelling, and in `success_criterion_verbatim_attestation`, and never as\n742:       a label of anything.\n743:       WHEN SU IS ASSIGNED: see `success_criterion_v3_additions`, which states\n744:       the routing rule and, critically, its PRECEDENCE relative to S3 -- SU\n745:       never masks a disagreement.\n746:       WHAT SU ASSERTS: that at this cell, over this seed set, at this scale,\n747:       under this contract's budget, THE MEASUREMENT DOES NOT SEPARATE\n748:       FEASIBLE FROM INFEASIBLE. It is a statement about the resolution of the\n749:       instrument, not about the world. It supports no hypothesis-status\n750:       movement in either direction and closes no lane.\n751: \n752:     \"a = 1/16 INDEPENDENCE RULING (v3 amendment item 10, ADDITIVE -- discharges non-blocking defect D6; FIXED IN THE CONTRACT, NOT ROUTED TO A REVIEW JOINT)\": >-\n753:       THE STANDING CONTAMINATION, restated because the ruling is meaningless\n754:       without it: two commit messages reachable from the branch this contract\n755:       was authored on (84233e8c3, 376c6660e) state the a = 1/16 verdict in\n756:       plain text. That is a PERMANENT, UNREPAIRABLE contamination of any\n757:       future blind reading at a = 1/16 on this branch. The derivation packet\n758:       reduces the exposure -- a re-deriver obeying the allowlist runs no git\n759:       history command at all -- but does not eliminate it, and nothing in\n760:       this contract claims it does.\n761:       THE RULING, ASYMMETRIC AND BINDING:\n762:         AGREEMENT between the blind and production readings at a = 1/16\n763:         carries ZERO independence weight, from the outset, at both scales.\n764:         Not \"reduced\", not \"weakened pending review\": zero.\n765:         DISAGREEMENT at a = 1/16 retains FULL weight, and additionally\n766:         triggers falsification condition F2 and AGENTS.md rule 12\n767:         (independent review-breakthrough at max effort).\n768:       WHY ASYMMETRIC. An agreement produced because the re-deriver already\n769:       knew the answer is, by this contract's own account of the\n770:       contamination, indistinguishable from one produced because the answer\n771:       is right; a weight no observation can revise is not a weight, so any\n772:       nonzero independence credit at that cell would be unfalsifiable. The\n773:       converse does not hold: a DISAGREEMENT reached despite two commit\n774:       messages stating the opposite verdict is strong evidence precisely\n775:       because the contamination pushes the other way.\n776:       WHY IT IS FIXED HERE RATHER THAN LEFT TO A REVIEWER. The refused draft\n777:       set a = 1/16's independence to \"WEAKENED\" and left the adjective to a\n778:       review joint, while itself recording that the contamination is\n779:       undetectable downstream -- which asks a post-hoc reviewer to arbitrate\n780:       a word rather than attack a rule. A rule stated in advance can be\n781:       attacked in advance.\n782:       WHAT IT COSTS THIS BATCH: nothing. a = 1/16 has two jobs that need no\n783:       independence at all -- it is DECAY-A's low-a endpoint, and it is a\n784:       cross-scale consistency read.\n785:       DEFECT A DISCLOSURE, APPENDED (TASK-20260907-7cce3e, per\n786:       DEC-20260907-2c4beb / amendments/v2_to_v3.gate-outcome.yaml\n787:       `blocking_defects[A]`; nothing above this sentence is edited): this\n788:       inventory of standing leaks -- until now naming only the two a = 1/16\n789:       commit messages (84233e8c3, 376c6660e) -- omitted a THIRD leak, at\n790:       a = 1/8, introduced by `v3_r2_addendum.objective_v3_r2` further below\n791:       in this same file (approximately lines 2220-2222), which states a\n792:       cited, resolved verdict: \"It is confirmed ceiling-feasible at\n793:       N = 2^24 at strength `preliminary` (EV-ECDLP-6783b8 /\n794:       DEC-20260907-8d8782)...\". Like the two a = 1/16 leaks above, it is\n795:       NOT eliminated by disclosure; it is CONTAINED TODAY ONLY because\n796:       `prohibitions.md` section 2 blanket-forbids a Stage A'' re-deriver\n\n(Output capped at 50 KB. Showing lines 1-796. Use offset=797 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"experiment:\n  id: EXP-ECDLP-6ac801\n  id_allocation_provenance: >-\n    UNCHANGED by this v3 amendment: no new experiment identifier is minted;\n    this is the same EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 record, amended additively per\n    `protocol_amendment` below. v1's and v2's own id_allocation_provenance\n    notes stand at their own paths and are not restated here.\n  hypothesis_id: H-ECDLP-37dc01\n  question_id: RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5\n  goal_id: null\n  goal_id_note: >-\n    UNCHANGED from v2, verbatim in substance: RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5 and\n    H-ECDLP-37dc01 are themselves unbound to a GOAL record. This v3 amendment\n    was authored under GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f (batch BATCH-48ef8b), which is a\n    COORDINATION binding of the authoring lane and is NOT written into this\n    field: the hypothesis-to-goal binding is not this contract's to create.\n  derived_from_decision: DEC-20260906-bcc097\n  derived_from_decision_note: >-\n    UNCHANGED from v2. This v3 amendment's own triggering decisions are named\n    separately in `protocol_amendment` below, and do not replace v1's","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml","text":"experiment:\n  id: EXP-ECDLP-6ac801\n  id_allocation_provenance: >-\n    UNCHANGED by this v3 amendment: no new experiment identifier is minted;\n    this is the same EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 record, amended additively per\n    `protocol_amendment` below. v1's and v2's own id_allocation_provenance\n    notes stand at their own paths and are not restated here.\n  hypothesis_id: H-ECDLP-37dc01\n  question_id: RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5\n  goal_id: null\n  goal_id_note: >-\n    UNCHANGED from v2, verbatim in substance: RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5 and\n    H-ECDLP-37dc01 are themselves unbound to a GOAL record. This v3 amendment\n    was authored under GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f (batch BATCH-48ef8b), which is a\n    COORDINATION binding of the authoring lane and is NOT written into this\n    field: the hypothesis-to-goal binding is not this contract's to create.\n  derived_from_decision: DEC-20260906-bcc097\n  derived_from_decision_note: >-\n    UNCHANGED from v2. This v3 amendment's own triggering decisions are named\n    separately in `protocol_amendment` below, and do not replace v1's\n    derivation.\n  derived_from_idea: null\n\n  version: 3\n  status: approved\n  approved_by: coordinator\n  frozen: true\n  execution_authorized: true\n  gate_fields_note: >-\n    SUPERSEDED IN EFFECT BY `approval_note` BELOW, PRESERVED VERBATIM FOR\n    HISTORY (this sentence added by the approving gate; nothing above it in\n    this note is edited): this paragraph originally read \"DELIBERATE AND\n    BINDING. This v3 contract is NOT approved, NOT frozen and NOT authorized\n    for execution...\" That was true from authoring (TASK-20260907-058c69,\n    BATCH-48ef8b) through two prior independent-gate cycles\n    (DEC-20260907-4e34c5 on the v1-to-v2 predecessor draft; DEC-20260907-2c4beb\n    `revise` on this exact v2-to-v3-r2 revision) until the approval recorded in\n    `approval_note`. The original text, UNCHANGED below this sentence:\n    DELIBERATE AND BINDING. This v3 contract is NOT approved, NOT frozen and\n    NOT authorized for execution. It was authored by TASK-20260907-058c69\n    (coordinator, BATCH-48ef8b), and that session may not gate it: authorship\n    is not approval. Until an INDEPENDENT approval gate -- a coordinator\n    session that authored none of these artifacts -- records a committed\n    decision, no run under this v3 contract is evidence, by this contract's\n    own first `invalidation_rules` entry (carried verbatim from v2) and by the\n    appended v3 entry that names the gate-outcome record explicitly. The\n    approved v2 contract at experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml\n    remains in force, unedited and byte-identical, and this record changes\n    nothing about it or about the runs executed under v1.\n  approval_note: >-\n    APPROVED by an INDEPENDENT approval-gate coordinator session (gate task\n    TASK-20260907-e17c05, decision DEC-20260907-b4f2a9) that authored none of\n    specification.v3.yaml, amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml, the v3_r2_addendum, the\n    derivation-packet files, DEC-20260907-2c4beb, or TASK-20260907-7cce3e's\n    fixes. This approval rests on TASK-20260907-7cce3e (the post-gate fix\n    batch) discharging, correctly and completely, all four required fixes\n    named by DEC-20260907-2c4beb / amendments/v2_to_v3.gate-outcome.yaml\n    `required_fixes` -- independently re-verified by this gate, not accepted\n    on the fix task's own say-so. See DEC-20260907-b4f2a9 for the full,\n    per-defect independent re-verification (including its own explicit\n    disclosure of this gate session's tool limits: it has no Bash/shell, so\n    fix (4)'s sha256/script re-run was corroborated by source-code reading and\n    cross-reference against the separately committed\n    experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/archives/TASK-20260907-7cce3e/fix-receipt.json,\n    not by this session independently re-executing sha256sum or the script\n    itself). Approving this contract text does not re-open D1/D2/D3 (sound,\n    per both prior gates), does not predetermine any cell's verdict at\n    a in {1/16, 1/8, 3/16}, and does not move H-ECDLP-37dc01's status. It\n    authorizes dispatch of Stage A'' (the blind re-derivation under the\n    derivation packet) and, once sealed, Stage B/C's own execution under this\n    contract's stage plan -- nothing under v3 was evidence before this\n    record, and nothing here itself IS evidence: no run has occurred.\n\n  protocol_amendment:\n    version: 3\n    supersedes: 2\n    from_version: 2\n    to_version: 3\n    amendment_record: experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml\n    amendment_id: PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3\n    amends_which_document: >-\n      THE APPROVED ONE. The identifier PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v1-to-v2 names TWO\n      records (identifier collision IC-1, disposed of by DEC-20260907-b6bcf4\n      and NOT reopened here). This v3 amends the APPROVED, FROZEN v2 at\n      experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml with its amendment at\n      experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/v1_to_v2.yaml. It does NOT amend\n      the refused sidecar draft at\n      experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/{specification.v2.BATCH-e9fd22-proposed.yaml,\n      amendments/v1_to_v2.BATCH-e9fd22-proposed.yaml}, whose status\n      `revision_required` is unchanged by this record. See\n      `amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml` `amends` for the full disposition and the\n      sha256 of every file this amendment must not touch.\n    triggering_decisions:\n      - 'DEC-20260907-b6bcf4 (the lane close and rerank: RANK 1 = author this amendment; the compatibility read CR-1 and its four binding conditions; CR-1a)'\n      - 'DEC-20260907-4e34c5 (the approval gate refusal that identified D1, D2, D3 as blocking and D4-D7 as non-blocking, and TF-1)'\n    triggering_reports:\n      - coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-e9fd22/tasks/TASK-20260907-f65c6e/approval_review.yaml\n    amended_by: coordinator\n    amended_at: '2026-09-07'\n    amended_at_note: >-\n      This role holds no independent clock; the date is the runtime-supplied\n      calendar date, per the same disclosure every prior record in this lane\n      carries. The commit time is authoritative.\n    prior_frozen_path: experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml\n    prior_frozen_sha256: a989f8c2aea27ef79997b401ca475f74f87b45fc5f5762ab7ddf385878c9891c\n    prior_frozen_sha256_provenance: >-\n      COMPUTED by this authoring session with `sha256sum` over the committed\n      bytes at that path, not reused from any receipt and not estimated. It\n      DIFFERS from the hash recorded for the same literal path by\n      TASK-20260907-4ce154's snapshot receipt, because that receipt hashed\n      BATCH-e9fd22's own draft, which occupied this path when that snapshot\n      was taken and was later moved to the sidecar path by commit 465c01cba.\n      Both hashes are correct for their own bytes at their own commit; the\n      difference is the concrete residual cost of IC-1 and is disclosed here\n      so no reader mistakes it for a defect. See `amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml`\n      `additivity_check` for the full four-file check.\n    authority_to_change: >-\n      THE APPROVED CONTRACT'S OWN `invalidation_rules` ITEM 7, verbatim: \"Any\n      post-hoc change to the a-grid, N, r, T_sel, or the G3-style feasibility\n      criterion beyond what THIS versioned contract states: requires a further\n      versioned protocol_amendment; runs already executed are never\n      re-scored.\" This IS that further versioned protocol_amendment. Its\n      binding condition holds: RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-001..006 are never re-scored\n      under this contract and enter it in exactly ONE role, as the REFERENCE\n      of control (h). The one wide-scope item item 7 does not name is the SEED\n      COUNT; the authority used for that is control (e)'s own stated\n      rationale, argued a fortiori in control (g), and it is recorded as the\n      weaker warrant it is rather than assimilated to item 7. See\n      `amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml` `authority_to_change` for the full argument\n      and the fallback if a gate rejects it.\n    reason: >-\n      An independent approval gate (TASK-20260907-f65c6e, DEC-20260907-4e34c5)\n      REFUSED a proposed wide-scope v1-to-v2 draft on three blocking defects.\n      Two of the three are live IN THE APPROVED v2 as well, not only in the\n      refused draft, and that is why this amendment exists rather than a\n      narrower one.\n        D2 (THE REASON THIS OUTRANKS EVERYTHING ELSE): the strings `cap`,\n      `CAP_MULT`, `cycle_mass` and `capped_mass` appear ZERO times in the\n      approved v2. That contract is `execution_authorized: true` and requires\n      a freshly sealed blind re-derivation of the a = 1/8 cell, so a\n      from-scratch re-deriver working from its text alone MUST INVENT A CAP\n      CONVENTION -- and production's cap = ceil(8*W) truncates every walk and\n      every basin. Worse, the refused draft asserted the basin partition is\n      exhaustive (sum_d b(d) = N) while production leaves DP-free-cycle mass\n      and beyond-cap mass unassigned. This is the same class of gap that\n      produced the original a = 1/8 blind-versus-production disagreement,\n      relocated from the selection weight to the cap. v3 states the cap as a\n      formula in the measured quantities and replaces the false identity with\n      an exact accounting.\n        D3: the Coordinator's directional prior sat in plain text on the\n      re-deriver's own required reading path, and neither leaking path was on\n      any blind list. v3 replaces the DENYLIST MECHANISM with an enumerated,\n      hashed, self-contained ALLOWLIST (`blind_rederivation.v3_derivation_packet`),\n      because a blind discipline a fresh re-deriver cannot obey from the text\n      it is given is not a blind discipline.\n        D1: T must be 64 at N = 2^20 per the frozen T_OF_NBITS table, not the\n      102 that round(2^20^(1/3)) gives. Against the approved v2 this is a\n      BLANK TO FILL, not a value to contradict: v2 states nothing at N = 2^20.\n        Four non-blocking defects D4 (tie-break key unspecified), D5 (verdicts\n      resting on an underspecified bootstrap), D6 (a = 1/16 contamination left\n      to a review joint) and D7 (a null object of the wrong shape) are folded\n      in at the same time. See `amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml` for the worked\n      discharge of each.\n    what_changes_summary: >-\n      ADDITIVE THROUGHOUT. Nine appended `definitions` keys (the cap\n      convention and its residual accounting; the DP predicate's floor and\n      independent key; the tie-break key stream; T/T_sel at the second scale;\n      the W/cap table at all eight cells; the 25-seed set; the interval\n      estimator; the fresh label SU; the a = 1/16 independence ruling). Two\n      appended `blind_rederivation` sub-keys (`v3_derivation_packet`,\n      `v3_rerequirement_stage_a_dprime`) with all eight v1 fields and v2's own\n      `v2_rerequirement_a_1_8` retained byte-identically. Eight appended\n      `controls` items (g)-(n) with (a)-(f) byte-identical. Appended\n      stopping_rules, invalidation_rules, required_artifacts, interpretation,\n      tail_checks and distinguishable_outcomes entries, with every v1/v2 entry\n      retained verbatim. Separate additive keys carrying the v3 grid\n      (`independent_variables_v3`), the v3 metrics\n      (`metrics.primary_v3_additions`), the v3 replication\n      (`replication_v3`), the SU routing (`success_criterion_v3_additions`)\n      and the v3 falsification additions. Two ADVISORY budget numbers raised\n      (maximum_runs 8 -> 30, total_cpu_hours 1 -> 6); the two MACHINE\n      PROTECTION numbers unchanged (maximum_memory_gb 8, maximum_workers 1).\n      One field is deliberately NOT restated verbatim and the deviation is\n      declared: `preregistered_prediction`, for leak-discipline reasons given\n      in that field. Nothing in v1, in the approved v2, in either sidecar, or\n      under experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/runs/ is edited by one byte.\n    binding: >-\n      This amendment AUTHORIZES NOTHING. It does not authorize a run, a\n      re-seal, a review round, or a hypothesis-status movement, and it\n      approves neither itself nor this contract -- see `gate_fields_note`\n      above and `invalidation_rules`' appended v3 entry. It asserts no\n      research finding: no measurement, timing, margin, pass-count, interval\n      or verdict originates in it. What it produces is a contract text whose\n      quantities a from-scratch re-deriver can derive without inventing a\n      convention. Whether the corrected cap convention could change any\n      cell's verdict is UNMEASURED, and the direction of any induced\n      difference is unpredictable from the contract; nothing here is evidence\n      for or against G3 feasibility at any a.\n\n  status_history_note: >-\n    v1's gate fields at specification.yaml and v2's gate fields at\n    specification.v2.yaml are UNCHANGED and remain in force for their own\n    content: v1's for the already-executed Stage B/C runs\n    (RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-001..006, never re-scored), v2's for the explicit weight\n    formula and the scoped a = 1/8 re-seal requirement. This v3 record's own\n    gate fields are `proposed` / null / false / false and govern ONLY the new,\n    additive content introduced by this amendment. H-ECDLP-37dc01's status is\n    NOT moved by this record and carries no new `status_history` entry: there\n    is no evidence to add one for.\n\n  approval_note: >-\n    NOT APPROVED, AND NOT SELF-APPROVABLE. This differs deliberately from v1's\n    and v2's own approval pattern, and the difference is the point.\n      v1 and v2 were each authored and gated inside one lane under the\n    standing research-budget authorization, then presented to the user for\n    confirmation. v3 is NOT: an independent approval gate refused this\n    contract's predecessor draft (DEC-20260907-4e34c5) precisely because\n    contract text and implementation had drifted, and DEC-20260907-b6bcf4\n    `limitations` records explicitly that a fresh v3 gate must REPEAT the\n    contract-versus-implementation comparison rather than inherit it -- in\n    particular against the APPROVED v2's text, which no gate has yet done.\n      So the gate for this contract is a SEPARATE TASK IN A FRESH SESSION that\n    authored none of these artifacts, and it records its outcome in its own\n    additive record at\n    experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/v2_to_v3.gate-outcome.yaml -- NOT\n    by editing this file. Two reasons, one mechanical and one substantive: the\n    dispatcher permits exactly one owning task per artifact path\n    (tools/research_dispatch.py `validate_queue`), and BATCH-e9fd22's gate\n    wrote its outcome into the object it gated, which had to be reverted by\n    another session afterwards (PD-1, DEC-20260907-4e34c5). A gate outcome in\n    its own record leaves the gated bytes exactly as archived.\n      The standing research-budget authorization (CLAUDE.md \"Research budgets:\n    progress first\") removes the need for repeated USER budget approval. It\n    does not remove the need for an INDEPENDENT SCIENTIFIC GATE, and this\n    record does not treat it as though it did.\n\n  designed_by: coordinator\n  designed_at: '2026-09-07'\n  designed_at_note: >-\n    This role holds no independent clock; the date is the runtime-supplied\n    calendar date, per the same disclosure every prior record in this lane\n    carries.\n\n  title: >-\n    THE STAGE-0 T/2 DISCREPANCY, RE-CHECKED AT SCALE AND BLIND: does the\n    ORIGINAL clause (C1) claim -- a re-selected table with T_sel = T/2\n    reaching the static full-T table's steady-state ceiling -- become\n    G3-feasible at a SMALLER a than H-ECDLP-37dc01's stated test_boundary\n    (a in {1/4, 1/2}) names, specifically a in {1/16, 1/8}, and where does\n    the crossing between a = 1/8 and a = 3/16 fall, when re-measured at\n    N = 2^24 exact basins (one scale up from the v2 Stage 0 a-scan's\n    N = 2^20) under a FROZEN, mandatory blind re-derivation rather than a\n    second read of the same executor table that produced the discrepancy?\n  title_v3_scope_note: >-\n    The title above is v1's, retained verbatim. v3 adds a SECOND SCALE\n    (N = 2^20, the scale at which the original discrepancy was found), widens\n    the seed set from 5 to 25, and gates every verdict on a from-scratch\n    re-derivation whose readable inputs are an enumerated packet rather than a\n    prohibition list. The question is unchanged; what changes is the\n    derivability of its quantities and the power of its controls.\n\n  context: >-\n    UNCHANGED from v1/v2 in substance and retained by reference rather than\n    restated, so that no sentence of it drifts: see\n    experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml `context` (itself\n    byte-identical to v1's), which records how DEC-20260906-bcc097's closing\n    of BATCH-f3a30a surfaced the Stage 0 a-scan reading, how the orchestrating\n    session confirmed it by a second arithmetic route, and why\n    DEC-20260906-bcc097 RANK 1 required an independent from-scratch\n    re-derivation rather than a third read of the same table.\n  context_v3_addition: >-\n    WHAT HAS HAPPENED SINCE v2 WAS APPROVED, and why this contract exists.\n      (1) v1's Stage B/C executed and completed (RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-001..006,\n    6/6 completed_valid). v2 was approved to state the selection weight\n    formula explicitly and to require a fresh, sealed a = 1/8 re-derivation\n    under it.\n      (2) A wide-scope draft amendment was then authored in a separate lane\n    (BATCH-e9fd22) and submitted to an INDEPENDENT approval gate, which\n    REFUSED it (TASK-20260907-f65c6e, DEC-20260907-4e34c5) on three blocking\n    defects and recorded four more as non-blocking. The gate ALSO did\n    something more valuable than refuse: it reproduced all three primary\n    quantities at all 20 committed cells from the pinned instrument to a worst\n    absolute deviation of 0.000e+00 (TF-1), which is what makes this\n    contract's reproduction control achievable rather than aspirational.\n      (3) That lane closed (DEC-20260907-b6bcf4) and its rerank set RANK 1 to\n    exactly this record, under a compatibility read CR-1 with four binding\n    conditions, discharging D2 first, then D3, then D1.\n      (4) THE FINDING THAT MAKES THIS URGENT RATHER THAN TIDY (CR-1a): D2 is\n    live in the APPROVED v2, not merely in the refused draft. The approved\n    contract is execution_authorized and demands a blind re-derivation whose\n    central object -- the exact basin partition -- it truncates at a cap it\n    never mentions. Any re-derivation sealed against that text is sealed\n    against a convention its author had to guess.\n\n  hypothesis_test_boundary_note: >-\n    UNCHANGED from v1/v2: H-ECDLP-37dc01's own `statement` and\n    `test_boundary.parameters` scope `a` to {1/4, 1/2} ONLY, so testing at\n    a in {1/16, 1/8, 3/16} is OUTSIDE that stated boundary, and that widening\n    was disclosed additively on H-ECDLP-37dc01 itself\n    (`test_boundary.boundary_amendments`, 2026-09-07) rather than smuggled in.\n    See experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml\n    `hypothesis_test_boundary_note` for the full text, retained by reference\n    so no sentence drifts.\n  hypothesis_test_boundary_note_v3_addition: >-\n    v3 ADDS A SECOND N (2^20) BESIDE THE EXISTING N = 2^24, and that is a\n    FURTHER scope disclosure of the same kind. It is NOT a further widening of\n    the hypothesis's `a` boundary -- the a_grid is unchanged at\n    {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4} -- and it requires no edit to H-ECDLP-37dc01,\n    because N = 2^20 is where the Stage 0 discrepancy this lineage\n    investigates was originally read, and the already-recorded boundary\n    amendment covers the a-range at issue. NO HYPOTHESIS FIELD IS TOUCHED BY\n    THIS CONTRACT. This contract holds no authority to move\n    H-ECDLP-37dc01's status and does not; it stays `analyzed`.\n\n  objective: >-\n    UNCHANGED from v1/v2 for the N = 2^24 arm, retained by reference: see\n    experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml `objective`. v1's Stage\n    B/C already discharged that objective at all four a-values, and those runs\n    are not re-run and not re-scored by this contract.\n  objective_v3: >-\n    v3's OWN OBJECTIVE, stated in full because it is what the executor and the\n    re-deriver are held to.\n      For each a in {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4}, at BOTH N = 2^20 (T = 64,\n    T_sel = 32) and N = 2^24 (T = 256, T_sel = 128), r = 2, over 25\n    pre-registered seeds (1..25), compute per (N, a, seed): the exact\n    top-T_sel basin share, the STATIC(T)_{r=2} exact coverage, their\n    difference (the G3-style margin), and the four accounting quantities the\n    cap convention makes necessary (cycle_mass, capped_mass, capped_walks, and\n    the residual fraction). Apply the v2 G3-style feasibility criterion,\n    verbatim, to determine at each (N, a) whether T_sel = T/2 is G3-feasible.\n      Do this INDEPENDENTLY TWICE: once as STAGE A'' (a from-scratch blind\n    re-derivation whose entire permitted reading before its seal is the\n    enumerated derivation packet), and once as STAGE B''/C'' (production,\n    reusing the commit-pinned instrument). Then compare, per (N, a), on the\n    PASS-COUNT and the SIGN OF THE MEAN MARGIN -- two resampling-free\n    integers-and-signs quantities -- never on an interval endpoint.\n      Run every declared control, each of which has a state of the world in\n    which it fires on a correct implementation. Report the a = 1/4 cell FIRST,\n    because it is this batch's known-false object.\n      NOTHING ABOUT THIS OBJECTIVE PREDICTS AN OUTCOME. The contract states no\n    expected verdict, pass-count, margin or crossing bracket at a = 1/16,\n    a = 1/8 or a = 3/16 at either N; see `preregistered_prediction` for where\n    the Coordinator's expectation is recorded and why it is not here.\n\n  definitions: # v2 AMENDMENT NOTE, RETAINED: every key from \"N\" down to and\n               # including \"STATIC(T)_r pool-selection weight formula (v2\n               # amendment item 1...)\" is reproduced BYTE-IDENTICALLY from the\n               # APPROVED experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml\n               # `definitions`. v3 AMENDMENT NOTE: NINE new keys are APPENDED\n               # after them, each marked \"(v3 amendment item k, ADDITIVE)\".\n               # No existing wording is touched. Where a v3 key ADDS a value\n               # at a scale v2 left blank, it says so explicitly and leaves\n               # every v2 number in force.\n    N: \"order of the group (or size of the set for the generic instrument); fixed at 2^24 = 16777216 for this contract (one scale up from the v2 Stage 0 a-scan's N = 2^20)\"\n    T: \"nominal table size N^{1/3} rounded = 256 at N = 2^24\"\n    T_sel: \"number of entries STORED (the advice); FIXED at T/2 = 128 for this contract (the ORIGINAL clause (C1) value, not the v2 grid's 0.65T/0.75T)\"\n    W: \"expected walk length between DPs, W = sqrt(a N / T); theta = 1/W\"\n    a: \"T W^2 / N; a_grid = {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4} for this contract (see `hypothesis_test_boundary_note`)\"\n    r: \"precomputation pool ratio; FIXED at r = 2 for this contract (the value at which the original discrepancy was found; matches the operating point found feasible)\"\n    exact top-T_sel basin share: >-\n      the exact fraction of the N points whose walk terminates, under the\n      exact (non-sampled) basin partition of the DP-truncated functional\n      graph, in one of the T_sel largest basins by size -- computed by full\n      enumeration, not walked online, exactly as v1/v2's `exact_basins`\n      procedure and Stage 0's own a-scan compute it.\n    STATIC(T)_r exact coverage: >-\n      the exact fraction of the N points covered by the T basins selected\n      by the published Bernstein-Lange weight from an r T-distinct-DP\n      precomputation pool at ratio r, read exactly (not sampled) from the\n      same basin partition -- v1/v2's own STATIC(T) arm's exact-coverage\n      reading.\n    \"G3-style feasibility criterion (this contract's operative rule, IDENTICAL IN FORM to experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/specification.v2.yaml `inputs.g3_gate_procedure`, reused verbatim to prevent the exact definitional/units mismatch that is this contract's own outcome (b))\": >-\n      at a given a, T_sel = T/2 is G3-FEASIBLE iff exact top-T_sel basin\n      share >= STATIC(T)_r exact coverage in >= 4 of the 5 seeds; otherwise\n      G3-INFEASIBLE (equivalently, per-seed rho_ORACLE = the smallest\n      T_sel/T at which the exact share equals STATIC(T)'s coverage; T/2 is\n      feasible at a seed iff rho_ORACLE < 0.5 at that seed -- the SAME\n      arithmetic the orchestrating session's second, independent\n      confirmation used on EV-ECDLP-f6b3f5).\n    crossing point: >-\n      the (open) interval between the largest a at which T_sel = T/2 is\n      G3-feasible and the smallest a at which it is not, as bracketed by\n      this contract's own a_grid; this contract locates the crossing to\n      within the grid's own resolution (between 1/8 and 3/16, per the\n      Stage 0 N = 2^20 reading) and does NOT interpolate a point estimate\n      beyond that bracket (a finer grid is out of scope; see `out_of_scope`).\n    seed: \"walk-key seed for the generic instrument; 5 seeds per a, matching Stage 0's and v2's own seed count.\"\n    \"STATIC(T)_r pool-selection weight formula (v2 amendment item 1, ADDITIVE -- resolves the underspecification named by protocol_amendment.reason and by TASK-20260907-80e198 validation_report.yaml `a_1_8_disagreement_root_cause`)\": >-\n      \"STATIC(T)_r exact coverage\" above names \"the published\n      Bernstein-Lange weight\" but v1's own text never stated the formula --\n      a genuine gap in the frozen contract, not a physics disagreement (see\n      `protocol_amendment.reason`). The formula, stated explicitly and\n      completely for the first time in this contract by this amendment, IS:\n\n        weight_d = S_d + 4 * W * h_d\n\n      where, for each distinguished point (DP) d collected into the r*T\n      precomputation pool during pool generation (uniform random restarts,\n      batched, every walk charged):\n        - \"d\" is one DP entry in the r*T-distinct-DP pool (an index into the\n          pool, not a group element by itself beyond its DP identity).\n        - \"S_d\" is the SUM, over every pool-construction walk that\n          terminated at DP d, of that walk's GENERATING-WALK LENGTH (the\n          number of steps from that walk's own start/restart point to its\n          termination at d). A DP hit by three separate walks of lengths\n          L1, L2, L3 has S_d = L1 + L2 + L3.\n        - \"h_d\" is the HIT COUNT of DP d: the number of distinct\n          pool-construction walks that terminated at d (h_d = 3 in the\n          example above).\n        - \"W\" is `definitions.W` above (the expected walk length between\n          DPs, W = sqrt(a N / T)), the SAME W used everywhere else in this\n          contract; the constant multiplier on the h_d term is exactly 4\n          (not 4W^2, not W/4 -- the literal coefficient is \"4 * W\").\n      The T pool entries with the T LARGEST values of weight_d (ties broken\n      by an arbitrary but fixed key, per the tie-break discipline already\n      used by the reused instrument) are SELECTED into STATIC(T)_r's table;\n      \"STATIC(T)_r exact coverage\" is then read, exactly (not sampled), as\n      the true exact-basin coverage of that SELECTED set -- the selection\n      is by the realistic estimator weight_d above, never by the selected\n      entries' own true exact basin size (an oracle selection is a\n      DIFFERENT, NOT-STATIC(T)_r, and objectively worse-performing-for-the-\n      table-builder quantity; see `protocol_amendment.reason` for the\n      demonstrated numerical effect of conflating the two).\n      SOURCE / PRIOR ART: this is the published Bernstein-Lange\n      selection-weight formula for a distinguished-point precomputation\n      pool (the \"published Bernstein-Lange weight\" `STATIC(T)_r exact\n      coverage` above already names), and it is ALREADY IMPLEMENTED,\n      unchanged, by this contract's own reused Stage B instrument: class\n      `Pool`, method `weights`, in\n      experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/source_v2/instrument.py, lines 445-446\n      (verified by direct read of that file at this amendment's authoring\n      time): `def weights(self, W: float) -> np.ndarray: return\n      np.asarray(self.S, dtype=np.float64) + 4.0 * W *\n      np.asarray(self.h, dtype=np.float64)`, where `self.S` and `self.h`\n      are accumulated per-DP exactly as `S_d`/`h_d` are defined above (see\n      `Pool.add_or_credit`/`Pool.credit_index` in the same file, which\n      accumulate `self.S[j] += length` and `self.h[j] += count` per\n      pool-construction walk credited to pool index j). This formula\n      GOVERNS, and always has governed, Stage B/C's already-executed\n      production runs (RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-001..006); this amendment adds NO\n      new computation to Stage B/C and does not re-run it. It exists solely\n      so that any FUTURE independent from-scratch (blind) re-derivation of\n      STATIC(T)_r under this contract has the same formula available that\n      production has always used, closing the gap that produced\n      TASK-20260907-80e198's a = 1/8 sealed disagreement.\n\n    \"WALK CAP (v3 amendment item 1, ADDITIVE -- discharges blocking defect D2 of DEC-20260907-4e34c5; THE MOST LOAD-BEARING ADDITION IN THIS AMENDMENT)\": >-\n      THE PROBLEM THIS CLOSES. Every quantity in this contract is read off a\n      basin partition that production TRUNCATES at a walk cap. The strings\n      `cap`, `CAP_MULT`, `cycle_mass` and `capped_mass` appear ZERO times in\n      the approved v2 (and zero times in v1), so a from-scratch re-deriver\n      had to invent the convention. The independent gate that refused this\n      contract's predecessor draft found exactly this, and called it the same\n      class of gap as the one that produced the original a = 1/8 sealed\n      disagreement -- relocated from the selection weight to the cap.\n\n      THE CONVENTION, AS A FORMULA IN THE MEASURED QUANTITIES:\n\n        cap(N, a) = ceil( 8 * W(N, a) ),   W(N, a) = sqrt( a * N / T(N) )\n\n      with T(N) the frozen table T(2^20) = 64, T(2^24) = 256, T(2^30) = 1024\n      (see `T (v3 amendment item 4...)` below).\n\n      WHAT `cap` IS, EXACTLY. A COUNT OF WALK STEPS (group operations); a\n      non-negative integer; the LEAST INTEGER >= 8*W. It is NOT 8*W\n      truncated, NOT round(8*W), and NOT a distance in any other unit. The\n      multiplier is exactly 8. In production the float64 value of 8*W is\n      passed through math.ceil and then int(...).\n\n      READ OFF THE PRODUCTION IMPLEMENTATION, NOT PARAPHRASED FROM A\n      DECISION RECORD. The three governing lines, verbatim, from\n      experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/source_v2/instrument.py -- the\n      commit-pinned instrument this contract's own `instrument` field names\n      and Stage B imports:\n        line 31: `CAP_MULT = 8                                  # cap = 8W`\n        line 75: `self.W = math.sqrt(self.a * self.N / self.T)`\n        line 77: `self.cap = int(math.ceil(CAP_MULT * self.W))`\n\n      WHERE THE CAP BITES -- BOTH PLACES, BOTH BINDING:\n        (i) THE EXACT BASIN PARTITION. `exact_basins` assigns a point to a\n        basin only if its distance to its first DP is <= cap; see\n        `EXACT-BASIN RESIDUAL MASS ACCOUNTING (v3 amendment item 2...)`\n        below for the exact three-class partition and the accounting\n        identity that replaces the false claim that the partition is\n        exhaustive.\n        (ii) POOL CONSTRUCTION. `walk_to_dp` (instrument.py lines 126-151)\n        stops at the cap: its loop condition is\n        `while active.size and steps < P.cap` (line 141), it returns\n        terminal = -1 for a capped walk, and it charges\n        `length[active] = P.cap` to the survivors (line 150).\n        `generate_pools` (lines 243-289) then charges EVERY walk's length to\n        the precomputation cost (`P_cost += L`, line 268) but credits ONLY\n        the terminating ones: a capped walk (t < 0) increments a\n        `capped_walks` counter and contributes NOTHING to any S_d or h_d,\n        while a terminating walk credits `S[j] += L` and `h[j] += 1` at its\n        DP's pool index.\n        CONSEQUENCE, STATED BECAUSE IT IS EXACTLY WHAT A RE-DERIVER WOULD\n        GET WRONG: a pool-construction walk that reaches the cap is charged\n        its `cap` steps and credits NO S_d and NO h_d. A reading that\n        instead credits a capped walk to the DP it would eventually have\n        reached computes a different weight_d, hence a different\n        STATIC(T)_{r} selection, hence a different exact coverage. Both\n        readings MUST report `capped_walks` per cell so this is checkable\n        rather than invisible.\n\n      A CONSEQUENCE OF THE FORMULA, NOT A MEASUREMENT: because cap grows\n      like sqrt(a*N/T) while the walk-length distribution has mean W, the\n      cap sits at 8 mean walk lengths. This contract makes NO claim about\n      how much mass that leaves unassigned at any cell; that is a measured\n      quantity of this batch, required per cell of both readings, and is\n      reported, never predicted.\n\n    \"EXACT-BASIN RESIDUAL MASS ACCOUNTING (v3 amendment item 2, ADDITIVE -- the second half of D2's discharge; replaces a FALSE identity with an exact one)\": >-\n      THE FALSE STATEMENT, NAMED SO IT CANNOT PROPAGATE. The refused sidecar\n      draft (experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.BATCH-e9fd22-proposed.yaml,\n      lines 92 and 169) asserts that the basin partition is exhaustive:\n      \"sum over all d of b(d) = N\". THAT IS FALSE of the object production\n      computes, and it is stated here explicitly -- rather than merely\n      omitted -- because a reader arriving from that draft will have seen it\n      and must be told which way it was resolved. THE APPROVED v2 IS SILENT\n      on the question, so v3 retracts no approved sentence; it fills a\n      silence and corrects a draft.\n\n      THE THREE DISJOINT, EXHAUSTIVE CLASSES. For each of the N points x let\n      dist(x) be the number of walk steps from x to the first distinguished\n      point on its forward orbit, and reach(x) the predicate that such a DP\n      exists at all. `exact_basins` (instrument.py lines 194-215) computes\n      dist by pointer doubling with DPs made absorbing, saturates dist at\n      sat = 2^n_bits for points with no DP on their orbit, and then\n      partitions the N points into:\n        (1) ASSIGNED:     reach(x) AND dist(x) <= cap.\n                          line 209: `ok = reach & (dist <= P.cap)`\n        (2) CYCLE MASS:   NOT reach(x) -- a DP-free cycle, or a tail feeding\n                          one.\n                          line 210: `cycle_mass = int((~reach).sum())`\n        (3) CAPPED MASS:  reach(x) AND dist(x) > cap.\n                          line 211: `capped_mass = int((reach & ~ok).sum())`\n      BASIN SIZES ARE COUNTED OVER CLASS (1) ALONE. Lines 212-213:\n      `idx = np.searchsorted(dps, nxt[ok]...)` then\n      `size = np.bincount(idx, minlength=len(dps))`. So sum_d b(d) is\n      exactly the cardinality of class (1).\n\n      WHERE THE RESIDUAL GOES: NOWHERE. It is not assigned to any basin, not\n      redistributed, and not silently discarded -- it is REPORTED, as the two\n      named integer fields `Basins.cycle_mass` and `Basins.capped_mass`\n      (declared at instrument.py lines 164-165 with the comments \"points that\n      never reach a DP (DP-free cycle and its tails)\" and \"points whose first\n      DP lies beyond the cap\"). A point on a DP-free cycle, a point in a tail\n      feeding such a cycle, and a point whose first DP lies beyond the cap\n      all belong to NO basin.\n\n      THE TRUE RELATION, WHICH REPLACES THE FALSE IDENTITY:\n\n        sum over all DPs d of b(d)  =  N - cycle_mass - capped_mass\n\n      equivalently, as an exact accounting identity every reading must\n      satisfy in integer arithmetic with ZERO tolerance:\n\n        sum_d b(d)  +  cycle_mass  +  capped_mass  =  N\n\n      This is an identity of the object `exact_basins` computes, NOT an\n      empirical claim: classes (1), (2), (3) are disjoint and exhaustive over\n      the N points by construction. Because it cannot fail on a correct\n      implementation it is carried as a STRUCTURAL SELF-CHECK (control item\n      (n)) and NOT as a control -- see that item for why the distinction is\n      load-bearing here.\n\n      A COROLLARY WORTH STATING BECAUSE IT CATCHES A REAL DEFECT CLASS: every\n      DP lies in its own basin, so b(d) >= 1 for every DP d. At a DP,\n      dist = 0 (line 202, `dist = (~dp).astype(np.int32)`) and 0 <= cap, so\n      every DP is in class (1) and is counted into its own bincount bucket. A\n      reading that produces b(d) = 0 for some DP has a defect.\n\n      DERIVED QUANTITY, REQUIRED PER CELL OF BOTH READINGS:\n        residual_fraction = (cycle_mass + capped_mass) / N\n      reported alongside cycle_mass, capped_mass and capped_walks. This\n      contract states NO expected value for it at any cell.\n\n    \"DP PREDICATE AND ITS INDEPENDENT KEY (v3 amendment item 3, ADDITIVE -- so no second convention has to be invented either)\": >-\n      The approved v2's `instrument` field names the DP predicate in words\n      (\"DP predicate hash64(x) < floor(2^64 / W) with an independent key\").\n      v3 states it as a formula, for the same reason it states the cap: a\n      re-deriver must not have to guess a rounding or a key derivation.\n        theta = 1/W  (instrument.py line 76: `self.theta = 1.0 / self.W`)\n        dp_threshold = floor( 2^64 / W )  -- instrument.py line 83:\n          `self.dp_threshold = int(math.floor((1 << 64) / self.W))`\n        the predicate is  mix64( x XOR K_dp ) < dp_threshold\n        with the DP key derived independently of the walk key:\n          K_dp = mix64( K XOR 0xD1B54A32D192ED03 )   (instrument.py line 82)\n          K    = mix64( 0x9E3779B97F4A7C15 + seed )  (instrument.py line 84)\n      FLOOR, not round and not ceil. The DP key is derived from the walk key\n      by a fixed XOR-then-mix, so the marking is independent of the step\n      function while remaining a deterministic function of the seed. A\n      re-deriver implementing its own mix function will produce a DIFFERENT\n      concrete instance at the same seed; that is expected and is not a\n      defect, because agreement is judged on pass-counts and signs over 25\n      seeds, never on per-seed coincidence.\n\n    \"T (v3 amendment item 4, ADDITIVE -- discharges blocking defect D1; FILLS A BLANK, CONTRADICTS NO APPROVED VALUE)\": >-\n      v2's `definitions.T` above reads \"nominal table size N^{1/3} rounded =\n      256 at N = 2^24\" and states NOTHING at N = 2^20. That value stays in\n      force, byte-identical, and this key adds the second scale.\n        T(2^20) = 64      T(2^24) = 256      T(2^30) = 1024\n      THE FROZEN SOURCE, quoted verbatim from\n      experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/specification.v2.yaml line 223:\n        \"T: nominal table size N^{1/3} rounded, i.e. 64 at 2^20, 256 at 2^24,\n         1024 at 2^30\"\n      CORROBORATED BY THE COMMIT-PINNED INSTRUMENT, verbatim from\n      instrument.py line 29:\n        `T_OF_NBITS = {20: 64, 24: 256, 30: 1024}      # T = N^{1/3} rounded, as frozen`\n      and line 74: `self.T = T_OF_NBITS[self.n_bits]`.\n      T = 64 AT N = 2^20, NOT 102. The refused sidecar draft stated 102, and\n      the arithmetic of its stated rule is right -- round(2^20^(1/3)) = 102 --\n      which is exactly why the value must be pinned to the TABLE rather than\n      to the rule. THE PINNED INSTRUMENT HAS NO CODE PATH TO 102: T is a\n      dictionary lookup keyed on n_bits, with no fallback and no\n      round(N**(1/3)) expression anywhere in the file. At 2^24 and 2^30 the\n      table and round(N^{1/3}) coincide; 2^20 is the one scale where they\n      diverge, and 2^20 is the scale v3 adds. A reading that uses 102 at\n      N = 2^20 is invalid under this contract (see `invalidation_rules`).\n\n    \"T_sel (v3 amendment item 5, ADDITIVE -- follows T; v2's N = 2^24 value unchanged)\": >-\n      v2's `definitions.T_sel` above reads \"FIXED at T/2 = 128 for this\n      contract\" and stays in force, byte-identical, at N = 2^24. v3 adds:\n        T_sel = T/2  at every scale, hence\n        T_sel(2^20) = 32       T_sel(2^24) = 128   (v2's value, unchanged)\n      T_sel = T/2 remains THE ORIGINAL clause (C1) value and the only stored\n      size any verdict is read at. The DECAY-TSEL control additionally READS\n      T/4 and T/8 -- at N = 2^20 that is 16 and 8, at N = 2^24 that is 64 and\n      32 -- and those readings gate nothing except through control (l)'s own\n      stated clauses.\n\n    \"W AND cap AT EVERY CELL OF THIS CONTRACT'S GRID (v3 amendment item 6, ADDITIVE -- DERIVED FROM THE FORMULAS ABOVE, MEASURED FROM NOTHING)\": >-\n      Tabulated so that no reader, gate or re-deriver has to recompute eight\n      square roots to check a manifest. EVERY ROW IS A CONSEQUENCE OF\n      W = sqrt(a*N/T) AND cap = ceil(8*W) WITH T FROM THE FROZEN TABLE. No\n      row is read off any run, and no row is a result.\n\n        N = 2^20, T = 64:\n          a = 1/16 -> W = 32                 -> cap = 256\n          a = 1/8  -> W = 45.254833996...    -> cap = 363\n          a = 3/16 -> W = 55.425625842...    -> cap = 444\n          a = 1/4  -> W = 64                 -> cap = 512\n\n        N = 2^24, T = 256:\n          a = 1/16 -> W = 64                 -> cap = 512\n          a = 1/8  -> W = 90.509667992...    -> cap = 725\n          a = 3/16 -> W = 110.851251684...   -> cap = 887\n          a = 1/4  -> W = 128                -> cap = 1024\n\n      The BINDING definition is the formula, never the printed decimal:\n      W is used at float64 precision and cap is the integer above. A reading\n      whose cap differs from the value in this table at any cell has either\n      used a different T or a different multiplier, and is invalid under this\n      contract (see `invalidation_rules`).\n\n    \"SEED SET (v3 amendment item 7, ADDITIVE -- 25 pre-registered seeds; v2's 5-seed field unchanged and retained as a subgroup)\": >-\n      v2's `definitions.seed` above (\"5 seeds per a, matching Stage 0's and\n      v2's own seed count\") stays in force byte-identically and now describes\n      a NAMED SUBGROUP rather than the whole set. v3 pre-registers:\n        SEEDS = {1, 2, ..., 25}, the same 25 integers at every (N, a) cell,\n        in both readings, and in every control arm.\n        SEEDS_V1COMPARABLE = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}, a distinguished SUBGROUP of the\n        above, which is the seed set control (h) reproduces against and the\n        only seed set whose reading is directly comparable to the committed\n        v1 cells.\n      FIXED BEFORE EXECUTION, and fixed as a LIST rather than a count, so\n      that \"25 seeds\" cannot be satisfied by 25 seeds of someone's choosing\n      after seeing five of them. The 25-seed reading and the 5-seed subgroup\n      reading are reported SEPARATELY and are NEVER composited into one\n      number (control (g)).\n      Seed streams are the v1 construction, unchanged: the walk key, the DP\n      key, the target/phi/null/tie-break streams are all derived from the\n      integer seed exactly as instrument.py's `Params.__post_init__` derives\n      them (lines 84-91), so seeds 6..25 are the same KIND of object as seeds\n      1..5 and add power without changing the instrument.\n\n    \"INTERVAL ESTIMATOR (v3 amendment item 8, ADDITIVE -- discharges non-blocking defect D5; ROUTES ONLY, GATES NOTHING)\": >-\n      WHAT IT IS NOT FOR, FIRST, BECAUSE THAT IS THE DEFECT BEING CLOSED.\n      NO VERDICT, NO CONTROL CLAUSE AND NO AGREEMENT TEST IN THIS CONTRACT\n      DEPENDS ON A BOOTSTRAP. G3-FEASIBLE and G3-INFEASIBLE are functions of\n      the integer pass-count k alone. Blind-versus-production agreement is\n      judged on (k, sign of mean margin) alone. Both are exact and\n      resampling-free, so two independent implementations compute them\n      identically or differ for a reason about the quantity.\n\n      WHAT IT IS FOR: routing a cell to the fresh label SU (CONFIRMED\n      UNRESOLVED) -- see `SU ... (v3 amendment item 9...)` below -- which is\n      not a feasibility verdict and supports no hypothesis movement in either\n      direction.\n\n      THE PRIMARY ESTIMATOR, SPECIFIED TO THE CALL:\n        method:      PERCENTILE bootstrap (not BCa, not basic, not studentised)\n        statistic:   the MEAN over seeds of the per-seed margin at that\n                     (N, a) cell\n        resample:    i.i.d. with replacement over the 25 per-seed margins,\n                     preserving cell membership; seeds are the resampling\n                     unit\n        B:           10000 resamples\n        rng:         numpy.random.default_rng(20260907 + 1000*n_bits +\n                     round(10000*a)), constructed FRESH per cell so a cell's\n                     interval does not depend on the order cells were\n                     processed in\n        endpoints:   the 2.5th and 97.5th percentiles of the B resample\n                     means, via numpy.percentile(..., method='linear')\n                     (numpy's default), stated explicitly because\n                     percentile-method choice is a real source of\n                     implementation divergence\n      BCa IS REPORTED BESIDE IT AS CONTEXT ONLY, with its own variant and\n      parameters recorded by whoever computes it, and NO RULE OF THIS\n      CONTRACT DEPENDS ON IT. Two implementations that disagree on BCa\n      disagree about nothing this contract decides.\n\n      WHY THIS IS STRONGER THAN PINNING A BCa VARIANT, and what it costs.\n      Pinning the variant would make the interval reproducible for two\n      implementations sharing a library and still not for two that do not,\n      and it would leave a verdict resting on machinery whose failure mode is\n      invisible at a near-zero cell. Removing the interval from every verdict\n      removes the failure mode instead of documenting it. THE COST, STATED:\n      this contract buys no interval-based confidence statement about\n      feasibility, and a cell whose interval straddles zero is routed to SU\n      rather than called either way. That is the honest reading, and it is\n      why SU exists.\n      A ROUTING DIFFERENCE BETWEEN THE TWO READINGS is reported as INTERVAL-\n      METHOD SENSITIVITY, never as S3 DISAGREEMENT.\n\n    \"SU -- THE FRESH LABEL FOR THE INTERVAL-ROUTED OUTCOME (v3 amendment item 9, ADDITIVE -- S1/S2/S3 keep the approved v2's meanings; NO 'S4' EXISTS IN THIS CONTRACT)\": >-\n      THE LABEL: SU (CONFIRMED UNRESOLVED).\n      WHY A FRESH LABEL AND NOT S3. The approved v2's S3 means DISAGREEMENT\n      between the blind and production readings. The refused sidecar draft\n      re-used \"S3\" for CONFIRMED UNRESOLVED and put DISAGREEMENT at \"S4\" --\n      a label collision under one experiment identifier, where one label\n      would denote two different outcomes depending on which document a\n      reader had open. This experiment has already paid for one collision at\n      the amendment identifier (IC-1); a second, at the outcome labels, is\n      not a disclosed cost but a pattern. So: S1, S2 and S3 keep the approved\n      v2's meanings VERBATIM (see `success_criterion`, reproduced\n      byte-identically below), and the interval-routed outcome is SU. NO\n      OUTCOME OF THIS CONTRACT IS LABELLED S4: the string occurs only in this\n      key's own name, in the sentence above describing the refused draft's\n      labelling, and in `success_criterion_verbatim_attestation`, and never as\n      a label of anything.\n      WHEN SU IS ASSIGNED: see `success_criterion_v3_additions`, which states\n      the routing rule and, critically, its PRECEDENCE relative to S3 -- SU\n      never masks a disagreement.\n      WHAT SU ASSERTS: that at this cell, over this seed set, at this scale,\n      under this contract's budget, THE MEASUREMENT DOES NOT SEPARATE\n      FEASIBLE FROM INFEASIBLE. It is a statement about the resolution of the\n      instrument, not about the world. It supports no hypothesis-status\n      movement in either direction and closes no lane.\n\n    \"a = 1/16 INDEPENDENCE RULING (v3 amendment item 10, ADDITIVE -- discharges non-blocking defect D6; FIXED IN THE CONTRACT, NOT ROUTED TO A REVIEW JOINT)\": >-\n      THE STANDING CONTAMINATION, restated because the ruling is meaningless\n      without it: two commit messages reachable from the branch this contract\n      was authored on (84233e8c3, 376c6660e) state the a = 1/16 verdict in\n      plain text. That is a PERMANENT, UNREPAIRABLE contamination of any\n      future blind reading at a = 1/16 on this branch. The derivation packet\n      reduces the exposure -- a re-deriver obeying the allowlist runs no git\n      history command at all -- but does not eliminate it, and nothing in\n      this contract claims it does.\n      THE RULING, ASYMMETRIC AND BINDING:\n        AGREEMENT between the blind and production readings at a = 1/16\n        carries ZERO independence weight, from the outset, at both scales.\n        Not \"reduced\", not \"weakened pending review\": zero.\n        DISAGREEMENT at a = 1/16 retains FULL weight, and additionally\n        triggers falsification condition F2 and AGENTS.md rule 12\n        (independent review-breakthrough at max effort).\n      WHY ASYMMETRIC. An agreement produced because the re-deriver already\n      knew the answer is, by this contract's own account of the\n      contamination, indistinguishable from one produced because the answer\n      is right; a weight no observation can revise is not a weight, so any\n      nonzero independence credit at that cell would be unfalsifiable. The\n      converse does not hold: a DISAGREEMENT reached despite two commit\n      messages stating the opposite verdict is strong evidence precisely\n      because the contamination pushes the other way.\n      WHY IT IS FIXED HERE RATHER THAN LEFT TO A REVIEWER. The refused draft\n      set a = 1/16's independence to \"WEAKENED\" and left the adjective to a\n      review joint, while itself recording that the contamination is\n      undetectable downstream -- which asks a post-hoc reviewer to arbitrate\n      a word rather than attack a rule. A rule stated in advance can be\n      attacked in advance.\n      WHAT IT COSTS THIS BATCH: nothing. a = 1/16 has two jobs that need no\n      independence at all -- it is DECAY-A's low-a endpoint, and it is a\n      cross-scale consistency read.\n      DEFECT A DISCLOSURE, APPENDED (TASK-20260907-7cce3e, per\n      DEC-20260907-2c4beb / amendments/v2_to_v3.gate-outcome.yaml\n      `blocking_defects[A]`; nothing above this sentence is edited): this\n      inventory of standing leaks -- until now naming only the two a = 1/16\n      commit messages (84233e8c3, 376c6660e) -- omitted a THIRD leak, at\n      a = 1/8, introduced by `v3_r2_addendum.objective_v3_r2` further below\n      in this same file (approximately lines 2220-2222), which states a\n      cited, resolved verdict: \"It is confirmed ceiling-feasible at\n      N = 2^24 at strength `preliminary` (EV-ECDLP-6783b8 /\n      DEC-20260907-8d8782)...\". Like the two a = 1/16 leaks above, it is\n      NOT eliminated by disclosure; it is CONTAINED TODAY ONLY because\n      `prohibitions.md` section 2 blanket-forbids a Stage A'' re-deriver","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":796,"totalLines":797,"truncated":true}},"title":"experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml","time":{"start":1789086801466,"end":1789086801474}},"id":"prt_08de21a8b001NA5Th4s11qqRxj","sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","messageID":"msg_08ddd1710001NIH17n1bejhbhF"}}
