{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1789086870507,"sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","part":{"id":"prt_08de32bdd001uIFtCUKM3pCz4m","messageID":"msg_08de22b49001UqMOgFLjQouZpv","sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","snapshot":"723e35ce6957fa0016bc732d12d941e3a37884eb","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789086874316,"sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-acba8dce3e0fc3bb","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml","offset":797,"limit":800},"output":"<path>/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n797:       from reading `specification.v3.yaml` at all. The leaked text itself\n798:       remains verbatim in `objective_v3_r2`, unredacted and unmoved -- this\n799:       paragraph discloses its existence and location, it does not repair\n800:       it.\n801: \n802:   instrument: >-\n803:     IDENTICAL to experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/specification.v2.yaml\n804:     `instrument.generic_walk` and `inputs.exact_basins`, reused verbatim\n805:     (f(x) = mix64(x XOR K) mod N, DP predicate hash64(x) < floor(2^64 / W)\n806:     with an independent key; exact-basin enumeration procedure unchanged\n807:     from v1). No curve arm (generic instrument only; certificate kind:\n808:     none). The PRODUCTION computation (Stage B below) may reuse\n809:     experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/source_v2/'s exact-basin code by explicit\n810:     citation in its manifest (commit-pinned); the REQUIRED blind\n811:     re-derivation (Stage A) may NOT (see `blind_rederivation.blind_from`).\n812:   instrument_v3_note: >-\n813:     UNCHANGED, and now stated as formulas rather than by name: the DP\n814:     predicate's floor and independent-key derivation, the walk cap, and the\n815:     exact-basin residual accounting are given explicitly in `definitions`\n816:     items 1, 2 and 3 above. This is not a change of instrument -- it is the\n817:     same commit-pinned instrument, with the conventions it has always\n818:     implemented now derivable from the contract's own text. THE PRODUCTION\n819:     READING MUST REUSE THE PINNED INSTRUMENT and cite its commit in the\n820:     manifest; THE BLIND READING MUST NOT OPEN IT before its seal (the\n821:     allowlist in `blind_rederivation.v3_derivation_packet` does not contain\n822:     it, and `blind_from` continues to name it).\n823: \n824:   inputs:\n825:     stage_plan: >-\n826:       UNCHANGED from v1/v2 for the already-executed work, retained by\n827:       reference so no sentence drifts: see\n828:       experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml `inputs.stage_plan`\n829:       for Stage A (the original blind re-derivation), Stage B (v1's executed\n830:       exact-basin generation at N = 2^24, 5 seeds) and Stage C (v1's\n831:       analysis). Stage B/C is ALREADY COMPLETE (RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-001..006,\n832:       6/6 completed_valid), is NOT re-run by this contract, and is NEVER\n833:       re-scored under it.\n834:     stage_plan_v3: >-\n835:       v3's OWN STAGES. Three, and the first must be sealed before the second\n836:       is opened by the same agent.\n837: \n838:       STAGE A'' (BLIND RE-DERIVATION, REQUIRED, NON-NEGOTIABLE). A designated\n839:       independent agent, in a session that authored none of this contract's\n840:       artifacts, implements the quantity from scratch and SEALS it. ITS ENTIRE\n841:       PERMITTED READING BEFORE THE SEAL IS THE ENUMERATED DERIVATION PACKET\n842:       (`blind_rederivation.v3_derivation_packet`) -- not this contract, not\n843:       the amendment, not a handoff, not a task card, not a queue, not a\n844:       decision, not a run, not a commit message. Grid: both scales, all four\n845:       a, all 25 seeds. Deliverables per (N, a, seed): exact top-T_sel basin\n846:       share, STATIC(T)_{r=2} exact coverage, margin, cycle_mass, capped_mass,\n847:       capped_walks, residual_fraction, and the count of pool entries tied at\n848:       the T-th largest weight. Per (N, a): pass-count k out of 25, mean\n849:       margin and its sign, the percentile interval, and the same for the\n850:       seeds 1..5 subgroup reported separately.\n851: \n852:       STAGE B'' (PRODUCTION, exact-basin generation). The commit-pinned\n853:       instrument, cited by commit in every manifest. N in {2^20, 2^24};\n854:       a_grid = {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4}; r = 2; T_sel = T/2 (32 and 128); seeds\n855:       1..25. Zero online re-selected (RESEL-L) arms -- this is an\n856:       exact-enumeration measurement only, as in v1. Same per-cell deliverable\n857:       list as Stage A''. Additionally, the control arms: NULL-ORACLE-RAND\n858:       (uniform) as the gating null, its size-biased variant as a diagnostic,\n859:       NULL-RANDSEL retained non-gating, NULL-SHUF as a fenced-off diagnostic,\n860:       and the T/4 and T/8 readings that control (l) needs. THE N = 2^20 ARM\n861:       RUNS FIRST, because it is roughly 16x cheaper and shakes the pipeline\n862:       out before the expensive scale.\n863: \n864:       STAGE C'' (ANALYSIS). Apply the G3-style feasibility criterion at each\n865:       (N, a) to BOTH readings independently. Evaluate the a = 1/4 cell FIRST.\n866:       Evaluate every control and report each as fired or not fired, with the\n867:       quantity it was read from. Compare the two readings on (k, sign of mean\n868:       margin), per (N, a); route to SU where the routing rule applies; report\n869:       the crossing bracket at each scale, or report plainly that no clean\n870:       crossing is confirmed. Report the seeds 1..5 subgroup separately from\n871:       the 25-seed reading and NEVER composite them. Report the\n872:       tie-break-induced symmetric difference of the two Sel_static sets, and\n873:       the residual-mass accounting identity's exact satisfaction, per cell of\n874:       both readings.\n875:     arms: >-\n876:       UNCHANGED from v1/v2 for the primary reading, verbatim in substance:\n877:       two exact-coverage readings only per (a, seed) -- STATIC(T)_{r=2} exact\n878:       coverage, and the exact top-T_sel basin share. No ORACLE, RESEL-L,\n879:       NULL-A, CAP, RHO, or STATIC2T arm is run; those test the re-selection\n880:       MECHANISM (already the subject of EXP-ECDLP-612fb1) and remain out of\n881:       scope for this narrow ceiling-feasibility check (see `out_of_scope`).\n882:     arms_v3_addition: >-\n883:       v3 ADDS CONTROL ARMS ONLY, all read off the SAME exact basin partition\n884:       as the primary arms, none of them an online re-selection batch:\n885:       (i) NULL-ORACLE-RAND (uniform), the gating null: the ORACLE side is\n886:       replaced by a uniformly random T_sel-subset of the DPs of the SAME\n887:       enumerated partition, cov_static held fixed and read off identically;\n888:       (ii) NULL-ORACLE-RAND (size-biased), diagnostic only, direction\n889:       declared unpredictable in advance; (iii) NULL-RANDSEL, retained,\n890:       non-gating, low power disclosed; (iv) NULL-SHUF, diagnostic, explicitly\n891:       not a G3 null; (v) the T/4 and T/8 top-share readings control (l)\n892:       needs. The primary arm count per cell is unchanged.\n893:     exact_basins: \"unchanged from v1/v2, verbatim, restricted to N = 2^24 and the a_grid above.\"\n894:     exact_basins_v3_addition: >-\n895:       Same procedure, unchanged, now run at N = 2^20 as well, and now with\n896:       the cap and residual accounting stated in `definitions` items 1 and 2\n897:       rather than left implicit. cycle_mass, capped_mass and\n898:       residual_fraction are REQUIRED OUTPUTS of every exact-basin\n899:       enumeration under this contract, in both readings.\n900: \n901:   blind_rederivation:\n902:     required: true\n903:     frozen: true\n904:     quantity: >-\n905:       exact top-T_sel (= T/2) basin share and STATIC(T)_{r=2} exact coverage\n906:       at each a in {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4}, N = 2^24, from the exact\n907:       basin-partition definition alone (a uniformly random function on N\n908:       points truncated at an independent Bernoulli(1/W) marking, per\n909:       HEUR-BLT-1) -- NOT a re-read of any run's own analysis output and NOT\n910:       an inspection of experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/source_v2/'s\n911:       implementation before the seal.\n912:     parameters: \"N = 2^24; a_grid = {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4}; r = 2; T_sel = T/2 = 128; 5 seeds\"\n913:     procedure: >-\n914:       A designated independent reviewer (validator or, if none is assigned,\n915:       the executor acting under a strict pre-registration discipline)\n916:       writes their own from-scratch computation of the quantity above, SEALS\n917:       it (commits it to their own task directory with a hash and timestamp,\n918:       exactly as TASK-20260906-bc1cfc's J2 sealed its result before opening\n919:       any run artifact), and ONLY THEN opens: (i) this experiment's own\n920:       Stage B/C run output, (ii) the original EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 v2 Stage 0\n921:       a-scan data that produced the discrepancy. The sealed file and its\n922:       hash/timestamp are a REQUIRED artifact (see `required_artifacts`).\n923:     blind_from:\n924:       - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/source_v2/\n925:       - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/runs/RUN-ECDLP-612fb1-v2-ascan-*/\n926:       - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/runs/RUN-ECDLP-612fb1-v2-analysis-001/\n927:       - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/runs/ (this experiment's own outputs, once they exist)\n928:     comparison_rule: >-\n929:       The blind result and Stage B/C's production result are compared cell\n930:       by cell (per a). Agreement (same PASS/FAIL pattern, margins within\n931:       seed-to-seed noise) is required before ANY cell's G3-style verdict is\n932:       reported as more than a single, unreviewed reading; disagreement is\n933:       itself the headline result of this batch (see `distinguishable_outcomes`\n934:       (b)) and is never resolved by picking one side without a stated,\n935:       checkable reason (e.g. a demonstrated units/definition mismatch).\n936:     non_negotiable_note: >-\n937:       This step exists BECAUSE the discrepancy this contract investigates\n938:       was itself found by re-reading the same executor table twice by two\n939:       different arithmetic routes, not by an independent from-scratch\n940:       computation -- DEC-20260906-bcc097's RANK 1 explicitly requires the\n941:       latter. A run set completed without a sealed blind re-derivation is\n942:       NOT evidence under this contract (see `invalidation_rules`).\n943:     v2_rerequirement_a_1_8: # ADDITIVE, v2 amendment item 2 -- everything above this key is BYTE-IDENTICAL to v1\n944:       status: REQUIRED, scoped narrowly to the single a = 1/8 cell\n945:       trigger: >-\n946:         TASK-20260907-80e198's sealed Stage A blind re-derivation (5/5\n947:         seeds at a = 1/16, 0/5 at a = 3/16, 0/5 at a = 1/4, 1/5 at a = 1/8)\n948:         used an oracle true-exact-basin-size STATIC(T)_r selection because\n949:         v1's `definitions` underspecified the weight formula. Only the\n950:         a = 1/8 cell's PASS/FAIL VERDICT actually flips between the oracle\n951:         rule and the now-explicit `STATIC(T)_r pool-selection weight\n952:         formula` (a = 1/16 and a = 1/4 are robust to the choice of rule per\n953:         `postseal_diagnostic_v2_clean.py`'s own controlled result; a = 3/16\n954:         moves from 0/5 to 2/5 but remains solidly G3-INFEASIBLE by the\n955:         >= 4/5 threshold either way, so it does not need re-sealing).\n956:       scope: >-\n957:         ONLY the a = 1/8 cell (N = 2^24, r = 2, T_sel = T/2 = 128, 5 seeds)\n958:         is re-derived under this requirement. The other three cells\n959:         (a = 1/16, a = 3/16, a = 1/4) already show CLEAN AGREEMENT between\n960:         Stage A and Stage B/C under EITHER selection rule and are NOT\n961:         re-opened, re-sealed, or re-run by this amendment; DEC-20260907-9b1b02\n962:         already records their S1/S2/S2 verdicts as settled by this batch.\n963:       new_artifact_requirement: >-\n964:         The next Stage A blind re-derivation performed under this v2\n965:         definition MUST be a NEW, freshly created and freshly sealed\n966:         artifact. It may NOT edit, append to, or replace\n967:         TASK-20260907-80e198's own sealed_blind_rederivation.json (an\n968:         immutable record, per rule 2, of exactly what was computed under\n969:         v1's underspecified definitions -- \"runs already executed are never\n970:         re-scored\", `invalidation_rules`), and it may NOT edit or reuse any\n971:         file under experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/runs/ (Stage B/C's own,\n972:         already-committed, already-correct production output, per Stage B/C\n973:         `unchanged` note in `inputs.stage_plan` above). It must live at its\n974:         own new task directory under a new TASK-* handoff, with its own\n975:         hash and timestamp, exactly mirroring how TASK-20260907-80e198's own\n976:         seal was produced (see `procedure` above, unchanged).\n977:       seal_timing_requirement: >-\n978:         The new re-derivation must be SEALED (hashed and timestamped) BEFORE\n979:         the reviewer performing it opens ANY `blind_from` path listed above,\n980:         exactly as `procedure` above already requires for a first-time Stage\n981:         A derivation. In particular, the reviewer performing this re-seal\n982:         must NOT read TASK-20260907-80e198's own sealed_blind_rederivation.json,\n983:         blind_rederivation.py, or postseal_diagnostic*.py contents before\n984:         sealing their own new computation, so that the corrected formula is\n985:         applied independently rather than copied from the prior task's\n986:         post-hoc diagnostic scripts (those scripts remain readable\n987:         background/citation material for the Coordinator and for a\n988:         subsequent audit, never a substitute for an independent re-seal).\n989:       what_does_not_need_to_be_rerun: >-\n990:         Stage B/C's existing production result for a = 1/8 (5/5 seeds,\n991:         G3-FEASIBLE, RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-001..006, already computed correctly\n992:         under this exact formula, per `a_1_8_disagreement_root_cause`'s\n993:         `what_production_actually_does`) does NOT need to be re-run. Only\n994:         Stage A's blind re-derivation at a = 1/8 is being redone; the new\n995:         sealed a = 1/8 result is compared, cell by cell, against the\n996:         ALREADY-EXISTING production a = 1/8 reading recorded in\n997:         experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/runs/RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-{001..005}/'s\n998:         own raw-result.json and summary.json (unchanged, unedited, exactly\n999:         as committed).\n1000:       resolution_rule: >-\n1001:         Only AFTER this re-sealed a = 1/8 result is produced and compared\n1002:         may a = 1/8 be reported, by a further committed Coordinator\n1003:         decision, as S1 CONFIRMED FEASIBLE, S2 CONFIRMED INFEASIBLE, or a\n1004:         genuinely new S3 DISAGREEMENT (per `success_criterion`'s own S1/S2/S3\n1005:         taxonomy, unchanged by this amendment). This amendment does not\n1006:         itself predetermine which of those three outcomes will result.\n1007: \n1008:     v3_derivation_packet: # ADDITIVE, v3 amendment item 11 -- everything above this key,\n1009:                           # INCLUDING v2_rerequirement_a_1_8, is BYTE-IDENTICAL to the\n1010:                           # approved v2. This appends inside a block carrying\n1011:                           # `frozen: true` by exactly the precedent the approved v2 set\n1012:                           # against itself with v2_rerequirement_a_1_8.\n1013:       status: 'REQUIRED for any Stage A'''' re-derivation under this v3 contract'\n1014:       discharges: 'blocking defect D3 of DEC-20260907-4e34c5, and archive-time observations AO-2 and AO-3'\n1015:       what_the_defect_was: >-\n1016:         The Coordinator's directional prior sat in plain text in a handoff\n1017:         (ledger/handoffs/TASK-20260907-e423d5.yaml\n1018:         `review_plan.coordinator_prior`) and in a committed dispatch queue,\n1019:         and a task card named that handoff as the re-deriver's own\n1020:         `review_plan_path` -- so the re-deriver was INSTRUCTED to read the\n1021:         prior before sealing. Neither path was on any blind list.\n1022:       why_this_is_not_fixed_by_adding_two_paths_to_a_list: >-\n1023:         Three reasons, each read off the committed record.\n1024:         (i) A DENYLIST CANNOT BE SHOWN COMPLETE. It enumerates what must not\n1025:         be read out of a repository of thousands of identifier-bearing paths\n1026:         that grows every batch; \"no further leak path exists\" is not a\n1027:         statement any author can support, and the gate found two the previous\n1028:         author had missed.\n1029:         (ii) THE LISTS DRIFT, DEMONSTRABLY. AO-3 records that the two blind\n1030:         lists for the SAME re-derivation had already diverged, so the\n1031:         re-deriver had two answers to one question.\n1032:         (iii) IT DEPENDS ON A CONVENTION RECORDED ELSEWHERE. AO-2 records a\n1033:         direct contradiction between a contract's `not_blind_from` (two paths\n1034:         MUST be read) and a handoff's `blind_from` (those same two paths\n1035:         added), resolvable only by a convention stated in a decision record.\n1036:         A BLIND DISCIPLINE A FRESH RE-DERIVER CANNOT OBEY FROM THE TEXT IT IS\n1037:         GIVEN IS NOT A BLIND DISCIPLINE -- and that is the standard the entire\n1038:         re-seal exists to meet.\n1039:       the_mechanism: 'AN ALLOWLIST REPLACES THE DENYLIST AS AUTHORITATIVE.'\n1040:       packet_path: experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/derivation-packet/PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3/\n1041:       the_rule_in_one_sentence: >-\n1042:         Until its own seal exists, the Stage A'' re-deriver reads EXACTLY the\n1043:         files enumerated in the packet's own MANIFEST.yaml and NOTHING ELSE\n1044:         in this repository -- not this contract, not the amendment, not a\n1045:         handoff, not a task card, not a queue, not a decision, not a run, not\n1046:         a commit message, and no output of any git history command.\n1047:       contents:\n1048:         - 'MANIFEST.yaml -- the complete readable-file list with sha256 for each, the reading rule, the seal procedure, and the declaration that the packet carries no prior and no result. IT IS THE FIRST FILE THE RE-DERIVER OPENS, so the discipline is stated in the only text the re-deriver may read.'\n1049:         - 'quantity.md -- the STATEMENT of the quantity and the parameters, quoting this contract''s `definitions` and `inputs` verbatim: the instrument, the DP predicate, the exact-basin partition, the cap and its residual accounting, pool construction, the selection weight and its tie-break, the top-T_sel share, the exact coverage, the margin, the pass-count rule, the seed set, and the interval estimator.'\n1050:         - 'deliverables.md -- what to produce and in what shape, with the joints the re-deriver owns stated WITHOUT any expectation of how any of them will come out.'\n1051:         - 'prohibitions.md -- the reading rule as an operational checklist, including the two mechanical prohibitions (no git log/show/blame; no reading of any commit message before the seal) and the honest disclosure that two commit messages already reachable on the authoring branch state a prior cell''s verdict.'\n1052:       why_it_is_the_repair:\n1053:         - 'FINITE, ENUMERATED AND HASHED. Completeness is a property of a closed four-file list, not a claim about a repository. \"Did I read something I should not have\" becomes decidable by the re-deriver itself.'\n1054:         - 'SELF-CONTAINED. The manifest lives inside the packet and is read first, so the discipline depends on no convention recorded in a decision record -- which is AO-2''s failure and the sharpest form of D3.'\n1055:         - 'LEAK-FREE BY CONSTRUCTION AND CHECKABLY SO. The packet contains no prior, no verdict, no pass-count, no margin, no interval and no number produced by any prior run at any cell of the quantity under test. It is not merely asserted clean: it is four files a gate reads end to end.'\n1056:         - 'IT DISSOLVES AO-2 RATHER THAN ADJUDICATING IT. Under an allowlist there is no file the re-deriver is both required and forbidden to read, because \"forbidden\" is the complement of the list.'\n1057:         - 'IT MAKES ONE LIST AUTHORITATIVE WITHOUT EDITING A FROZEN FIELD. `blind_from` above stays byte-identical and is demoted to CORROBORATING; see `precedence` below.'\n1058:       precedence: >-\n1059:         WHERE THE PACKET AND ANY DENYLIST COULD DIFFER, THE PACKET GOVERNS\n1060:         for the question \"may I read this before my seal\". `blind_from`\n1061:         above, and any future review plan's `blind_from` for this experiment,\n1062:         are CORROBORATING: they warn a denylist-only reader and they may add\n1063:         paths, but they cannot widen what the packet permits, and nothing\n1064:         load-bearing turns on their contents. Two lists that cannot disagree\n1065:         about anything load-bearing cannot drift into a contradiction.\n1066:       normativity: >-\n1067:         THE CONTRACT GOVERNS ON DEFINITIONS. quantity.md quotes this\n1068:         contract's `definitions` and `inputs` verbatim and adds no\n1069:         definitional content of its own. If the packet and this contract are\n1070:         ever found to differ on any definitional point, THIS CONTRACT GOVERNS,\n1071:         the packet is defective, and the difference is a REPORTABLE DEFECT of\n1072:         amendment PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3 -- never a licence for the\n1073:         re-deriver to choose. Verifying that the packet says exactly what this\n1074:         contract says, and nothing more, is an explicit joint of this\n1075:         contract's approval gate.\n1076:       the_one_disclosed_inclusion: >-\n1077:         DISCLOSED RATHER THAN SMUGGLED. The packet states that T_sel = T/2 at\n1078:         a = 1/4, r = 2, N = 2^24 is ESTABLISHED G3-INFEASIBLE by\n1079:         EV-ECDLP-60e266, and that the re-deriver must report the a = 1/4 cell\n1080:         FIRST.\n1081:         WHY NECESSARY: a = 1/4 is this batch's KNOWN-FALSE OBJECT, carried\n1082:         from control (b). \"Controls before belief\" requires the identical\n1083:         measurement be run against an object whose answer is known, and a\n1084:         re-deriver not told which object that is cannot run the control.\n1085:         WHY BOUNDED: it concerns a = 1/4 ONLY. The packet states no verdict,\n1086:         expectation, pass-count, margin, share, coverage or interval at\n1087:         a = 1/16, a = 1/8 or a = 3/16 at either N -- and a = 1/8 is the\n1088:         decision-changing cell this lineage exists to resolve. It says what\n1089:         the instrument must REPRODUCE, not what the open cells will do.\n1090:       where_the_prior_lives_instead:\n1091:         path: coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-48ef8b/priors/coordinator_prior.SEALED.yaml\n1092:         why_it_is_kept: >-\n1093:           AGENTS.md \"Review architecture\" REQUIRES the Coordinator's prior to\n1094:           be recorded before any reviewer runs: \"three reviewers concurred\"\n1095:           and \"three reviewers concurred with what the Coordinator already\n1096:           believed\" are different findings, and only a pre-recorded prior\n1097:           separates them. THE ANSWER TO A LEAKING PRIOR IS NEVER TO STOP\n1098:           RECORDING IT.\n1099:         properties:\n1100:           - 'It is NOT in the derivation packet, so under the allowlist it is unreadable before the seal without an explicit violation.'\n1101:           - 'It is named on the corroborating denylist below and must be named on every future review plan''s `blind_from` for this experiment.'\n1102:           - 'It is the ONLY place in its batch carrying a directional expectation: that lane''s queue, task cards, handoffs, opening decision and commit messages state no prior, no verdict, no margin and no number at any cell of the quantity under test.'\n1103:           - 'It is committed in the lane''s opening snapshot, so the commit that carries it is itself proof the prior predates every reviewer -- a STRONGER discharge of the AGENTS.md requirement than a prior recorded in a handoff, not a weaker one.'\n1104:         contains_no_authority: >-\n1105:           It records an expectation and nothing else: no instruction to any\n1106:           reviewer, no assignment, no authority. A reviewer's joints and\n1107:           deliverables come from the packet, which is why the packet can be\n1108:           prior-free at all.\n1109:       corroborating_denylist_v3_additions: >-\n1110:         NOT AN EDIT OF `blind_from` ABOVE, which stays byte-identical. These\n1111:         paths are additionally named here, and must be named on every future\n1112:         review plan's `blind_from` for this experiment, so that a\n1113:         denylist-only reader is warned even though the packet is what governs:\n1114:           coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-48ef8b/priors/\n1115:           ledger/handoffs/TASK-20260907-e423d5.yaml\n1116:           coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-e9fd22/\n1117:           coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-48ef8b/\n1118:           ledger/decisions/ (every DEC-* of this lineage)\n1119:           ledger/evidence/ (every EV-* of this lineage)\n1120:           ledger/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/\n1121:           experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.BATCH-e9fd22-proposed.yaml\n1122:           experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/\n1123:           experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml (THIS FILE)\n1124:           coordination/experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/\n1125:         THE LIST IS NOT CLAIMED COMPLETE. That is the whole point of D3's\n1126:         repair: completeness is claimed for the ALLOWLIST, which is four\n1127:         files, and never for this.\n1128:       seal_procedure_unchanged: >-\n1129:         The seal itself is `procedure` above, byte-identical and in force: the\n1130:         re-deriver commits its own from-scratch computation to its own task\n1131:         directory with a hash and a timestamp, and only then opens anything\n1132:         outside the packet. v3 changes WHAT MAY BE READ BEFORE THE SEAL, not\n1133:         what a seal is.\n1134: \n1135:     v3_rerequirement_stage_a_dprime: # ADDITIVE, v3 amendment item 12\n1136:       status: 'REQUIRED; supersedes NOTHING and re-scores NOTHING'\n1137:       scope: >-\n1138:         A FRESH Stage A'' blind re-derivation over the FULL v3 grid: N in\n1139:         {2^20, 2^24}, a in {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4}, r = 2, T_sel = T/2, seeds\n1140:         1..25. It is a NEW artifact at a NEW task directory with its own hash\n1141:         and timestamp.\n1142:       why_the_full_grid_and_not_only_a_1_8: >-\n1143:         v2's `v2_rerequirement_a_1_8` scoped its re-seal to a = 1/8 because\n1144:         only that cell's verdict flipped under the corrected WEIGHT formula.\n1145:         D2 is different in kind: the CAP enters every cell of every scale,\n1146:         through the basin partition itself and through pool construction, so\n1147:         no cell is known robust to it. Scoping the v3 re-seal to one cell\n1148:         would assume exactly what is unmeasured. THIS IS A STATEMENT ABOUT\n1149:         WHAT IS UNKNOWN, NOT A PREDICTION THAT ANY CELL WILL MOVE.\n1150:       relation_to_the_v2_requirement: >-\n1151:         `v2_rerequirement_a_1_8` above is UNCHANGED, byte-identical, and\n1152:         remains in force under the approved v2 for its own narrow purpose. A\n1153:         Stage A'' re-derivation satisfying THIS requirement also covers the\n1154:         a = 1/8 cell it names, but does not retroactively discharge it under\n1155:         v2's own terms and does not touch TASK-20260907-80e198's sealed\n1156:         artifact, which stays immutable as the record of what was computed\n1157:         under v1's underspecified definitions.\n1158:       immutability_requirement: >-\n1159:         The Stage A'' artifact may NOT edit, append to, or replace\n1160:         TASK-20260907-80e198's sealed_blind_rederivation.json, any file under\n1161:         experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/runs/, or anything under\n1162:         coordination/experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/batches/BATCH-3c7493/. It\n1163:         lives at its own new task directory. A violation is invalid under\n1164:         `invalidation_rules`, per rule 2.\n1165:       independence_requirement: >-\n1166:         The agent performing Stage A'' must be in a session that authored\n1167:         neither this contract, nor amendment PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3, nor\n1168:         the derivation packet. Authorship of the packet is disqualifying for\n1169:         obeying it: the author knows what was deliberately left out.\n1170: \n1171:   controls: # v3 AMENDMENT NOTE: items (a) through (f) below are reproduced\n1172:             # BYTE-IDENTICALLY from the APPROVED\n1173:             # experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml `controls`.\n1174:             # Items (g) through (n) are APPENDED by this v3 amendment. In\n1175:             # particular control (e) SEED-COUNT PARITY is NOT edited: the\n1176:             # 25-seed extension is argued a fortiori from (e)'s own stated\n1177:             # rationale in the appended item (g), per CR-1 COND-4.\n1178:     - >-\n1179:       (a) BLIND RE-DERIVATION CONTROL (REQUIRED, frozen): see\n1180:       `blind_rederivation`. No cell is evidence before the seal exists.\n1181:     - >-\n1182:       (b) a = 1/4 REPLICATION CONTROL: T_sel = T/2 at a = 1/4, r = 2,\n1183:       N = 2^24 is ALREADY established as G3-INFEASIBLE (G3 FAIL 10/10 seeds,\n1184:       EV-ECDLP-60e266). This contract's own fresh 5 seeds at a = 1/4 must\n1185:       reproduce that FAIL. A PASS here at a = 1/4 invalidates this batch's\n1186:       instrument (see `invalidation_rules`), independent of any other cell's\n1187:       result.\n1188:     - >-\n1189:       (c) EXACT-COVERAGE NON-EXCEEDANCE: no exact top-T_sel share may exceed\n1190:       1.0 or the exact top-T share (T > T_sel); an exceedance is an\n1191:       implementation error, not a result (mirrors v1/v2's own structural\n1192:       tell).\n1193:     - >-\n1194:       (d) DEFINITIONAL IDENTITY WITH THE v2 G3 RULE: the feasibility\n1195:       criterion applied here is REUSED VERBATIM from\n1196:       experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/specification.v2.yaml\n1197:       `inputs.g3_gate_procedure`, not re-derived or re-worded, specifically\n1198:       to rule out a units/definition mismatch as the source of any\n1199:       confirmed discrepancy (this contract's own outcome (b) names that\n1200:       possibility explicitly and this control is what would surface it).\n1201:     - >-\n1202:       (e) SEED-COUNT PARITY: 5 seeds per a, matching Stage 0's and v2's own\n1203:       seed count, so this batch's statistical power is comparable, not\n1204:       thinner, than the batch that produced the original discrepancy.\n1205:     - >-\n1206:       (f) [v2 AMENDMENT, ADDITIVE] SELECTION-FORMULA IDENTITY: the re-sealed\n1207:       a = 1/8 blind re-derivation required by\n1208:       `blind_rederivation.v2_rerequirement_a_1_8` must apply EXACTLY the\n1209:       `STATIC(T)_r pool-selection weight formula (v2 amendment item 1)`\n1210:       stated in `definitions` above, with no further drift or\n1211:       reinterpretation; a re-seal that silently applies yet a third,\n1212:       different reading of \"the published Bernstein-Lange weight\" would\n1213:       repeat, not resolve, the underspecification this amendment exists to\n1214:       close.\n1215:     - >-\n1216:       (g) [v3 AMENDMENT, ADDITIVE] SEED-COUNT PARITY EXTENSION.\n1217:       CONTROL (e) IS QUOTED HERE IN FULL AND IS NOT EDITED: \"(e) SEED-COUNT\n1218:       PARITY: 5 seeds per a, matching Stage 0's and v2's own seed count, so\n1219:       this batch's statistical power is comparable, not thinner, than the\n1220:       batch that produced the original discrepancy.\"\n1221:       THE ARGUMENT, FROM (e)'S OWN STATED RATIONALE: (e) exists to protect a\n1222:       property it names explicitly -- power \"comparable, not thinner\" than\n1223:       the batch that produced the original discrepancy. v3 runs 25 seeds per\n1224:       (N, a), the same integer-seeded streams by the same construction, so\n1225:       the power is STRICTLY GREATER and never thinner. (e) is therefore\n1226:       satisfied A FORTIORI, not overridden.\n1227:       THE AUTHORITY GAP, STATED RATHER THAN PAPERED OVER: the seed set is the\n1228:       one wide-scope item the approved contract's `invalidation_rules` item 7\n1229:       does NOT name, so item 7 confers no authority over it. The warrant used\n1230:       here is (e)'s own rationale, which is WEAKER than item 7 and is recorded\n1231:       as such. A gate that rejects this reading should say so; the fallback\n1232:       needing no new warrant is to run seeds 1..5 only, which costs the wide\n1233:       scope its power.\n1234:       THE CONTROL ITSELF FIRES WHEN: the 25-seed reading and the seeds 1..5\n1235:       subgroup reading are composited into one number anywhere; or the\n1236:       subgroup reading is omitted; or fewer than 25 of the pre-registered\n1237:       seeds are run at a cell whose verdict is reported; or the seed set\n1238:       differs between the two readings or between any treatment and control\n1239:       arm.\n1240:     - >-\n1241:       (h) [v3 AMENDMENT, ADDITIVE] CROSS-SCALE REPRODUCTION CONTROL, anchored\n1242:       at N = 2^24 where a committed reference exists.\n1243:       THE CHECK: at N = 2^24, a in {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4}, seeds 1..5, the\n1244:       PRODUCTION reading's exact top-T_sel share, STATIC(T)_{r=2} exact\n1245:       coverage and margin must each equal the committed value in the\n1246:       corresponding RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-001..005 summary.json to within 1e-9\n1247:       ABSOLUTE. A larger deviation FIRES THIS CONTROL.\n1248:       IT DOES NOT RE-SCORE THE COMMITTED RUNS. They are the REFERENCE, never\n1249:       the subject: no byte under experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/runs/ is read\n1250:       for anything but comparison, and none is written. This is the binding\n1251:       condition of `invalidation_rules` item 7 (\"runs already executed are\n1252:       never re-scored\") and it is honoured exactly.\n1253:       THE TOLERANCE IS NOT INVENTED: the independent gate that refused this\n1254:       contract's predecessor draft reproduced all three quantities at all 20\n1255:       committed cells from the pinned instrument to a WORST ABSOLUTE\n1256:       DEVIATION OF 0.000e+00, so the target is known achievable and a nonzero\n1257:       residual is a real signal rather than a tolerance artifact.\n1258:       THE 1e-9 TOLERANCE APPLIES TO THE PRODUCTION READING ONLY, where the\n1259:       tie-break key stream is identical by construction. It does NOT apply to\n1260:       the blind reading, whose key stream necessarily differs (see (o) and\n1261:       `definitions` item on the tie-break).\n1262:       WHAT \"CROSS-SCALE\" MEANS HERE, STATED PLAINLY BECAUSE IT IS A\n1263:       DELIBERATE NARROWING: this contract spans two scales, and the\n1264:       reproduction anchor sits at the scale that HAS committed cells. AT\n1265:       N = 2^20 THERE IS NO REFERENCE -- this experiment has never run there --\n1266:       so v3 reads a CROSS-SCALE CONSISTENCY comparison at N = 2^20 and\n1267:       declares it EXPLICITLY NOT A CONTROL: it has nothing to pass or fail\n1268:       against. Inventing a reference there would have been a fabrication.\n1269:     - >-\n1270:       (i) [v3 AMENDMENT, ADDITIVE] NULL-ORACLE-RAND (UNIFORM) -- THE GATING\n1271:       NULL OBJECT. Discharges non-blocking defect D7.\n1272:       THE NULL: replace the ORACLE side of the comparison -- the top-T_sel\n1273:       basins by TRUE SIZE over the whole exact partition -- by a UNIFORMLY\n1274:       RANDOM T_sel-subset of the DPs of the SAME enumerated partition. Hold\n1275:       cov_static fixed, read the coverage of the random subset off the SAME\n1276:       basin-size array by the SAME arithmetic, and form\n1277:       margin_null = (random subset's exact coverage) - cov_static.\n1278:       ONE SUBSTITUTION, SAME UNIVERSE, SAME READ-OFF, SAME PREDICATE. This is\n1279:       what D7 asked for: the refused draft's null changed the selection rule\n1280:       AND the universe (its arm ranged over the r*T pool while the real arm\n1281:       ranges over the whole partition), so its guaranteed negativity was\n1282:       bought largely by the universe change and the size ratio rather than by\n1283:       the weight carrying information.\n1284:       IT FIRES WHEN: margin_null(s) >= 0 in more than 1 of the 25 seeds at\n1285:       any (N, a) cell, or the reported MEAN margin_null is non-negative at\n1286:       any cell.\n1287:       WHY ITS CONCLUSION IS KNOWN FALSE BY ARGUMENT, NOT BY DATA: cov_static\n1288:       is the exact coverage of T = 2*T_sel pool entries selected by\n1289:       weight_d = S_d + 4*W*h_d, and both factors of that weight increase with\n1290:       basin size for a structural reason -- a DP with a larger basin is\n1291:       reached by MORE uniform-restart pool walks (larger h_d) and those walks\n1292:       start from a larger set of points (larger S_d) -- while the pool itself\n1293:       over-samples large basins, since a DP enters it only when some restart\n1294:       walk reaches it. A UNIFORMLY random T_sel-subset of all DPs has by\n1295:       construction NO correlation with basin size: its expected mass is T_sel\n1296:       times the MEAN basin mass over a DP set of size order N/W, the\n1297:       overwhelming majority of whose basins are small. So margin_null must be\n1298:       negative. NO COMMITTED NUMBER IS USED IN THIS ARGUMENT AND NONE IS\n1299:       ASSERTED BY IT -- which is exactly why the control is falsifiable: a\n1300:       structural argument can be wrong.\n1301:     - >-\n1302:       (j) [v3 AMENDMENT, ADDITIVE] NULL-ORACLE-RAND (SIZE-BIASED) --\n1303:       DIAGNOSTIC ONLY, GATES NOTHING.\n1304:       Same substitution as (i) but with the T_sel-subset drawn with\n1305:       probability proportional to basin size. ITS DIRECTION IS DECLARED\n1306:       UNPREDICTABLE IN ADVANCE and no verdict depends on it: a size-biased\n1307:       draw is deliberately competitive with the oracle, and this contract\n1308:       cannot honestly pre-register which way it falls. Reported because the\n1309:       GAP between (i) and (j) measures how much of the oracle's advantage is\n1310:       size-correlation alone -- which is informative -- and fenced off from\n1311:       every verdict because a control whose direction cannot be stated in\n1312:       advance is not a control.\n1313:     - >-\n1314:       (k) [v3 AMENDMENT, ADDITIVE] NULL-RANDSEL -- RETAINED, NON-GATING, LOW\n1315:       POWER DISCLOSED IN THE CONTRACT.\n1316:       THE NULL: replace weight_d selection by a uniformly random T-subset of\n1317:       the r*T POOL, and compare the top-T_sel share against that random\n1318:       selection's coverage.\n1319:       IT FIRES WHEN: margin_null_pool(s) >= 0 in more than 1 of the 25 seeds\n1320:       at any cell.\n1321:       ITS POWER IS LOW AND THAT IS STATED HERE RATHER THAN LEFT FOR A\n1322:       REVIEWER TO DISCOVER: the independent gate recomputed this quantity on\n1323:       the committed cells and found it one to two orders of magnitude beyond\n1324:       its own declared firing threshold at every cell, because its arm ranges\n1325:       over the r*T pool while the real arm ranges over the whole partition\n1326:       (D7). It CAN fire, but on nothing short of a gross defect. RETAINED as\n1327:       a check on the weight ESTIMATOR specifically -- which is what it is\n1328:       genuinely shaped for -- and DEMOTED from gating to reported.\n1329:     - >-\n1330:       (l) [v3 AMENDMENT, ADDITIVE] DECAY-A -- THE DECLARED DECAY CONTROL, AND\n1331:       THIS BATCH'S LOAD-BEARING ARTIFACT DETECTOR. Declared decay parameter:\n1332:       a. Rationale: docs/inventor-protocol.md \"controls before belief\" -- a\n1333:       quantity that fails to decay when the parameter meant to destroy it\n1334:       increases is the canonical artifact tell.\n1335:       CLAUSE (i) MONOTONE DECAY, BINDING: the mean margin over the 25 seeds\n1336:       must be STRICTLY DECREASING across a = 1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4 at each N\n1337:       separately. A SINGLE non-monotone step fires it.\n1338:       CLAUSE (ii) PAIRED DIFFERENCES, CONTEXT ONLY, BINDS NOTHING: the paired\n1339:       per-seed differences between adjacent a-values, reported with their\n1340:       percentile intervals. Reported for interpretation; no verdict and no\n1341:       other clause depends on it, per `definitions` item on the interval\n1342:       estimator (D5).\n1343:       CLAUSE (iii) EXTERNAL ANCHOR, BINDING, AND THE ONLY CLAUSE ANCHORED\n1344:       OUTSIDE THIS BATCH: at a = 1/4, the mean margin must be NEGATIVE and\n1345:       the pass-count k must be at most 5 of 25. The anchor is\n1346:       EV-ECDLP-60e266's independently established a = 1/4 G3-infeasibility --\n1347:       a result of a DIFFERENT batch, cited and never re-scored here.\n1348:       WHY CLAUSE (i) IS NOT AN IDENTITY: each a is a DIFFERENT INSTRUMENT,\n1349:       with its own W, DP rate, cap, and basin partition. No arithmetic\n1350:       relates the four means, so a correct implementation can produce a\n1351:       non-monotone sequence.\n1352:       WHY CLAUSE (iii) CARRIES THE LOAD: it is the one clause a\n1353:       self-consistent but WRONG implementation cannot pass automatically,\n1354:       because its reference is external to everything this batch computes.\n1355:     - >-\n1356:       (m) [v3 AMENDMENT, ADDITIVE] DECAY-TSEL -- SECOND DECAY CONTROL, WEAKER\n1357:       THAN (l), WEAKNESS DISCLOSED, AND WITH THE PREVIOUS GATE'S TAUTOLOGICAL\n1358:       CLAUSE DELIBERATELY NOT REINTRODUCED.\n1359:       CLAUSE (i) BINDING: at T_sel = T/8, margin(s) >= 0 in more than 1 of the\n1360:       25 seeds at any a fires this control.\n1361:       RE-CHECKED AGAINST THE CODE RATHER THAN CARRIED ON TRUST: cov_static is\n1362:       a function of the T weight-selected pool entries and is INDEPENDENT of\n1363:       T_sel (experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/source/run_stageb.py line 96\n1364:       selects T, never T_sel), while share_top(T/8) is a strict prefix of\n1365:       share_top(T/2). NOTHING in either expression forces\n1366:       share_top(T/8) < cov_static, so the clause is NOT an identity and can\n1367:       fail on a correct implementation. What it detects: a T/8-entry oracle\n1368:       table already matching STATIC(T)'s coverage, i.e. a comparison that is\n1369:       not measuring stored-advice efficiency at all but is an\n1370:       everything-passes artifact.\n1371:       CLAUSE (ii) BINDING, WEAK: rho_ORACLE must be non-decreasing in a at\n1372:       each N. Not forced by arithmetic, but on the read grid\n1373:       {1/8, 1/4, 1/2} rho_ORACLE takes few values, so this is effectively a\n1374:       COARSE ordering check on the same directional claim (l) makes.\n1375:       DISCLOSED, not hidden.\n1376:       ITS POWER IS LOW AND THAT IS STATED: the independent gate found clause\n1377:       (i) comfortably satisfied on every committed cell.\n1378:       THE CLAUSE THE PREVIOUS GATE CORRECTLY REMOVED IS NOT REINTRODUCED:\n1379:       margin(T/2) > margin(T/4) > margin(T/8) holds BY ARITHMETIC on every\n1380:       correct implementation, because the three share_top values are nested\n1381:       prefixes of one descending sort while cov_static is common to all\n1382:       three. It appears in this contract ONLY inside item (o), labelled a\n1383:       structural self-check, and never as a control.\n1384:     - >-\n1385:       (n) [v3 AMENDMENT, ADDITIVE] NULL-SHUF -- DIAGNOSTIC, EXPLICITLY NOT A\n1386:       G3 NULL, AND DECLARED UNUSABLE AS ONE IN THE CONTRACT RATHER THAN\n1387:       QUIETLY DROPPED.\n1388:       Permuting basin sizes across the pool's DPs, holding the size multiset\n1389:       and the weights fixed, makes cov_static COLLAPSE -- which makes G3 pass\n1390:       MORE easily. THAT IS THE WRONG DIRECTION FOR A FEASIBILITY NULL:\n1391:       carrying it as one would mean carrying a control that fires in the\n1392:       direction of the claim, which is worse than having no null at all.\n1393:       NOTHING GATES ON IT. It is retained and reported because the collapse\n1394:       itself is informative about whether weight_d carries basin-size\n1395:       information, and it is fenced off from every verdict, every clause and\n1396:       every agreement test.\n1397:     - >-\n1398:       (o) [v3 AMENDMENT, ADDITIVE] STRUCTURAL SELF-CHECKS -- NOT CONTROLS,\n1399:       AND LABELLED SO DELIBERATELY.\n1400:       Each item below CANNOT FAIL on a correct implementation, so its passing\n1401:       means nothing beyond \"no defect of this kind\". Calling any of them a\n1402:       control would repeat exactly the vacuity the independent gate correctly\n1403:       removed from a DECAY-TSEL clause of the refused draft, and this contract\n1404:       does not do that.\n1405:       (o1) BASIN-MASS ACCOUNTING: sum_d b(d) + cycle_mass + capped_mass = N\n1406:       EXACTLY, in integer arithmetic, with ZERO tolerance, at every cell of\n1407:       BOTH readings; and b(d) >= 1 for every DP d. Cannot fail because the\n1408:       three classes are disjoint and exhaustive by construction (see\n1409:       `definitions` item 2). It fires exactly when a reading implements no\n1410:       cap, or assigns residual mass to a basin, or double-counts -- which is\n1411:       D2's failure mode and the reason the check exists.\n1412:       (o2) EXACT-COVERAGE NESTING: share_top(T/8) <= share_top(T/4) <=\n1413:       share_top(T/2) <= share_top(T) <= 1.0, and cov_static <= share_top(T).\n1414:       Cannot fail: nested prefixes of a descending sort of non-negative basin\n1415:       sizes, and an exact coverage of T DPs that cannot exceed the T largest\n1416:       basins. THIS SUBSUMES v2's CONTROL (c), which is retained above\n1417:       verbatim and unedited; (o2) records honestly that (c) is an identity\n1418:       rather than a control.\n1419:       (o3) MARGIN NESTING IN T_sel: margin(T/2) > margin(T/4) > margin(T/8)\n1420:       at every cell. Cannot fail, for the reason given in item (m): this is\n1421:       the clause the previous gate removed, kept here ONLY as a self-check.\n1422:       A VIOLATION OF ANY OF (o1)-(o3) IS AN IMPLEMENTATION ERROR AND STOPS\n1423:       THE CELL AS completed_invalid (see `stopping_rules`), never folded into\n1424:       a pass-count.\n1425: \n1426:   controls_falsifiability_summary: >-\n1427:     REQUIRED READING FOR THE GATE, and the honest power gradient of this\n1428:     batch. Of the fifteen declared items: ELEVEN are controls with a\n1429:     reachable failing world on a correct implementation -- (a), (b), (d), (e),\n1430:     (f), (g), (h), (i), (k), (l), (m); THREE are structural self-checks and\n1431:     are labelled as such rather than as controls -- (c) (retained verbatim\n1432:     from v2, honestly re-described in (o2)), and (o1)-(o3); and TWO are\n1433:     diagnostics explicitly fenced off from every verdict -- (j) and (n).\n1434:     THE LOAD IS NOT EVENLY DISTRIBUTED, and pretending otherwise would be\n1435:     the defect: control (l) clause (iii) is the ONLY clause anchored OUTSIDE\n1436:     this batch and carries most of the artifact-detection load; control (i)\n1437:     is the shape-matched gating null that D7 asked for; controls (k) and (m)\n1438:     are corroboration with DISCLOSED low power; control (h) is the sharpest\n1439:     check available on pipeline identity, because its target is known\n1440:     achievable to 0.000e+00.\n1441: \n1442:   independent_variables: # v2's list, retained verbatim; it governs the N = 2^24 arm\n1443:     - \"N: fixed, 2^24\"\n1444:     - \"a: {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4}\"\n1445:     - \"r: fixed, 2\"\n1446:     - \"T_sel: fixed, T/2 = 128\"\n1447:     - \"seed: {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}\"\n1448:     - \"reading: {blind (Stage A), production (Stage B/C)}\"\n1449:   independent_variables_v3: # ADDITIVE; the operative grid for v3 runs\n1450:     - \"N: {2^20, 2^24} -- two scales; v2's 'fixed, 2^24' entry above is retained verbatim and remains the description of the arm it governs\"\n1451:     - \"a: {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4} -- UNCHANGED from v2\"\n1452:     - \"r: fixed, 2 -- UNCHANGED from v2\"\n1453:     - \"T_sel: fixed at T/2 (= 32 at N = 2^20, = 128 at N = 2^24); T/4 and T/8 additionally READ for control (m) only\"\n1454:     - \"seed: {1, ..., 25}; the subgroup {1, 2, 3, 4, 5} is reported separately and is the only seed set control (h) reproduces against\"\n1455:     - \"reading: {blind (Stage A''), production (Stage B''/C'')}\"\n1456:     - \"control arm: {primary, NULL-ORACLE-RAND uniform, NULL-ORACLE-RAND size-biased, NULL-RANDSEL, NULL-SHUF}\"\n1457:   independent_variables_v3_note: >-\n1458:     THE TWO LISTS ARE NOT IN CONFLICT AND NEITHER IS EDITED. v2's list stays\n1459:     byte-identical and continues to describe the arm v1 executed and v2\n1460:     governs. `independent_variables_v3` is the grid for runs executed under\n1461:     THIS contract, once and if it is approved. Where they differ (N, seed,\n1462:     T_sel readings, control arms), the v3 list governs v3 runs and the v2\n1463:     list governs nothing new.\n1464: \n1465:   metrics:\n1466:     primary: # CR-1 COND-3: REPRODUCED BYTE-IDENTICALLY FROM THE APPROVED v2. NOT EDITED.\n1467:       - \"per (a, seed): exact top-T_sel basin share minus STATIC(T)_{r=2} exact coverage (the G3-style margin); sign and magnitude\"\n1468:       - \"per a: pass-count out of 5 seeds (margin >= 0); G3-style feasibility verdict (>= 4/5 -> FEASIBLE, else INFEASIBLE)\"\n1469:       - \"crossing bracket: the pair of adjacent a-grid values straddling the FEASIBLE/INFEASIBLE boundary, per `definitions.crossing point`\"\n1470:       - \"blind-vs-production agreement per (a, seed): same sign, margins within the two readings' own seed-to-seed noise; and per-a agreement on the pass-count/verdict\"\n1471:       - \"a = 1/4 replication control: pass-count out of 5 seeds, compared against EV-ECDLP-60e266's 5/5 FAIL at 2^24\"\n1472:     secondary:\n1473:       - \"exact top-T_sel share and STATIC(T)_{r=2} exact coverage individually, per (a, seed), for auditability\"\n1474:       - \"wall clock and peak RSS per run, for budget accounting only\"\n1475:     primary_v3_additions: # ADDITIVE; `primary` above is untouched, per CR-1 COND-3\n1476:       - \"per (N, a, seed): the G3-style margin, at BOTH scales, over the 25 pre-registered seeds\"\n1477:       - \"per (N, a): pass-count k out of 25 (margin >= 0), and the G3-style feasibility verdict by the SAME >= 4/5 proportional rule applied to 25 seeds (i.e. k >= 20); the seeds 1..5 subgroup's own pass-count out of 5 by v2's rule verbatim, reported SEPARATELY and never composited\"\n1478:       - \"per (N, a): mean margin over the 25 seeds and its SIGN -- the second of the two quantities blind-versus-production agreement is judged on\"\n1479:       - \"per (N, a): the percentile bootstrap interval of the mean margin, used ONLY to route a cell to SU; BCa reported beside it as context, gating nothing\"\n1480:       - \"per (N, a): cycle_mass, capped_mass, capped_walks and residual_fraction = (cycle_mass + capped_mass)/N, in BOTH readings, with the accounting identity's exact satisfaction recorded\"\n1481:       - \"per (N, a): the number of pool entries TIED at the T-th largest weight, and the cardinality of the symmetric difference of the two readings' Sel_static sets\"\n1482:       - \"per (N, a): margin_null for NULL-ORACLE-RAND (uniform, gating), its size-biased variant (diagnostic), NULL-RANDSEL (non-gating) and NULL-SHUF (diagnostic), each over the same 25 seeds\"\n1483:       - \"per (N, a): rho_ORACLE and the T/4 and T/8 top-share readings that control (m) evaluates\"\n1484:       - \"per control: FIRED or NOT FIRED, with the exact quantity and cell it was read from -- a control whose outcome is not reported counts as not run, not as passed\"\n1485:     metrics_v3_note: >-\n1486:       THE VERDICT-BEARING METRICS ARE RESAMPLING-FREE BY DESIGN. The\n1487:       pass-count k is an integer and the sign of the mean margin is a sign;\n1488:       two independent implementations compute both identically or differ for\n1489:       a reason about the quantity. The only bootstrap in this contract routes\n1490:       to SU and gates nothing. This is D5's discharge, and it is why an\n1491:       interval-method disagreement between the two readings is reported as\n1492:       interval-method sensitivity rather than as S3.\n1493: \n1494:   heuristic_under_test: null\n1495:   heuristic_note: >-\n1496:     UNCHANGED from v1/v2: this contract does not validate or re-validate\n1497:     HEUR-BLT-1/2/7; it is a direct exact-enumeration measurement. HEUR-BLT-1\n1498:     (the random-function basin law) is the same standing assumption\n1499:     EXP-ECDLP-869870 and EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 already carry; nothing here adds to\n1500:     or subtracts from its own validation status. v3 ADDS NO HEURISTIC: the cap\n1501:     convention is not a heuristic but a stated implementation convention, and\n1502:     the structural argument for control (i)'s known-false direction is an\n1503:     argument about that convention's consequences, not a numbered heuristic\n1504:     this contract asks anyone to accept.\n1505: \n1506:   preregistered_prediction:\n1507:     deviation_declared: >-\n1508:       THIS IS THE ONE FIELD v3 DOES NOT RESTATE VERBATIM, AND THE DEVIATION\n1509:       IS DECLARED RATHER THAN QUIET. It is NOT one of the fields CR-1 COND-3\n1510:       pins verbatim (those are `success_criterion` S1/S2/S3 and\n1511:       `metrics.primary`, both reproduced byte-identically above).\n1512:       WHY: the approved v2's `preregistered_prediction` states DIRECTIONAL\n1513:       EXPECTATIONS AND PER-SEED MARGIN VALUES at a = 1/16, a = 1/8 and\n1514:       a = 3/16. Restating them inline here would put a directional prior with\n1515:       numbers into the contract text -- the same class of leak as D3, in the\n1516:       one document a re-deriver is most likely to reach for. So v3 carries\n1517:       the v1/v2 prediction BY REFERENCE and records its own additions in a\n1518:       sealed file off the reading path.\n1519:     v1_v2_prediction_retained_by_reference: >-\n1520:       UNCHANGED AND STILL ON THE RECORD, at\n1521:       experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml\n1522:       `preregistered_prediction` (itself byte-identical to v1's). It is\n1523:       committed, immutable and timestamped before v1's Stage B/C ran, so its\n1524:       pre-registration is intact and is not weakened by being cited rather\n1525:       than copied. v3 does not restate, revise, retract or re-score it.\n1526:     quantity: >-\n1527:       G3-style feasibility verdict (per `definitions`) at each a in\n1528:       {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4}, at N = 2^20 and at N = 2^24, r = 2,\n1529:       T_sel = T/2, over the 25 pre-registered seeds; plus the crossing\n1530:       bracket at each scale.\n1531:     v3_prediction_location:\n1532:       path: coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-48ef8b/priors/coordinator_prior.SEALED.yaml\n1533:       what_is_there: >-\n1534:         The authoring Coordinator's expectation for the cells v3 adds, and its\n1535:         expectation of what the approval gate will find. Written and committed\n1536:         at lane opening, BEFORE any reviewer or re-deriver runs, which is what\n1537:         AGENTS.md \"Review architecture\" requires and why the prior is kept\n1538:         rather than deleted.\n1539:       why_not_here: >-\n1540:         Because a prior in the contract is a prior on the re-deriver's most\n1541:         natural reading path. The sealed file is NOT in the derivation packet,\n1542:         so under the allowlist it is unreadable before the seal without an\n1543:         explicit violation, and it is named on the corroborating denylist.\n\n(Output capped at 50 KB. Showing lines 797-1543. Use offset=1544 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"      from reading `specification.v3.yaml` at all. The leaked text itself\n      remains verbatim in `objective_v3_r2`, unredacted and unmoved -- this\n      paragraph discloses its existence and location, it does not repair\n      it.\n\n  instrument: >-\n    IDENTICAL to experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/specification.v2.yaml\n    `instrument.generic_walk` and `inputs.exact_basins`, reused verbatim\n    (f(x) = mix64(x XOR K) mod N, DP predicate hash64(x) < floor(2^64 / W)\n    with an independent key; exact-basin enumeration procedure unchanged\n    from v1). No curve arm (generic instrument only; certificate kind:\n    none). The PRODUCTION computation (Stage B below) may reuse\n    experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/source_v2/'s exact-basin code by explicit\n    citation in its manifest (commit-pinned); the REQUIRED blind\n    re-derivation (Stage A) may NOT (see `blind_rederivation.blind_from`).\n  instrument_v3_note: >-\n    UNCHANGED, and now stated as formulas rather than by name: the DP\n    predicate's floor and independent-key derivation, the walk cap, and the\n    exact-basin residual accounting are given explicitly in `definitions`\n    items 1, 2 and 3 above. This is not a change of instrument -- it is the","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml","text":"      from reading `specification.v3.yaml` at all. The leaked text itself\n      remains verbatim in `objective_v3_r2`, unredacted and unmoved -- this\n      paragraph discloses its existence and location, it does not repair\n      it.\n\n  instrument: >-\n    IDENTICAL to experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/specification.v2.yaml\n    `instrument.generic_walk` and `inputs.exact_basins`, reused verbatim\n    (f(x) = mix64(x XOR K) mod N, DP predicate hash64(x) < floor(2^64 / W)\n    with an independent key; exact-basin enumeration procedure unchanged\n    from v1). No curve arm (generic instrument only; certificate kind:\n    none). The PRODUCTION computation (Stage B below) may reuse\n    experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/source_v2/'s exact-basin code by explicit\n    citation in its manifest (commit-pinned); the REQUIRED blind\n    re-derivation (Stage A) may NOT (see `blind_rederivation.blind_from`).\n  instrument_v3_note: >-\n    UNCHANGED, and now stated as formulas rather than by name: the DP\n    predicate's floor and independent-key derivation, the walk cap, and the\n    exact-basin residual accounting are given explicitly in `definitions`\n    items 1, 2 and 3 above. This is not a change of instrument -- it is the\n    same commit-pinned instrument, with the conventions it has always\n    implemented now derivable from the contract's own text. THE PRODUCTION\n    READING MUST REUSE THE PINNED INSTRUMENT and cite its commit in the\n    manifest; THE BLIND READING MUST NOT OPEN IT before its seal (the\n    allowlist in `blind_rederivation.v3_derivation_packet` does not contain\n    it, and `blind_from` continues to name it).\n\n  inputs:\n    stage_plan: >-\n      UNCHANGED from v1/v2 for the already-executed work, retained by\n      reference so no sentence drifts: see\n      experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml `inputs.stage_plan`\n      for Stage A (the original blind re-derivation), Stage B (v1's executed\n      exact-basin generation at N = 2^24, 5 seeds) and Stage C (v1's\n      analysis). Stage B/C is ALREADY COMPLETE (RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-001..006,\n      6/6 completed_valid), is NOT re-run by this contract, and is NEVER\n      re-scored under it.\n    stage_plan_v3: >-\n      v3's OWN STAGES. Three, and the first must be sealed before the second\n      is opened by the same agent.\n\n      STAGE A'' (BLIND RE-DERIVATION, REQUIRED, NON-NEGOTIABLE). A designated\n      independent agent, in a session that authored none of this contract's\n      artifacts, implements the quantity from scratch and SEALS it. ITS ENTIRE\n      PERMITTED READING BEFORE THE SEAL IS THE ENUMERATED DERIVATION PACKET\n      (`blind_rederivation.v3_derivation_packet`) -- not this contract, not\n      the amendment, not a handoff, not a task card, not a queue, not a\n      decision, not a run, not a commit message. Grid: both scales, all four\n      a, all 25 seeds. Deliverables per (N, a, seed): exact top-T_sel basin\n      share, STATIC(T)_{r=2} exact coverage, margin, cycle_mass, capped_mass,\n      capped_walks, residual_fraction, and the count of pool entries tied at\n      the T-th largest weight. Per (N, a): pass-count k out of 25, mean\n      margin and its sign, the percentile interval, and the same for the\n      seeds 1..5 subgroup reported separately.\n\n      STAGE B'' (PRODUCTION, exact-basin generation). The commit-pinned\n      instrument, cited by commit in every manifest. N in {2^20, 2^24};\n      a_grid = {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4}; r = 2; T_sel = T/2 (32 and 128); seeds\n      1..25. Zero online re-selected (RESEL-L) arms -- this is an\n      exact-enumeration measurement only, as in v1. Same per-cell deliverable\n      list as Stage A''. Additionally, the control arms: NULL-ORACLE-RAND\n      (uniform) as the gating null, its size-biased variant as a diagnostic,\n      NULL-RANDSEL retained non-gating, NULL-SHUF as a fenced-off diagnostic,\n      and the T/4 and T/8 readings that control (l) needs. THE N = 2^20 ARM\n      RUNS FIRST, because it is roughly 16x cheaper and shakes the pipeline\n      out before the expensive scale.\n\n      STAGE C'' (ANALYSIS). Apply the G3-style feasibility criterion at each\n      (N, a) to BOTH readings independently. Evaluate the a = 1/4 cell FIRST.\n      Evaluate every control and report each as fired or not fired, with the\n      quantity it was read from. Compare the two readings on (k, sign of mean\n      margin), per (N, a); route to SU where the routing rule applies; report\n      the crossing bracket at each scale, or report plainly that no clean\n      crossing is confirmed. Report the seeds 1..5 subgroup separately from\n      the 25-seed reading and NEVER composite them. Report the\n      tie-break-induced symmetric difference of the two Sel_static sets, and\n      the residual-mass accounting identity's exact satisfaction, per cell of\n      both readings.\n    arms: >-\n      UNCHANGED from v1/v2 for the primary reading, verbatim in substance:\n      two exact-coverage readings only per (a, seed) -- STATIC(T)_{r=2} exact\n      coverage, and the exact top-T_sel basin share. No ORACLE, RESEL-L,\n      NULL-A, CAP, RHO, or STATIC2T arm is run; those test the re-selection\n      MECHANISM (already the subject of EXP-ECDLP-612fb1) and remain out of\n      scope for this narrow ceiling-feasibility check (see `out_of_scope`).\n    arms_v3_addition: >-\n      v3 ADDS CONTROL ARMS ONLY, all read off the SAME exact basin partition\n      as the primary arms, none of them an online re-selection batch:\n      (i) NULL-ORACLE-RAND (uniform), the gating null: the ORACLE side is\n      replaced by a uniformly random T_sel-subset of the DPs of the SAME\n      enumerated partition, cov_static held fixed and read off identically;\n      (ii) NULL-ORACLE-RAND (size-biased), diagnostic only, direction\n      declared unpredictable in advance; (iii) NULL-RANDSEL, retained,\n      non-gating, low power disclosed; (iv) NULL-SHUF, diagnostic, explicitly\n      not a G3 null; (v) the T/4 and T/8 top-share readings control (l)\n      needs. The primary arm count per cell is unchanged.\n    exact_basins: \"unchanged from v1/v2, verbatim, restricted to N = 2^24 and the a_grid above.\"\n    exact_basins_v3_addition: >-\n      Same procedure, unchanged, now run at N = 2^20 as well, and now with\n      the cap and residual accounting stated in `definitions` items 1 and 2\n      rather than left implicit. cycle_mass, capped_mass and\n      residual_fraction are REQUIRED OUTPUTS of every exact-basin\n      enumeration under this contract, in both readings.\n\n  blind_rederivation:\n    required: true\n    frozen: true\n    quantity: >-\n      exact top-T_sel (= T/2) basin share and STATIC(T)_{r=2} exact coverage\n      at each a in {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4}, N = 2^24, from the exact\n      basin-partition definition alone (a uniformly random function on N\n      points truncated at an independent Bernoulli(1/W) marking, per\n      HEUR-BLT-1) -- NOT a re-read of any run's own analysis output and NOT\n      an inspection of experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/source_v2/'s\n      implementation before the seal.\n    parameters: \"N = 2^24; a_grid = {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4}; r = 2; T_sel = T/2 = 128; 5 seeds\"\n    procedure: >-\n      A designated independent reviewer (validator or, if none is assigned,\n      the executor acting under a strict pre-registration discipline)\n      writes their own from-scratch computation of the quantity above, SEALS\n      it (commits it to their own task directory with a hash and timestamp,\n      exactly as TASK-20260906-bc1cfc's J2 sealed its result before opening\n      any run artifact), and ONLY THEN opens: (i) this experiment's own\n      Stage B/C run output, (ii) the original EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 v2 Stage 0\n      a-scan data that produced the discrepancy. The sealed file and its\n      hash/timestamp are a REQUIRED artifact (see `required_artifacts`).\n    blind_from:\n      - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/source_v2/\n      - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/runs/RUN-ECDLP-612fb1-v2-ascan-*/\n      - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/runs/RUN-ECDLP-612fb1-v2-analysis-001/\n      - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/runs/ (this experiment's own outputs, once they exist)\n    comparison_rule: >-\n      The blind result and Stage B/C's production result are compared cell\n      by cell (per a). Agreement (same PASS/FAIL pattern, margins within\n      seed-to-seed noise) is required before ANY cell's G3-style verdict is\n      reported as more than a single, unreviewed reading; disagreement is\n      itself the headline result of this batch (see `distinguishable_outcomes`\n      (b)) and is never resolved by picking one side without a stated,\n      checkable reason (e.g. a demonstrated units/definition mismatch).\n    non_negotiable_note: >-\n      This step exists BECAUSE the discrepancy this contract investigates\n      was itself found by re-reading the same executor table twice by two\n      different arithmetic routes, not by an independent from-scratch\n      computation -- DEC-20260906-bcc097's RANK 1 explicitly requires the\n      latter. A run set completed without a sealed blind re-derivation is\n      NOT evidence under this contract (see `invalidation_rules`).\n    v2_rerequirement_a_1_8: # ADDITIVE, v2 amendment item 2 -- everything above this key is BYTE-IDENTICAL to v1\n      status: REQUIRED, scoped narrowly to the single a = 1/8 cell\n      trigger: >-\n        TASK-20260907-80e198's sealed Stage A blind re-derivation (5/5\n        seeds at a = 1/16, 0/5 at a = 3/16, 0/5 at a = 1/4, 1/5 at a = 1/8)\n        used an oracle true-exact-basin-size STATIC(T)_r selection because\n        v1's `definitions` underspecified the weight formula. Only the\n        a = 1/8 cell's PASS/FAIL VERDICT actually flips between the oracle\n        rule and the now-explicit `STATIC(T)_r pool-selection weight\n        formula` (a = 1/16 and a = 1/4 are robust to the choice of rule per\n        `postseal_diagnostic_v2_clean.py`'s own controlled result; a = 3/16\n        moves from 0/5 to 2/5 but remains solidly G3-INFEASIBLE by the\n        >= 4/5 threshold either way, so it does not need re-sealing).\n      scope: >-\n        ONLY the a = 1/8 cell (N = 2^24, r = 2, T_sel = T/2 = 128, 5 seeds)\n        is re-derived under this requirement. The other three cells\n        (a = 1/16, a = 3/16, a = 1/4) already show CLEAN AGREEMENT between\n        Stage A and Stage B/C under EITHER selection rule and are NOT\n        re-opened, re-sealed, or re-run by this amendment; DEC-20260907-9b1b02\n        already records their S1/S2/S2 verdicts as settled by this batch.\n      new_artifact_requirement: >-\n        The next Stage A blind re-derivation performed under this v2\n        definition MUST be a NEW, freshly created and freshly sealed\n        artifact. It may NOT edit, append to, or replace\n        TASK-20260907-80e198's own sealed_blind_rederivation.json (an\n        immutable record, per rule 2, of exactly what was computed under\n        v1's underspecified definitions -- \"runs already executed are never\n        re-scored\", `invalidation_rules`), and it may NOT edit or reuse any\n        file under experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/runs/ (Stage B/C's own,\n        already-committed, already-correct production output, per Stage B/C\n        `unchanged` note in `inputs.stage_plan` above). It must live at its\n        own new task directory under a new TASK-* handoff, with its own\n        hash and timestamp, exactly mirroring how TASK-20260907-80e198's own\n        seal was produced (see `procedure` above, unchanged).\n      seal_timing_requirement: >-\n        The new re-derivation must be SEALED (hashed and timestamped) BEFORE\n        the reviewer performing it opens ANY `blind_from` path listed above,\n        exactly as `procedure` above already requires for a first-time Stage\n        A derivation. In particular, the reviewer performing this re-seal\n        must NOT read TASK-20260907-80e198's own sealed_blind_rederivation.json,\n        blind_rederivation.py, or postseal_diagnostic*.py contents before\n        sealing their own new computation, so that the corrected formula is\n        applied independently rather than copied from the prior task's\n        post-hoc diagnostic scripts (those scripts remain readable\n        background/citation material for the Coordinator and for a\n        subsequent audit, never a substitute for an independent re-seal).\n      what_does_not_need_to_be_rerun: >-\n        Stage B/C's existing production result for a = 1/8 (5/5 seeds,\n        G3-FEASIBLE, RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-001..006, already computed correctly\n        under this exact formula, per `a_1_8_disagreement_root_cause`'s\n        `what_production_actually_does`) does NOT need to be re-run. Only\n        Stage A's blind re-derivation at a = 1/8 is being redone; the new\n        sealed a = 1/8 result is compared, cell by cell, against the\n        ALREADY-EXISTING production a = 1/8 reading recorded in\n        experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/runs/RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-{001..005}/'s\n        own raw-result.json and summary.json (unchanged, unedited, exactly\n        as committed).\n      resolution_rule: >-\n        Only AFTER this re-sealed a = 1/8 result is produced and compared\n        may a = 1/8 be reported, by a further committed Coordinator\n        decision, as S1 CONFIRMED FEASIBLE, S2 CONFIRMED INFEASIBLE, or a\n        genuinely new S3 DISAGREEMENT (per `success_criterion`'s own S1/S2/S3\n        taxonomy, unchanged by this amendment). This amendment does not\n        itself predetermine which of those three outcomes will result.\n\n    v3_derivation_packet: # ADDITIVE, v3 amendment item 11 -- everything above this key,\n                          # INCLUDING v2_rerequirement_a_1_8, is BYTE-IDENTICAL to the\n                          # approved v2. This appends inside a block carrying\n                          # `frozen: true` by exactly the precedent the approved v2 set\n                          # against itself with v2_rerequirement_a_1_8.\n      status: 'REQUIRED for any Stage A'''' re-derivation under this v3 contract'\n      discharges: 'blocking defect D3 of DEC-20260907-4e34c5, and archive-time observations AO-2 and AO-3'\n      what_the_defect_was: >-\n        The Coordinator's directional prior sat in plain text in a handoff\n        (ledger/handoffs/TASK-20260907-e423d5.yaml\n        `review_plan.coordinator_prior`) and in a committed dispatch queue,\n        and a task card named that handoff as the re-deriver's own\n        `review_plan_path` -- so the re-deriver was INSTRUCTED to read the\n        prior before sealing. Neither path was on any blind list.\n      why_this_is_not_fixed_by_adding_two_paths_to_a_list: >-\n        Three reasons, each read off the committed record.\n        (i) A DENYLIST CANNOT BE SHOWN COMPLETE. It enumerates what must not\n        be read out of a repository of thousands of identifier-bearing paths\n        that grows every batch; \"no further leak path exists\" is not a\n        statement any author can support, and the gate found two the previous\n        author had missed.\n        (ii) THE LISTS DRIFT, DEMONSTRABLY. AO-3 records that the two blind\n        lists for the SAME re-derivation had already diverged, so the\n        re-deriver had two answers to one question.\n        (iii) IT DEPENDS ON A CONVENTION RECORDED ELSEWHERE. AO-2 records a\n        direct contradiction between a contract's `not_blind_from` (two paths\n        MUST be read) and a handoff's `blind_from` (those same two paths\n        added), resolvable only by a convention stated in a decision record.\n        A BLIND DISCIPLINE A FRESH RE-DERIVER CANNOT OBEY FROM THE TEXT IT IS\n        GIVEN IS NOT A BLIND DISCIPLINE -- and that is the standard the entire\n        re-seal exists to meet.\n      the_mechanism: 'AN ALLOWLIST REPLACES THE DENYLIST AS AUTHORITATIVE.'\n      packet_path: experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/derivation-packet/PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3/\n      the_rule_in_one_sentence: >-\n        Until its own seal exists, the Stage A'' re-deriver reads EXACTLY the\n        files enumerated in the packet's own MANIFEST.yaml and NOTHING ELSE\n        in this repository -- not this contract, not the amendment, not a\n        handoff, not a task card, not a queue, not a decision, not a run, not\n        a commit message, and no output of any git history command.\n      contents:\n        - 'MANIFEST.yaml -- the complete readable-file list with sha256 for each, the reading rule, the seal procedure, and the declaration that the packet carries no prior and no result. IT IS THE FIRST FILE THE RE-DERIVER OPENS, so the discipline is stated in the only text the re-deriver may read.'\n        - 'quantity.md -- the STATEMENT of the quantity and the parameters, quoting this contract''s `definitions` and `inputs` verbatim: the instrument, the DP predicate, the exact-basin partition, the cap and its residual accounting, pool construction, the selection weight and its tie-break, the top-T_sel share, the exact coverage, the margin, the pass-count rule, the seed set, and the interval estimator.'\n        - 'deliverables.md -- what to produce and in what shape, with the joints the re-deriver owns stated WITHOUT any expectation of how any of them will come out.'\n        - 'prohibitions.md -- the reading rule as an operational checklist, including the two mechanical prohibitions (no git log/show/blame; no reading of any commit message before the seal) and the honest disclosure that two commit messages already reachable on the authoring branch state a prior cell''s verdict.'\n      why_it_is_the_repair:\n        - 'FINITE, ENUMERATED AND HASHED. Completeness is a property of a closed four-file list, not a claim about a repository. \"Did I read something I should not have\" becomes decidable by the re-deriver itself.'\n        - 'SELF-CONTAINED. The manifest lives inside the packet and is read first, so the discipline depends on no convention recorded in a decision record -- which is AO-2''s failure and the sharpest form of D3.'\n        - 'LEAK-FREE BY CONSTRUCTION AND CHECKABLY SO. The packet contains no prior, no verdict, no pass-count, no margin, no interval and no number produced by any prior run at any cell of the quantity under test. It is not merely asserted clean: it is four files a gate reads end to end.'\n        - 'IT DISSOLVES AO-2 RATHER THAN ADJUDICATING IT. Under an allowlist there is no file the re-deriver is both required and forbidden to read, because \"forbidden\" is the complement of the list.'\n        - 'IT MAKES ONE LIST AUTHORITATIVE WITHOUT EDITING A FROZEN FIELD. `blind_from` above stays byte-identical and is demoted to CORROBORATING; see `precedence` below.'\n      precedence: >-\n        WHERE THE PACKET AND ANY DENYLIST COULD DIFFER, THE PACKET GOVERNS\n        for the question \"may I read this before my seal\". `blind_from`\n        above, and any future review plan's `blind_from` for this experiment,\n        are CORROBORATING: they warn a denylist-only reader and they may add\n        paths, but they cannot widen what the packet permits, and nothing\n        load-bearing turns on their contents. Two lists that cannot disagree\n        about anything load-bearing cannot drift into a contradiction.\n      normativity: >-\n        THE CONTRACT GOVERNS ON DEFINITIONS. quantity.md quotes this\n        contract's `definitions` and `inputs` verbatim and adds no\n        definitional content of its own. If the packet and this contract are\n        ever found to differ on any definitional point, THIS CONTRACT GOVERNS,\n        the packet is defective, and the difference is a REPORTABLE DEFECT of\n        amendment PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3 -- never a licence for the\n        re-deriver to choose. Verifying that the packet says exactly what this\n        contract says, and nothing more, is an explicit joint of this\n        contract's approval gate.\n      the_one_disclosed_inclusion: >-\n        DISCLOSED RATHER THAN SMUGGLED. The packet states that T_sel = T/2 at\n        a = 1/4, r = 2, N = 2^24 is ESTABLISHED G3-INFEASIBLE by\n        EV-ECDLP-60e266, and that the re-deriver must report the a = 1/4 cell\n        FIRST.\n        WHY NECESSARY: a = 1/4 is this batch's KNOWN-FALSE OBJECT, carried\n        from control (b). \"Controls before belief\" requires the identical\n        measurement be run against an object whose answer is known, and a\n        re-deriver not told which object that is cannot run the control.\n        WHY BOUNDED: it concerns a = 1/4 ONLY. The packet states no verdict,\n        expectation, pass-count, margin, share, coverage or interval at\n        a = 1/16, a = 1/8 or a = 3/16 at either N -- and a = 1/8 is the\n        decision-changing cell this lineage exists to resolve. It says what\n        the instrument must REPRODUCE, not what the open cells will do.\n      where_the_prior_lives_instead:\n        path: coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-48ef8b/priors/coordinator_prior.SEALED.yaml\n        why_it_is_kept: >-\n          AGENTS.md \"Review architecture\" REQUIRES the Coordinator's prior to\n          be recorded before any reviewer runs: \"three reviewers concurred\"\n          and \"three reviewers concurred with what the Coordinator already\n          believed\" are different findings, and only a pre-recorded prior\n          separates them. THE ANSWER TO A LEAKING PRIOR IS NEVER TO STOP\n          RECORDING IT.\n        properties:\n          - 'It is NOT in the derivation packet, so under the allowlist it is unreadable before the seal without an explicit violation.'\n          - 'It is named on the corroborating denylist below and must be named on every future review plan''s `blind_from` for this experiment.'\n          - 'It is the ONLY place in its batch carrying a directional expectation: that lane''s queue, task cards, handoffs, opening decision and commit messages state no prior, no verdict, no margin and no number at any cell of the quantity under test.'\n          - 'It is committed in the lane''s opening snapshot, so the commit that carries it is itself proof the prior predates every reviewer -- a STRONGER discharge of the AGENTS.md requirement than a prior recorded in a handoff, not a weaker one.'\n        contains_no_authority: >-\n          It records an expectation and nothing else: no instruction to any\n          reviewer, no assignment, no authority. A reviewer's joints and\n          deliverables come from the packet, which is why the packet can be\n          prior-free at all.\n      corroborating_denylist_v3_additions: >-\n        NOT AN EDIT OF `blind_from` ABOVE, which stays byte-identical. These\n        paths are additionally named here, and must be named on every future\n        review plan's `blind_from` for this experiment, so that a\n        denylist-only reader is warned even though the packet is what governs:\n          coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-48ef8b/priors/\n          ledger/handoffs/TASK-20260907-e423d5.yaml\n          coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-e9fd22/\n          coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-48ef8b/\n          ledger/decisions/ (every DEC-* of this lineage)\n          ledger/evidence/ (every EV-* of this lineage)\n          ledger/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/\n          experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.BATCH-e9fd22-proposed.yaml\n          experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/\n          experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml (THIS FILE)\n          coordination/experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/\n        THE LIST IS NOT CLAIMED COMPLETE. That is the whole point of D3's\n        repair: completeness is claimed for the ALLOWLIST, which is four\n        files, and never for this.\n      seal_procedure_unchanged: >-\n        The seal itself is `procedure` above, byte-identical and in force: the\n        re-deriver commits its own from-scratch computation to its own task\n        directory with a hash and a timestamp, and only then opens anything\n        outside the packet. v3 changes WHAT MAY BE READ BEFORE THE SEAL, not\n        what a seal is.\n\n    v3_rerequirement_stage_a_dprime: # ADDITIVE, v3 amendment item 12\n      status: 'REQUIRED; supersedes NOTHING and re-scores NOTHING'\n      scope: >-\n        A FRESH Stage A'' blind re-derivation over the FULL v3 grid: N in\n        {2^20, 2^24}, a in {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4}, r = 2, T_sel = T/2, seeds\n        1..25. It is a NEW artifact at a NEW task directory with its own hash\n        and timestamp.\n      why_the_full_grid_and_not_only_a_1_8: >-\n        v2's `v2_rerequirement_a_1_8` scoped its re-seal to a = 1/8 because\n        only that cell's verdict flipped under the corrected WEIGHT formula.\n        D2 is different in kind: the CAP enters every cell of every scale,\n        through the basin partition itself and through pool construction, so\n        no cell is known robust to it. Scoping the v3 re-seal to one cell\n        would assume exactly what is unmeasured. THIS IS A STATEMENT ABOUT\n        WHAT IS UNKNOWN, NOT A PREDICTION THAT ANY CELL WILL MOVE.\n      relation_to_the_v2_requirement: >-\n        `v2_rerequirement_a_1_8` above is UNCHANGED, byte-identical, and\n        remains in force under the approved v2 for its own narrow purpose. A\n        Stage A'' re-derivation satisfying THIS requirement also covers the\n        a = 1/8 cell it names, but does not retroactively discharge it under\n        v2's own terms and does not touch TASK-20260907-80e198's sealed\n        artifact, which stays immutable as the record of what was computed\n        under v1's underspecified definitions.\n      immutability_requirement: >-\n        The Stage A'' artifact may NOT edit, append to, or replace\n        TASK-20260907-80e198's sealed_blind_rederivation.json, any file under\n        experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/runs/, or anything under\n        coordination/experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/batches/BATCH-3c7493/. It\n        lives at its own new task directory. A violation is invalid under\n        `invalidation_rules`, per rule 2.\n      independence_requirement: >-\n        The agent performing Stage A'' must be in a session that authored\n        neither this contract, nor amendment PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3, nor\n        the derivation packet. Authorship of the packet is disqualifying for\n        obeying it: the author knows what was deliberately left out.\n\n  controls: # v3 AMENDMENT NOTE: items (a) through (f) below are reproduced\n            # BYTE-IDENTICALLY from the APPROVED\n            # experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml `controls`.\n            # Items (g) through (n) are APPENDED by this v3 amendment. In\n            # particular control (e) SEED-COUNT PARITY is NOT edited: the\n            # 25-seed extension is argued a fortiori from (e)'s own stated\n            # rationale in the appended item (g), per CR-1 COND-4.\n    - >-\n      (a) BLIND RE-DERIVATION CONTROL (REQUIRED, frozen): see\n      `blind_rederivation`. No cell is evidence before the seal exists.\n    - >-\n      (b) a = 1/4 REPLICATION CONTROL: T_sel = T/2 at a = 1/4, r = 2,\n      N = 2^24 is ALREADY established as G3-INFEASIBLE (G3 FAIL 10/10 seeds,\n      EV-ECDLP-60e266). This contract's own fresh 5 seeds at a = 1/4 must\n      reproduce that FAIL. A PASS here at a = 1/4 invalidates this batch's\n      instrument (see `invalidation_rules`), independent of any other cell's\n      result.\n    - >-\n      (c) EXACT-COVERAGE NON-EXCEEDANCE: no exact top-T_sel share may exceed\n      1.0 or the exact top-T share (T > T_sel); an exceedance is an\n      implementation error, not a result (mirrors v1/v2's own structural\n      tell).\n    - >-\n      (d) DEFINITIONAL IDENTITY WITH THE v2 G3 RULE: the feasibility\n      criterion applied here is REUSED VERBATIM from\n      experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/specification.v2.yaml\n      `inputs.g3_gate_procedure`, not re-derived or re-worded, specifically\n      to rule out a units/definition mismatch as the source of any\n      confirmed discrepancy (this contract's own outcome (b) names that\n      possibility explicitly and this control is what would surface it).\n    - >-\n      (e) SEED-COUNT PARITY: 5 seeds per a, matching Stage 0's and v2's own\n      seed count, so this batch's statistical power is comparable, not\n      thinner, than the batch that produced the original discrepancy.\n    - >-\n      (f) [v2 AMENDMENT, ADDITIVE] SELECTION-FORMULA IDENTITY: the re-sealed\n      a = 1/8 blind re-derivation required by\n      `blind_rederivation.v2_rerequirement_a_1_8` must apply EXACTLY the\n      `STATIC(T)_r pool-selection weight formula (v2 amendment item 1)`\n      stated in `definitions` above, with no further drift or\n      reinterpretation; a re-seal that silently applies yet a third,\n      different reading of \"the published Bernstein-Lange weight\" would\n      repeat, not resolve, the underspecification this amendment exists to\n      close.\n    - >-\n      (g) [v3 AMENDMENT, ADDITIVE] SEED-COUNT PARITY EXTENSION.\n      CONTROL (e) IS QUOTED HERE IN FULL AND IS NOT EDITED: \"(e) SEED-COUNT\n      PARITY: 5 seeds per a, matching Stage 0's and v2's own seed count, so\n      this batch's statistical power is comparable, not thinner, than the\n      batch that produced the original discrepancy.\"\n      THE ARGUMENT, FROM (e)'S OWN STATED RATIONALE: (e) exists to protect a\n      property it names explicitly -- power \"comparable, not thinner\" than\n      the batch that produced the original discrepancy. v3 runs 25 seeds per\n      (N, a), the same integer-seeded streams by the same construction, so\n      the power is STRICTLY GREATER and never thinner. (e) is therefore\n      satisfied A FORTIORI, not overridden.\n      THE AUTHORITY GAP, STATED RATHER THAN PAPERED OVER: the seed set is the\n      one wide-scope item the approved contract's `invalidation_rules` item 7\n      does NOT name, so item 7 confers no authority over it. The warrant used\n      here is (e)'s own rationale, which is WEAKER than item 7 and is recorded\n      as such. A gate that rejects this reading should say so; the fallback\n      needing no new warrant is to run seeds 1..5 only, which costs the wide\n      scope its power.\n      THE CONTROL ITSELF FIRES WHEN: the 25-seed reading and the seeds 1..5\n      subgroup reading are composited into one number anywhere; or the\n      subgroup reading is omitted; or fewer than 25 of the pre-registered\n      seeds are run at a cell whose verdict is reported; or the seed set\n      differs between the two readings or between any treatment and control\n      arm.\n    - >-\n      (h) [v3 AMENDMENT, ADDITIVE] CROSS-SCALE REPRODUCTION CONTROL, anchored\n      at N = 2^24 where a committed reference exists.\n      THE CHECK: at N = 2^24, a in {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4}, seeds 1..5, the\n      PRODUCTION reading's exact top-T_sel share, STATIC(T)_{r=2} exact\n      coverage and margin must each equal the committed value in the\n      corresponding RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-001..005 summary.json to within 1e-9\n      ABSOLUTE. A larger deviation FIRES THIS CONTROL.\n      IT DOES NOT RE-SCORE THE COMMITTED RUNS. They are the REFERENCE, never\n      the subject: no byte under experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/runs/ is read\n      for anything but comparison, and none is written. This is the binding\n      condition of `invalidation_rules` item 7 (\"runs already executed are\n      never re-scored\") and it is honoured exactly.\n      THE TOLERANCE IS NOT INVENTED: the independent gate that refused this\n      contract's predecessor draft reproduced all three quantities at all 20\n      committed cells from the pinned instrument to a WORST ABSOLUTE\n      DEVIATION OF 0.000e+00, so the target is known achievable and a nonzero\n      residual is a real signal rather than a tolerance artifact.\n      THE 1e-9 TOLERANCE APPLIES TO THE PRODUCTION READING ONLY, where the\n      tie-break key stream is identical by construction. It does NOT apply to\n      the blind reading, whose key stream necessarily differs (see (o) and\n      `definitions` item on the tie-break).\n      WHAT \"CROSS-SCALE\" MEANS HERE, STATED PLAINLY BECAUSE IT IS A\n      DELIBERATE NARROWING: this contract spans two scales, and the\n      reproduction anchor sits at the scale that HAS committed cells. AT\n      N = 2^20 THERE IS NO REFERENCE -- this experiment has never run there --\n      so v3 reads a CROSS-SCALE CONSISTENCY comparison at N = 2^20 and\n      declares it EXPLICITLY NOT A CONTROL: it has nothing to pass or fail\n      against. Inventing a reference there would have been a fabrication.\n    - >-\n      (i) [v3 AMENDMENT, ADDITIVE] NULL-ORACLE-RAND (UNIFORM) -- THE GATING\n      NULL OBJECT. Discharges non-blocking defect D7.\n      THE NULL: replace the ORACLE side of the comparison -- the top-T_sel\n      basins by TRUE SIZE over the whole exact partition -- by a UNIFORMLY\n      RANDOM T_sel-subset of the DPs of the SAME enumerated partition. Hold\n      cov_static fixed, read the coverage of the random subset off the SAME\n      basin-size array by the SAME arithmetic, and form\n      margin_null = (random subset's exact coverage) - cov_static.\n      ONE SUBSTITUTION, SAME UNIVERSE, SAME READ-OFF, SAME PREDICATE. This is\n      what D7 asked for: the refused draft's null changed the selection rule\n      AND the universe (its arm ranged over the r*T pool while the real arm\n      ranges over the whole partition), so its guaranteed negativity was\n      bought largely by the universe change and the size ratio rather than by\n      the weight carrying information.\n      IT FIRES WHEN: margin_null(s) >= 0 in more than 1 of the 25 seeds at\n      any (N, a) cell, or the reported MEAN margin_null is non-negative at\n      any cell.\n      WHY ITS CONCLUSION IS KNOWN FALSE BY ARGUMENT, NOT BY DATA: cov_static\n      is the exact coverage of T = 2*T_sel pool entries selected by\n      weight_d = S_d + 4*W*h_d, and both factors of that weight increase with\n      basin size for a structural reason -- a DP with a larger basin is\n      reached by MORE uniform-restart pool walks (larger h_d) and those walks\n      start from a larger set of points (larger S_d) -- while the pool itself\n      over-samples large basins, since a DP enters it only when some restart\n      walk reaches it. A UNIFORMLY random T_sel-subset of all DPs has by\n      construction NO correlation with basin size: its expected mass is T_sel\n      times the MEAN basin mass over a DP set of size order N/W, the\n      overwhelming majority of whose basins are small. So margin_null must be\n      negative. NO COMMITTED NUMBER IS USED IN THIS ARGUMENT AND NONE IS\n      ASSERTED BY IT -- which is exactly why the control is falsifiable: a\n      structural argument can be wrong.\n    - >-\n      (j) [v3 AMENDMENT, ADDITIVE] NULL-ORACLE-RAND (SIZE-BIASED) --\n      DIAGNOSTIC ONLY, GATES NOTHING.\n      Same substitution as (i) but with the T_sel-subset drawn with\n      probability proportional to basin size. ITS DIRECTION IS DECLARED\n      UNPREDICTABLE IN ADVANCE and no verdict depends on it: a size-biased\n      draw is deliberately competitive with the oracle, and this contract\n      cannot honestly pre-register which way it falls. Reported because the\n      GAP between (i) and (j) measures how much of the oracle's advantage is\n      size-correlation alone -- which is informative -- and fenced off from\n      every verdict because a control whose direction cannot be stated in\n      advance is not a control.\n    - >-\n      (k) [v3 AMENDMENT, ADDITIVE] NULL-RANDSEL -- RETAINED, NON-GATING, LOW\n      POWER DISCLOSED IN THE CONTRACT.\n      THE NULL: replace weight_d selection by a uniformly random T-subset of\n      the r*T POOL, and compare the top-T_sel share against that random\n      selection's coverage.\n      IT FIRES WHEN: margin_null_pool(s) >= 0 in more than 1 of the 25 seeds\n      at any cell.\n      ITS POWER IS LOW AND THAT IS STATED HERE RATHER THAN LEFT FOR A\n      REVIEWER TO DISCOVER: the independent gate recomputed this quantity on\n      the committed cells and found it one to two orders of magnitude beyond\n      its own declared firing threshold at every cell, because its arm ranges\n      over the r*T pool while the real arm ranges over the whole partition\n      (D7). It CAN fire, but on nothing short of a gross defect. RETAINED as\n      a check on the weight ESTIMATOR specifically -- which is what it is\n      genuinely shaped for -- and DEMOTED from gating to reported.\n    - >-\n      (l) [v3 AMENDMENT, ADDITIVE] DECAY-A -- THE DECLARED DECAY CONTROL, AND\n      THIS BATCH'S LOAD-BEARING ARTIFACT DETECTOR. Declared decay parameter:\n      a. Rationale: docs/inventor-protocol.md \"controls before belief\" -- a\n      quantity that fails to decay when the parameter meant to destroy it\n      increases is the canonical artifact tell.\n      CLAUSE (i) MONOTONE DECAY, BINDING: the mean margin over the 25 seeds\n      must be STRICTLY DECREASING across a = 1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4 at each N\n      separately. A SINGLE non-monotone step fires it.\n      CLAUSE (ii) PAIRED DIFFERENCES, CONTEXT ONLY, BINDS NOTHING: the paired\n      per-seed differences between adjacent a-values, reported with their\n      percentile intervals. Reported for interpretation; no verdict and no\n      other clause depends on it, per `definitions` item on the interval\n      estimator (D5).\n      CLAUSE (iii) EXTERNAL ANCHOR, BINDING, AND THE ONLY CLAUSE ANCHORED\n      OUTSIDE THIS BATCH: at a = 1/4, the mean margin must be NEGATIVE and\n      the pass-count k must be at most 5 of 25. The anchor is\n      EV-ECDLP-60e266's independently established a = 1/4 G3-infeasibility --\n      a result of a DIFFERENT batch, cited and never re-scored here.\n      WHY CLAUSE (i) IS NOT AN IDENTITY: each a is a DIFFERENT INSTRUMENT,\n      with its own W, DP rate, cap, and basin partition. No arithmetic\n      relates the four means, so a correct implementation can produce a\n      non-monotone sequence.\n      WHY CLAUSE (iii) CARRIES THE LOAD: it is the one clause a\n      self-consistent but WRONG implementation cannot pass automatically,\n      because its reference is external to everything this batch computes.\n    - >-\n      (m) [v3 AMENDMENT, ADDITIVE] DECAY-TSEL -- SECOND DECAY CONTROL, WEAKER\n      THAN (l), WEAKNESS DISCLOSED, AND WITH THE PREVIOUS GATE'S TAUTOLOGICAL\n      CLAUSE DELIBERATELY NOT REINTRODUCED.\n      CLAUSE (i) BINDING: at T_sel = T/8, margin(s) >= 0 in more than 1 of the\n      25 seeds at any a fires this control.\n      RE-CHECKED AGAINST THE CODE RATHER THAN CARRIED ON TRUST: cov_static is\n      a function of the T weight-selected pool entries and is INDEPENDENT of\n      T_sel (experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/source/run_stageb.py line 96\n      selects T, never T_sel), while share_top(T/8) is a strict prefix of\n      share_top(T/2). NOTHING in either expression forces\n      share_top(T/8) < cov_static, so the clause is NOT an identity and can\n      fail on a correct implementation. What it detects: a T/8-entry oracle\n      table already matching STATIC(T)'s coverage, i.e. a comparison that is\n      not measuring stored-advice efficiency at all but is an\n      everything-passes artifact.\n      CLAUSE (ii) BINDING, WEAK: rho_ORACLE must be non-decreasing in a at\n      each N. Not forced by arithmetic, but on the read grid\n      {1/8, 1/4, 1/2} rho_ORACLE takes few values, so this is effectively a\n      COARSE ordering check on the same directional claim (l) makes.\n      DISCLOSED, not hidden.\n      ITS POWER IS LOW AND THAT IS STATED: the independent gate found clause\n      (i) comfortably satisfied on every committed cell.\n      THE CLAUSE THE PREVIOUS GATE CORRECTLY REMOVED IS NOT REINTRODUCED:\n      margin(T/2) > margin(T/4) > margin(T/8) holds BY ARITHMETIC on every\n      correct implementation, because the three share_top values are nested\n      prefixes of one descending sort while cov_static is common to all\n      three. It appears in this contract ONLY inside item (o), labelled a\n      structural self-check, and never as a control.\n    - >-\n      (n) [v3 AMENDMENT, ADDITIVE] NULL-SHUF -- DIAGNOSTIC, EXPLICITLY NOT A\n      G3 NULL, AND DECLARED UNUSABLE AS ONE IN THE CONTRACT RATHER THAN\n      QUIETLY DROPPED.\n      Permuting basin sizes across the pool's DPs, holding the size multiset\n      and the weights fixed, makes cov_static COLLAPSE -- which makes G3 pass\n      MORE easily. THAT IS THE WRONG DIRECTION FOR A FEASIBILITY NULL:\n      carrying it as one would mean carrying a control that fires in the\n      direction of the claim, which is worse than having no null at all.\n      NOTHING GATES ON IT. It is retained and reported because the collapse\n      itself is informative about whether weight_d carries basin-size\n      information, and it is fenced off from every verdict, every clause and\n      every agreement test.\n    - >-\n      (o) [v3 AMENDMENT, ADDITIVE] STRUCTURAL SELF-CHECKS -- NOT CONTROLS,\n      AND LABELLED SO DELIBERATELY.\n      Each item below CANNOT FAIL on a correct implementation, so its passing\n      means nothing beyond \"no defect of this kind\". Calling any of them a\n      control would repeat exactly the vacuity the independent gate correctly\n      removed from a DECAY-TSEL clause of the refused draft, and this contract\n      does not do that.\n      (o1) BASIN-MASS ACCOUNTING: sum_d b(d) + cycle_mass + capped_mass = N\n      EXACTLY, in integer arithmetic, with ZERO tolerance, at every cell of\n      BOTH readings; and b(d) >= 1 for every DP d. Cannot fail because the\n      three classes are disjoint and exhaustive by construction (see\n      `definitions` item 2). It fires exactly when a reading implements no\n      cap, or assigns residual mass to a basin, or double-counts -- which is\n      D2's failure mode and the reason the check exists.\n      (o2) EXACT-COVERAGE NESTING: share_top(T/8) <= share_top(T/4) <=\n      share_top(T/2) <= share_top(T) <= 1.0, and cov_static <= share_top(T).\n      Cannot fail: nested prefixes of a descending sort of non-negative basin\n      sizes, and an exact coverage of T DPs that cannot exceed the T largest\n      basins. THIS SUBSUMES v2's CONTROL (c), which is retained above\n      verbatim and unedited; (o2) records honestly that (c) is an identity\n      rather than a control.\n      (o3) MARGIN NESTING IN T_sel: margin(T/2) > margin(T/4) > margin(T/8)\n      at every cell. Cannot fail, for the reason given in item (m): this is\n      the clause the previous gate removed, kept here ONLY as a self-check.\n      A VIOLATION OF ANY OF (o1)-(o3) IS AN IMPLEMENTATION ERROR AND STOPS\n      THE CELL AS completed_invalid (see `stopping_rules`), never folded into\n      a pass-count.\n\n  controls_falsifiability_summary: >-\n    REQUIRED READING FOR THE GATE, and the honest power gradient of this\n    batch. Of the fifteen declared items: ELEVEN are controls with a\n    reachable failing world on a correct implementation -- (a), (b), (d), (e),\n    (f), (g), (h), (i), (k), (l), (m); THREE are structural self-checks and\n    are labelled as such rather than as controls -- (c) (retained verbatim\n    from v2, honestly re-described in (o2)), and (o1)-(o3); and TWO are\n    diagnostics explicitly fenced off from every verdict -- (j) and (n).\n    THE LOAD IS NOT EVENLY DISTRIBUTED, and pretending otherwise would be\n    the defect: control (l) clause (iii) is the ONLY clause anchored OUTSIDE\n    this batch and carries most of the artifact-detection load; control (i)\n    is the shape-matched gating null that D7 asked for; controls (k) and (m)\n    are corroboration with DISCLOSED low power; control (h) is the sharpest\n    check available on pipeline identity, because its target is known\n    achievable to 0.000e+00.\n\n  independent_variables: # v2's list, retained verbatim; it governs the N = 2^24 arm\n    - \"N: fixed, 2^24\"\n    - \"a: {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4}\"\n    - \"r: fixed, 2\"\n    - \"T_sel: fixed, T/2 = 128\"\n    - \"seed: {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}\"\n    - \"reading: {blind (Stage A), production (Stage B/C)}\"\n  independent_variables_v3: # ADDITIVE; the operative grid for v3 runs\n    - \"N: {2^20, 2^24} -- two scales; v2's 'fixed, 2^24' entry above is retained verbatim and remains the description of the arm it governs\"\n    - \"a: {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4} -- UNCHANGED from v2\"\n    - \"r: fixed, 2 -- UNCHANGED from v2\"\n    - \"T_sel: fixed at T/2 (= 32 at N = 2^20, = 128 at N = 2^24); T/4 and T/8 additionally READ for control (m) only\"\n    - \"seed: {1, ..., 25}; the subgroup {1, 2, 3, 4, 5} is reported separately and is the only seed set control (h) reproduces against\"\n    - \"reading: {blind (Stage A''), production (Stage B''/C'')}\"\n    - \"control arm: {primary, NULL-ORACLE-RAND uniform, NULL-ORACLE-RAND size-biased, NULL-RANDSEL, NULL-SHUF}\"\n  independent_variables_v3_note: >-\n    THE TWO LISTS ARE NOT IN CONFLICT AND NEITHER IS EDITED. v2's list stays\n    byte-identical and continues to describe the arm v1 executed and v2\n    governs. `independent_variables_v3` is the grid for runs executed under\n    THIS contract, once and if it is approved. Where they differ (N, seed,\n    T_sel readings, control arms), the v3 list governs v3 runs and the v2\n    list governs nothing new.\n\n  metrics:\n    primary: # CR-1 COND-3: REPRODUCED BYTE-IDENTICALLY FROM THE APPROVED v2. NOT EDITED.\n      - \"per (a, seed): exact top-T_sel basin share minus STATIC(T)_{r=2} exact coverage (the G3-style margin); sign and magnitude\"\n      - \"per a: pass-count out of 5 seeds (margin >= 0); G3-style feasibility verdict (>= 4/5 -> FEASIBLE, else INFEASIBLE)\"\n      - \"crossing bracket: the pair of adjacent a-grid values straddling the FEASIBLE/INFEASIBLE boundary, per `definitions.crossing point`\"\n      - \"blind-vs-production agreement per (a, seed): same sign, margins within the two readings' own seed-to-seed noise; and per-a agreement on the pass-count/verdict\"\n      - \"a = 1/4 replication control: pass-count out of 5 seeds, compared against EV-ECDLP-60e266's 5/5 FAIL at 2^24\"\n    secondary:\n      - \"exact top-T_sel share and STATIC(T)_{r=2} exact coverage individually, per (a, seed), for auditability\"\n      - \"wall clock and peak RSS per run, for budget accounting only\"\n    primary_v3_additions: # ADDITIVE; `primary` above is untouched, per CR-1 COND-3\n      - \"per (N, a, seed): the G3-style margin, at BOTH scales, over the 25 pre-registered seeds\"\n      - \"per (N, a): pass-count k out of 25 (margin >= 0), and the G3-style feasibility verdict by the SAME >= 4/5 proportional rule applied to 25 seeds (i.e. k >= 20); the seeds 1..5 subgroup's own pass-count out of 5 by v2's rule verbatim, reported SEPARATELY and never composited\"\n      - \"per (N, a): mean margin over the 25 seeds and its SIGN -- the second of the two quantities blind-versus-production agreement is judged on\"\n      - \"per (N, a): the percentile bootstrap interval of the mean margin, used ONLY to route a cell to SU; BCa reported beside it as context, gating nothing\"\n      - \"per (N, a): cycle_mass, capped_mass, capped_walks and residual_fraction = (cycle_mass + capped_mass)/N, in BOTH readings, with the accounting identity's exact satisfaction recorded\"\n      - \"per (N, a): the number of pool entries TIED at the T-th largest weight, and the cardinality of the symmetric difference of the two readings' Sel_static sets\"\n      - \"per (N, a): margin_null for NULL-ORACLE-RAND (uniform, gating), its size-biased variant (diagnostic), NULL-RANDSEL (non-gating) and NULL-SHUF (diagnostic), each over the same 25 seeds\"\n      - \"per (N, a): rho_ORACLE and the T/4 and T/8 top-share readings that control (m) evaluates\"\n      - \"per control: FIRED or NOT FIRED, with the exact quantity and cell it was read from -- a control whose outcome is not reported counts as not run, not as passed\"\n    metrics_v3_note: >-\n      THE VERDICT-BEARING METRICS ARE RESAMPLING-FREE BY DESIGN. The\n      pass-count k is an integer and the sign of the mean margin is a sign;\n      two independent implementations compute both identically or differ for\n      a reason about the quantity. The only bootstrap in this contract routes\n      to SU and gates nothing. This is D5's discharge, and it is why an\n      interval-method disagreement between the two readings is reported as\n      interval-method sensitivity rather than as S3.\n\n  heuristic_under_test: null\n  heuristic_note: >-\n    UNCHANGED from v1/v2: this contract does not validate or re-validate\n    HEUR-BLT-1/2/7; it is a direct exact-enumeration measurement. HEUR-BLT-1\n    (the random-function basin law) is the same standing assumption\n    EXP-ECDLP-869870 and EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 already carry; nothing here adds to\n    or subtracts from its own validation status. v3 ADDS NO HEURISTIC: the cap\n    convention is not a heuristic but a stated implementation convention, and\n    the structural argument for control (i)'s known-false direction is an\n    argument about that convention's consequences, not a numbered heuristic\n    this contract asks anyone to accept.\n\n  preregistered_prediction:\n    deviation_declared: >-\n      THIS IS THE ONE FIELD v3 DOES NOT RESTATE VERBATIM, AND THE DEVIATION\n      IS DECLARED RATHER THAN QUIET. It is NOT one of the fields CR-1 COND-3\n      pins verbatim (those are `success_criterion` S1/S2/S3 and\n      `metrics.primary`, both reproduced byte-identically above).\n      WHY: the approved v2's `preregistered_prediction` states DIRECTIONAL\n      EXPECTATIONS AND PER-SEED MARGIN VALUES at a = 1/16, a = 1/8 and\n      a = 3/16. Restating them inline here would put a directional prior with\n      numbers into the contract text -- the same class of leak as D3, in the\n      one document a re-deriver is most likely to reach for. So v3 carries\n      the v1/v2 prediction BY REFERENCE and records its own additions in a\n      sealed file off the reading path.\n    v1_v2_prediction_retained_by_reference: >-\n      UNCHANGED AND STILL ON THE RECORD, at\n      experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml\n      `preregistered_prediction` (itself byte-identical to v1's). It is\n      committed, immutable and timestamped before v1's Stage B/C ran, so its\n      pre-registration is intact and is not weakened by being cited rather\n      than copied. v3 does not restate, revise, retract or re-score it.\n    quantity: >-\n      G3-style feasibility verdict (per `definitions`) at each a in\n      {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4}, at N = 2^20 and at N = 2^24, r = 2,\n      T_sel = T/2, over the 25 pre-registered seeds; plus the crossing\n      bracket at each scale.\n    v3_prediction_location:\n      path: coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-48ef8b/priors/coordinator_prior.SEALED.yaml\n      what_is_there: >-\n        The authoring Coordinator's expectation for the cells v3 adds, and its\n        expectation of what the approval gate will find. Written and committed\n        at lane opening, BEFORE any reviewer or re-deriver runs, which is what\n        AGENTS.md \"Review architecture\" requires and why the prior is kept\n        rather than deleted.\n      why_not_here: >-\n        Because a prior in the contract is a prior on the re-deriver's most\n        natural reading path. The sealed file is NOT in the derivation packet,\n        so under the allowlist it is unreadable before the seal without an\n        explicit violation, and it is named on the corroborating denylist.","lineStart":797,"lineEnd":1543,"totalLines":1544,"truncated":true}},"title":"experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml","time":{"start":1789086874303,"end":1789086874312}},"id":"prt_08de331ab001W4hM4rGJ9RGomx","sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","messageID":"msg_08de22b49001UqMOgFLjQouZpv"}}
