{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789087319485,"sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-862fd453abbe73ba","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/ledger/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/goal.yaml"},"output":"<path>/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/ledger/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/goal.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: research_goal:\n2:   id: GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f\n3:   id_allocation_provenance: >-\n4:     Token minted 2026-09-06 by the orchestrating session with `python3\n5:     tools/allocate_id.py --next goal --area ECDLP`, confirmed free with\n6:     `--check`, and relayed to the coordinator in the in-session campaign-open\n7:     handoff. Not derived by scanning state. Every other identifier named in\n8:     this record (BATCH-9c5410, TASK-20260906-67f1ab, TASK-20260906-2d30dd,\n9:     DEC-20260906-2b1387, TASK-20260906-3623b9, TASK-20260906-d17254,\n10:     TASK-20260906-7a2446, TASK-20260906-7ec3ea, TASK-20260906-90e7cf) was\n11:     pre-minted and `--check`ed the same way by that session; the coordinator\n12:     minted nothing and grepped for nothing.\n13:   title: >-\n14:     Batch ECDLP with precomputation: fewer stored distinguished points at\n15:     fixed online cost\n16:   objective: >-\n17:     Measure, with independent validation and red-team review, whether the\n18:     batch-reselected fixed-size table (H-ECDLP-37dc01, contract\n19:     EXP-ECDLP-612fb1) and the basin-partition coverage instrument\n20:     (H-ECDLP-3550b8, contract EXP-ECDLP-869870) answer RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5 in\n21:     EITHER direction with a measured constant and a confidence interval:\n22:     whether the number of stored distinguished points T needed for a fixed\n23:     per-target online cost and success probability can be reduced below the\n24:     selected Bernstein-Lange table in a fully charged (P, S, L, epsilon, U)\n25:     cost model, and by what factor. Every result of this campaign is\n26:     constant-factor, generic, claim_tier toy, and sits under the\n27:     Corrigan-Gibbs-Kogan S T^2 = Omega~(eps N) ceiling (KN-LIT-013); no\n28:     exponent is targeted and the campaign says so at every step. A negative\n29:     batch narrows the constant's known range; only a measured obstruction\n30:     block per docs/inventor-protocol.md closes a lane.\n31:   question_ids:\n32:   - RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5\n33:   active_hypothesis_ids:\n34:   - H-ECDLP-37dc01\n35:   - H-ECDLP-3550b8\n36:   status: active\n37:   impediments: []\n38:   runtime:\n39:     provider: none\n40:     goal_id: GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f\n41:   ecc_classification: >-\n42:     Area ECDLP is declared in orchestration/research-priority.yaml\n43:     `ecc_areas` (read through tools/ecc_priority.py, never inferred from the\n44:     identifier prefix), so this goal is ECC by policy: it is selected before\n45:     every non-ECC goal at every selection point, and its campaign budget\n46:     carries no batch or wall-clock ceiling (AGENTS.md \"ECC comes first\",\n47:     user instruction 2026-09-04). Unlimited removes the ceiling, not the duty\n48:     to rank -- every batch on this goal still ranks its task ahead of doing\n49:     nothing.\n50:   campaign_budget:\n51:     maximum_batches: null\n52:     total_wall_clock_seconds: null\n53:     max_concurrent: 2\n54:     unlimited_budget_note_20260906: >-\n55:       ECC goal: campaign budget is UNLIMITED by declared policy\n56:       (orchestration/research-priority.yaml, user instruction 2026-09-04);\n57:       maximum_batches and total_wall_clock_seconds are null from creation\n58:       and check_ecc_budget_is_unlimited enforces it. max_concurrent stays\n59:       bounded -- it is machine headroom, not a research budget: this is a\n60:       4-core, 15 GB container and 2 is its headroom (each contract declares\n61:       maximum_workers 1 and maximum_memory_gb 8). Per-experiment budgets\n62:       remain those frozen in each contract and are never raised by this\n63:       field.\n64:   current_batch_id: null\n65:   current_batch_id_note_20260907_e9fd22: >-\n66:     Set to null by TASK-20260907-9e7580: BATCH-e9fd22 is CLOSED (see\n67:     `batch_e9fd22_disposition`) and this head owns no other open lane. Previous\n68:     value: BATCH-e9fd22. It is not repointed at BATCH-8f3e86 -- that is another\n69:     session's open lane on another branch and this head does not write its\n70:     entries. The next session opening a lane on this goal sets both this field\n71:     and `dispatch_queue_path` to its own.\n72:   dispatch_queue_path: coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-e9fd22/dispatch_queue.json\n73:   dispatch_queue_path_note_20260907_e9fd22: >-\n74:     Left pointing at BATCH-e9fd22's queue, which is the last queue this head\n75:     owned and is now terminal: TASK-20260907-d47b50, TASK-20260907-4ce154,\n76:     TASK-20260907-f65c6e, TASK-20260907-ceb8cf and TASK-20260907-9e7580 are\n77:     `completed` and the five downstream tasks are `cancelled` with a recorded\n78:     reason, so rendering it offers nothing. It is retained rather than nulled\n79:     so the record of what this lane's graph was stays reachable from the head.\n80:   open_batches: []\n81:   open_batches_note_20260907_e9fd22: >-\n82:     Emptied by TASK-20260907-9e7580 on closing BATCH-e9fd22. THIS LIST IS NOT\n83:     THE AUTHORITATIVE SET OF OPEN LANES ON THIS GOAL: it holds only lanes\n84:     registered through this head, and lane state lives in write-once side files\n85:     (`coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/lanes/`). Read\n86:     `python3 tools/goal_lanes.py lanes GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f` instead. As of\n87:     2026-09-07 that command reports BATCH-8f3e86 OPEN on branch\n88:     cursor/run-experiments-batch-93e3 (opened by coordinator-ecdlp-8f3e86) --\n89:     recorded here as a fact read from the tool, deliberately NOT added to this\n90:     list, because adding it would be writing another lane's head entry.\n91:   open_batches_note_20260907_48ef8b: >-\n92:     Re-read by TASK-20260907-1aa16f on closing BATCH-48ef8b, and STILL EMPTY.\n93:     `python3 tools/goal_lanes.py lanes GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f` as of 2026-09-07 now\n94:     reports EVERY lane of this goal CLOSED -- BATCH-1e7251, BATCH-252a44,\n95:     BATCH-289698, BATCH-8f3e86, BATCH-e9fd22, BATCH-f3a30a, and BATCH-48ef8b\n96:     itself on its own close. BATCH-8f3e86, which the note above records as OPEN\n97:     and which was open when that note was written, closed on branch\n98:     cursor/run-experiments-batch-93e3 (PR #829, merged to main at f24293a5f) and\n99:     arrived on this branch in the origin/main merge 4e737c70e. THIS LIST IS\n100:     STILL NOT THE AUTHORITATIVE SET OF OPEN LANES (finding CT-3 of\n101:     DEC-20260907-52f2a0, carried below): read the side files through\n102:     `tools/goal_lanes.py`, never this key.\n103:   approval_decision_ids:\n104:   - DEC-20260906-2b1387\n105:   - DEC-20260906-806501\n106:   - DEC-20260907-4e34c5\n107:   - DEC-20260907-adbe7e\n108:   evidence_review_decision_ids:\n109:   - DEC-20260906-1f5b71\n110:   - DEC-20260906-bcc097\n111:   - DEC-20260907-ece434\n112:   lane_decision_ids_20260907_e9fd22:\n113:     added_by: TASK-20260907-9e7580\n114:     note: >-\n115:       The three decisions of lane BATCH-e9fd22, listed with their roles because\n116:       no existing list on this head fits all three. DEC-20260907-4e34c5 is also\n117:       added to `approval_decision_ids` above, being a protocol-approval gate\n118:       decision (verb `revise`). The other two have no home list: a\n119:       batch-opening `expand` and a lane-closing `synthesize` are neither\n120:       approvals nor evidence reviews, and inventing a place for them in an\n121:       existing list would misfile them.\n122:     decisions:\n123:       - id: DEC-20260907-38e5ae\n124:         role: lane opening and rerank (verb `expand`); approved no protocol and authorised no run\n125:         task: TASK-20260907-d47b50\n126:       - id: DEC-20260907-4e34c5\n127:         role: approval gate on PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v1-to-v2 as proposed in this lane (verb `revise`); refused the contract text on three blocking defects\n128:         task: TASK-20260907-f65c6e (fresh session; authored none of the gated artifacts)\n129:       - id: DEC-20260907-b6bcf4\n130:         role: lane close, compatibility read and rerank (verb `synthesize`); created no evidence record and changed no status\n131:         task: TASK-20260907-9e7580\n132:   lane_decision_ids_20260907_48ef8b:\n133:     added_by: TASK-20260907-1aa16f\n134:     note: >-\n135:       The three decisions of lane BATCH-48ef8b, listed with their roles for the\n136:       same reason BATCH-e9fd22's were: no existing list on this head fits all\n137:       three. DEC-20260907-adbe7e is also added to `approval_decision_ids` above,\n138:       being a protocol-approval gate decision (verb `revise`). The other two\n139:       have no home list -- a batch-opening authorship and a lane-closing\n140:       `synthesize` are neither approvals nor evidence reviews.\n141:     decisions:\n142:       - id: DEC-20260907-52f2a0\n143:         role: >-\n144:           lane opening and protocol authorship; approved no protocol and\n145:           authorised no run. Designing is not approving.\n146:         task: TASK-20260907-058c69\n147:       - id: DEC-20260907-adbe7e\n148:         role: >-\n149:           approval gate on PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3 (verb `revise`); recorded\n150:           all seven predecessor defects D1-D7 as DISCHARGED and refused on seven\n151:           blocking findings of its own about the coherence of the contract's own\n152:           instruction text\n153:         task: TASK-20260907-9c0626 (fresh session; authored none of the gated artifacts)\n154:       - id: DEC-20260907-de6b71\n155:         role: >-\n156:           lane close, prior-versus-outcome comparison and rerank (verb\n157:           `synthesize`); created no evidence record, reviewed none, and changed\n158:           no status\n159:         task: TASK-20260907-1aa16f\n160:   batch_48ef8b_disposition: >-\n161:     revised, closed by TASK-20260907-1aa16f / TASK-20260907-38f086\n162:     (DEC-20260907-de6b71; checkpoint\n163:     ledger/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/checkpoints/BATCH-48ef8b.yaml; lane close\n164:     report under the batch's TASK-20260907-1aa16f directory). Lane on\n165:     cursor/ecdlp-bbc21f-g3-feasibility-review-276e (PR #825), opened by\n166:     DEC-20260907-52f2a0. It authored PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3\n167:     (specification.v3.yaml, amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml, and a four-file derivation\n168:     packet whose reading path is a CLOSED POSITIVE ALLOWLIST rather than a\n169:     denylist), snapshot-archived it alone at 176b7d93e, and had it GATED by a\n170:     fresh Coordinator session that authored none of it. THE GATE RETURNED\n171:     `revise` (DEC-20260907-adbe7e) -- and it recorded ALL SEVEN PREDECESSOR\n172:     DEFECTS D1-D7 OF DEC-20260907-4e34c5 AS GENUINELY DISCHARGED, so a second\n173:     `revise` is NOT a re-refusal. It verified by RECOMPUTATION rather than by\n174:     reading (the cap convention and cap = ceil(8W) re-derived at all eight\n175:     (N, a) cells with zero discrepancies; the three-term basin-mass accounting\n176:     identity recomputed and closing at all 20 committed cells of\n177:     RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-001..005; every allowlist sha256 with zero mismatches; a\n178:     failing world constructed or refused for each of the fifteen declared\n179:     control items) and refused instead on SEVEN BLOCKING FINDINGS ABOUT THE\n180:     COHERENCE OF THE CONTRACT'S OWN INSTRUCTION TEXT: CF-1 (required_artifacts\n181:     demands a firing status for six items the contract elsewhere declares have\n182:     no firing condition, leaving an executor no correct action -- the round's one\n183:     OPERATIVE defect), CF-2 (the external anchor called \"independently\n184:     established\" where EV-ECDLP-60e266 reads `strength: preliminary`), CF-4\n185:     (DECAY-A clause (i) routing the batch's most severe falsification off a\n186:     zero-tolerance comparison while the interval estimator that could calibrate\n187:     it is declared to bind nothing), CF-5 (a summary partitioning fifteen items\n188:     as 11+3+2), LO-1 (the author's self-reported letter offset between the two\n189:     normative documents, ruled NOT ACCEPTABLE with a recorded remedy), and XR-1\n190:     / XR-2 (permuted and doubly-attributed CR-1 conditions), plus three\n191:     non-blocking. THE MATHEMATICS PASSED AND THE CONTRACT TEXT FAILED, in both\n192:     rounds -- recorded as finding TG-1 with the AM-1 authorship method it names.\n193:     NO RUN EVER EXECUTED IN THIS LANE: no evidence record exists, no hypothesis\n194:     status moved, no review verdict or attestation was obtained, and no\n195:     measurement about the ECDLP originates here. H-ECDLP-37dc01 stays `analyzed`\n196:     with no status_history entry. NO TASK WAS CANCELLED -- all six ran and all\n197:     six are `completed`, because this queue deliberately offered no producer\n198:     task at all, which is the repair for the five cancellations BATCH-e9fd22\n199:     owed. The lane's own LEAK DISCIPLINE HELD UNDER THE GATE'S AUDIT, across the\n200:     queue, all six task cards, all six handoffs, the opening decision, the\n201:     snapshot receipt and four commit messages -- the predecessor's exact failure\n202:     did not recur. Verified commits: snapshot 176b7d93e (backfilled at\n203:     c94a71b47), gate ledger archive bc4828129 (backfilled at 09c2e702b). THE\n204:     LANE ALSO CARRIES OUT ONE FINDING AGAINST AN APPROVED RECORD: CF-3, a\n205:     self-contradiction in the APPROVED, execution_authorized\n206:     experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml about the a = 1/4 anchor's\n207:     seed count and scale, settled by EV-ECDLP-60e266 lines 150-155; its remedy is\n208:     a SUPERSEDING RECORD, never an edit, its gate-named owner BATCH-8f3e86 has\n209:     closed, and DEC-20260907-de6b71 reassigns it as a required carried item of\n210:     the successor. Successor is the next_action below. Two premises this lane\n211:     opened under moved while it ran -- see\n212:     `external_work_advancing_this_goal_20260907_48ef8b`.\n213:   batch_e9fd22_disposition: >-\n214:     revised, closed by TASK-20260907-9e7580 (DEC-20260907-b6bcf4; checkpoint\n215:     ledger/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/checkpoints/BATCH-e9fd22.yaml). Lane on\n216:     cursor/ecdlp-bbc21f-g3-feasibility-review-276e (PR #825), opened by\n217:     DEC-20260907-38e5ae. It authored a wide 25-seed, two-scale, four-control\n218:     v1-to-v2 amendment of EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 and had it GATED AND REFUSED\n219:     (`revise`, DEC-20260907-4e34c5) by a fresh Coordinator session on three\n220:     blocking contract defects -- T stated as 102 at N = 2^20 against the frozen\n221:     64; the basin partition asserted exhaustive with cap = ceil(8W) absent\n222:     entirely; and the Coordinator's directional prior sitting on the Stage A'\n223:     re-deriver's pre-seal reading path in two committed files on no blind list.\n224:     NO RUN EVER EXECUTED IN THIS LANE: no evidence record exists, no hypothesis\n225:     status moved, and no measurement about the ECDLP originates here.\n226:     H-ECDLP-37dc01 stays `analyzed` with no status_history entry. Five\n227:     downstream tasks (e423d5 executor, 60957d snapshot, 6a2b2e validator,\n228:     3dff63 red team, 022c19 ledger archive) are CANCELLED with a recorded\n229:     reason -- they depended on an approved contract that does not exist -- and\n230:     the declared review round NEVER OPENED, so no joint was attested and the\n231:     recorded Coordinator prior stands untested. Verified commits: snapshot\n232:     5856b36e8 (backfilled at 752023e32), gate ledger archive f996864d2. The\n233:     lane produced four things worth carrying: TF-1 (the gate session's 20-cell\n234:     verification that weight_d = S_d + 4*W*h_d is the rule v1 production\n235:     computed), HB-1 (the head-blindness finding, below), IC-1 (one experiment\n236:     identifier now carries two v1-to-v2 amendments under one amendment id --\n237:     one approved and frozen, one `revision_required`; neither renamed, neither\n238:     superseded, disposition in DEC-20260907-b6bcf4), and CR-1 (the\n239:     compatibility read: the wide scope CAN be carried additively as a v2-to-v3\n240:     on the approved v2, under four named conditions). Successor is RANK 1 of\n241:     the next_action below. This lane's close writes no entry of BATCH-8f3e86.\n242:   batch_1e7251_disposition: >-\n243:     refine, closed by TASK-20260907-c264db (DEC-20260907-ece434,\n244:     EV-ECDLP-855daf). Disjoint lane on cursor/run-experiments-e393\n245:     (PR #821) executed PA-ECDLP-869870-v1-to-v2: 16/16 completed_valid\n246:     at N=2^24, a=1/4, T=256, 8 keys x splitmix64 + murmur3_fmix64;\n247:     snapshot 13bf12d0b; blinded J1-J4 all hold/PASS. fixture_gate_v2\n248:     not scored (O(theta) not_evaluated). H-ECDLP-3550b8 stays analyzed.\n249:     Goal-head next_action RANK 1/2 left untouched for other sessions.\n250:     This lane's successor is the O(theta) instantiation or a raw-gate\n251:     amendment (checkpoint BATCH-1e7251.yaml).\n252:   batch_f3a30a_disposition: >-\n253:     support (narrowly scoped), closed by TASK-20260906-ae5bb4\n254:     (DEC-20260906-bcc097). The v2-execution batch: the amended, approved\n255:     contract (DEC-20260906-806501) ran to completion (16 of 16 planned runs,\n256:     TASK-20260906-5e78c7: Stage 0 a-scan, Stage 1v2 at 2^24, Stage 2v2 at\n257:     2^30, Stage 4v2 analysis; all completed_valid), was snapshot-archived\n258:     alone at 22e80f133 (TASK-20260906-1e5ea4), and was reviewed by two\n259:     mutually blind fresh sessions under a review_plan written first\n260:     (validator TASK-20260906-bc1cfc: J1 HOLDS_WITH_FINDINGS, J2 HOLDS; red\n261:     team TASK-20260906-a6b415: J3 HOLDS_WITH_FINDINGS, J4\n262:     HOLDS_WITH_FINDINGS; no breaking artifact on any of the four owned\n263:     joints). EV-ECDLP-f6b3f5 (H-ECDLP-37dc01, direction supports, strength\n264:     preliminary, proof_status empirical_only): G3 PASSES 5/5 seeds at all\n265:     four tested (N, T_sel) cells (unlike v1's T_sel = T/2 cell, FAIL 10/10),\n266:     so every S1_v2/F1_v2 outcome is a real, gate-cleared measurement; S1_v2\n267:     MET at 3 of 4 cells (2^24 0.65T borderline and 0.75T; 2^30 0.75T), NOT\n268:     MET at 2^30 0.65T; F1_v2 fires nowhere; S2_v2 (one-sided null) NOT MET\n269:     at every cell (NULL-A's own perturbation 2-3x the measured effect).\n270:     Per the frozen v2 contract's own OVERALL wording this supports a\n271:     RE-SCOPED effect clause (T_sel in {0.65T, 0.75T}, S_peak charged, 881-\n272:     1029.5 bits/T) -- it does NOT rehabilitate clause (C1) as originally\n273:     stated (T_sel = T/2), which remains contradicted by disjointness,\n274:     unchanged from BATCH-289698. This Coordinator additionally surfaced an\n275:     discrepancy in the executor's own Stage 0 a-scan interpretation,\n276:     subsequently NUMERICALLY CONFIRMED by the orchestrating session from the\n277:     raw per-seed run data by a second, independent route: applying the\n278:     contract's own G3 rule directly shows T_sel = T/2 IS G3-feasible at\n279:     a = 1/16 (5/5 seeds, margins +0.0196/+0.0122/+0.0240/+0.0163/+0.0092)\n280:     and a = 1/8 (4/5 seeds, margins +0.0032/-0.0020/+0.0103/+0.0050/+0.0071)\n281:     -- directly contradicting execution_report.yaml's stated \"no feasible\n282:     point found.\" The numbers are confirmed; FORMAL independent review\n283:     (blind rederivation, proves-too-much control) has not yet been applied,\n284:     so this is carried forward as RANK 1 of the next action, not adopted as\n285:     a hypothesis-relevant finding. Hypothesis status stays `analyzed`\n286:     (status_history entry added, no procedural transition): single\n287:     unreplicated batch, S2_v2's unresolved magnitude confound, the missing\n288:     permanent null-collapse regression fixture (red team J4 coverage-gap\n289:     finding), and the not-yet-formally-reviewed Stage 0 discrepancy all\n290:     argue against promotion. Checkpoint shard checkpoints/BATCH-f3a30a.yaml.\n291:   batch_289698_disposition: >-\n292:     weaken, closed by TASK-20260906-aa3dd2 (DEC-20260906-1f5b71). The first\n293:     execution batch: both approved contracts ran to completion\n294:     (EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 37 runs incl. Stage 3 curve cells, 19850/19850\n295:     certificates; EXP-ECDLP-869870 24 runs, 404028 certificates), were\n296:     snapshot-archived alone at 840df8a5 (TASK-20260906-7a2446), and were\n297:     reviewed by two mutually blind fresh sessions under a review_plan\n298:     written first (validator TASK-20260906-7ec3ea: J1, J2\n299:     HOLDS_WITH_FINDINGS; red team TASK-20260906-90e7cf: J3 BROKEN, J4\n300:     BROKEN narrowly); check_review_independence.py PASS. The Coordinator's\n301:     recorded prior (S1-S4 pass, rho_T(8T) near 0.51, break if any in J1)\n302:     was OVERTURNED on J3 and J1 was clean. EV-ECDLP-60e266 (H-ECDLP-37dc01,\n303:     direction weakens, strength preliminary, proof_status derivation, full\n304:     obstruction block): the T/2 re-selected table does NOT reach static T\n305:     (S1 CI-separated below at both N and on the curve; F1's 0.85 letter not\n306:     met; the outcome in a cell the contract did not name) and was\n307:     infeasible by disjointness at a = 1/4 (exact top-T/2 share below\n308:     STATIC(T) coverage in 10/10 seeds); measured rho_T(8T) = 0.654 [0.620,\n309:     0.700] (2^24) / 0.688 [0.664, 0.706] (2^30), rho_T(16T) = 0.619 /\n310:     0.632, oracle floor about 0.55, S_peak 2.6-8.9 T, early-batch penalty\n311:     0.13-0.15; a tradeoff point under RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5's fewer_DP\n312:     definition; mechanism clauses supported at toy scale. EV-ECDLP-31e91c\n313:     (H-ECDLP-3550b8, neutral, inconclusive): the 2^24 fixture gate FAILED\n314:     (one cost cell by 0.0005, four precomputation cells) so the 2^24+ cells\n315:     are invalid-for-interpretation under rule 3; nothing scored; the\n316:     headline cell is band-edge under re-keying (J2-F1). Both hypotheses\n317:     specified -> approved -> running -> analyzed (never weakened /\n318:     supported from one batch). C1 and C3 met on the verified commit of that\n319:     archive (negative direction; obstruction over the tested scope); C2 NOT\n320:     met. Checkpoint shard checkpoints/BATCH-289698.yaml.\n321:   batch_252a44_disposition: >-\n322:     approve_experiment, closed by TASK-20260906-773a2e.\n323:   completion_criteria_progress_20260906_f3a30a: >-\n324:     Recorded additively by TASK-20260906-ae5bb4 (BATCH-f3a30a's ledger\n325:     archive). The `status` fields in `completion_criteria` below (C1, C3)\n326:     are flipped from OPEN to MET by this authorship: BATCH-289698's own\n327:     checkpoint already narratively established C1 and C3 as met on the\n328:     verified BATCH-289698 commit, but explicitly deferred flipping the\n329:     declarative `status` field to \"the successor ledger archive\"; that flip\n330:     was not performed by BATCH-252a44's archive (an approval-only batch with\n331:     no evidence review), so it is performed here, now that BATCH-289698's\n332:     commit is long since verified. C1 is MET, in EITHER-direction terms per\n333:     its own statement: the negative T_sel = T/2 finding (EV-ECDLP-60e266)\n334:     and this batch's re-scoped, G3-gated T_sel_grid_v2 measurement\n335:     (EV-ECDLP-f6b3f5) together are the committed, independently validated\n336:     and red-teamed evidence the criterion asks for, on the tested\n337:     (N, a, r, k, cap, walk, solver) grid at claim_tier toy. C3 is MET,\n338:     unchanged: EV-ECDLP-60e266's obstruction block (T_sel = T/2 dis