79:     status: MET\n480:     status_note: >-\n481:       Flipped OPEN -> MET by TASK-20260906-ae5bb4 (BATCH-f3a30a), per\n482:       completion_criteria_progress_20260906_f3a30a: EV-ECDLP-60e266's\n483:       obstruction block (T_sel = T/2 disjointness at a = 1/4, with a\n484:       genuine resource_check) satisfies this criterion, unchanged and not\n485:       retested by BATCH-f3a30a.\n486:   pause_conditions:\n487:   - a snapshot or ledger archive fails post-commit verification\n488:   - a required review policy cannot be honoured without a silent downgrade\n489:   - the toy-curve arm cannot certify a solved logarithm\n490:   - the user declines approval and gives no revision direction\n491:   runtime_constraint_note: >-\n492:     Recorded before dispatch, as on GOAL-ECRANK-002. Under the claude_code\n493:     runtime the `coordinator` subagent has no shell, so it cannot itself run\n494:     `git add`/`git commit`/`git push` or `gh pr create`. For THIS campaign the\n495:     split is declared up front: the Coordinator authors every archive record\n496:     and every status transition via Write, and the orchestrating session\n497:     performs only the mechanical git and PR commands over exactly the paths\n498:     the Coordinator declared. Authorship of state transitions stays with the\n499:     Coordinator; only the shell call moves. Each archive receipt records this\n500:     split so it is auditable and never mistaken for a worker committing to\n501:     shared state.\n502:   next_action_superseded_20260906_9c5410: >-\n503:     ONE ACTION, and it is a GATE, not compute. Put the approval question for\n504:     the two unapproved frozen contracts EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 (H-ECDLP-37dc01, the\n505:     batch-reselected fixed-size table) and EXP-ECDLP-869870 (H-ECDLP-3550b8,\n506:     the basin-partition coverage instrument) to the USER, per\n507:     design-experiment step 4 and the GOAL-ECRANK-002 precedent\n508:     (DEC-20260905-2d466e, BATCH-832f3d); the exact question text is in the\n509:     BATCH-9c5410 batch report. The question has NOT yet been put and nothing\n510:     in this record asserts an answer. On the recorded answer run\n511:     TASK-20260906-67f1ab (approval authorship, coordinator inline under the\n512:     declared fallback): ON APPROVAL of a contract, its gate fields only\n513:     (status, approved_by, approval_note, frozen, execution_authorized --\n514:     protocol fields byte-identical, version stays 1) and the executor\n515:     handoffs TASK-20260906-3623b9 (EXP-ECDLP-612fb1) and/or\n516:     TASK-20260906-d17254 (EXP-ECDLP-869870) carrying each contract's budget\n517:     envelope verbatim; ON DECLINE, no gate field changes, no executor\n518:     handoff, and both hypotheses staying `specified`. Then\n519:     TASK-20260906-2d30dd (ledger archive, runs ALONE) AUTHORS\n520:     DEC-20260906-2b1387 -- approve_experiment with the question and the\n521:     user's answer recorded verbatim, or `revise` with the user's stated\n522:     reason -- exactly as 59fb55 authored DEC-20260905-2d466e in the\n523:     precedent, binds it with the package and this goal head, and the branch\n524:     is pushed and its PR refreshed naming the records. Until that archive\n525:     lands and is verified: approved_by stays null on both contracts and zero\n526:     compute is spent. RANK 2 (the NEXT batch, opened only after that ledger\n527:     archive merges to main): the EXECUTION batch dispatching the approved\n528:     executor task(s) from the approved contract(s) on main, with the snapshot\n529:     TASK-20260906-7a2446, the validator TASK-20260906-7ec3ea (blind\n530:     re-derivation of the 1.79 fixture and of the exact top-T share at 2^24\n531:     from the statement of the quantities) and the red team\n532:     TASK-20260906-90e7cf (the null and fixture-procedure design) RESERVED, all\n533:     three under a review_plan written BEFORE either reviewer runs; those three\n534:     ids are reserved, not dispatchable, and appear in no queue yet. RANK 3:\n535:     /design-experiment on IDEA-20260906-a3d6ae (the growth-with-relations\n536:     comparator that EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 cites as its frontier point) and on the\n537:     c-sweep of IDEA-20260906-05ffb8 (scored by the 869870 instrument);\n538:     IDEA-20260906-cf3b76 (walk-rule invariance of C_max) and\n539:     IDEA-20260906-ac100b (the (B1)-(B3) derivation, a validator task) as\n540:     cheap closures. C1, C2 and C3 are all OPEN. Batch history: none --\n541:     BATCH-9c5410 is this campaign's first batch.\n542:   next_action_superseded_20260906_289698: >-\n543:     RANK 1: open the execution batch BATCH-289698 on branch\n544:     claude/batch-dlp-precomputation-nov7vh from the approved contracts\n545:     (DEC-20260906-2b1387): executor tasks TASK-20260906-3623b9\n546:     (EXP-ECDLP-612fb1, Stage G + Stages 1-2) and TASK-20260906-d17254\n547:     (EXP-ECDLP-869870, Stages 1-2), then snapshot TASK-20260906-7a2446 alone,\n548:     then validator TASK-20260906-7ec3ea and red team TASK-20260906-90e7cf as\n549:     fresh independent sessions under a review_plan written first, then ledger\n550:     archive TASK-20260906-aa3dd2 with EV records, decision, and hypothesis\n551:     transitions. RANK 2: Stage 3 and the curve arms if budget remains. RANK 3:\n552:     design IDEA-20260906-a3d6ae and the c-sweep of IDEA-20260906-05ffb8;\n553:     cf3b76 and ac100b as cheap closures. C1, C2 and C3 are all OPEN. Batch\n554:     history: BATCH-9c5410 (approval gate, zero execution) at\n555:     DEC-20260906-2b1387.\n556:   next_action_superseded_20260906_252a44: >-\n557:     RANK 1 (the ONE next action; a new BATCH-<tok> minted at opening, after\n558:     the BATCH-289698 ledger archive is verified and merged to main): author\n559:     a VERSIONED AMENDMENT v2 of EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 under\n560:     experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/amendments/ (v1 frozen and untouched;\n561:     executed runs never re-scored) carrying DEC-20260906-1f5b71's items\n562:     (a)-(h): a ceiling-feasibility gate G3 from the exact basins (exact\n563:     top-T_sel share >= STATIC(T) exact coverage in >= 4/5 seeds before S1 is\n564:     testable; failure = untestable, never negative); an S1 non-vacuity\n565:     guard (STATIC(T) eps_ss >= 0.5 and CI-separated above RHO by >= 0.30;\n566:     tolerance 5% of the STATIC(T) - RHO gap; rho_T CI excluding 1.0 and\n567:     uncensored; U_ss/U* margins relative); S2 restated one-sided as the\n568:     null's expected sign (NULL-A gain not CI-separated above zero and\n569:     <= 0.5 x the RESEL-L gain; the null's own perturbation recorded); the\n570:     headline restated as T_resel/T_static at fixed success WITH S_peak\n571:     CHARGED, reported as the frontier tuple (T_sel/T, S_peak/T, P/sqrt(NT),\n572:     L, eps_ss, eps_cum, U, early penalty) with rho_ORACLE and rho_cum\n573:     beside rho_ss and U* stated explicitly when unreachable; HEUR-BLT-7\n574:     with the admitted-walk count; the pool cap applied per admission so\n575:     CAP(2T) is 2 T; fit_cutoff None -> G1 FAIL with the two bijection seeds\n576:     as a permanent negative fixture; and the 2^20 a-scan of ORACLE(T/2) -\n577:     STATIC(T) run FIRST (seconds per cell) with (C6) replaced by the\n578:     ordering prediction rho_ORACLE(a = 1/4) < rho_ORACLE(a = 1/2). Put the\n579:     amendment to the USER (design-experiment step 4) and record the answer\n580:     in a committed approval decision; THEN a re-run batch under v2 at\n581:     T_sel in {0.65T, 0.75T} at N in {2^24, 2^30}, a = 1/4, r = 2, k = 4,\n582:     5 seeds, S_peak charged, PAIRED with /design-experiment on\n583:     IDEA-20260906-a3d6ae (the growth-type comparator the obstruction's\n584:     resource_check names) so the re-run's frontier table has its fair\n585:     comparator; snapshot alone, mutually blind validator and red team under\n586:     a review_plan written first, then ledger archive -- the replication\n587:     that `weaken` on H-ECDLP-37dc01 owes before any further transition.\n588:     That successor archive also flips the completion_criteria status\n589:     fields (C1 met, C3 met, C2 open) after this archive's post-commit\n590:     verification. RANK 2: the EXP-ECDLP-869870 successor cell -- a\n591:     re-keyed 2^24 fixture (>= 8 keys per instrument, murmur3 and splitmix64\n592:     as the validator's J2 ran them, capped-mass fraction beside every cell)\n593:     under a versioned amendment that states the O(theta) correction before\n594:     comparing at 2^24 or gates at 2^30, fits the N-drift trend on\n595:     2^22-2^24, re-states the survival-slope band against the finite-theta\n596:     Borel value under the declared estimator, and runs the gate in its own\n597:     run record before any later stage; V1-V5 / M1-M5 scored and the\n598:     constants citable (and C2 closable) only after it passes. RANK 3: the\n599:     IDEA-20260906-05ffb8 c-sweep (scored by the validated instrument),\n600:     IDEA-20260906-cf3b76 (walk-rule invariance of C_max; the labelled\n601:     r_walk = 16 / 32 KS observations on TOY-P24-a6ee37f9 are its first data\n602:     points) and IDEA-20260906-ac100b (the (B1)-(B3) derivation as a\n603:     validator task) as cheap closures. Criteria after BATCH-289698: C1 met\n604:     (negative direction, preliminary) and C3 met (T/2 cell, a = 1/4) on the\n605:     verified commit; C2 NOT met. Batch history: BATCH-9c5410 (approval\n606:     gate, zero execution) at DEC-20260906-2b1387; BATCH-289698 (first\n607:     execution batch, weaken) at DEC-20260906-1f5b71.\n608:   next_action_superseded_20260906_f3a30a: >-\n609:     \"RANK 1: open the execution batch (a new BATCH-<tok>, minted at opening)\n610:     on branch claude/batch-dlp-precomputation-nov7vh from the approved v2\n611:     contract (DEC-20260906-806501): executor task TASK-20260906-5e78c7\n612:     (source_v2/, Stage 0 a-scan first, then Stage 1v2/2v2 at T_sel in\n613:     {0.65T,0.75T}, N in {2^24,2^30}), then a Coordinator snapshot alone,\n614:     then an independent validator and red team under a review_plan written\n615:     before either runs (same posture as BATCH-289698: mutual blindness, a\n616:     pre-recorded Coordinator prior, at least one proves-too-much object and\n617:     one blind re-derivation), then a ledger archive with EV/DEC records and\n618:     the H-ECDLP-37dc01 status transition the results warrant. RANK 2: the\n619:     EXP-ECDLP-869870 successor cell (re-keyed 2^24 fixture) under its own\n620:     versioned amendment, per DEC-20260906-1f5b71's EXP_ECDLP_869870\n621:     disposition. RANK 3: IDEA-20260906-a3d6ae (growth-type comparator) and\n622:     the c-sweep/cf3b76/ac100b closures.\" DISCHARGED IN FULL for\n623:     EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 by BATCH-f3a30a (DEC-20260906-bcc097); RANK 2 and\n624:     RANK 3 above are UNCHANGED and carried forward, now re-ranked as RANK 3\n625:     and RANK 4 of the new next_action below, behind a new RANK 1/2 this\n626:     archive opens.\n627:   rerank_20260907_e9fd22:\n628:     by: DEC-20260907-38e5ae\n629:     batch_opened: BATCH-e9fd22\n630:     what_changed: >-\n631:       The next_action recorded on 2026-09-06 was STALE, not wrong when written.\n632:       Its RANK 1 (the N = 2^24 exact-basin, blind-re-derived check of whether\n633:       T_sel = T/2 is G3-feasible at a in {1/16, 1/8}) WAS EXECUTED on 2026-09-07\n634:       as EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 under BATCH-3c7493, with a sealed blind re-derivation\n635:       and a proves-too-much control, and was ledger-archived at commit 84233e8c3\n636:       under DEC-20260907-9b1b02. This goal's own bookkeeping never saw it:\n637:       DEC-20260907-9b1b02 carries goal_id: null, and BATCH-3c7493 was opened\n638:       under coordination/experiments/ rather than under this goal's lane\n639:       directory, so no checkpoint shard was written against this head. The\n640:       next_action below is REPLACED by DEC-20260907-9b1b02's own ranking, which\n641:       supersedes it on the merits and on the date.\n642:     outcome_of_the_superseded_rank_1: >-\n643:       Recorded in DEC-20260907-9b1b02 and EV-ECDLP-2e9680, cited here and not\n644:       restated: three of four cells resolved with both readings agreeing, and\n645:       one cell (a = 1/8) resolved to a genuine blind-versus-production\n646:       disagreement whose root cause was traced to an underspecification in\n647:       EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 v1's own contract text. Nothing in this rerank asserts,\n648:       re-scores, or reinterprets any of those findings.\n649:     superseded_next_action_preserved_verbatim: >-\n650:       Held once, byte-for-byte, under the top-level key\n651:       `next_action_superseded_20260906` below. It is stored in exactly one place\n652:       on purpose: a superseded ranking copied into two keys is a ranking that\n653:       can later disagree with itself, and a reader has no way to tell which copy\n654:       is the original.\n655:     lane_note: >-\n656:       Additive to this head only. No other lane's entries are touched. The three\n657:       prior lanes (BATCH-252a44, BATCH-289698, BATCH-f3a30a) remain closed and\n658:       their checkpoint shards are unmodified.\n659:   external_work_advancing_this_goal_20260907_e9fd22:\n660:     added_by: TASK-20260907-9e7580\n661:     finding_id: HB-1\n662:     why_this_key_exists: >-\n663:       THE HEAD WAS BLIND TO WORK THAT ADVANCED THIS GOAL, AND IT WILL BE AGAIN\n664:       UNLESS THE RECORDS ARE NAMED HERE. The next_action committed 2026-09-06\n665:       asked for exactly the N = 2^24 exact-basin, blind-re-derived check of\n666:       T_sel = T/2 at a in {1/16, 1/8} that EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 had already\n667:       performed and archived. Three independent mechanisms hid it: BATCH-3c7493\n668:       was opened under coordination/experiments/ rather than under this goal's\n669:       lane directory, so `tools/goal_lanes.py lanes` never listed it; its\n670:       dispatch queue carries `goal_id: GOAL-ECDLP-001` because\n671:       EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 and H-ECDLP-37dc01 both declare `goal_id: null`; and no\n672:       checkpoint shard was ever written for it under this goal's\n673:       `checkpoints/`. Each alone is sufficient. GENERIC STATEMENT: work\n674:       archived against one goal identifier is invisible to the head of the goal\n675:       it actually advances, and a head read is no substitute for reading the\n676:       decisions.\n677:     records_that_advance_this_goal_despite_carrying_goal_id_null_or_GOAL_ECDLP_001:\n678:       - id: EXP-ECDLP-6ac801\n679:         what: 'the N = 2^24 exact-basin G3-feasibility contract at a in {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4}, r = 2, T_sel = T/2; declares goal_id: null'\n680:         paths: 'experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/ (specification.yaml v1 frozen; specification.v2.yaml APPROVED, another lane''s; specification.v2.BATCH-e9fd22-proposed.yaml revision_required)'\n681:       - id: BATCH-3c7493\n682:         what: 'the batch that executed it (6 runs RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-001..006, all completed_valid, plus the sealed Stage A blind re-derivation TASK-20260907-80e198); its queue carries goal_id: GOAL-ECDLP-001'\n683:         paths: coordination/experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/batches/BATCH-3c7493/\n684:         registered_as_a_lane_of_this_goal: false\n685:         checkpoint_shard_under_this_goal: none\n686:       - id: EV-ECDLP-2e9680\n687:         what: 'its per-cell evidence: a = 1/16 S1 CONFIRMED FEASIBLE (blind and production agreeing 5/5), a = 3/16 and a = 1/4 S2 CONFIRMED INFEASIBLE, a = 1/8 S3 DISAGREEMENT at the literal sealed level'\n688:       - id: DEC-20260907-9b1b02\n689:         what: >-\n690:           THE AUTHORITATIVE CURRENT SCIENCE RANKING FOR THIS GOAL, and the\n691:           record any session resuming here must read before the next_action\n692:           below. It records a = 1/8 as GENUINELY OPEN, root-causes the\n693:           disagreement to an underspecification in v1's own contract text\n694:           rather than to a scientific question, declines to relabel the cell on\n695:           a post-hoc non-blind diagnostic, and leaves four ranked next actions\n696:           standing. Committed at 84233e8c3.\n697:     what_this_key_does_not_do: >-\n698:       It changes no `goal_id` field, creates no GOAL binding on any record, and\n699:       does not retroactively register BATCH-3c7493 as a lane. Those are\n700:       additive acts on records this lane does not own and they stay as RANK 5\n701:       of the next_action below. This key is a POINTER so the next head read is\n702:       not blind; the records themselves are unmodified.\n703:     scope: >-\n704:       Observed on this goal for BATCH-3c7493 / EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 only. No other\n705:       goal was audited for the same pattern.\n706:   external_work_advancing_this_goal_20260907_48ef8b:\n707:     added_by: TASK-20260907-1aa16f\n708:     finding_id: HB-1 (SECOND RECORDED RECURRENCE)\n709:     carries_forward_verbatim_in_substance: >-\n710:       EVERY BINDING THE PREDECESSOR RECORDED IN\n711:       `external_work_advancing_this_goal_20260907_e9fd22` ABOVE STILL HOLDS AND\n712:       IS NOT RESTATED HERE. EXP-ECDLP-6ac801, BATCH-3c7493, EV-ECDLP-2e9680 and\n713:       DEC-20260907-9b1b02 all advance THIS goal while declaring\n714:       `goal_id: GOAL-ECDLP-001` or `null`; none of their `goal_id` fields is\n715:       changed by this close and BATCH-3c7493 is still not registered as a lane.\n716:       This key ADDS the records that landed since, and records that the same\n717:       mechanism cost this lane something concrete.\n718:     why_this_key_exists: >-\n719:       HB-1 RECURRED, AND ITS COST THIS TIME IS NAMEABLE: THIS LANE'S OWN RANK 1\n720:       WAS AUTHORED AGAINST A PREMISE THAT HAD ALREADY BEEN OVERTAKEN ON MAIN.\n721:       The lane was opened on the premise -- carried by the goal head's\n722:       next_action and by DEC-20260907-b6bcf4 -- that the a = 1/8 cell of\n723:       EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 is GENUINELY OPEN. It is not: the Stage A' re-seal under\n724:       the approved v2 had already run and been archived. Commit 0dbbbd9a0 was\n725:       reachable at this lane's opening snapshot 176b7d93e, but this lane's\n726:       opening deliberately writes no head, so this close is the first head write\n727:       on this branch with it reachable. NO RECORD IS AT FAULT. The mechanism is\n728:       exactly the one HB-1 named: work archived against one goal identifier is\n729:       invisible to the head of the goal it advances, and a head read is no\n730:       substitute for reading the decisions.\n731:     records_that_advance_this_goal_and_were_not_visible_from_this_head:\n732:       - id: EV-ECDLP-6783b8\n733:         what: >-\n734:           TASK-20260907-2db9aa's freshly sealed, from-scratch blind\n735:           re-derivation of a = 1/8 at N = 2^24 under the approved v2's\n736:           now-explicit selection formula, using a wholly independent\n737:           implementation (independently constructed uniform random self-map\n738:           table, independent Bernoulli marking, exact binary-lifting absorption\n739:           -- NOT source_v2/instrument.py) with the required proves-too-much\n740:           control at a = 1/4. Terminal verdict S1 CONFIRMED FEASIBLE under v2's\n741:           own taxonomy: the two readings AGREE on the categorical verdict, with\n742:           one opposite-sign draw in the blind sample disclosed and judged within\n743:           seed-to-seed noise at the contract's most borderline cell.\n744:           `strength: preliminary`, `claim_tier: toy`.\n745:       - id: DEC-20260907-8d8782\n746:         what: >-\n747:           Its evidence-review decision, verb `support`, scoped exactly to that\n748:           ceiling-feasibility confirmation, recording its own RANK 1 (the v2\n749:           amendment and the a = 1/8 re-seal) as DISCHARGED. Committed at\n750:           0dbbbd9a0, reachable on this branch through the 631c524a7 merge.\n751:       - id: BATCH-8f3e86 (now CLOSED)\n752:         what: >-\n753:           Another session's lane on cursor/run-experiments-batch-93e3, CLOSED\n754:           2026-09-07 (PR #829, merged to main at f24293a5f; checkpoint\n755:           ledger/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/checkpoints/BATCH-8f3e86.yaml). It\n756:           measured the same question on a DIFFERENT experiment (EXP-ECDLP-612fb1\n757:           v3) and reached a structurally identical result at a = 1/8:\n758:           EV-ECDLP-6a4ebc (`strength: preliminary`), DEC-20260907-6d9427 (verb\n759:           `replicate`). Its validator joint J2 is recorded BREAKS on the\n760:           per-seed sign disagreement, and its residual R3 -- an independent third\n761:           angle -- is NOT discharged, because its STAGE 3B imports the same\n762:           frozen source_v2/instrument.py that EXP-ECDLP-6ac801's production arm\n763:           imported. ITS ENTRIES ON THIS HEAD ARE NOT WRITTEN BY THIS CLOSE and\n764:           none were found to write; it is recorded here as a fact read from\n765:           `tools/goal_lanes.py` and from committed records.\n766:     what_these_records_do_and_do_not_settle: >-\n767:       a = 1/8 IS CONFIRMED CEILING-FEASIBLE AT N = 2^24 AT `preliminary`\n768:       STRENGTH, twice, on two instruments. That is all. Both records are\n769:       `preliminary` and `claim_tier: toy` by their own declarations, both rest on\n770:       small samples, one carries a review joint recorded BREAKS on a per-seed\n771:       sign disagreement and an undischarged independent-third-angle residual, and\n772:       neither is reviewed, re-scored or promoted by this close. What they jointly\n773:       establish is that a = 1/8 is a BORDERLINE CELL, which is why the successor\n774:       contract's objective statement must be rewritten rather than inherited.\n775:     carried_finding_CT_3: >-\n776:       THE HEAD IS STILL NOT A RELIABLE INDEX OF WHICH LANES ARE LIVE, exactly as\n777:       DEC-20260907-52f2a0 recorded it as CT-3: `current_batch_id` is null,\n778:       `dispatch_queue_path` names a closed lane, and `open_batches` is empty.\n779:       Its 2026-09-07 statement that BATCH-8f3e86 is open is now stale as well\n\n(Output capped at 50 KB. Showing lines 1-779. Use offset=780 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"research_goal:\n  id: GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f\n  id_allocation_provenance: >-\n    Token minted 2026-09-06 by the orchestrating session with `python3\n    tools/allocate_id.py --next goal --area ECDLP`, confirmed free with\n    `--check`, and relayed to the coordinator in the in-session campaign-open\n    handoff. Not derived by scanning state. Every other identifier named in\n    this record (BATCH-9c5410, TASK-20260906-67f1ab, TASK-20260906-2d30dd,\n    DEC-20260906-2b1387, TASK-20260906-3623b9, TASK-20260906-d17254,\n    TASK-20260906-7a2446, TASK-20260906-7ec3ea, TASK-20260906-90e7cf) was\n    pre-minted and `--check`ed the same way by that session; the coordinator\n    minted nothing and grepped for nothing.\n  title: >-\n    Batch ECDLP with precomputation: fewer stored distinguished points at\n    fixed online cost\n  objective: >-\n    Measure, with independent validation and red-team review, whether the\n    batch-reselected fixed-size table (H-ECDLP-37dc01, contract\n    EXP-ECDLP-612fb1) and the basin-partition coverage instrument\n    (H-ECDLP-3550b8, contract EXP-ECDLP-869870) answer RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5 in","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/ledger/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/goal.yaml","text":"research_goal:\n  id: GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f\n  id_allocation_provenance: >-\n    Token minted 2026-09-06 by the orchestrating session with `python3\n    tools/allocate_id.py --next goal --area ECDLP`, confirmed free with\n    `--check`, and relayed to the coordinator in the in-session campaign-open\n    handoff. Not derived by scanning state. Every other identifier named in\n    this record (BATCH-9c5410, TASK-20260906-67f1ab, TASK-20260906-2d30dd,\n    DEC-20260906-2b1387, TASK-20260906-3623b9, TASK-20260906-d17254,\n    TASK-20260906-7a2446, TASK-20260906-7ec3ea, TASK-20260906-90e7cf) was\n    pre-minted and `--check`ed the same way by that session; the coordinator\n    minted nothing and grepped for nothing.\n  title: >-\n    Batch ECDLP with precomputation: fewer stored distinguished points at\n    fixed online cost\n  objective: >-\n    Measure, with independent validation and red-team review, whether the\n    batch-reselected fixed-size table (H-ECDLP-37dc01, contract\n    EXP-ECDLP-612fb1) and the basin-partition coverage instrument\n    (H-ECDLP-3550b8, contract EXP-ECDLP-869870) answer RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5 in\n    EITHER direction with a measured constant and a confidence interval:\n    whether the number of stored distinguished points T needed for a fixed\n    per-target online cost and success probability can be reduced below the\n    selected Bernstein-Lange table in a fully charged (P, S, L, epsilon, U)\n    cost model, and by what factor. Every result of this campaign is\n    constant-factor, generic, claim_tier toy, and sits under the\n    Corrigan-Gibbs-Kogan S T^2 = Omega~(eps N) ceiling (KN-LIT-013); no\n    exponent is targeted and the campaign says so at every step. A negative\n    batch narrows the constant's known range; only a measured obstruction\n    block per docs/inventor-protocol.md closes a lane.\n  question_ids:\n  - RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5\n  active_hypothesis_ids:\n  - H-ECDLP-37dc01\n  - H-ECDLP-3550b8\n  status: active\n  impediments: []\n  runtime:\n    provider: none\n    goal_id: GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f\n  ecc_classification: >-\n    Area ECDLP is declared in orchestration/research-priority.yaml\n    `ecc_areas` (read through tools/ecc_priority.py, never inferred from the\n    identifier prefix), so this goal is ECC by policy: it is selected before\n    every non-ECC goal at every selection point, and its campaign budget\n    carries no batch or wall-clock ceiling (AGENTS.md \"ECC comes first\",\n    user instruction 2026-09-04). Unlimited removes the ceiling, not the duty\n    to rank -- every batch on this goal still ranks its task ahead of doing\n    nothing.\n  campaign_budget:\n    maximum_batches: null\n    total_wall_clock_seconds: null\n    max_concurrent: 2\n    unlimited_budget_note_20260906: >-\n      ECC goal: campaign budget is UNLIMITED by declared policy\n      (orchestration/research-priority.yaml, user instruction 2026-09-04);\n      maximum_batches and total_wall_clock_seconds are null from creation\n      and check_ecc_budget_is_unlimited enforces it. max_concurrent stays\n      bounded -- it is machine headroom, not a research budget: this is a\n      4-core, 15 GB container and 2 is its headroom (each contract declares\n      maximum_workers 1 and maximum_memory_gb 8). Per-experiment budgets\n      remain those frozen in each contract and are never raised by this\n      field.\n  current_batch_id: null\n  current_batch_id_note_20260907_e9fd22: >-\n    Set to null by TASK-20260907-9e7580: BATCH-e9fd22 is CLOSED (see\n    `batch_e9fd22_disposition`) and this head owns no other open lane. Previous\n    value: BATCH-e9fd22. It is not repointed at BATCH-8f3e86 -- that is another\n    session's open lane on another branch and this head does not write its\n    entries. The next session opening a lane on this goal sets both this field\n    and `dispatch_queue_path` to its own.\n  dispatch_queue_path: coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-e9fd22/dispatch_queue.json\n  dispatch_queue_path_note_20260907_e9fd22: >-\n    Left pointing at BATCH-e9fd22's queue, which is the last queue this head\n    owned and is now terminal: TASK-20260907-d47b50, TASK-20260907-4ce154,\n    TASK-20260907-f65c6e, TASK-20260907-ceb8cf and TASK-20260907-9e7580 are\n    `completed` and the five downstream tasks are `cancelled` with a recorded\n    reason, so rendering it offers nothing. It is retained rather than nulled\n    so the record of what this lane's graph was stays reachable from the head.\n  open_batches: []\n  open_batches_note_20260907_e9fd22: >-\n    Emptied by TASK-20260907-9e7580 on closing BATCH-e9fd22. THIS LIST IS NOT\n    THE AUTHORITATIVE SET OF OPEN LANES ON THIS GOAL: it holds only lanes\n    registered through this head, and lane state lives in write-once side files\n    (`coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/lanes/`). Read\n    `python3 tools/goal_lanes.py lanes GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f` instead. As of\n    2026-09-07 that command reports BATCH-8f3e86 OPEN on branch\n    cursor/run-experiments-batch-93e3 (opened by coordinator-ecdlp-8f3e86) --\n    recorded here as a fact read from the tool, deliberately NOT added to this\n    list, because adding it would be writing another lane's head entry.\n  open_batches_note_20260907_48ef8b: >-\n    Re-read by TASK-20260907-1aa16f on closing BATCH-48ef8b, and STILL EMPTY.\n    `python3 tools/goal_lanes.py lanes GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f` as of 2026-09-07 now\n    reports EVERY lane of this goal CLOSED -- BATCH-1e7251, BATCH-252a44,\n    BATCH-289698, BATCH-8f3e86, BATCH-e9fd22, BATCH-f3a30a, and BATCH-48ef8b\n    itself on its own close. BATCH-8f3e86, which the note above records as OPEN\n    and which was open when that note was written, closed on branch\n    cursor/run-experiments-batch-93e3 (PR #829, merged to main at f24293a5f) and\n    arrived on this branch in the origin/main merge 4e737c70e. THIS LIST IS\n    STILL NOT THE AUTHORITATIVE SET OF OPEN LANES (finding CT-3 of\n    DEC-20260907-52f2a0, carried below): read the side files through\n    `tools/goal_lanes.py`, never this key.\n  approval_decision_ids:\n  - DEC-20260906-2b1387\n  - DEC-20260906-806501\n  - DEC-20260907-4e34c5\n  - DEC-20260907-adbe7e\n  evidence_review_decision_ids:\n  - DEC-20260906-1f5b71\n  - DEC-20260906-bcc097\n  - DEC-20260907-ece434\n  lane_decision_ids_20260907_e9fd22:\n    added_by: TASK-20260907-9e7580\n    note: >-\n      The three decisions of lane BATCH-e9fd22, listed with their roles because\n      no existing list on this head fits all three. DEC-20260907-4e34c5 is also\n      added to `approval_decision_ids` above, being a protocol-approval gate\n      decision (verb `revise`). The other two have no home list: a\n      batch-opening `expand` and a lane-closing `synthesize` are neither\n      approvals nor evidence reviews, and inventing a place for them in an\n      existing list would misfile them.\n    decisions:\n      - id: DEC-20260907-38e5ae\n        role: lane opening and rerank (verb `expand`); approved no protocol and authorised no run\n        task: TASK-20260907-d47b50\n      - id: DEC-20260907-4e34c5\n        role: approval gate on PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v1-to-v2 as proposed in this lane (verb `revise`); refused the contract text on three blocking defects\n        task: TASK-20260907-f65c6e (fresh session; authored none of the gated artifacts)\n      - id: DEC-20260907-b6bcf4\n        role: lane close, compatibility read and rerank (verb `synthesize`); created no evidence record and changed no status\n        task: TASK-20260907-9e7580\n  lane_decision_ids_20260907_48ef8b:\n    added_by: TASK-20260907-1aa16f\n    note: >-\n      The three decisions of lane BATCH-48ef8b, listed with their roles for the\n      same reason BATCH-e9fd22's were: no existing list on this head fits all\n      three. DEC-20260907-adbe7e is also added to `approval_decision_ids` above,\n      being a protocol-approval gate decision (verb `revise`). The other two\n      have no home list -- a batch-opening authorship and a lane-closing\n      `synthesize` are neither approvals nor evidence reviews.\n    decisions:\n      - id: DEC-20260907-52f2a0\n        role: >-\n          lane opening and protocol authorship; approved no protocol and\n          authorised no run. Designing is not approving.\n        task: TASK-20260907-058c69\n      - id: DEC-20260907-adbe7e\n        role: >-\n          approval gate on PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3 (verb `revise`); recorded\n          all seven predecessor defects D1-D7 as DISCHARGED and refused on seven\n          blocking findings of its own about the coherence of the contract's own\n          instruction text\n        task: TASK-20260907-9c0626 (fresh session; authored none of the gated artifacts)\n      - id: DEC-20260907-de6b71\n        role: >-\n          lane close, prior-versus-outcome comparison and rerank (verb\n          `synthesize`); created no evidence record, reviewed none, and changed\n          no status\n        task: TASK-20260907-1aa16f\n  batch_48ef8b_disposition: >-\n    revised, closed by TASK-20260907-1aa16f / TASK-20260907-38f086\n    (DEC-20260907-de6b71; checkpoint\n    ledger/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/checkpoints/BATCH-48ef8b.yaml; lane close\n    report under the batch's TASK-20260907-1aa16f directory). Lane on\n    cursor/ecdlp-bbc21f-g3-feasibility-review-276e (PR #825), opened by\n    DEC-20260907-52f2a0. It authored PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3\n    (specification.v3.yaml, amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml, and a four-file derivation\n    packet whose reading path is a CLOSED POSITIVE ALLOWLIST rather than a\n    denylist), snapshot-archived it alone at 176b7d93e, and had it GATED by a\n    fresh Coordinator session that authored none of it. THE GATE RETURNED\n    `revise` (DEC-20260907-adbe7e) -- and it recorded ALL SEVEN PREDECESSOR\n    DEFECTS D1-D7 OF DEC-20260907-4e34c5 AS GENUINELY DISCHARGED, so a second\n    `revise` is NOT a re-refusal. It verified by RECOMPUTATION rather than by\n    reading (the cap convention and cap = ceil(8W) re-derived at all eight\n    (N, a) cells with zero discrepancies; the three-term basin-mass accounting\n    identity recomputed and closing at all 20 committed cells of\n    RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-001..005; every allowlist sha256 with zero mismatches; a\n    failing world constructed or refused for each of the fifteen declared\n    control items) and refused instead on SEVEN BLOCKING FINDINGS ABOUT THE\n    COHERENCE OF THE CONTRACT'S OWN INSTRUCTION TEXT: CF-1 (required_artifacts\n    demands a firing status for six items the contract elsewhere declares have\n    no firing condition, leaving an executor no correct action -- the round's one\n    OPERATIVE defect), CF-2 (the external anchor called \"independently\n    established\" where EV-ECDLP-60e266 reads `strength: preliminary`), CF-4\n    (DECAY-A clause (i) routing the batch's most severe falsification off a\n    zero-tolerance comparison while the interval estimator that could calibrate\n    it is declared to bind nothing), CF-5 (a summary partitioning fifteen items\n    as 11+3+2), LO-1 (the author's self-reported letter offset between the two\n    normative documents, ruled NOT ACCEPTABLE with a recorded remedy), and XR-1\n    / XR-2 (permuted and doubly-attributed CR-1 conditions), plus three\n    non-blocking. THE MATHEMATICS PASSED AND THE CONTRACT TEXT FAILED, in both\n    rounds -- recorded as finding TG-1 with the AM-1 authorship method it names.\n    NO RUN EVER EXECUTED IN THIS LANE: no evidence record exists, no hypothesis\n    status moved, no review verdict or attestation was obtained, and no\n    measurement about the ECDLP originates here. H-ECDLP-37dc01 stays `analyzed`\n    with no status_history entry. NO TASK WAS CANCELLED -- all six ran and all\n    six are `completed`, because this queue deliberately offered no producer\n    task at all, which is the repair for the five cancellations BATCH-e9fd22\n    owed. The lane's own LEAK DISCIPLINE HELD UNDER THE GATE'S AUDIT, across the\n    queue, all six task cards, all six handoffs, the opening decision, the\n    snapshot receipt and four commit messages -- the predecessor's exact failure\n    did not recur. Verified commits: snapshot 176b7d93e (backfilled at\n    c94a71b47), gate ledger archive bc4828129 (backfilled at 09c2e702b). THE\n    LANE ALSO CARRIES OUT ONE FINDING AGAINST AN APPROVED RECORD: CF-3, a\n    self-contradiction in the APPROVED, execution_authorized\n    experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml about the a = 1/4 anchor's\n    seed count and scale, settled by EV-ECDLP-60e266 lines 150-155; its remedy is\n    a SUPERSEDING RECORD, never an edit, its gate-named owner BATCH-8f3e86 has\n    closed, and DEC-20260907-de6b71 reassigns it as a required carried item of\n    the successor. Successor is the next_action below. Two premises this lane\n    opened under moved while it ran -- see\n    `external_work_advancing_this_goal_20260907_48ef8b`.\n  batch_e9fd22_disposition: >-\n    revised, closed by TASK-20260907-9e7580 (DEC-20260907-b6bcf4; checkpoint\n    ledger/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/checkpoints/BATCH-e9fd22.yaml). Lane on\n    cursor/ecdlp-bbc21f-g3-feasibility-review-276e (PR #825), opened by\n    DEC-20260907-38e5ae. It authored a wide 25-seed, two-scale, four-control\n    v1-to-v2 amendment of EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 and had it GATED AND REFUSED\n    (`revise`, DEC-20260907-4e34c5) by a fresh Coordinator session on three\n    blocking contract defects -- T stated as 102 at N = 2^20 against the frozen\n    64; the basin partition asserted exhaustive with cap = ceil(8W) absent\n    entirely; and the Coordinator's directional prior sitting on the Stage A'\n    re-deriver's pre-seal reading path in two committed files on no blind list.\n    NO RUN EVER EXECUTED IN THIS LANE: no evidence record exists, no hypothesis\n    status moved, and no measurement about the ECDLP originates here.\n    H-ECDLP-37dc01 stays `analyzed` with no status_history entry. Five\n    downstream tasks (e423d5 executor, 60957d snapshot, 6a2b2e validator,\n    3dff63 red team, 022c19 ledger archive) are CANCELLED with a recorded\n    reason -- they depended on an approved contract that does not exist -- and\n    the declared review round NEVER OPENED, so no joint was attested and the\n    recorded Coordinator prior stands untested. Verified commits: snapshot\n    5856b36e8 (backfilled at 752023e32), gate ledger archive f996864d2. The\n    lane produced four things worth carrying: TF-1 (the gate session's 20-cell\n    verification that weight_d = S_d + 4*W*h_d is the rule v1 production\n    computed), HB-1 (the head-blindness finding, below), IC-1 (one experiment\n    identifier now carries two v1-to-v2 amendments under one amendment id --\n    one approved and frozen, one `revision_required`; neither renamed, neither\n    superseded, disposition in DEC-20260907-b6bcf4), and CR-1 (the\n    compatibility read: the wide scope CAN be carried additively as a v2-to-v3\n    on the approved v2, under four named conditions). Successor is RANK 1 of\n    the next_action below. This lane's close writes no entry of BATCH-8f3e86.\n  batch_1e7251_disposition: >-\n    refine, closed by TASK-20260907-c264db (DEC-20260907-ece434,\n    EV-ECDLP-855daf). Disjoint lane on cursor/run-experiments-e393\n    (PR #821) executed PA-ECDLP-869870-v1-to-v2: 16/16 completed_valid\n    at N=2^24, a=1/4, T=256, 8 keys x splitmix64 + murmur3_fmix64;\n    snapshot 13bf12d0b; blinded J1-J4 all hold/PASS. fixture_gate_v2\n    not scored (O(theta) not_evaluated). H-ECDLP-3550b8 stays analyzed.\n    Goal-head next_action RANK 1/2 left untouched for other sessions.\n    This lane's successor is the O(theta) instantiation or a raw-gate\n    amendment (checkpoint BATCH-1e7251.yaml).\n  batch_f3a30a_disposition: >-\n    support (narrowly scoped), closed by TASK-20260906-ae5bb4\n    (DEC-20260906-bcc097). The v2-execution batch: the amended, approved\n    contract (DEC-20260906-806501) ran to completion (16 of 16 planned runs,\n    TASK-20260906-5e78c7: Stage 0 a-scan, Stage 1v2 at 2^24, Stage 2v2 at\n    2^30, Stage 4v2 analysis; all completed_valid), was snapshot-archived\n    alone at 22e80f133 (TASK-20260906-1e5ea4), and was reviewed by two\n    mutually blind fresh sessions under a review_plan written first\n    (validator TASK-20260906-bc1cfc: J1 HOLDS_WITH_FINDINGS, J2 HOLDS; red\n    team TASK-20260906-a6b415: J3 HOLDS_WITH_FINDINGS, J4\n    HOLDS_WITH_FINDINGS; no breaking artifact on any of the four owned\n    joints). EV-ECDLP-f6b3f5 (H-ECDLP-37dc01, direction supports, strength\n    preliminary, proof_status empirical_only): G3 PASSES 5/5 seeds at all\n    four tested (N, T_sel) cells (unlike v1's T_sel = T/2 cell, FAIL 10/10),\n    so every S1_v2/F1_v2 outcome is a real, gate-cleared measurement; S1_v2\n    MET at 3 of 4 cells (2^24 0.65T borderline and 0.75T; 2^30 0.75T), NOT\n    MET at 2^30 0.65T; F1_v2 fires nowhere; S2_v2 (one-sided null) NOT MET\n    at every cell (NULL-A's own perturbation 2-3x the measured effect).\n    Per the frozen v2 contract's own OVERALL wording this supports a\n    RE-SCOPED effect clause (T_sel in {0.65T, 0.75T}, S_peak charged, 881-\n    1029.5 bits/T) -- it does NOT rehabilitate clause (C1) as originally\n    stated (T_sel = T/2), which remains contradicted by disjointness,\n    unchanged from BATCH-289698. This Coordinator additionally surfaced an\n    discrepancy in the executor's own Stage 0 a-scan interpretation,\n    subsequently NUMERICALLY CONFIRMED by the orchestrating session from the\n    raw per-seed run data by a second, independent route: applying the\n    contract's own G3 rule directly shows T_sel = T/2 IS G3-feasible at\n    a = 1/16 (5/5 seeds, margins +0.0196/+0.0122/+0.0240/+0.0163/+0.0092)\n    and a = 1/8 (4/5 seeds, margins +0.0032/-0.0020/+0.0103/+0.0050/+0.0071)\n    -- directly contradicting execution_report.yaml's stated \"no feasible\n    point found.\" The numbers are confirmed; FORMAL independent review\n    (blind rederivation, proves-too-much control) has not yet been applied,\n    so this is carried forward as RANK 1 of the next action, not adopted as\n    a hypothesis-relevant finding. Hypothesis status stays `analyzed`\n    (status_history entry added, no procedural transition): single\n    unreplicated batch, S2_v2's unresolved magnitude confound, the missing\n    permanent null-collapse regression fixture (red team J4 coverage-gap\n    finding), and the not-yet-formally-reviewed Stage 0 discrepancy all\n    argue against promotion. Checkpoint shard checkpoints/BATCH-f3a30a.yaml.\n  batch_289698_disposition: >-\n    weaken, closed by TASK-20260906-aa3dd2 (DEC-20260906-1f5b71). The first\n    execution batch: both approved contracts ran to completion\n    (EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 37 runs incl. Stage 3 curve cells, 19850/19850\n    certificates; EXP-ECDLP-869870 24 runs, 404028 certificates), were\n    snapshot-archived alone at 840df8a5 (TASK-20260906-7a2446), and were\n    reviewed by two mutually blind fresh sessions under a review_plan\n    written first (validator TASK-20260906-7ec3ea: J1, J2\n    HOLDS_WITH_FINDINGS; red team TASK-20260906-90e7cf: J3 BROKEN, J4\n    BROKEN narrowly); check_review_independence.py PASS. The Coordinator's\n    recorded prior (S1-S4 pass, rho_T(8T) near 0.51, break if any in J1)\n    was OVERTURNED on J3 and J1 was clean. EV-ECDLP-60e266 (H-ECDLP-37dc01,\n    direction weakens, strength preliminary, proof_status derivation, full\n    obstruction block): the T/2 re-selected table does NOT reach static T\n    (S1 CI-separated below at both N and on the curve; F1's 0.85 letter not\n    met; the outcome in a cell the contract did not name) and was\n    infeasible by disjointness at a = 1/4 (exact top-T/2 share below\n    STATIC(T) coverage in 10/10 seeds); measured rho_T(8T) = 0.654 [0.620,\n    0.700] (2^24) / 0.688 [0.664, 0.706] (2^30), rho_T(16T) = 0.619 /\n    0.632, oracle floor about 0.55, S_peak 2.6-8.9 T, early-batch penalty\n    0.13-0.15; a tradeoff point under RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5's fewer_DP\n    definition; mechanism clauses supported at toy scale. EV-ECDLP-31e91c\n    (H-ECDLP-3550b8, neutral, inconclusive): the 2^24 fixture gate FAILED\n    (one cost cell by 0.0005, four precomputation cells) so the 2^24+ cells\n    are invalid-for-interpretation under rule 3; nothing scored; the\n    headline cell is band-edge under re-keying (J2-F1). Both hypotheses\n    specified -> approved -> running -> analyzed (never weakened /\n    supported from one batch). C1 and C3 met on the verified commit of that\n    archive (negative direction; obstruction over the tested scope); C2 NOT\n    met. Checkpoint shard checkpoints/BATCH-289698.yaml.\n  batch_252a44_disposition: >-\n    approve_experiment, closed by TASK-20260906-773a2e.\n  completion_criteria_progress_20260906_f3a30a: >-\n    Recorded additively by TASK-20260906-ae5bb4 (BATCH-f3a30a's ledger\n    archive). The `status` fields in `completion_criteria` below (C1, C3)\n    are flipped from OPEN to MET by this authorship: BATCH-289698's own\n    checkpoint already narratively established C1 and C3 as met on the\n    verified BATCH-289698 commit, but explicitly deferred flipping the\n    declarative `status` field to \"the successor ledger archive\"; that flip\n    was not performed by BATCH-252a44's archive (an approval-only batch with\n    no evidence review), so it is performed here, now that BATCH-289698's\n    commit is long since verified. C1 is MET, in EITHER-direction terms per\n    its own statement: the negative T_sel = T/2 finding (EV-ECDLP-60e266)\n    and this batch's re-scoped, G3-gated T_sel_grid_v2 measurement\n    (EV-ECDLP-f6b3f5) together are the committed, independently validated\n    and red-teamed evidence the criterion asks for, on the tested\n    (N, a, r, k, cap, walk, solver) grid at claim_tier toy. C3 is MET,\n    unchanged: EV-ECDLP-60e266's obstruction block (T_sel = T/2 disjointness\n    at a = 1/4) still carries a complete measured obstruction with a genuine\n    resource_check; nothing in EV-ECDLP-f6b3f5 alters it (T_sel = T/2 was\n    not retested this batch). C2 stays OPEN, unchanged, pending the\n    EXP-ECDLP-869870 re-keyed fixture successor (RANK 3 of this archive's\n    next_action). This flip does NOT imply RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5 is closed, and\n    does NOT imply H-ECDLP-37dc01's status has moved beyond `analyzed`\n    (unaffected by this administrative completion-criteria bookkeeping);\n    see batch_f3a30a_disposition and the hypothesis's own status_history for\n    the actual research content.\n  completion_criteria_progress_20260906_289698: >-\n    Recorded additively; the status fields in completion_criteria below\n    are left OPEN in this authorship and are flipped by the successor\n    ledger archive once the post-commit verifier accepts\n    TASK-20260906-aa3dd2's commit (a transition from an unverified archive\n    is not official). C1: MET on that verified commit, in the NEGATIVE\n    direction -- EV-ECDLP-60e266 is a committed, independently validated\n    and red-teamed evidence record reporting T_resel(U)/T_static at fixed\n    (L, epsilon) at a = 1/4 with CIs (0.654 [0.620, 0.700] at 8T, 2^24;\n    0.688 [0.664, 0.706] at 2^30; 0.619 / 0.632 at 16T), the early-batch\n    penalty (0.146 [0.121, 0.166]; 0.131 [0.121, 0.141]), U_ss and U*\n    (> 16T; U* unreachable), the NULL-A / NULL-B outcomes and the phi\n    decay, with the T/2 table remaining CI-separated below static T at\n    U = 16T; strength preliminary (single batch), and the pre-registered\n    S1 was infeasible by ceiling, so the constant is delivered but the\n    feasible comparison (T_sel about 0.65-0.75 T with S_peak charged) is\n    owed to the v2 re-run. C2: NOT MET -- the instrument's measurements are\n    committed with CI and model beside (RUN-ECDLP-869870-024 constants\n    table) but V1 failed at 2^24 and every constant from 2^24 upward\n    carries the rule-3 invalid-for-interpretation label; C2 closes only\n    after the re-keyed fixture cell validates the instrument. C3: MET on\n    the verified commit for the T/2 cell at a = 1/4 -- EV-ECDLP-60e266\n    carries a complete measured obstruction block (quantities, values with\n    CIs, measured_by run ids, scope, resource_check examined true with\n    three readings); it closes nothing beyond that scope and does not close\n    RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5.\n  batch_9c5410_disposition: >-\n    approve_experiment, closed by TASK-20260906-2d30dd. BATCH-9c5410 was the\n    approval gate with zero execution: the user answered \"Approve both as\n    frozen (Recommended)\" on 2026-09-06 (re-affirmed \"Approved\" in chat the\n    same day), recorded verbatim in DEC-20260906-2b1387; EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 and\n    EXP-ECDLP-869870 are approved at version 1 (five gate fields only) with\n    executor handoffs TASK-20260906-3623b9 and TASK-20260906-d17254 written.\n    No run exists; H-ECDLP-37dc01 and H-ECDLP-3550b8 stay `specified`; C1,\n    C2, C3 stay OPEN.\n  latest_verified_commit: bc48281293f0a8adc7f806e6d4c1d95bcc7d5073\n  latest_verified_commit_note_20260907_48ef8b: >-\n    ADVANCED by TASK-20260907-1aa16f from f996864d2613d2fae9c397191cb0de49ba8449cd\n    (BATCH-e9fd22's gate ledger archive, whose note is preserved verbatim below)\n    to bc48281293f0a8adc7f806e6d4c1d95bcc7d5073 -- TASK-20260907-3edbf0's ledger\n    archive of the approval-gate decision DEC-20260907-adbe7e, parent\n    4e737c70e646fda9de388c883fcae00b2148d6d2, base origin/main checked at\n    e6059f4de563be3cb1f1b25383782ab9a708352f and MERGED at 4e737c70e (never\n    rebased), clean, with no conflict in any ledger record, run artifact or\n    knowledge entry, so no superseding record was needed. Its receipt is\n    coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-48ef8b/archives/TASK-20260907-3edbf0/ledger-receipt.json\n    (committed sha256\n    871541a2d99c64e6be5dd937c65ef3bee60af1ee394942c848c4f07cbe15e881), its four\n    declared `path_sha256` entries are content-verified against the tree, and\n    after the queue backfill at 09c2e702b `tools/research_dispatch.py --claims\n    refs` reports `completed_archive_commits_verified: passed`. THIS LANE'S\n    TERMINAL ARCHIVE COMMIT IS NOT NAMED HERE, for the same reason ceb8cf's\n    receipt could not name its own: this field is written INSIDE that commit, so\n    a value pointing at it would have to hash itself. It is recorded in\n    TASK-20260907-38f086's receipt and in the queue's archive block, and the next\n    lane advances this field past it.\n  latest_verified_commit_note_20260907_e9fd22: >-\n    ADVANCED by TASK-20260907-9e7580 from a97ac6e23f82ab608bce801507e028a2841a7bb4\n    (BATCH-f3a30a's verified follow-up, preserved verbatim in\n    `latest_verified_commit_note` below) to\n    f996864d2613d2fae9c397191cb0de49ba8449cd -- TASK-20260907-ceb8cf's ledger\n    archive of DEC-20260907-4e34c5, parent 475ca4419c6d1ac2ae572ef4512b25402b16dfc9,\n    base origin/main checked at 1d7bdff902cf3091b1e6ba54b4b49e778e514cd7 and\n    MERGED (never rebased). Its receipt is\n    coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-e9fd22/archives/TASK-20260907-ceb8cf/ledger-receipt.json\n    (committed sha256 f022501063eb9fed619b8f80bcd229bed69f4fc1b3a1b27d58a6f29a87ce1180),\n    whose four declared `path_sha256` entries are content-verified against the\n    tree; its queue archive block carries `commit_sha: null` by construction\n    and is backfilled in this close's own separate follow-up commit, after\n    which `tools/research_dispatch.py --claims refs` reports\n    `completed_archive_commits_verified: passed`. THIS CLOSE'S OWN TWO COMMITS\n    ARE NOT NAMED HERE, for the same reason ceb8cf's receipt could not name\n    its own: this field is written inside the first of them, so a value\n    pointing at it would have to hash itself. The next lane advances this\n    field past them.\n  latest_verified_commit_note: >-\n    Advanced by the orchestrating session to BATCH-f3a30a's ledger archive\n    verified follow-up commit (TASK-20260906-ae5bb4's read_scope fix,\n    a97ac6e23f82ab608bce801507e028a2841a7bb4), after\n    `tools/research_dispatch.py` reported `completed_archive_commits_verified:\n    passed` and all 5 BATCH-f3a30a tasks terminal/completed. The ledger\n    archive's own content commit is a10b39329463dca6e30c09358d5d282bc7bc715e\n    (backfilled at d87b9f68a). Previous value (TASK-20260906-aa3dd2,\n    preserved above the arrow): eaae31a0fc6c3a55fee3ea171afc3e98e9a1862d,\n    the BATCH-252a44 approval-authorship ledger commit.\n    Further note (TASK-20260906-773a2e, this authorship, coordinator role\n    without a shell): this value is likewise NOT advanced here. The\n    orchestrating session advances it to this batch's (BATCH-252a44)\n    ledger-archive commit in its own separate, verified follow-up commit\n    after the post-commit verifier accepts DEC-20260906-806501 and this\n    goal-head update, exactly as it did for BATCH-9c5410 and BATCH-289698.\n  completion_criteria:\n  - id: C1\n    statement: >-\n      A committed evidence record for EXP-ECDLP-612fb1, independently\n      validated and red-teamed, reporting T_resel(U)/T_static at fixed\n      (L, epsilon) at a = 1/4 with a confidence interval, the early-batch\n      penalty (first 10% of the batch, U_ss and cumulative U*), and the\n      outcomes of the NULL-A / NULL-B nulls and the phi decay -- in EITHER\n      direction: the T/2 re-selected table reaching static T within CI at\n      U = 8T (S1-S4), or remaining CI-separated below it at U = 16T (F1), on\n      the tested (N, a, r, k, cap, walk, solver) grid at claim_tier toy.\n    status: MET\n    status_note: >-\n      Flipped OPEN -> MET by TASK-20260906-ae5bb4 (BATCH-f3a30a), per\n      completion_criteria_progress_20260906_f3a30a: EV-ECDLP-60e266\n      (negative direction, T_sel = T/2) and EV-ECDLP-f6b3f5 (re-scoped\n      T_sel_grid_v2, direction supports) together are the committed,\n      independently validated and red-teamed evidence this criterion's\n      \"in EITHER direction\" text asks for, on the tested grid at\n      claim_tier toy.\n  - id: C2\n    statement: >-\n      The instrument EXP-ECDLP-869870 committed with its basin-law\n      measurements (survival slope, cutoff), its oracle-ceiling measurements\n      (exact top-T share against C_max(a)), its published-rule measurements\n      (the seven-cell primary-source fixture and C_rule/C_oracle as a\n      function of N/T), and their N-independence verdict across 2^20..2^30\n      (V5), each with a confidence interval and the model value beside it,\n      never in one column.\n    status: OPEN\n  - id: C3\n    statement: >-\n      CLOSURE STANDARD, failing a positive on C1: a committed evidence record\n      carrying a complete measured `obstruction` block per\n      docs/inventor-protocol.md -- the quantity that bounds the gain\n      (rho_T(16T) with its CI, or the static table's measured estimation-loss\n      gap to the exact oracle share), its value with units and error bars,\n      the runs it is read from, the scope it is claimed over, and a genuinely\n      asked resource_check. A closure whose obstruction is prose does not meet\n      this criterion.\n    status: MET\n    status_note: >-\n      Flipped OPEN -> MET by TASK-20260906-ae5bb4 (BATCH-f3a30a), per\n      completion_criteria_progress_20260906_f3a30a: EV-ECDLP-60e266's\n      obstruction block (T_sel = T/2 disjointness at a = 1/4, with a\n      genuine resource_check) satisfies this criterion, unchanged and not\n      retested by BATCH-f3a30a.\n  pause_conditions:\n  - a snapshot or ledger archive fails post-commit verification\n  - a required review policy cannot be honoured without a silent downgrade\n  - the toy-curve arm cannot certify a solved logarithm\n  - the user declines approval and gives no revision direction\n  runtime_constraint_note: >-\n    Recorded before dispatch, as on GOAL-ECRANK-002. Under the claude_code\n    runtime the `coordinator` subagent has no shell, so it cannot itself run\n    `git add`/`git commit`/`git push` or `gh pr create`. For THIS campaign the\n    split is declared up front: the Coordinator authors every archive record\n    and every status transition via Write, and the orchestrating session\n    performs only the mechanical git and PR commands over exactly the paths\n    the Coordinator declared. Authorship of state transitions stays with the\n    Coordinator; only the shell call moves. Each archive receipt records this\n    split so it is auditable and never mistaken for a worker committing to\n    shared state.\n  next_action_superseded_20260906_9c5410: >-\n    ONE ACTION, and it is a GATE, not compute. Put the approval question for\n    the two unapproved frozen contracts EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 (H-ECDLP-37dc01, the\n    batch-reselected fixed-size table) and EXP-ECDLP-869870 (H-ECDLP-3550b8,\n    the basin-partition coverage instrument) to the USER, per\n    design-experiment step 4 and the GOAL-ECRANK-002 precedent\n    (DEC-20260905-2d466e, BATCH-832f3d); the exact question text is in the\n    BATCH-9c5410 batch report. The question has NOT yet been put and nothing\n    in this record asserts an answer. On the recorded answer run\n    TASK-20260906-67f1ab (approval authorship, coordinator inline under the\n    declared fallback): ON APPROVAL of a contract, its gate fields only\n    (status, approved_by, approval_note, frozen, execution_authorized --\n    protocol fields byte-identical, version stays 1) and the executor\n    handoffs TASK-20260906-3623b9 (EXP-ECDLP-612fb1) and/or\n    TASK-20260906-d17254 (EXP-ECDLP-869870) carrying each contract's budget\n    envelope verbatim; ON DECLINE, no gate field changes, no executor\n    handoff, and both hypotheses staying `specified`. Then\n    TASK-20260906-2d30dd (ledger archive, runs ALONE) AUTHORS\n    DEC-20260906-2b1387 -- approve_experiment with the question and the\n    user's answer recorded verbatim, or `revise` with the user's stated\n    reason -- exactly as 59fb55 authored DEC-20260905-2d466e in the\n    precedent, binds it with the package and this goal head, and the branch\n    is pushed and its PR refreshed naming the records. Until that archive\n    lands and is verified: approved_by stays null on both contracts and zero\n    compute is spent. RANK 2 (the NEXT batch, opened only after that ledger\n    archive merges to main): the EXECUTION batch dispatching the approved\n    executor task(s) from the approved contract(s) on main, with the snapshot\n    TASK-20260906-7a2446, the validator TASK-20260906-7ec3ea (blind\n    re-derivation of the 1.79 fixture and of the exact top-T share at 2^24\n    from the statement of the quantities) and the red team\n    TASK-20260906-90e7cf (the null and fixture-procedure design) RESERVED, all\n    three under a review_plan written BEFORE either reviewer runs; those three\n    ids are reserved, not dispatchable, and appear in no queue yet. RANK 3:\n    /design-experiment on IDEA-20260906-a3d6ae (the growth-with-relations\n    comparator that EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 cites as its frontier point) and on the\n    c-sweep of IDEA-20260906-05ffb8 (scored by the 869870 instrument);\n    IDEA-20260906-cf3b76 (walk-rule invariance of C_max) and\n    IDEA-20260906-ac100b (the (B1)-(B3) derivation, a validator task) as\n    cheap closures. C1, C2 and C3 are all OPEN. Batch history: none --\n    BATCH-9c5410 is this campaign's first batch.\n  next_action_superseded_20260906_289698: >-\n    RANK 1: open the execution batch BATCH-289698 on branch\n    claude/batch-dlp-precomputation-nov7vh from the approved contracts\n    (DEC-20260906-2b1387): executor tasks TASK-20260906-3623b9\n    (EXP-ECDLP-612fb1, Stage G + Stages 1-2) and TASK-20260906-d17254\n    (EXP-ECDLP-869870, Stages 1-2), then snapshot TASK-20260906-7a2446 alone,\n    then validator TASK-20260906-7ec3ea and red team TASK-20260906-90e7cf as\n    fresh independent sessions under a review_plan written first, then ledger\n    archive TASK-20260906-aa3dd2 with EV records, decision, and hypothesis\n    transitions. RANK 2: Stage 3 and the curve arms if budget remains. RANK 3:\n    design IDEA-20260906-a3d6ae and the c-sweep of IDEA-20260906-05ffb8;\n    cf3b76 and ac100b as cheap closures. C1, C2 and C3 are all OPEN. Batch\n    history: BATCH-9c5410 (approval gate, zero execution) at\n    DEC-20260906-2b1387.\n  next_action_superseded_20260906_252a44: >-\n    RANK 1 (the ONE next action; a new BATCH-<tok> minted at opening, after\n    the BATCH-289698 ledger archive is verified and merged to main): author\n    a VERSIONED AMENDMENT v2 of EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 under\n    experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/amendments/ (v1 frozen and untouched;\n    executed runs never re-scored) carrying DEC-20260906-1f5b71's items\n    (a)-(h): a ceiling-feasibility gate G3 from the exact basins (exact\n    top-T_sel share >= STATIC(T) exact coverage in >= 4/5 seeds before S1 is\n    testable; failure = untestable, never negative); an S1 non-vacuity\n    guard (STATIC(T) eps_ss >= 0.5 and CI-separated above RHO by >= 0.30;\n    tolerance 5% of the STATIC(T) - RHO gap; rho_T CI excluding 1.0 and\n    uncensored; U_ss/U* margins relative); S2 restated one-sided as the\n    null's expected sign (NULL-A gain not CI-separated above zero and\n    <= 0.5 x the RESEL-L gain; the null's own perturbation recorded); the\n    headline restated as T_resel/T_static at fixed success WITH S_peak\n    CHARGED, reported as the frontier tuple (T_sel/T, S_peak/T, P/sqrt(NT),\n    L, eps_ss, eps_cum, U, early penalty) with rho_ORACLE and rho_cum\n    beside rho_ss and U* stated explicitly when unreachable; HEUR-BLT-7\n    with the admitted-walk count; the pool cap applied per admission so\n    CAP(2T) is 2 T; fit_cutoff None -> G1 FAIL with the two bijection seeds\n    as a permanent negative fixture; and the 2^20 a-scan of ORACLE(T/2) -\n    STATIC(T) run FIRST (seconds per cell) with (C6) replaced by the\n    ordering prediction rho_ORACLE(a = 1/4) < rho_ORACLE(a = 1/2). Put the\n    amendment to the USER (design-experiment step 4) and record the answer\n    in a committed approval decision; THEN a re-run batch under v2 at\n    T_sel in {0.65T, 0.75T} at N in {2^24, 2^30}, a = 1/4, r = 2, k = 4,\n    5 seeds, S_peak charged, PAIRED with /design-experiment on\n    IDEA-20260906-a3d6ae (the growth-type comparator the obstruction's\n    resource_check names) so the re-run's frontier table has its fair\n    comparator; snapshot alone, mutually blind validator and red team under\n    a review_plan written first, then ledger archive -- the replication\n    that `weaken` on H-ECDLP-37dc01 owes before any further transition.\n    That successor archive also flips the completion_criteria status\n    fields (C1 met, C3 met, C2 open) after this archive's post-commit\n    verification. RANK 2: the EXP-ECDLP-869870 successor cell -- a\n    re-keyed 2^24 fixture (>= 8 keys per instrument, murmur3 and splitmix64\n    as the validator's J2 ran them, capped-mass fraction beside every cell)\n    under a versioned amendment that states the O(theta) correction before\n    comparing at 2^24 or gates at 2^30, fits the N-drift trend on\n    2^22-2^24, re-states the survival-slope band against the finite-theta\n    Borel value under the declared estimator, and runs the gate in its own\n    run record before any later stage; V1-V5 / M1-M5 scored and the\n    constants citable (and C2 closable) only after it passes. RANK 3: the\n    IDEA-20260906-05ffb8 c-sweep (scored by the validated instrument),\n    IDEA-20260906-cf3b76 (walk-rule invariance of C_max; the labelled\n    r_walk = 16 / 32 KS observations on TOY-P24-a6ee37f9 are its first data\n    points) and IDEA-20260906-ac100b (the (B1)-(B3) derivation as a\n    validator task) as cheap closures. Criteria after BATCH-289698: C1 met\n    (negative direction, preliminary) and C3 met (T/2 cell, a = 1/4) on the\n    verified commit; C2 NOT met. Batch history: BATCH-9c5410 (approval\n    gate, zero execution) at DEC-20260906-2b1387; BATCH-289698 (first\n    execution batch, weaken) at DEC-20260906-1f5b71.\n  next_action_superseded_20260906_f3a30a: >-\n    \"RANK 1: open the execution batch (a new BATCH-<tok>, minted at opening)\n    on branch claude/batch-dlp-precomputation-nov7vh from the approved v2\n    contract (DEC-20260906-806501): executor task TASK-20260906-5e78c7\n    (source_v2/, Stage 0 a-scan first, then Stage 1v2/2v2 at T_sel in\n    {0.65T,0.75T}, N in {2^24,2^30}), then a Coordinator snapshot alone,\n    then an independent validator and red team under a review_plan written\n    before either runs (same posture as BATCH-289698: mutual blindness, a\n    pre-recorded Coordinator prior, at least one proves-too-much object and\n    one blind re-derivation), then a ledger archive with EV/DEC records and\n    the H-ECDLP-37dc01 status transition the results warrant. RANK 2: the\n    EXP-ECDLP-869870 successor cell (re-keyed 2^24 fixture) under its own\n    versioned amendment, per DEC-20260906-1f5b71's EXP_ECDLP_869870\n    disposition. RANK 3: IDEA-20260906-a3d6ae (growth-type comparator) and\n    the c-sweep/cf3b76/ac100b closures.\" DISCHARGED IN FULL for\n    EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 by BATCH-f3a30a (DEC-20260906-bcc097); RANK 2 and\n    RANK 3 above are UNCHANGED and carried forward, now re-ranked as RANK 3\n    and RANK 4 of the new next_action below, behind a new RANK 1/2 this\n    archive opens.\n  rerank_20260907_e9fd22:\n    by: DEC-20260907-38e5ae\n    batch_opened: BATCH-e9fd22\n    what_changed: >-\n      The next_action recorded on 2026-09-06 was STALE, not wrong when written.\n      Its RANK 1 (the N = 2^24 exact-basin, blind-re-derived check of whether\n      T_sel = T/2 is G3-feasible at a in {1/16, 1/8}) WAS EXECUTED on 2026-09-07\n      as EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 under BATCH-3c7493, with a sealed blind re-derivation\n      and a proves-too-much control, and was ledger-archived at commit 84233e8c3\n      under DEC-20260907-9b1b02. This goal's own bookkeeping never saw it:\n      DEC-20260907-9b1b02 carries goal_id: null, and BATCH-3c7493 was opened\n      under coordination/experiments/ rather than under this goal's lane\n      directory, so no checkpoint shard was written against this head. The\n      next_action below is REPLACED by DEC-20260907-9b1b02's own ranking, which\n      supersedes it on the merits and on the date.\n    outcome_of_the_superseded_rank_1: >-\n      Recorded in DEC-20260907-9b1b02 and EV-ECDLP-2e9680, cited here and not\n      restated: three of four cells resolved with both readings agreeing, and\n      one cell (a = 1/8) resolved to a genuine blind-versus-production\n      disagreement whose root cause was traced to an underspecification in\n      EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 v1's own contract text. Nothing in this rerank asserts,\n      re-scores, or reinterprets any of those findings.\n    superseded_next_action_preserved_verbatim: >-\n      Held once, byte-for-byte, under the top-level key\n      `next_action_superseded_20260906` below. It is stored in exactly one place\n      on purpose: a superseded ranking copied into two keys is a ranking that\n      can later disagree with itself, and a reader has no way to tell which copy\n      is the original.\n    lane_note: >-\n      Additive to this head only. No other lane's entries are touched. The three\n      prior lanes (BATCH-252a44, BATCH-289698, BATCH-f3a30a) remain closed and\n      their checkpoint shards are unmodified.\n  external_work_advancing_this_goal_20260907_e9fd22:\n    added_by: TASK-20260907-9e7580\n    finding_id: HB-1\n    why_this_key_exists: >-\n      THE HEAD WAS BLIND TO WORK THAT ADVANCED THIS GOAL, AND IT WILL BE AGAIN\n      UNLESS THE RECORDS ARE NAMED HERE. The next_action committed 2026-09-06\n      asked for exactly the N = 2^24 exact-basin, blind-re-derived check of\n      T_sel = T/2 at a in {1/16, 1/8} that EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 had already\n      performed and archived. Three independent mechanisms hid it: BATCH-3c7493\n      was opened under coordination/experiments/ rather than under this goal's\n      lane directory, so `tools/goal_lanes.py lanes` never listed it; its\n      dispatch queue carries `goal_id: GOAL-ECDLP-001` because\n      EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 and H-ECDLP-37dc01 both declare `goal_id: null`; and no\n      checkpoint shard was ever written for it under this goal's\n      `checkpoints/`. Each alone is sufficient. GENERIC STATEMENT: work\n      archived against one goal identifier is invisible to the head of the goal\n      it actually advances, and a head read is no substitute for reading the\n      decisions.\n    records_that_advance_this_goal_despite_carrying_goal_id_null_or_GOAL_ECDLP_001:\n      - id: EXP-ECDLP-6ac801\n        what: 'the N = 2^24 exact-basin G3-feasibility contract at a in {1/16, 1/8, 3/16, 1/4}, r = 2, T_sel = T/2; declares goal_id: null'\n        paths: 'experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/ (specification.yaml v1 frozen; specification.v2.yaml APPROVED, another lane''s; specification.v2.BATCH-e9fd22-proposed.yaml revision_required)'\n      - id: BATCH-3c7493\n        what: 'the batch that executed it (6 runs RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-001..006, all completed_valid, plus the sealed Stage A blind re-derivation TASK-20260907-80e198); its queue carries goal_id: GOAL-ECDLP-001'\n        paths: coordination/experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/batches/BATCH-3c7493/\n        registered_as_a_lane_of_this_goal: false\n        checkpoint_shard_under_this_goal: none\n      - id: EV-ECDLP-2e9680\n        what: 'its per-cell evidence: a = 1/16 S1 CONFIRMED FEASIBLE (blind and production agreeing 5/5), a = 3/16 and a = 1/4 S2 CONFIRMED INFEASIBLE, a = 1/8 S3 DISAGREEMENT at the literal sealed level'\n      - id: DEC-20260907-9b1b02\n        what: >-\n          THE AUTHORITATIVE CURRENT SCIENCE RANKING FOR THIS GOAL, and the\n          record any session resuming here must read before the next_action\n          below. It records a = 1/8 as GENUINELY OPEN, root-causes the\n          disagreement to an underspecification in v1's own contract text\n          rather than to a scientific question, declines to relabel the cell on\n          a post-hoc non-blind diagnostic, and leaves four ranked next actions\n          standing. Committed at 84233e8c3.\n    what_this_key_does_not_do: >-\n      It changes no `goal_id` field, creates no GOAL binding on any record, and\n      does not retroactively register BATCH-3c7493 as a lane. Those are\n      additive acts on records this lane does not own and they stay as RANK 5\n      of the next_action below. This key is a POINTER so the next head read is\n      not blind; the records themselves are unmodified.\n    scope: >-\n      Observed on this goal for BATCH-3c7493 / EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 only. No other\n      goal was audited for the same pattern.\n  external_work_advancing_this_goal_20260907_48ef8b:\n    added_by: TASK-20260907-1aa16f\n    finding_id: HB-1 (SECOND RECORDED RECURRENCE)\n    carries_forward_verbatim_in_substance: >-\n      EVERY BINDING THE PREDECESSOR RECORDED IN\n      `external_work_advancing_this_goal_20260907_e9fd22` ABOVE STILL HOLDS AND\n      IS NOT RESTATED HERE. EXP-ECDLP-6ac801, BATCH-3c7493, EV-ECDLP-2e9680 and\n      DEC-20260907-9b1b02 all advance THIS goal while declaring\n      `goal_id: GOAL-ECDLP-001` or `null`; none of their `goal_id` fields is\n      changed by this close and BATCH-3c7493 is still not registered as a lane.\n      This key ADDS the records that landed since, and records that the same\n      mechanism cost this lane something concrete.\n    why_this_key_exists: >-\n      HB-1 RECURRED, AND ITS COST THIS TIME IS NAMEABLE: THIS LANE'S OWN RANK 1\n      WAS AUTHORED AGAINST A PREMISE THAT HAD ALREADY BEEN OVERTAKEN ON MAIN.\n      The lane was opened on the premise -- carried by the goal head's\n      next_action and by DEC-20260907-b6bcf4 -- that the a = 1/8 cell of\n      EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 is GENUINELY OPEN. It is not: the Stage A' re-seal under\n      the approved v2 had already run and been archived. Commit 0dbbbd9a0 was\n      reachable at this lane's opening snapshot 176b7d93e, but this lane's\n      opening deliberately writes no head, so this close is the first head write\n      on this branch with it reachable. NO RECORD IS AT FAULT. The mechanism is\n      exactly the one HB-1 named: work archived against one goal identifier is\n      invisible to the head of the goal it advances, and a head read is no\n      substitute for reading the decisions.\n    records_that_advance_this_goal_and_were_not_visible_from_this_head:\n      - id: EV-ECDLP-6783b8\n        what: >-\n          TASK-20260907-2db9aa's freshly sealed, from-scratch blind\n          re-derivation of a = 1/8 at N = 2^24 under the approved v2's\n          now-explicit selection formula, using a wholly independent\n          implementation (independently constructed uniform random self-map\n          table, independent Bernoulli marking, exact binary-lifting absorption\n          -- NOT source_v2/instrument.py) with the required proves-too-much\n          control at a = 1/4. Terminal verdict S1 CONFIRMED FEASIBLE under v2's\n          own taxonomy: the two readings AGREE on the categorical verdict, with\n          one opposite-sign draw in the blind sample disclosed and judged within\n          seed-to-seed noise at the contract's most borderline cell.\n          `strength: preliminary`, `claim_tier: toy`.\n      - id: DEC-20260907-8d8782\n        what: >-\n          Its evidence-review decision, verb `support`, scoped exactly to that\n          ceiling-feasibility confirmation, recording its own RANK 1 (the v2\n          amendment and the a = 1/8 re-seal) as DISCHARGED. Committed at\n          0dbbbd9a0, reachable on this branch through the 631c524a7 merge.\n      - id: BATCH-8f3e86 (now CLOSED)\n        what: >-\n          Another session's lane on cursor/run-experiments-batch-93e3, CLOSED\n          2026-09-07 (PR #829, merged to main at f24293a5f; checkpoint\n          ledger/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/checkpoints/BATCH-8f3e86.yaml). It\n          measured the same question on a DIFFERENT experiment (EXP-ECDLP-612fb1\n          v3) and reached a structurally identical result at a = 1/8:\n          EV-ECDLP-6a4ebc (`strength: preliminary`), DEC-20260907-6d9427 (verb\n          `replicate`). Its validator joint J2 is recorded BREAKS on the\n          per-seed sign disagreement, and its residual R3 -- an independent third\n          angle -- is NOT discharged, because its STAGE 3B imports the same\n          frozen source_v2/instrument.py that EXP-ECDLP-6ac801's production arm\n          imported. ITS ENTRIES ON THIS HEAD ARE NOT WRITTEN BY THIS CLOSE and\n          none were found to write; it is recorded here as a fact read from\n          `tools/goal_lanes.py` and from committed records.\n    what_these_records_do_and_do_not_settle: >-\n      a = 1/8 IS CONFIRMED CEILING-FEASIBLE AT N = 2^24 AT `preliminary`\n      STRENGTH, twice, on two instruments. That is all. Both records are\n      `preliminary` and `claim_tier: toy` by their own declarations, both rest on\n      small samples, one carries a review joint recorded BREAKS on a per-seed\n      sign disagreement and an undischarged independent-third-angle residual, and\n      neither is reviewed, re-scored or promoted by this close. What they jointly\n      establish is that a = 1/8 is a BORDERLINE CELL, which is why the successor\n      contract's objective statement must be rewritten rather than inherited.\n    carried_finding_CT_3: >-\n      THE HEAD IS STILL NOT A RELIABLE INDEX OF WHICH LANES ARE LIVE, exactly as\n      DEC-20260907-52f2a0 recorded it as CT-3: `current_batch_id` is null,\n      `dispatch_queue_path` names a closed lane, and `open_batches` is empty.\n      Its 2026-09-07 statement that BATCH-8f3e86 is open is now stale as well","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":779,"totalLines":780,"truncated":true}},"title":"ledger/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/goal.yaml","time":{"start":1789087319354,"end":1789087319476}},"id":"prt_08de9fff2001O84fGVX1lMJTbP","sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","messageID":"msg_08de8e190001fUKV0HtzaAJxji"}}
