{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789087406407,"sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-8e80765c071abaa6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/ledger/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/goal.yaml","offset":780},"output":"<path>/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/ledger/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/goal.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n780:       (see `open_batches_note_20260907_48ef8b`), which is CT-3 demonstrating\n781:       itself rather than a new defect. LANE LIVENESS IS READ FROM THE WRITE-ONCE\n782:       SIDE FILES under coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/lanes/ via\n783:       `python3 tools/goal_lanes.py lanes GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f`, which is what those\n784:       files exist for. Recorded so the discrepancy is not read as damage and not\n785:       repaired by editing a record another session may be working.\n786:     what_this_key_does_not_do: >-\n787:       It changes no `goal_id` field, creates no GOAL binding on any record, does\n788:       not retroactively register any batch as a lane, and writes no entry of any\n789:       other lane. Those remain additive acts on records this lane does not own\n790:       and they stay in the ranking, to be done OPPORTUNISTICALLY inside\n791:       whichever lane next opens -- HB-1 has now cost this goal twice, and it\n792:       still does not justify a lane of its own.\n793:     scope: >-\n794:       Observed on this goal for BATCH-3c7493 / EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 and for this\n795:       lane's own opening premise. No other goal was audited for the same\n796:       pattern.\n797:   next_action: >-\n798:     RANK 1 (the ONE next action; this goal's ranked ECC work, successor to\n799:     BATCH-d7e987 authorship recorded in DEC-20260907-d806f5): a FRESH\n800:     independent approval gate on PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3-r2 (the addenda\n801:     now on experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml and\n802:     amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml, plus amendments/v2_cf3_control_b.yaml and\n803:     the AM-1 report under BATCH-d7e987). Session must be neither\n804:     TASK-20260907-b1b54b, nor TASK-20260907-058c69, nor TASK-20260907-9c0626.\n805:     Confirm the ten remedies landed, the two normative documents agree\n806:     letter for letter on the controls, and nothing frozen moved. NO RUN\n807:     under v3 until that gate sets the four gate fields. The authoring\n808:     work DEC-20260907-de6b71 named is DONE; the text below is retained\n809:     as the remedy list the gate checks, not as work still owed to author.\n810:     PRIOR RANK-1 TEXT (DEC-20260907-de6b71), now the gate's checklist:\n811:     AUTHOR A SUPERSEDING\n812:     REVISION of experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml and\n813:     experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml AT A NEW SNAPSHOT,\n814:     discharging the seven blocking findings of DEC-20260907-adbe7e (CF-1, CF-2,\n815:     CF-4, CF-5, LO-1, XR-1, XR-2) and the three non-blocking ones (XR-3,\n816:     J1-CITE, CT2-CHAR), per the per-item remedies in the gate's own\n817:     `verdict_block.what_a_revision_must_contain`. NOT ONE BYTE of the\n818:     TASK-20260907-6077f2 snapshot (176b7d93e) may be rewritten and no approved or\n819:     frozen record may be touched -- every item sits in v3-appended text or in the\n820:     amendment, so none requires it, which is exactly the ground on which the gate\n821:     ruled the author's \"the files are archived\" objection does not hold: the\n822:     ARCHIVE is immutable and the CONTRACT is not, v3 reads `approved_by: null`,\n823:     and no run exists under it. DO NOT REOPEN what the gate checked and passed --\n824:     the cap convention, the three-term accounting identity, the allowlist\n825:     mechanism, the two-scale scope, and every block CR-1 pins byte-identical --\n826:     because a revision that re-derived any of them would spend effort where none\n827:     is owed. THEN a FRESH independent gate on the revision, in a session that is\n828:     neither the author nor TASK-20260907-9c0626, with a NARROWER scope: confirm\n829:     the ten remedies landed, confirm the two normative documents now agree letter\n830:     for letter on the identity and count of the controls, confirm nothing frozen\n831:     moved. THREE REQUIRED CARRIED ITEMS. (1) BINDING -- REWRITE THE OBJECTIVE\n832:     STATEMENT. v3 may NOT inherit the premise that a = 1/8 is unresolved: it is\n833:     confirmed ceiling-feasible at N = 2^24 at `preliminary` strength\n834:     (EV-ECDLP-6783b8 / DEC-20260907-8d8782), corroborated on a different\n835:     experiment (EV-ECDLP-6a4ebc / DEC-20260907-6d9427). What v3 now measures is\n836:     the ROBUSTNESS AND N-DEPENDENCE of the crossing bracket at a borderline cell\n837:     -- which is what its wider seed set, its interval estimator and its fresh\n838:     straddling-interval label are for. This is a binding condition because a\n839:     stale premise has now been inherited twice. (2) RAISE CF-3's SUPERSEDING\n840:     RECORD against the APPROVED experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml,\n841:     correcting control (b) at line 537 to match metrics.primary at line 584 and\n842:     EV-ECDLP-60e266's own two-scale seed split (lines 150-155). Its gate-named\n843:     owner BATCH-8f3e86 HAS CLOSED, so this lane inherits it. NEVER an edit to the\n844:     approved file. (3) RUN AND ARCHIVE THE AM-1 SELF-CONSISTENCY PASS before\n845:     submitting to the gate, as a task artifact, with its five mechanical checks\n846:     (item-set identity, partition arithmetic, quantifier range, cross-reference\n847:     resolution, pointer freshness) and their output -- this is where AM-1's\n848:     claim, that a script would have caught five of this round's seven blocking\n849:     findings, actually gets tested instead of asserted. A new committed decision\n850:     must set v3's four gate fields before any executor runs; until then\n851:     specification.v3.yaml stays UNAPPROVED and NOT execution-authorized and NO\n852:     RUN MAY EXECUTE UNDER IT. WHY FIRST, and what it was ranked against:\n853:     DEC-20260907-de6b71 `rationale` gives the reasons in full; in short, its work\n854:     is fully specified and bounded by an enumerated remedy list, the gate's own\n855:     ruling is that the repair cost is at its MINIMUM NOW and rises monotonically\n856:     (dearer after approval, and after execution `invalidation_rules` item 7\n857:     forbids re-scoring what has run), its purpose is now BETTER motivated than\n858:     when the lane opened rather than obsolete, it is the cheapest of the five\n859:     candidates by a wide margin, and it UNBLOCKS RANK 2 rather than competing\n860:     with it.\n861:     RANK 2 (PROMOTED from third on new facts; the goal's largest genuine gap):\n862:     the ONLINE RESEL-L arm at the confirmed-feasible a values, mirroring\n863:     EXP-ECDLP-612fb1's online-arm design, with a heuristic-validation component\n864:     against HEUR-BLT-7. It moved up because its blocking precondition -- a\n865:     confirmed-feasible operating point to run an online arm AT -- now exists at\n866:     TWO a values rather than one (a = 1/16 per DEC-20260907-9b1b02 /\n867:     EV-ECDLP-2e9680; a = 1/8 per DEC-20260907-8d8782 / EV-ECDLP-6783b8), and\n868:     DEC-20260907-8d8782's own RANK 2 says exactly this. Every ceiling result this\n869:     goal holds is SILENT on whether the online lower-bracket mechanism REACHES\n870:     that ceiling at any achievable batch size U, and ZERO online arms have ever\n871:     been run, so no hypothesis-status promotion beyond ceiling-feasibility may be\n872:     considered before it does. It is still second because its comparison target\n873:     is the ceiling and the ceiling's definitional gap is LIVE in the approved v2\n874:     (DEC-20260907-b6bcf4 CR-1a: `cap`, `CAP_MULT`, `cycle_mass` and `capped_mass`\n875:     appear ZERO times in it), so an arm run today would be read against a\n876:     definition a from-scratch re-deriver cannot recover. Fix the definition at\n877:     RANK 1, then measure against it -- an ordering with a reason, not a deferral.\n878:     Carried alongside it, unchanged from DEC-20260906-bcc097 RANK 2 and\n879:     outstanding before ANY promotion beyond `analyzed` on any clause of\n880:     H-ECDLP-37dc01: the EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 amendment items -- a permanent v2-native\n881:     null-collapse regression fixture, the S2_v2 magnitude confound, S_peak_bits\n882:     from the finer per-target tracker, a bootstrap CI on the CAP(2T, T_sel)\n883:     retention ratio, and the G3 N = 2^30 binding/informational ambiguity.\n884:     RANK 3 (completion criterion C2, this goal's ONLY OPEN criterion): discharge\n885:     its blocker on EXP-ECDLP-869870 -- instantiate the O(theta) correction under\n886:     an additive amendment, or file an amendment that explicitly gates on the raw\n887:     residual, per BATCH-1e7251's checkpoint `lane_next_action` and\n888:     DEC-20260907-ece434 -- then score `fixture_gate_v2`, only then V2-V5 /\n889:     M1-M5, and compose the basin-law, oracle-ceiling and published-rule\n890:     measurements with their CIs and the N-independence verdict across\n891:     2^20..2^30 that C2's text requires. BATCH-1e7251 is CLOSED and this successor\n892:     is unclaimed: claim it with `tools/goal_lanes.py claim` before dispatching.\n893:     RANKED THIRD DESPITE BEING THE ONLY OPEN CRITERION -- the strongest argument\n894:     any candidate here has, and it still loses: its blocker is INSTRUMENTAL\n895:     rather than scientific, its next step is ALSO an amendment authorship so it\n896:     gains nothing in immediacy, and completing the criterion tally while the\n897:     central clause sits at `preliminary` on small samples would optimise the\n898:     wrong quantity. C1 and C3 being MET makes that more tempting, not more\n899:     justified.\n900:     RANK 4 (the EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 successor BATCH-8f3e86's close owes, RE-SCOPED\n901:     against a record its own lane could not see): DEC-20260907-6d9427 leaves two\n902:     frozen-text defects for additive correction (residual R3's false three-way\n903:     independence claim; the false measure-zero tie-break claim) and names as its\n904:     own RANK 1 a G3 re-derivation by an implementation genuinely independent of\n905:     experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/source_v2/instrument.py at a in {1/16, 1/8}.\n906:     RE-SCOPE IT FIRST: TASK-20260907-2db9aa's Stage A' re-seal (EV-ECDLP-6783b8)\n907:     already used an independently constructed self-map, independent Bernoulli\n908:     marking and exact binary-lifting absorption -- NOT source_v2/instrument.py --\n909:     at a = 1/8 and a = 1/4, N = 2^24. That is a CANDIDATE third angle at a = 1/8\n910:     which BATCH-8f3e86 did not have in view, and this head does NOT assert it\n911:     discharges R3: whether it does is a question for whoever owns\n912:     EXP-ECDLP-612fb1, on the record. What is clearly still owed is a = 1/16,\n913:     which EV-ECDLP-6783b8 explicitly does not retest.\n914:     RANK 5 (cheap, small, untouched, plus one piece of housekeeping with a\n915:     measured cost): IDEA-20260906-a3d6ae (the growth-type comparator\n916:     EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 cites as its frontier point) and the cheap closures\n917:     IDEA-20260906-05ffb8 (the c-sweep), IDEA-20260906-cf3b76 (walk-rule\n918:     invariance of C_max) and IDEA-20260906-ac100b (the (B1)-(B3) derivation, a\n919:     validator task). None attempted, none blocked; last only because none bears\n920:     on the borderline cell or on C2. CARRIED WITH THEM: bind EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 and\n921:     H-ECDLP-37dc01 to `goal_id: GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f` rather than `null`, and\n922:     register BATCH-3c7493 as a closed lane of this goal, so `tools/goal_lanes.py`\n923:     can see the work that advances it. HB-1 HAS NOW RECURRED TWICE with a\n924:     nameable cost each time -- once it made this head's RANK 1 ask for work\n925:     already landed, once it made BATCH-48ef8b's own RANK 1 rest on a premise\n926:     already overtaken on main. Both are additive record changes on records no\n927:     closed lane owned. DO THEM OPPORTUNISTICALLY INSIDE WHICHEVER LANE NEXT\n928:     OPENS: they do not justify a lane of their own, and dispatching one would be\n929:     exactly the make-work an unlimited ECC budget invites.\n930:     GOAL STATUS: `active`, `impediments` EMPTY. NO completion criterion closes\n931:     this goal -- C1 MET, C3 MET, C2 OPEN -- and DEC-20260907-de6b71\n932:     `goal_closure_assessment` records the full reasoning: why a two-of-three\n933:     tally does not license `completed` even with the closure quorum SUSPENDED\n934:     (which is exactly why that decision declines rather than closes), why\n935:     neither `closed_at_budget` nor `cancelled` would be honest, and why the\n936:     decisive objection is on the merits -- the central hypothesis clause is\n937:     confirmed only at CEILING level, only at `preliminary` strength, and ZERO\n938:     ONLINE RESEL-L ARMS HAVE EVER BEEN RUN, so nothing yet bears on the question\n939:     RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5 actually asks. As of this close every lane of this goal is\n940:     CLOSED and the RANK 1 successor is UNCLAIMED.\n941:   next_action_superseded_20260907_48ef8b: >-\n942:     RANK 1 (this goal's ranked ECC work on its central question; successor to\n943:     the closed lane BATCH-e9fd22, per DEC-20260907-b6bcf4): AUTHOR\n944:     PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3 as experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml\n945:     BESIDE v1 and the APPROVED v2, editing neither. Discharge D2 FIRST -- state\n946:     cap = ceil(8*W), state that a point on a DP-free cycle or whose first DP\n947:     lies beyond the cap belongs to NO basin, state the true relation\n948:     sum_d b(d) = N - cycle_mass - capped_mass, require both readings to report\n949:     cycle_mass and capped_mass per cell, and state that a capped\n950:     pool-construction walk is charged and credits no S_d or h_d -- BECAUSE D2\n951:     IS LIVE IN THE APPROVED v2 AND NOT ONLY IN THE REFUSED DRAFT: `cap`,\n952:     `CAP_MULT`, `cycle_mass` and `capped_mass` appear ZERO times in\n953:     experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml, so the approved\n954:     contract's own required Stage A' re-seal hands a from-scratch re-deriver a\n955:     convention it must invent -- the same class of gap that produced the\n956:     a = 1/8 disagreement, relocated from the weight to the cap\n957:     (DEC-20260907-b6bcf4 CR-1a; magnitude and direction UNMEASURED, so this is\n958:     a risk of recurrence and not a prediction that any verdict flips). Then D3\n959:     (move the Coordinator's directional prior off the pre-seal reading path\n960:     into its own file; add that file, ledger/handoffs/TASK-20260907-e423d5.yaml,\n961:     the batch dispatch queue, DEC-20260907-4e34c5 and the gate's task directory\n962:     to `blind_from`; widen the contamination declaration from commit messages\n963:     to every committed path the re-deriver is instructed or likely to read\n964:     before sealing; name ONE authoritative blind list per AO-3). Then D1, which\n965:     against the approved v2 is a value to STATE rather than a contradiction to\n966:     repair: T = 64 and T_sel = 32 at N = 2^20 cited to EXP-ECDLP-612fb1\n967:     specification.v2.yaml line 223, or drop the second scale, which\n968:     DEC-20260907-9b1b02 RANK 1 never asked for. Then fold D4 (tie-break key),\n969:     D5 (decouple agreement from the bootstrap interval), D6 (a = 1/16\n970:     independence asymmetric and binding: zero weight for agreement, full weight\n971:     plus rule 12 for disagreement) and D7 (add a null of the real\n972:     measurement's SHAPE over the same basin universe). Carry the wide scope --\n973:     25 seeds with the seeds 1..5 subgroup reported separately, interval\n974:     estimation with an unresolved verdict, the externally anchored DECAY-A, the\n975:     de-tautologised DECAY-TSEL, and the reproduction control against the\n976:     committed v1 cells -- under DEC-20260907-b6bcf4's four conditions COND-1\n977:     (append the N = 2^20 arm; the approved v2 states nothing there, so there is\n978:     nothing to contradict), COND-2 (KEEP S1/S2/S3 with the approved v2's\n979:     meanings verbatim and give the new interval-routed outcome a FRESH label --\n980:     the refused draft renumbers them, which would make \"S3\" denote two\n981:     outcomes for one experiment, the same failure this experiment already\n982:     suffered at the amendment id), COND-3 (supersede control (e) SEED-COUNT\n983:     PARITY by APPENDING a control that quotes it verbatim; the seed set is the\n984:     one wide-scope item invalidation_rules item 7 does not name) and COND-4\n985:     (append sub-keys inside `blind_rederivation`, whose `frozen: true` the\n986:     approved v2 itself already appended under). v3 then requires ITS OWN FRESH\n987:     APPROVAL GATE in a session that authored none of it, and that gate must\n988:     RE-RUN the contract-versus-implementation comparison against the APPROVED\n989:     v2's text, which no gate has yet done -- D1 and D2 were both found that way\n990:     and neither is inheritable. A new committed decision must set v3's four\n991:     gate fields before any executor runs. THIS DOES NOT BLOCK, GATE OR CLAIM\n992:     BATCH-8f3e86, which is another session's open lane and whose approved\n993:     narrow re-seal can execute today.\n994:     RANK 2 (the only route to a complete criterion set): discharge C2's blocker\n995:     on EXP-ECDLP-869870 -- instantiate the O(theta) correction under an\n996:     additive amendment, or file an amendment that explicitly gates on the raw\n997:     residual, per BATCH-1e7251's checkpoint `lane_next_action` and\n998:     DEC-20260907-ece434 -- then score `fixture_gate_v2`, only then V2-V5 /\n999:     M1-M5, and compose the basin-law, oracle-ceiling and published-rule\n1000:     measurements with their CIs and the N-independence verdict across\n1001:     2^20..2^30 that C2's text requires. BATCH-1e7251 is CLOSED and this\n1002:     successor is unclaimed: claim it with `tools/goal_lanes.py claim` before\n1003:     dispatching. Ranked SECOND, not first, although C2 is the only OPEN\n1004:     criterion: its blocker is instrumental rather than scientific, its next\n1005:     step is also an amendment authorship so it gains nothing in immediacy, and\n1006:     completing the criterion tally while the central hypothesis clause sits\n1007:     unresolved at the operating point this goal cares about would optimise the\n1008:     wrong quantity. C1 and C3 being MET makes that more tempting, not more\n1009:     justified.\n1010:     RANK 3 (unchanged, carried from DEC-20260907-9b1b02 RANK 2, and the largest\n1011:     genuine gap this goal has): the ONLINE RESEL-L batch at the\n1012:     confirmed-feasible a values, mirroring EXP-ECDLP-612fb1's online-arm design,\n1013:     with a heuristic-validation component against HEUR-BLT-7. Every ceiling\n1014:     result this goal holds is SILENT on whether the online lower-bracket\n1015:     mechanism REACHES that ceiling at any achievable batch size U, and ZERO\n1016:     online arms have ever been run; no hypothesis-status promotion beyond\n1017:     ceiling-feasibility may be considered before it does. It stays third\n1018:     because it is the largest of the three and because its output would be read\n1019:     against a definition D2 leaves incomplete -- run it after v3 lands and the\n1020:     reading is uncontested. Carried alongside it, unchanged from\n1021:     DEC-20260906-bcc097 RANK 2: the v3 amendment items on EXP-ECDLP-612fb1\n1022:     (permanent v2-native null-collapse fixture; S2_v2 magnitude confound;\n1023:     S_peak_bits from the finer per-target tracker; a bootstrap CI on the\n1024:     CAP(2T,T_sel) retention ratio; the G3 N = 2^30 binding/informational\n1025:     ambiguity), outstanding before ANY promotion beyond `analyzed` on any\n1026:     clause of H-ECDLP-37dc01.\n1027:     RANK 4 (cheap, small, untouched): IDEA-20260906-a3d6ae (growth-type\n1028:     comparator) and the cheap closures IDEA-20260906-05ffb8,\n1029:     IDEA-20260906-cf3b76, IDEA-20260906-ac100b. None attempted, none blocked.\n1030:     Last only because none bears on the a = 1/8 cell or on C2.\n1031:     RANK 5 (housekeeping, and the reason HB-1 exists): decide whether\n1032:     EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 and H-ECDLP-37dc01 should carry\n1033:     `goal_id: GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f` rather than `null`, and whether BATCH-3c7493\n1034:     should be retroactively registered as a closed lane of this goal so its\n1035:     work is visible to `tools/goal_lanes.py`. Both are additive record changes\n1036:     on records BATCH-e9fd22 did not own. Mitigated for now by\n1037:     `external_work_advancing_this_goal_20260907_e9fd22` above, which names the\n1038:     four affected records so the next head read is not blind; the cause is not\n1039:     repaired.\n1040:     GOAL STATUS: `active`, `impediments` EMPTY. NO completion criterion closes\n1041:     this goal -- C1 MET, C3 MET, C2 OPEN -- and DEC-20260907-b6bcf4\n1042:     `goal_closure_assessment` records the full reasoning, including why a\n1043:     two-of-three tally does not license `completed` under the suspended quorum\n1044:     and why neither `closed_at_budget` nor `cancelled` would be honest.\n1045:   next_action_superseded_20260907_48ef8b_disposition: >-\n1046:     Preserved verbatim above, byte-for-byte, in exactly one place (a superseded\n1047:     ranking copied into two keys is a ranking that can later disagree with\n1048:     itself, and a reader has no way to tell which copy is the original).\n1049:     DISPOSITION, ITEM BY ITEM. Its RANK 1 -- author PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3\n1050:     discharging D2, D3 and D1 and carrying the wide scope under CR-1's four\n1051:     conditions, then gate it in a session that authored none of it -- IS\n1052:     DISCHARGED IN SUBSTANCE AND REFUSED IN FORM. BATCH-48ef8b authored exactly\n1053:     that amendment; an independent gate confirmed ALL SEVEN predecessor defects\n1054:     D1-D7 GENUINELY DISCHARGED, verified the cap convention derivable from v3's\n1055:     text alone, recomputed W and cap at all eight cells and the accounting\n1056:     identity at all 20 committed v1 cells, and confirmed the D3 repair by\n1057:     MECHANISM (a closed positive allowlist) rather than by list-lengthening --\n1058:     and then returned `revise` on seven findings of its own about the coherence\n1059:     of the contract's own instruction text (DEC-20260907-adbe7e). SO v3 IS NOT\n1060:     APPROVED, is not execution-authorized, and NO RUN MAY EXECUTE UNDER IT; the\n1061:     successor is the new RANK 1 above, which is a superseding revision at a new\n1062:     snapshot rather than a fresh authorship. Its RANK 2 (C2 on\n1063:     EXP-ECDLP-869870) is UNTOUCHED and is now RANK 3 -- demoted by one on the\n1064:     promotion below, not on any change in its own merits. Its RANK 3 (the online\n1065:     RESEL-L arm, with the EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 v3 items carried alongside) is\n1066:     PROMOTED to RANK 2, because its blocking precondition -- a confirmed-feasible\n1067:     operating point to run an online arm AT -- now exists at two a values rather\n1068:     than one (EV-ECDLP-6783b8 / DEC-20260907-8d8782 at a = 1/8, corroborated by\n1069:     EV-ECDLP-6a4ebc / DEC-20260907-6d9427). Its RANK 4 (the cheap-closure ideas)\n1070:     and RANK 5 (the HB-1 housekeeping) are UNCHANGED in substance and are merged\n1071:     into the new RANK 5, with the housekeeping's recurrence cost now recorded.\n1072:     ONE ITEM IS NEW AND IS NOT A RERANKING OF ANYTHING ABOVE: CF-3's superseding\n1073:     record against the APPROVED specification.v2.yaml, whose gate-named owner\n1074:     BATCH-8f3e86 closed while this lane ran, carried as a required item of\n1075:     RANK 1. Nothing in this rerank re-scores, reinterprets or retracts any\n1076:     committed finding, and no measurement originates in it. Reranked by\n1077:     TASK-20260907-1aa16f under DEC-20260907-de6b71, against a fact base that\n1078:     moved while the lane ran -- see\n1079:     `external_work_advancing_this_goal_20260907_48ef8b`.\n1080:   next_action_superseded_20260907_e9fd22: >-\n1081:     RANK 1 (IN FLIGHT as BATCH-e9fd22, opened by DEC-20260907-38e5ae): resolve\n1082:     a = 1/8. Per DEC-20260907-9b1b02's own RANK 1, EXP-ECDLP-6ac801's a = 1/8\n1083:     cell is genuinely OPEN -- its blind and production readings disagreed, and\n1084:     the cause was traced to an underspecification in that contract's own\n1085:     `definitions.STATIC(T)_r exact coverage` text, which names the\n1086:     Bernstein-Lange selection weight without stating it, so no from-scratch\n1087:     re-deriver could recover it. BATCH-e9fd22 carries: the versioned additive\n1088:     amendment PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v1-to-v2 stating weight_d = S_d + 4*W*h_d\n1089:     explicitly (PROPOSED, gated behind approval task TASK-20260907-f65c6e); a\n1090:     25-seed pre-registered production arm at N in {2^20, 2^24} with a null\n1091:     object (NULL-RANDSEL) and two decay controls; a FRESHLY SEALED independent\n1092:     blind re-derivation by a reviewer that has not read the prior one; and an\n1093:     independent red-team pass on the controls and the interpretation, which\n1094:     DEC-20260907-9b1b02 named as a disclosed gap of the prior batch.\n1095:     RANK 2 (unchanged, carried from DEC-20260907-9b1b02 RANK 2, gated on\n1096:     RANK 1): an online RESEL-L follow-up batch at the confirmed-feasible a\n1097:     values, mirroring EXP-ECDLP-612fb1's v1/v2 online-arm design, with a\n1098:     heuristic-validation component against HEUR-BLT-7. A ceiling-feasibility\n1099:     result does NOT demonstrate that the online lower-bracket mechanism reaches\n1100:     that ceiling at any achievable batch size U, and no hypothesis-status\n1101:     promotion beyond ceiling-feasibility may be considered before this runs.\n1102:     RANK 3 (unchanged, carried from DEC-20260906-bcc097 RANK 2 and\n1103:     DEC-20260907-9b1b02 RANK 3): the v3 amendment items on EXP-ECDLP-612fb1,\n1104:     outstanding before ANY hypothesis-status promotion beyond `analyzed` on any\n1105:     clause of H-ECDLP-37dc01 -- a permanent v2-native null-collapse regression\n1106:     fixture; resolution or explicit re-argument of the S2_v2 magnitude confound;\n1107:     S_peak_bits from the finer per-target tracker; a bootstrap CI on the\n1108:     CAP(2T,T_sel) retention ratio; resolution of the G3 N = 2^30\n1109:     binding/informational ambiguity. Untouched by BATCH-e9fd22.\n1110:     RANK 4 (unchanged): the EXP-ECDLP-869870 successor cell (re-keyed 2^24\n1111:     fixture, completion criterion C2) and the cheap closures\n1112:     IDEA-20260906-a3d6ae, IDEA-20260906-05ffb8, IDEA-20260906-cf3b76,\n1113:     IDEA-20260906-ac100b -- all ranked ahead of doing nothing on this\n1114:     ECC-priority campaign.\n1115:   next_action_superseded_20260907_e9fd22_disposition: >-\n1116:     Preserved verbatim above, byte-for-byte, in exactly one place (a superseded\n1117:     ranking copied into two keys is a ranking that can later disagree with\n1118:     itself). DISPOSITION, item by item. Its RANK 1 is DISCHARGED ONLY IN THE\n1119:     NEGATIVE: BATCH-e9fd22 ran to its approval gate and the gate REFUSED the\n1120:     protocol (DEC-20260907-4e34c5), so a = 1/8 IS NOT RESOLVED and this lane\n1121:     will not resolve it -- the successor is the new RANK 1 above. Its RANK 2\n1122:     (online RESEL-L) is UNCHANGED and is now RANK 3. Its RANK 3 (the\n1123:     EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 v3 items) is UNCHANGED and is carried alongside the new\n1124:     RANK 3. Its RANK 4 split: the EXP-ECDLP-869870 successor cell was EXECUTED\n1125:     by the disjoint lane BATCH-1e7251 (16/16 completed_valid, blinded J1-J4 all\n1126:     hold or PASS) but left `fixture_gate_v2` NOT SCORED, so C2 is still OPEN\n1127:     and that work is PROMOTED to the new RANK 2; the four cheap-closure ideas\n1128:     are UNCHANGED and are now RANK 4. Nothing in this rerank re-scores,\n1129:     reinterprets or retracts any committed finding, and no measurement\n1130:     originates in it. Reranked by TASK-20260907-9e7580 under\n1131:     DEC-20260907-b6bcf4.\n1132:   next_action_superseded_20260906: >-\n1133:     RANK 1: a small, independently reviewed follow-up (design + execute +\n1134:     review, or a v3 amendment item) resolving whether T_sel = T/2 is\n1135:     genuinely G3-feasible at a in {1/16, 1/8} on EXP-ECDLP-612fb1, ideally\n1136:     at N = 2^24 exact basins with a blind re-derivation -- per a discrepancy\n1137:     DEC-20260906-bcc097 surfaced in the v2 batch's own committed Stage 0\n1138:     a-scan data and the orchestrating session then NUMERICALLY CONFIRMED\n1139:     from the raw per-seed data by a second, independent route (T_sel = T/2\n1140:     G3-feasible at a = 1/16, 5/5 seeds, and a = 1/8, 4/5 seeds, r = 2,\n1141:     N = 2^20 -- contradicting the executor's own stated conclusion). The\n1142:     numbers are confirmed; FORMAL independent review (blind rederivation,\n1143:     proves-too-much control) is what RANK 1 still owes. If that review\n1144:     confirms feasibility this reopens clause (C1) of H-ECDLP-37dc01 at a\n1145:     different, smaller a. RANK 2: a v3 amendment to EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 before any\n1146:     hypothesis-status promotion beyond `analyzed` -- a permanent,\n1147:     committed null-collapse regression fixture (red team's J4 coverage-gap\n1148:     finding), an explicit resolution of the S2_v2 magnitude confound\n1149:     (NULL-A's perturbation measured 2-3x the effect at every cell this\n1150:     batch), S_peak_bits computed from the finer per-target tracker, a\n1151:     bootstrap CI on the CAP(2T,T_sel) retention ratio, and a resolution of\n1152:     the G3 N = 2^30 binding/informational ambiguity the validator surfaced.\n1153:     RANK 3 (unchanged from DEC-20260906-1f5b71): the EXP-ECDLP-869870\n1154:     successor cell (re-keyed 2^24 fixture). RANK 4 (unchanged): design\n1155:     IDEA-20260906-a3d6ae (growth-type comparator) and the\n1156:     c-sweep/cf3b76/ac100b cheap closures.\n1157:   owner: coordinator\n1158:   created_at: '2026-09-06'\n1159:   updated_at: '2026-09-07'\n\n(End of file - total 1159 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"      (see `open_batches_note_20260907_48ef8b`), which is CT-3 demonstrating\n      itself rather than a new defect. LANE LIVENESS IS READ FROM THE WRITE-ONCE\n      SIDE FILES under coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/lanes/ via\n      `python3 tools/goal_lanes.py lanes GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f`, which is what those\n      files exist for. Recorded so the discrepancy is not read as damage and not\n      repaired by editing a record another session may be working.\n    what_this_key_does_not_do: >-\n      It changes no `goal_id` field, creates no GOAL binding on any record, does\n      not retroactively register any batch as a lane, and writes no entry of any\n      other lane. Those remain additive acts on records this lane does not own\n      and they stay in the ranking, to be done OPPORTUNISTICALLY inside\n      whichever lane next opens -- HB-1 has now cost this goal twice, and it\n      still does not justify a lane of its own.\n    scope: >-\n      Observed on this goal for BATCH-3c7493 / EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 and for this\n      lane's own opening premise. No other goal was audited for the same\n      pattern.\n  next_action: >-\n    RANK 1 (the ONE next action; this goal's ranked ECC work, successor to\n    BATCH-d7e987 authorship recorded in DEC-20260907-d806f5): a FRESH","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/ledger/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/goal.yaml","text":"      (see `open_batches_note_20260907_48ef8b`), which is CT-3 demonstrating\n      itself rather than a new defect. LANE LIVENESS IS READ FROM THE WRITE-ONCE\n      SIDE FILES under coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/lanes/ via\n      `python3 tools/goal_lanes.py lanes GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f`, which is what those\n      files exist for. Recorded so the discrepancy is not read as damage and not\n      repaired by editing a record another session may be working.\n    what_this_key_does_not_do: >-\n      It changes no `goal_id` field, creates no GOAL binding on any record, does\n      not retroactively register any batch as a lane, and writes no entry of any\n      other lane. Those remain additive acts on records this lane does not own\n      and they stay in the ranking, to be done OPPORTUNISTICALLY inside\n      whichever lane next opens -- HB-1 has now cost this goal twice, and it\n      still does not justify a lane of its own.\n    scope: >-\n      Observed on this goal for BATCH-3c7493 / EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 and for this\n      lane's own opening premise. No other goal was audited for the same\n      pattern.\n  next_action: >-\n    RANK 1 (the ONE next action; this goal's ranked ECC work, successor to\n    BATCH-d7e987 authorship recorded in DEC-20260907-d806f5): a FRESH\n    independent approval gate on PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3-r2 (the addenda\n    now on experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml and\n    amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml, plus amendments/v2_cf3_control_b.yaml and\n    the AM-1 report under BATCH-d7e987). Session must be neither\n    TASK-20260907-b1b54b, nor TASK-20260907-058c69, nor TASK-20260907-9c0626.\n    Confirm the ten remedies landed, the two normative documents agree\n    letter for letter on the controls, and nothing frozen moved. NO RUN\n    under v3 until that gate sets the four gate fields. The authoring\n    work DEC-20260907-de6b71 named is DONE; the text below is retained\n    as the remedy list the gate checks, not as work still owed to author.\n    PRIOR RANK-1 TEXT (DEC-20260907-de6b71), now the gate's checklist:\n    AUTHOR A SUPERSEDING\n    REVISION of experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml and\n    experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml AT A NEW SNAPSHOT,\n    discharging the seven blocking findings of DEC-20260907-adbe7e (CF-1, CF-2,\n    CF-4, CF-5, LO-1, XR-1, XR-2) and the three non-blocking ones (XR-3,\n    J1-CITE, CT2-CHAR), per the per-item remedies in the gate's own\n    `verdict_block.what_a_revision_must_contain`. NOT ONE BYTE of the\n    TASK-20260907-6077f2 snapshot (176b7d93e) may be rewritten and no approved or\n    frozen record may be touched -- every item sits in v3-appended text or in the\n    amendment, so none requires it, which is exactly the ground on which the gate\n    ruled the author's \"the files are archived\" objection does not hold: the\n    ARCHIVE is immutable and the CONTRACT is not, v3 reads `approved_by: null`,\n    and no run exists under it. DO NOT REOPEN what the gate checked and passed --\n    the cap convention, the three-term accounting identity, the allowlist\n    mechanism, the two-scale scope, and every block CR-1 pins byte-identical --\n    because a revision that re-derived any of them would spend effort where none\n    is owed. THEN a FRESH independent gate on the revision, in a session that is\n    neither the author nor TASK-20260907-9c0626, with a NARROWER scope: confirm\n    the ten remedies landed, confirm the two normative documents now agree letter\n    for letter on the identity and count of the controls, confirm nothing frozen\n    moved. THREE REQUIRED CARRIED ITEMS. (1) BINDING -- REWRITE THE OBJECTIVE\n    STATEMENT. v3 may NOT inherit the premise that a = 1/8 is unresolved: it is\n    confirmed ceiling-feasible at N = 2^24 at `preliminary` strength\n    (EV-ECDLP-6783b8 / DEC-20260907-8d8782), corroborated on a different\n    experiment (EV-ECDLP-6a4ebc / DEC-20260907-6d9427). What v3 now measures is\n    the ROBUSTNESS AND N-DEPENDENCE of the crossing bracket at a borderline cell\n    -- which is what its wider seed set, its interval estimator and its fresh\n    straddling-interval label are for. This is a binding condition because a\n    stale premise has now been inherited twice. (2) RAISE CF-3's SUPERSEDING\n    RECORD against the APPROVED experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml,\n    correcting control (b) at line 537 to match metrics.primary at line 584 and\n    EV-ECDLP-60e266's own two-scale seed split (lines 150-155). Its gate-named\n    owner BATCH-8f3e86 HAS CLOSED, so this lane inherits it. NEVER an edit to the\n    approved file. (3) RUN AND ARCHIVE THE AM-1 SELF-CONSISTENCY PASS before\n    submitting to the gate, as a task artifact, with its five mechanical checks\n    (item-set identity, partition arithmetic, quantifier range, cross-reference\n    resolution, pointer freshness) and their output -- this is where AM-1's\n    claim, that a script would have caught five of this round's seven blocking\n    findings, actually gets tested instead of asserted. A new committed decision\n    must set v3's four gate fields before any executor runs; until then\n    specification.v3.yaml stays UNAPPROVED and NOT execution-authorized and NO\n    RUN MAY EXECUTE UNDER IT. WHY FIRST, and what it was ranked against:\n    DEC-20260907-de6b71 `rationale` gives the reasons in full; in short, its work\n    is fully specified and bounded by an enumerated remedy list, the gate's own\n    ruling is that the repair cost is at its MINIMUM NOW and rises monotonically\n    (dearer after approval, and after execution `invalidation_rules` item 7\n    forbids re-scoring what has run), its purpose is now BETTER motivated than\n    when the lane opened rather than obsolete, it is the cheapest of the five\n    candidates by a wide margin, and it UNBLOCKS RANK 2 rather than competing\n    with it.\n    RANK 2 (PROMOTED from third on new facts; the goal's largest genuine gap):\n    the ONLINE RESEL-L arm at the confirmed-feasible a values, mirroring\n    EXP-ECDLP-612fb1's online-arm design, with a heuristic-validation component\n    against HEUR-BLT-7. It moved up because its blocking precondition -- a\n    confirmed-feasible operating point to run an online arm AT -- now exists at\n    TWO a values rather than one (a = 1/16 per DEC-20260907-9b1b02 /\n    EV-ECDLP-2e9680; a = 1/8 per DEC-20260907-8d8782 / EV-ECDLP-6783b8), and\n    DEC-20260907-8d8782's own RANK 2 says exactly this. Every ceiling result this\n    goal holds is SILENT on whether the online lower-bracket mechanism REACHES\n    that ceiling at any achievable batch size U, and ZERO online arms have ever\n    been run, so no hypothesis-status promotion beyond ceiling-feasibility may be\n    considered before it does. It is still second because its comparison target\n    is the ceiling and the ceiling's definitional gap is LIVE in the approved v2\n    (DEC-20260907-b6bcf4 CR-1a: `cap`, `CAP_MULT`, `cycle_mass` and `capped_mass`\n    appear ZERO times in it), so an arm run today would be read against a\n    definition a from-scratch re-deriver cannot recover. Fix the definition at\n    RANK 1, then measure against it -- an ordering with a reason, not a deferral.\n    Carried alongside it, unchanged from DEC-20260906-bcc097 RANK 2 and\n    outstanding before ANY promotion beyond `analyzed` on any clause of\n    H-ECDLP-37dc01: the EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 amendment items -- a permanent v2-native\n    null-collapse regression fixture, the S2_v2 magnitude confound, S_peak_bits\n    from the finer per-target tracker, a bootstrap CI on the CAP(2T, T_sel)\n    retention ratio, and the G3 N = 2^30 binding/informational ambiguity.\n    RANK 3 (completion criterion C2, this goal's ONLY OPEN criterion): discharge\n    its blocker on EXP-ECDLP-869870 -- instantiate the O(theta) correction under\n    an additive amendment, or file an amendment that explicitly gates on the raw\n    residual, per BATCH-1e7251's checkpoint `lane_next_action` and\n    DEC-20260907-ece434 -- then score `fixture_gate_v2`, only then V2-V5 /\n    M1-M5, and compose the basin-law, oracle-ceiling and published-rule\n    measurements with their CIs and the N-independence verdict across\n    2^20..2^30 that C2's text requires. BATCH-1e7251 is CLOSED and this successor\n    is unclaimed: claim it with `tools/goal_lanes.py claim` before dispatching.\n    RANKED THIRD DESPITE BEING THE ONLY OPEN CRITERION -- the strongest argument\n    any candidate here has, and it still loses: its blocker is INSTRUMENTAL\n    rather than scientific, its next step is ALSO an amendment authorship so it\n    gains nothing in immediacy, and completing the criterion tally while the\n    central clause sits at `preliminary` on small samples would optimise the\n    wrong quantity. C1 and C3 being MET makes that more tempting, not more\n    justified.\n    RANK 4 (the EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 successor BATCH-8f3e86's close owes, RE-SCOPED\n    against a record its own lane could not see): DEC-20260907-6d9427 leaves two\n    frozen-text defects for additive correction (residual R3's false three-way\n    independence claim; the false measure-zero tie-break claim) and names as its\n    own RANK 1 a G3 re-derivation by an implementation genuinely independent of\n    experiments/EXP-ECDLP-612fb1/source_v2/instrument.py at a in {1/16, 1/8}.\n    RE-SCOPE IT FIRST: TASK-20260907-2db9aa's Stage A' re-seal (EV-ECDLP-6783b8)\n    already used an independently constructed self-map, independent Bernoulli\n    marking and exact binary-lifting absorption -- NOT source_v2/instrument.py --\n    at a = 1/8 and a = 1/4, N = 2^24. That is a CANDIDATE third angle at a = 1/8\n    which BATCH-8f3e86 did not have in view, and this head does NOT assert it\n    discharges R3: whether it does is a question for whoever owns\n    EXP-ECDLP-612fb1, on the record. What is clearly still owed is a = 1/16,\n    which EV-ECDLP-6783b8 explicitly does not retest.\n    RANK 5 (cheap, small, untouched, plus one piece of housekeeping with a\n    measured cost): IDEA-20260906-a3d6ae (the growth-type comparator\n    EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 cites as its frontier point) and the cheap closures\n    IDEA-20260906-05ffb8 (the c-sweep), IDEA-20260906-cf3b76 (walk-rule\n    invariance of C_max) and IDEA-20260906-ac100b (the (B1)-(B3) derivation, a\n    validator task). None attempted, none blocked; last only because none bears\n    on the borderline cell or on C2. CARRIED WITH THEM: bind EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 and\n    H-ECDLP-37dc01 to `goal_id: GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f` rather than `null`, and\n    register BATCH-3c7493 as a closed lane of this goal, so `tools/goal_lanes.py`\n    can see the work that advances it. HB-1 HAS NOW RECURRED TWICE with a\n    nameable cost each time -- once it made this head's RANK 1 ask for work\n    already landed, once it made BATCH-48ef8b's own RANK 1 rest on a premise\n    already overtaken on main. Both are additive record changes on records no\n    closed lane owned. DO THEM OPPORTUNISTICALLY INSIDE WHICHEVER LANE NEXT\n    OPENS: they do not justify a lane of their own, and dispatching one would be\n    exactly the make-work an unlimited ECC budget invites.\n    GOAL STATUS: `active`, `impediments` EMPTY. NO completion criterion closes\n    this goal -- C1 MET, C3 MET, C2 OPEN -- and DEC-20260907-de6b71\n    `goal_closure_assessment` records the full reasoning: why a two-of-three\n    tally does not license `completed` even with the closure quorum SUSPENDED\n    (which is exactly why that decision declines rather than closes), why\n    neither `closed_at_budget` nor `cancelled` would be honest, and why the\n    decisive objection is on the merits -- the central hypothesis clause is\n    confirmed only at CEILING level, only at `preliminary` strength, and ZERO\n    ONLINE RESEL-L ARMS HAVE EVER BEEN RUN, so nothing yet bears on the question\n    RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5 actually asks. As of this close every lane of this goal is\n    CLOSED and the RANK 1 successor is UNCLAIMED.\n  next_action_superseded_20260907_48ef8b: >-\n    RANK 1 (this goal's ranked ECC work on its central question; successor to\n    the closed lane BATCH-e9fd22, per DEC-20260907-b6bcf4): AUTHOR\n    PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3 as experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml\n    BESIDE v1 and the APPROVED v2, editing neither. Discharge D2 FIRST -- state\n    cap = ceil(8*W), state that a point on a DP-free cycle or whose first DP\n    lies beyond the cap belongs to NO basin, state the true relation\n    sum_d b(d) = N - cycle_mass - capped_mass, require both readings to report\n    cycle_mass and capped_mass per cell, and state that a capped\n    pool-construction walk is charged and credits no S_d or h_d -- BECAUSE D2\n    IS LIVE IN THE APPROVED v2 AND NOT ONLY IN THE REFUSED DRAFT: `cap`,\n    `CAP_MULT`, `cycle_mass` and `capped_mass` appear ZERO times in\n    experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml, so the approved\n    contract's own required Stage A' re-seal hands a from-scratch re-deriver a\n    convention it must invent -- the same class of gap that produced the\n    a = 1/8 disagreement, relocated from the weight to the cap\n    (DEC-20260907-b6bcf4 CR-1a; magnitude and direction UNMEASURED, so this is\n    a risk of recurrence and not a prediction that any verdict flips). Then D3\n    (move the Coordinator's directional prior off the pre-seal reading path\n    into its own file; add that file, ledger/handoffs/TASK-20260907-e423d5.yaml,\n    the batch dispatch queue, DEC-20260907-4e34c5 and the gate's task directory\n    to `blind_from`; widen the contamination declaration from commit messages\n    to every committed path the re-deriver is instructed or likely to read\n    before sealing; name ONE authoritative blind list per AO-3). Then D1, which\n    against the approved v2 is a value to STATE rather than a contradiction to\n    repair: T = 64 and T_sel = 32 at N = 2^20 cited to EXP-ECDLP-612fb1\n    specification.v2.yaml line 223, or drop the second scale, which\n    DEC-20260907-9b1b02 RANK 1 never asked for. Then fold D4 (tie-break key),\n    D5 (decouple agreement from the bootstrap interval), D6 (a = 1/16\n    independence asymmetric and binding: zero weight for agreement, full weight\n    plus rule 12 for disagreement) and D7 (add a null of the real\n    measurement's SHAPE over the same basin universe). Carry the wide scope --\n    25 seeds with the seeds 1..5 subgroup reported separately, interval\n    estimation with an unresolved verdict, the externally anchored DECAY-A, the\n    de-tautologised DECAY-TSEL, and the reproduction control against the\n    committed v1 cells -- under DEC-20260907-b6bcf4's four conditions COND-1\n    (append the N = 2^20 arm; the approved v2 states nothing there, so there is\n    nothing to contradict), COND-2 (KEEP S1/S2/S3 with the approved v2's\n    meanings verbatim and give the new interval-routed outcome a FRESH label --\n    the refused draft renumbers them, which would make \"S3\" denote two\n    outcomes for one experiment, the same failure this experiment already\n    suffered at the amendment id), COND-3 (supersede control (e) SEED-COUNT\n    PARITY by APPENDING a control that quotes it verbatim; the seed set is the\n    one wide-scope item invalidation_rules item 7 does not name) and COND-4\n    (append sub-keys inside `blind_rederivation`, whose `frozen: true` the\n    approved v2 itself already appended under). v3 then requires ITS OWN FRESH\n    APPROVAL GATE in a session that authored none of it, and that gate must\n    RE-RUN the contract-versus-implementation comparison against the APPROVED\n    v2's text, which no gate has yet done -- D1 and D2 were both found that way\n    and neither is inheritable. A new committed decision must set v3's four\n    gate fields before any executor runs. THIS DOES NOT BLOCK, GATE OR CLAIM\n    BATCH-8f3e86, which is another session's open lane and whose approved\n    narrow re-seal can execute today.\n    RANK 2 (the only route to a complete criterion set): discharge C2's blocker\n    on EXP-ECDLP-869870 -- instantiate the O(theta) correction under an\n    additive amendment, or file an amendment that explicitly gates on the raw\n    residual, per BATCH-1e7251's checkpoint `lane_next_action` and\n    DEC-20260907-ece434 -- then score `fixture_gate_v2`, only then V2-V5 /\n    M1-M5, and compose the basin-law, oracle-ceiling and published-rule\n    measurements with their CIs and the N-independence verdict across\n    2^20..2^30 that C2's text requires. BATCH-1e7251 is CLOSED and this\n    successor is unclaimed: claim it with `tools/goal_lanes.py claim` before\n    dispatching. Ranked SECOND, not first, although C2 is the only OPEN\n    criterion: its blocker is instrumental rather than scientific, its next\n    step is also an amendment authorship so it gains nothing in immediacy, and\n    completing the criterion tally while the central hypothesis clause sits\n    unresolved at the operating point this goal cares about would optimise the\n    wrong quantity. C1 and C3 being MET makes that more tempting, not more\n    justified.\n    RANK 3 (unchanged, carried from DEC-20260907-9b1b02 RANK 2, and the largest\n    genuine gap this goal has): the ONLINE RESEL-L batch at the\n    confirmed-feasible a values, mirroring EXP-ECDLP-612fb1's online-arm design,\n    with a heuristic-validation component against HEUR-BLT-7. Every ceiling\n    result this goal holds is SILENT on whether the online lower-bracket\n    mechanism REACHES that ceiling at any achievable batch size U, and ZERO\n    online arms have ever been run; no hypothesis-status promotion beyond\n    ceiling-feasibility may be considered before it does. It stays third\n    because it is the largest of the three and because its output would be read\n    against a definition D2 leaves incomplete -- run it after v3 lands and the\n    reading is uncontested. Carried alongside it, unchanged from\n    DEC-20260906-bcc097 RANK 2: the v3 amendment items on EXP-ECDLP-612fb1\n    (permanent v2-native null-collapse fixture; S2_v2 magnitude confound;\n    S_peak_bits from the finer per-target tracker; a bootstrap CI on the\n    CAP(2T,T_sel) retention ratio; the G3 N = 2^30 binding/informational\n    ambiguity), outstanding before ANY promotion beyond `analyzed` on any\n    clause of H-ECDLP-37dc01.\n    RANK 4 (cheap, small, untouched): IDEA-20260906-a3d6ae (growth-type\n    comparator) and the cheap closures IDEA-20260906-05ffb8,\n    IDEA-20260906-cf3b76, IDEA-20260906-ac100b. None attempted, none blocked.\n    Last only because none bears on the a = 1/8 cell or on C2.\n    RANK 5 (housekeeping, and the reason HB-1 exists): decide whether\n    EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 and H-ECDLP-37dc01 should carry\n    `goal_id: GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f` rather than `null`, and whether BATCH-3c7493\n    should be retroactively registered as a closed lane of this goal so its\n    work is visible to `tools/goal_lanes.py`. Both are additive record changes\n    on records BATCH-e9fd22 did not own. Mitigated for now by\n    `external_work_advancing_this_goal_20260907_e9fd22` above, which names the\n    four affected records so the next head read is not blind; the cause is not\n    repaired.\n    GOAL STATUS: `active`, `impediments` EMPTY. NO completion criterion closes\n    this goal -- C1 MET, C3 MET, C2 OPEN -- and DEC-20260907-b6bcf4\n    `goal_closure_assessment` records the full reasoning, including why a\n    two-of-three tally does not license `completed` under the suspended quorum\n    and why neither `closed_at_budget` nor `cancelled` would be honest.\n  next_action_superseded_20260907_48ef8b_disposition: >-\n    Preserved verbatim above, byte-for-byte, in exactly one place (a superseded\n    ranking copied into two keys is a ranking that can later disagree with\n    itself, and a reader has no way to tell which copy is the original).\n    DISPOSITION, ITEM BY ITEM. Its RANK 1 -- author PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3\n    discharging D2, D3 and D1 and carrying the wide scope under CR-1's four\n    conditions, then gate it in a session that authored none of it -- IS\n    DISCHARGED IN SUBSTANCE AND REFUSED IN FORM. BATCH-48ef8b authored exactly\n    that amendment; an independent gate confirmed ALL SEVEN predecessor defects\n    D1-D7 GENUINELY DISCHARGED, verified the cap convention derivable from v3's\n    text alone, recomputed W and cap at all eight cells and the accounting\n    identity at all 20 committed v1 cells, and confirmed the D3 repair by\n    MECHANISM (a closed positive allowlist) rather than by list-lengthening --\n    and then returned `revise` on seven findings of its own about the coherence\n    of the contract's own instruction text (DEC-20260907-adbe7e). SO v3 IS NOT\n    APPROVED, is not execution-authorized, and NO RUN MAY EXECUTE UNDER IT; the\n    successor is the new RANK 1 above, which is a superseding revision at a new\n    snapshot rather than a fresh authorship. Its RANK 2 (C2 on\n    EXP-ECDLP-869870) is UNTOUCHED and is now RANK 3 -- demoted by one on the\n    promotion below, not on any change in its own merits. Its RANK 3 (the online\n    RESEL-L arm, with the EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 v3 items carried alongside) is\n    PROMOTED to RANK 2, because its blocking precondition -- a confirmed-feasible\n    operating point to run an online arm AT -- now exists at two a values rather\n    than one (EV-ECDLP-6783b8 / DEC-20260907-8d8782 at a = 1/8, corroborated by\n    EV-ECDLP-6a4ebc / DEC-20260907-6d9427). Its RANK 4 (the cheap-closure ideas)\n    and RANK 5 (the HB-1 housekeeping) are UNCHANGED in substance and are merged\n    into the new RANK 5, with the housekeeping's recurrence cost now recorded.\n    ONE ITEM IS NEW AND IS NOT A RERANKING OF ANYTHING ABOVE: CF-3's superseding\n    record against the APPROVED specification.v2.yaml, whose gate-named owner\n    BATCH-8f3e86 closed while this lane ran, carried as a required item of\n    RANK 1. Nothing in this rerank re-scores, reinterprets or retracts any\n    committed finding, and no measurement originates in it. Reranked by\n    TASK-20260907-1aa16f under DEC-20260907-de6b71, against a fact base that\n    moved while the lane ran -- see\n    `external_work_advancing_this_goal_20260907_48ef8b`.\n  next_action_superseded_20260907_e9fd22: >-\n    RANK 1 (IN FLIGHT as BATCH-e9fd22, opened by DEC-20260907-38e5ae): resolve\n    a = 1/8. Per DEC-20260907-9b1b02's own RANK 1, EXP-ECDLP-6ac801's a = 1/8\n    cell is genuinely OPEN -- its blind and production readings disagreed, and\n    the cause was traced to an underspecification in that contract's own\n    `definitions.STATIC(T)_r exact coverage` text, which names the\n    Bernstein-Lange selection weight without stating it, so no from-scratch\n    re-deriver could recover it. BATCH-e9fd22 carries: the versioned additive\n    amendment PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v1-to-v2 stating weight_d = S_d + 4*W*h_d\n    explicitly (PROPOSED, gated behind approval task TASK-20260907-f65c6e); a\n    25-seed pre-registered production arm at N in {2^20, 2^24} with a null\n    object (NULL-RANDSEL) and two decay controls; a FRESHLY SEALED independent\n    blind re-derivation by a reviewer that has not read the prior one; and an\n    independent red-team pass on the controls and the interpretation, which\n    DEC-20260907-9b1b02 named as a disclosed gap of the prior batch.\n    RANK 2 (unchanged, carried from DEC-20260907-9b1b02 RANK 2, gated on\n    RANK 1): an online RESEL-L follow-up batch at the confirmed-feasible a\n    values, mirroring EXP-ECDLP-612fb1's v1/v2 online-arm design, with a\n    heuristic-validation component against HEUR-BLT-7. A ceiling-feasibility\n    result does NOT demonstrate that the online lower-bracket mechanism reaches\n    that ceiling at any achievable batch size U, and no hypothesis-status\n    promotion beyond ceiling-feasibility may be considered before this runs.\n    RANK 3 (unchanged, carried from DEC-20260906-bcc097 RANK 2 and\n    DEC-20260907-9b1b02 RANK 3): the v3 amendment items on EXP-ECDLP-612fb1,\n    outstanding before ANY hypothesis-status promotion beyond `analyzed` on any\n    clause of H-ECDLP-37dc01 -- a permanent v2-native null-collapse regression\n    fixture; resolution or explicit re-argument of the S2_v2 magnitude confound;\n    S_peak_bits from the finer per-target tracker; a bootstrap CI on the\n    CAP(2T,T_sel) retention ratio; resolution of the G3 N = 2^30\n    binding/informational ambiguity. Untouched by BATCH-e9fd22.\n    RANK 4 (unchanged): the EXP-ECDLP-869870 successor cell (re-keyed 2^24\n    fixture, completion criterion C2) and the cheap closures\n    IDEA-20260906-a3d6ae, IDEA-20260906-05ffb8, IDEA-20260906-cf3b76,\n    IDEA-20260906-ac100b -- all ranked ahead of doing nothing on this\n    ECC-priority campaign.\n  next_action_superseded_20260907_e9fd22_disposition: >-\n    Preserved verbatim above, byte-for-byte, in exactly one place (a superseded\n    ranking copied into two keys is a ranking that can later disagree with\n    itself). DISPOSITION, item by item. Its RANK 1 is DISCHARGED ONLY IN THE\n    NEGATIVE: BATCH-e9fd22 ran to its approval gate and the gate REFUSED the\n    protocol (DEC-20260907-4e34c5), so a = 1/8 IS NOT RESOLVED and this lane\n    will not resolve it -- the successor is the new RANK 1 above. Its RANK 2\n    (online RESEL-L) is UNCHANGED and is now RANK 3. Its RANK 3 (the\n    EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 v3 items) is UNCHANGED and is carried alongside the new\n    RANK 3. Its RANK 4 split: the EXP-ECDLP-869870 successor cell was EXECUTED\n    by the disjoint lane BATCH-1e7251 (16/16 completed_valid, blinded J1-J4 all\n    hold or PASS) but left `fixture_gate_v2` NOT SCORED, so C2 is still OPEN\n    and that work is PROMOTED to the new RANK 2; the four cheap-closure ideas\n    are UNCHANGED and are now RANK 4. Nothing in this rerank re-scores,\n    reinterprets or retracts any committed finding, and no measurement\n    originates in it. Reranked by TASK-20260907-9e7580 under\n    DEC-20260907-b6bcf4.\n  next_action_superseded_20260906: >-\n    RANK 1: a small, independently reviewed follow-up (design + execute +\n    review, or a v3 amendment item) resolving whether T_sel = T/2 is\n    genuinely G3-feasible at a in {1/16, 1/8} on EXP-ECDLP-612fb1, ideally\n    at N = 2^24 exact basins with a blind re-derivation -- per a discrepancy\n    DEC-20260906-bcc097 surfaced in the v2 batch's own committed Stage 0\n    a-scan data and the orchestrating session then NUMERICALLY CONFIRMED\n    from the raw per-seed data by a second, independent route (T_sel = T/2\n    G3-feasible at a = 1/16, 5/5 seeds, and a = 1/8, 4/5 seeds, r = 2,\n    N = 2^20 -- contradicting the executor's own stated conclusion). The\n    numbers are confirmed; FORMAL independent review (blind rederivation,\n    proves-too-much control) is what RANK 1 still owes. If that review\n    confirms feasibility this reopens clause (C1) of H-ECDLP-37dc01 at a\n    different, smaller a. RANK 2: a v3 amendment to EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 before any\n    hypothesis-status promotion beyond `analyzed` -- a permanent,\n    committed null-collapse regression fixture (red team's J4 coverage-gap\n    finding), an explicit resolution of the S2_v2 magnitude confound\n    (NULL-A's perturbation measured 2-3x the effect at every cell this\n    batch), S_peak_bits computed from the finer per-target tracker, a\n    bootstrap CI on the CAP(2T,T_sel) retention ratio, and a resolution of\n    the G3 N = 2^30 binding/informational ambiguity the validator surfaced.\n    RANK 3 (unchanged from DEC-20260906-1f5b71): the EXP-ECDLP-869870\n    successor cell (re-keyed 2^24 fixture). RANK 4 (unchanged): design\n    IDEA-20260906-a3d6ae (growth-type comparator) and the\n    c-sweep/cf3b76/ac100b cheap closures.\n  owner: coordinator\n  created_at: '2026-09-06'\n  updated_at: '2026-09-07'","lineStart":780,"lineEnd":1159,"totalLines":1159,"truncated":false}},"title":"ledger/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/goal.yaml","time":{"start":1789087406386,"end":1789087406401}},"id":"prt_08deb50f3001LG89Hl0aJCN2Zu","sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","messageID":"msg_08dea192d001svcwpL1hvhmcIj"}}
