{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789087673437,"sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-bf656efc0d09655c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/ledger/decisions/DEC-20260907-b4f2a9.yaml"},"output":"<path>/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/ledger/decisions/DEC-20260907-b4f2a9.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # The INDEPENDENT approval-gate decision that APPROVES PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3-r2\n2: # (specification.v3.yaml) after independently re-verifying TASK-20260907-7cce3e's\n3: # claimed discharge of all four required fixes named by DEC-20260907-2c4beb /\n4: # experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/v2_to_v3.gate-outcome.yaml. This\n5: # decision sets specification.v3.yaml's gate fields to approved/coordinator/\n6: # true/true. It asserts no research finding on the ECDLP and authorizes no\n7: # run of any kind beyond dispatch of Stage A'' and, after its seal, Stage B/C\n8: # execution under this now-frozen contract.\n9: \n10: coordinator_decision:\n11:   id: DEC-20260907-b4f2a9\n12:   id_allocation_provenance: >-\n13:     This gate session has no Bash/shell tool (Read, Grep, Glob, Write, Edit,\n14:     SendMessage only) and could not itself run `python3 tools/allocate_id.py\n15:     --next coordinator_decision --date 20260907` or `--check` it, exactly the\n16:     same disclosed limitation DEC-20260907-2c4beb's own session recorded. It\n17:     confirmed by Glob (`**/*b4f2a9*`) that no file exists anywhere in this\n18:     repository at that token before authoring this record. The orchestrating\n19:     session must run `python3 tools/allocate_id.py --check coordinator_decision\n20:     DEC-20260907-b4f2a9` before this record is treated as durable.\n21:   recorded_at: '2026-09-07'\n22:   goal_id: GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f\n23:   goal_id_note: >-\n24:     EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 and H-ECDLP-37dc01 both carry `goal_id: null` and this\n25:     decision does not change that. GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f is named because the\n26:     gated revision and its fixes were authored in that goal's lane\n27:     (BATCH-d7e987 / BATCH-48ef8b); no GOAL binding is created on any record.\n28:   question_id: RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5\n29:   experiment_id: EXP-ECDLP-6ac801\n30:   hypothesis_id: H-ECDLP-37dc01\n31:   batch_id: BATCH-d7e987\n32:   task_id: TASK-20260907-e17c05\n33: \n34:   gated_object:\n35:     what_was_gated: >-\n36:       PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3-r2, as amended by TASK-20260907-7cce3e's\n37:       post-gate fixes on top of DEC-20260907-2c4beb's `revise` verdict, as it\n38:       stood in experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml immediately\n39:       before this decision: `status: proposed`, `approved_by: null`, `frozen:\n40:       false`, `execution_authorized: false`.\n41:     paths:\n42:       contract: experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml\n43:       amendment: experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml\n44:       derivation_packet_dir: experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/derivation-packet/PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3/\n45:       prior_gate_outcome_record: experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/v2_to_v3.gate-outcome.yaml\n46:       prior_gate_decision: ledger/decisions/DEC-20260907-2c4beb.yaml\n47:       fix_task_handoff: ledger/handoffs/TASK-20260907-7cce3e.yaml\n48:       fix_receipt: experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/archives/TASK-20260907-7cce3e/fix-receipt.json\n49: \n50:   context: >-\n51:     DEC-20260907-2c4beb (`revise`) found PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3-r2\n52:     scientifically sound (D1/D2/D3 discharge SOUND, not reopened) but blocked\n53:     approval on four disclosure/consistency defects A-D. TASK-20260907-7cce3e\n54:     then authored fixes for defects A, B and C as ordinary draft-revision\n55:     edits to the still-unapproved v3 contract and packet, with defect D\n56:     (independent sha256 recomputation and am1_self_consistency.py re-run)\n57:     explicitly out of its scope and performed separately by \"the\n58:     orchestrating session (Bash)\" per `amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml\n59:     post_gate_fixes_applied.fix_4_defect_d`. This decision is a FRESH,\n60:     independent gate session -- not TASK-20260907-7cce3e, not\n61:     TASK-20260907-b1b54b, not TASK-20260907-9c0626, not TASK-20260907-058c69\n62:     -- that independently re-verified each of the four claimed fixes directly\n63:     against committed repository bytes rather than accepting\n64:     `post_gate_fixes_applied`'s self-report at face value, per this gate\n65:     task's own governing instruction.\n66: \n67:   leak_discipline_on_this_record: >-\n68:     BINDING, adopted verbatim from DEC-20260907-2c4beb and\n69:     specification.v3.yaml's own `leak_discipline_on_this_record`. This record\n70:     is not on the derivation packet's `readable_files` allowlist and must not\n71:     become a leak channel into a future Stage A'' re-derivation. It states no\n72:     per-cell G3 verdict, pass-count, margin value, margin sign, or crossing\n73:     bracket at a = 1/16, a = 1/8 or a = 3/16 at either N beyond citing the\n74:     ALREADY-DISCLOSED a = 1/8 leak text this decision confirms is now properly\n75:     disclosed (not newly revealed by this decision) and the already-disclosed\n76:     a = 1/4 control anchor.\n77: \n78:   decision: approve_experiment\n79: \n80:   decision_verb_note: >-\n81:     `approve_experiment`, mirroring DEC-20260906-806501's verb for the prior\n82:     approval on this experiment lineage (EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 v1-to-v2). Unlike\n83:     that decision, no fresh `user_confirmation_record` / AskUserQuestion step\n84:     is recorded here: this is the INDEPENDENT TECHNICAL APPROVAL GATE\n85:     specification.v3.yaml's own `gate_fields_note` names as the sole path to\n86:     execution authorization (a coordinator session that authored none of the\n87:     gated artifacts), the same class of decision DEC-20260907-2c4beb already\n88:     established as the applicable procedure for this exact gate when it\n89:     returned `revise` -- not a new first-time draft presentation requiring a\n90:     separate user-facing confirmation gate.\n91: \n92:   target_ids:\n93:     - PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3-r2\n94:     - EXP-ECDLP-6ac801\n95:     - TASK-20260907-e17c05\n96:     - TASK-20260907-7cce3e\n97:     - DEC-20260907-2c4beb\n98:   target_ids_note: >-\n99:     Added by the orchestrating session after independently re-verifying this\n100:     record and finding the schema's required `target_ids` field absent from\n101:     the gate subagent's own draft (tools/validate_ledger.py flagged it: 43\n102:     errors after this record's creation vs. the 42 pre-existing errors\n103:     fix-receipt.json's own verification_note disclosed). No other field in\n104:     this record is edited by this addition.\n105: \n106:   per_defect_independent_reverification:\n107:     defect_A:\n108:       claim: >-\n109:         TASK-20260907-7cce3e disclosed the a = 1/8 leak in\n110:         `leak_discipline_on_this_record` (specification.v3.yaml, appended\n111:         paragraph at approximately line 2174) and in the `protocol_amendment`\n112:         \"a = 1/16 INDEPENDENCE RULING\" standing-contamination sub-block\n113:         (appended paragraph at approximately line 753), without deleting or\n114:         rewording either existing disclosure entry.\n115:       independently_reverified: >-\n116:         CONFIRMED by direct read of both exact locations in the current\n117:         committed specification.v3.yaml. Both appended paragraphs are present,\n118:         each explicitly named \"DEFECT A DISCLOSURE\" and each citing\n119:         TASK-20260907-7cce3e and DEC-20260907-2c4beb by id, each naming the\n120:         exact leak text (\"It is confirmed ceiling-feasible at N = 2^24 at\n121:         strength `preliminary` (EV-ECDLP-6783b8 / DEC-20260907-8d8782)...\")\n122:         and its exact location (`v3_r2_addendum.objective_v3_r2`,\n123:         approximately lines 2220-2222), and each stating the leak is\n124:         CONTAINED TODAY ONLY because `prohibitions.md` blanket-forbids\n125:         reading `specification.v3.yaml`. Grepped `EV-ECDLP-6783b8` across the\n126:         whole file: exactly 3 hits -- the original leak in `objective_v3_r2`\n127:         (unmoved, verbatim, as the fix explicitly does not redact it) and the\n128:         two new disclosure paragraphs. No fourth, undisclosed occurrence\n129:         exists. The text immediately preceding each appended paragraph (the\n130:         pre-existing \"a = 1/16 INDEPENDENCE RULING\" content and the\n131:         pre-existing `leak_discipline_on_this_record` prose) is unchanged,\n132:         confirmed by direct read against the text quoted in\n133:         DEC-20260907-2c4beb `deciding_sentence` and the gate-outcome record's\n134:         own quoted blocks.\n135:       verdict: DISCHARGED, correctly and completely. No new problem introduced.\n136:     defect_B:\n137:       claim: >-\n138:         TASK-20260907-7cce3e rewrote quantity.md section 13 and MANIFEST.yaml\n139:         `the_one_disclosed_inclusion.what` to drop \"established\"/\"ESTABLISHED\"\n140:         and \"independent work\", replacing them with the r2-corrected\n141:         characterisation from `v3_r2_addendum.cf2_anchor_strength`.\n142:       independently_reverified: >-\n143:         Grepped `established|independent work` (case-insensitive) across the\n144:         WHOLE derivation-packet directory: exactly ONE hit, in\n145:         MANIFEST.yaml's `sha256_recomputed_note` (line 59), which is a\n146:         historical note DESCRIBING the correction itself (\"the stale\n147:         'established'/'independent work' a=1/4 characterization was\n148:         corrected\") -- not a live characterisation of EV-ECDLP-60e266. It is\n149:         quoted as the OLD, superseded phrase inside a note about what changed,\n150:         the same disclosure pattern this program's own defect-disclosure\n151:         paragraphs use elsewhere (e.g. Defect A's own disclosure quotes the\n152:         leaked text to name it). Zero occurrences remain as a live assertion\n153:         anywhere in quantity.md, deliverables.md or prohibitions.md.\n154:         Read quantity.md section 13 in full: it now reads \"`T_sel = T/2` at\n155:         `a = 1/4`... records G3-INFEASIBILITY at strength `preliminary`, on\n156:         one execution batch, with no independent implementation (evidence\n157:         record `EV-ECDLP-60e266`)\" -- checked WORD FOR WORD against\n158:         specification.v3.yaml `v3_r2_addendum.cf2_anchor_strength`'s own\n159:         corrected characterisation (\"EV-ECDLP-60e266 records a = 1/4\n160:         G3-infeasibility at strength `preliminary`, on one execution batch,\n161:         with no independent implementation\") and found to be an accurate\n162:         paraphrase carrying the identical claim, not merely different words.\n163:         MANIFEST.yaml's own `the_one_disclosed_inclusion.what` field checked\n164:         the same way: matches.\n165:       verdict: DISCHARGED, correctly and completely. The one remaining string\n166:         match is a disclosed historical note, not a live mischaracterization,\n167:         and is itself in keeping with this program's own disclosure norms.\n168:     defect_C:\n169:       claim: >-\n170:         TASK-20260907-7cce3e added an inline superseded-flag to the base\n171:         `required_artifacts` clause at specification.v3.yaml (approximately\n172:         line 1754/1770), pointing to\n173:         `v3_r2_addendum.cf1_required_artifacts_override` and\n174:         `required_artifacts_r2`, without deleting the base clause.\n175:       independently_reverified: >-\n176:         Read the exact `required_artifacts` list entry in full (line 1770).\n177:         The ORIGINAL fifteen-letter clause text (\"the control report: for\n178:         every declared control (a)-(o), per cell, FIRED or