d NOT literally reproduce required fix\n207:         (4)'s verification by direct command execution, and does not claim to\n208:         have done so. What follows is the strongest verification available\n209:         within this session's actual tool surface, performed BEFORE trusting\n210:         `post_gate_fixes_applied`'s prose account, not as a substitute\n211:         offered in place of a real shell-based check.\n212:       independently_reverified_by_alternate_means:\n213:         - >-\n214:           READ THE SCRIPT'S OWN SOURCE CODE\n215:           (coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-d7e987/tasks/TASK-20260907-b1b54b/am1_self_consistency.py)\n216:           rather than trusting a description of its behaviour: line 20,\n217:           `OUT = Path(__file__).with_name(\"am1_report.json\")`, and line 166,\n218:           `OUT.write_text(json.dumps(report, indent=2) + \"\\n\")` inside\n219:           `main()`. CONFIRMS the side-effect risk the prior gate found is\n220:           real and structural -- any bare re-run of this script DOES overwrite\n221:           `am1_report.json` in place, unconditionally.\n222:         - >-\n223:           READ THE CURRENT COMMITTED am1_report.json\n224:           (coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-d7e987/tasks/TASK-20260907-b1b54b/am1_report.json)\n225:           directly: it still shows `spec_sha256:\n226:           08cad9ac6621dc1aed776efe968b2663cfdaf01a3a34551a57b5be392c957eee`,\n227:           the value from BEFORE TASK-20260907-7cce3e edited\n228:           specification.v3.yaml. Since a bare re-run against the POST-fix tree\n229:           would necessarily write a DIFFERENT spec_sha256 (the file's bytes\n230:           changed), the fact that the currently committed file still shows\n231:           the OLD value is consistent with the claimed revert having actually\n232:           happened (or with the script simply never having run against this\n233:           exact path) -- and is NOT consistent with an unreverted, silently\n234:           corrupted deliverable, which is the one outcome that would have been\n235:           a genuine new problem.\n236:         - >-\n237:           FOUND AND READ A SEPARATELY COMMITTED, CONTENT-HASHED FIX RECEIPT\n238:           (experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/archives/TASK-20260907-7cce3e/fix-receipt.json,\n239:           `commit_sha: f95e8590fb6e5139ea6e56e145030bb285858903`) that this\n240:           gate went looking for rather than being pointed to, via Glob on\n241:           `**/*7cce3e*`. Its own `verification_note` states explicitly, in\n242:           its own words, that TASK-20260907-b1b54b's am1_report.json \"was\n243:           found modified as an unintended side effect of re-running\n244:           am1_self_consistency.py and was reverted via `git checkout --`\n245:           before this commit -- confirmed excluded from this commit's own\n246:           declared paths\". Its `staged_top_level_paths` list is checked\n247:           directly and does NOT include am1_report.json, consistent with\n248:           that claim. Its `path_sha256` map records well-formed 64-hex-char\n249:           sha256 values (individually counted by this gate, not merely\n250:           eyeballed) for specification.v3.yaml, amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml,\n251:           quantity.md, MANIFEST.yaml and the fix task's own handoff -- the\n252:           quantity.md value (7040669a...b68) matches exactly what is\n253:           currently declared inside MANIFEST.yaml itself, confirming no\n254:           further, later, undisclosed edit has occurred to that file since\n255:           this receipt's commit.\n256:         - >-\n257:           This is a DIFFERENT and WEAKER form of verification than literally\n258:           executing `sha256sum` and the script, and this decision does not\n259:           overstate it: it is cross-referencing three independently readable,\n260:           mutually corroborating, committed artifacts (the script's own logic,\n261:           the current file state, and a separately content-hashed receipt)\n262:           rather than accepting one paragraph of prose in\n263:           `post_gate_fixes_applied` on its own say-so. No contradiction was\n264:           found among the three. A session WITH Bash independently re-running\n265:           `sha256sum` against the three packet files and `git log\n266:           f95e8590fb6e5139ea6e56e145030bb285858903` to confirm the commit is\n267:           reachable remains the strictly stronger check and is not performed\n268:           here; it is not, in this decision's judgment, required to be\n269:           performed by THIS session specifically before approval, given the\n270:           convergent evidence above and the low residual risk (a false claim\n271:           in fix-receipt.json would itself be a fabrication under AGENTS.md\n272:           rule 5, a different and more severe problem than an unverified\n273:           hash, and nothing in the fix-receipt's content is inconsistent with\n274:           anything else this gate independently read).\n275:       verdict: >-\n276:         DISCHARGED on convergent, independently-sought corroborating evidence,\n277:         WITH THE ABOVE LIMITATION EXPLICITLY DISCLOSED rather than silently\n278:         elided. This is the one defect this decision does not claim to have\n279:         closed by literal command re-execution.\n280: \n281:   additivity_check:\n282:     verdict: no additivity violation found, independently re-verified\n283:     method: >-\n284:       Read `definitions` (specification.v3.yaml lines 313-413, up to and\n285:       including the `STATIC(T)_r pool-selection weight formula` key) side by\n286:       side against specification.v2.yaml `definitions` (lines 272-374) in\n287:       full: identical text, confirmed by direct visual comparison of this\n288:       gate's own two Read calls, not merely cited from a prior claim. Did the\n289:       same for `blind_rederivation` (v3 lines 869-974 up to and including\n290:       `v2_rerequirement_a_1_8`, against v2 lines 424-529), `controls` items\n291:       (a)-(f) (v3 lines 1146-1182, against v2 lines 531-568), and\n292:       `success_criterion` (v3 lines 1628-1652, against v2 lines 703-727).\n293:     result: >-\n294:       PASS on every field checked. New content in each block is appended\n295:       after the shared text, never interleaved, exactly as\n296:       DEC-20260907-2c4beb's own `additivity_check` and the gate-outcome\n297:       record's `additivity_check` state.\n298:     gate_fields_confirmed_unchanged_before_this_decision: >-\n299:       Grepped `^  status:|^  approved_by:|^  frozen:|^  execution_authorized:`\n300:       against specification.v3.yaml immediately before authoring this\n301:       decision's edits: `status: proposed`, `approved_by: null`, `frozen:\n302:       false`, `execution_authorized: false` -- exactly as DEC-20260907-2c4beb\n303:       left them. TASK-20260907-7cce3e's fixes did not sneak in an approval.\n304:     fix_task_confined_to_declared_edits: >-\n305:       Grepped `TASK-20260907-7cce3e` across the whole of specification.v3.yaml:\n306:       exactly 3 hits, at the two Defect A disclosure paragraphs and the one\n307:       Defect C flag -- matching the fix task's own handoff `deliverables` and\n308:       `completion_gate` exactly, with no stray fourth edit found anywhere in\n309:       the 2416-line file.\n310: \n311:   d1_d2_d3_discharge_status: >-\n312:     SOUND, UNCHANGED, NOT REOPENED. See DEC-20260907-2c4beb\n313:     `d1_d2_d3_discharge_status` and the gate-outcome record's own worked\n314:     check; nothing in TASK-20260907-7cce3e's fixes touches D1, D2 or D3, and\n315:     this decision does not re-derive them a third time.\n316: \n317:   blind_history_ruling: >-\n318:     UNCHANGED. No Stage A'' re-derivation has been attempted under v3 at any\n319:     point in this lineage; Defect A's leak (now properly disclosed) has\n320:     contaminated no actual blind reading. This approval is the point at which\n321:     Stage A'' dispatch becomes authorized, not a retroactive judgment about a\n322:     reading that has not happened.\n323: \n324:   other_observations_pausing_this_gate:\n325:     - >-\n326:       MANIFEST.yaml was edited TWICE since the original packet commit (once by\n327:       TASK-20260907-7cce3e for Defect B's wording, once more for the sha256\n328:       update), which could in principle have left a stale content-hash in an\n329:       earlier archive receipt for that exact path. CHECKED: the fix-receipt\n330:       (TASK-20260907-7cce3e/fix-receipt.json) records MANIFEST.yaml's\n331:       path_sha256 for its FINAL, post-both-edits state in one atomic archive\n332:       commit, so no intermediate, stale hash is left standing as an official\n333:       record. No action required.\n334:     - >-\n335:       `objective_v3_r2` (the leak itself) remains verbatim and unredacted\n336:       in-place, by design -- Defect A's fix is disclosure, not redaction, per\n337:       DEC-20260907-2c4beb's own required_fix option (1). This is not a\n338:       residual defect; it is the chosen and disclosed repair shape, and this\n339:       decision confirms it was the one actually implemented (option (2),\n340:       relocating the citation, was NOT taken, and the record is honest about\n341:       that).\n342:     - >-\n343:       This decision does not itself verify `tools/validate_ledger.py` cleanly\n344:       passes on the current tree (no Bash); the fix-receipt's\n345:       `verification_note` claims \"42 pre-existing origin/main errors...none\n346:       new\" but this gate did not re-run the tool to confirm the count. This is\n347:       disclosed as unverified rather than asserted, and is not treated as a\n348:       blocking defect given it is not one of the four named required fixes and\n349:       concerns campaign-wide ledger hygiene rather than this contract's own\n350:       soundness.\n351: \n352:   evidence_refs:\n353:     - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml (the approved contract; every cited block read in full at the cited lines by this session)\n354:     - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml (read in full for the additivity byte-comparison)\n355:     - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml (read in full; `post_gate_fixes_applied` block independently checked against the contract and packet)\n356:     - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/derivation-packet/PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3/{MANIFEST.yaml,quantity.md,deliverables.md,prohibitions.md} (all four read in full)\n357:     - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/archives/TASK-20260907-7cce3e/fix-receipt.json (the content-hashed archive receipt this gate located and cross-verified independently)\n358:     - ledger/handoffs/TASK-20260907-7cce3e.yaml (the fix task's own handoff and completion gate)\n359:     - coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-d7e987/tasks/TASK-20260907-b1b54b/{am1_self_consistency.py,am1_report.json} (script logic read directly; report's current committed state read directly)\n360:     - ledger/decisions/DEC-20260907-2c4beb.yaml (the prior `revise` gate this decision supersedes in outcome, not in place)\n361:     - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/v2_to_v3.gate-outcome.yaml (the prior gate-outcome record naming the four required fixes)\n362:     - ledger/decisions/DEC-20260906-806501.yaml (schema precedent for an `approve_experiment` decision on this experiment lineage)\n363: \n364:   limitations:\n365:     - >-\n366:       THIS DECISION ESTABLISHES NOTHING SCIENTIFIC. It approves a contract\n367:       TEXT and authorizes dispatch. It asserts no feasibility result at any a,\n368:       no crossing bracket, and no hypothesis-status movement. H-ECDLP-37dc01\n369:       remains at its current status, unchanged by this decision.\n370:     - >-\n371:       REQUIRED FIX (4) WAS NOT DISCHARGED BY A LITERAL RE-EXECUTION OF\n372:       `sha256sum` OR `am1_self_consistency.py` BY THIS SESSION, which has no\n373:       Bash/shell tool. It was corroborated by source-code reading, current-\n374:       file-state inspection, and cross-reference against a separately\n375:       committed, content-hashed fix receipt this gate located independently.\n376:       See `per_defect_independent_reverification.defect_D` for the full\n377:       disclosure of exactly what was and was not verified and why this\n378:       decision treats that as sufficient.\n379:     - >-\n380:       This decision does not itself confirm `tools/validate_ledger.py` runs\n381:       clean on the current tree; see `other_observations_pausing_this_gate`.\n382:     - >-\n383:       CLAIM TIER UNCHANGED AND UNENGAGED. Everything at issue remains\n384:       claim_tier toy, generic instrument, under the KN-LIT-013 ceiling. No\n385:       exponent is claimed or approached and the four asymptotic promotion\n386:       gates are not engaged.\n387:     - >-\n388:       MODEL BINDING NOT PROBE-VERIFIED. `python3 -m orchestration.adapter\n389:       doctor --probe` was not run by this session.\n390:     - >-\n391:       NO USER-FACING CONFIRMATION (AskUserQuestion) WAS OBTAINED FOR THIS\n392:       APPROVAL. Per `decision_verb_note`, this is the independent technical\n393:       approval gate the contract's own text names as sufficient, mirroring\n394:       DEC-20260907-2c4beb's own procedure when it returned `revise`; it is not\n395:       a first-time draft presentation of a wholly new contract.\n396: \n397:   next_actions:\n398:     - >-\n399:       RANK 1: dispatch Stage A'' (the blind re-derivation) to a designated\n400:       independent agent, in a session that authored none of\n401:       specification.v3.yaml, amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml, the v3_r2_addendum, the\n402:       derivation-packet files, TASK-20260907-7cce3e's fixes, or this decision\n403:       -- per `who_may_not_perform_this_task` in MANIFEST.yaml and this\n404:       contract's own `blind_rederivation.v3_derivation_packet`. That agent's\n405:       ENTIRE permitted reading before its own seal is the four-file\n406:       derivation packet; nothing else.\n407:     - >-\n408:       RANK 2: after Stage A'' seals, dispatch Stage B/C execution (if not\n409:       already satisfied by the already-committed RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-001..006 for\n410:       the N = 2^24 arm; the N = 2^20 arm and the full 25-seed grid are new\n411:       scope requiring fresh runs) as a bounded executor handoff citing this\n412:       decision and the now-frozen v3 contract.\n413:     - >-\n414:       RANK 3: no hypothesis-status promotion beyond H-ECDLP-37dc01's current\n415:       status on any clause proceeds until Stage A'' seals, Stage B/C\n416:       completes or is confirmed already satisfied, and a further Coordinator\n417:       evidence-review decision is made on the independently reviewed result\n418:       set.\n419:     - >-\n420:       RANK 4: a session WITH Bash access should, at its next convenient\n421:       touch of this lane, independently re-run `sha256sum` on\n422:       quantity.md/deliverables.md/prohibitions.md against MANIFEST.yaml's\n423:       declared values and confirm commit f95e8590fb6e5139ea6e56e145030bb285858903\n424:       is reachable, purely to convert this decision's corroborated-but-not-\n425:       directly-executed verification of required fix (4) into a directly\n426:       executed one. This is not a precondition of Stage A'' dispatch (RANK 1\n427:       is not blocked on it) because the convergent evidence already reviewed\n428:       leaves no live inconsistency to resolve.\n429: \n430:   knowledge_promotion:\n431:     promoted: []\n432:     not_warranted: >-\n433:       This is a protocol-approval gate decision with verb `approve_experiment`.\n434:       It cites no evidence record as new support, reviews no run set, and\n435:       asserts no research finding, so the promotion threshold (`support` or\n436:       `reject_scoped` on `replicated` or `strong` evidence) is not engaged.\n437:       Nothing durable about the ECDLP follows from approving a contract text.\n438:       A technique note on allowlist-based blind re-derivation packets (and on\n439:       this specific pattern of cross-referencing a content-hashed fix receipt\n440:       when a gate session lacks a shell) is a plausible future corpus item,\n441:       deferred until Stage A'' actually runs and demonstrates the repair works\n442:       end to end, which is the only thing that would make the note more than\n443:       an assertion.\n444:     knowledge_paths_staged: []\n445: \n446:   decided_by: coordinator\n447:   decided_at: '2026-09-07'\n448:   decided_at_note: >-\n449:     Runtime-supplied calendar date; this role holds no independent clock.\n450: \n451:   inference:\n452:     requested_policy: coordinator-orchestration-code\n453:     reasoning_effort: high\n454:     fallback_used: false\n455:     degraded_allowed: false\n456:     degraded_requirements: []\n457:     independent_session_required: true\n458:     resolved_model: >-\n459:       claude-sonnet-5, the model that actually answered this session,\n460:       recorded beside the requested policy per AGENTS.md \"Model policy\". The\n461:       requested policy was honoured; no substitution was requested or\n462:       accepted.\n463:     model_verified: >-\n464:       NOT probe-verified. `python3 -m orchestration.adapter doctor --probe`\n465:       was not run by this session. Disclosed rather than asserted.\n466:     runtime: 'Claude Code, coordinator subagent, fresh session'\n467:     session_provenance: >-\n468:       A FRESH Coordinator session that authored none of the gated artifacts:\n469:       not specification.v3.yaml, not amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml, not the\n470:       v3_r2_addendum, not the derivation-packet files, not\n471:       DEC-20260907-2c4beb, not TASK-20260907-7cce3e's fixes. It has Read,\n472:       Grep, Glob, Write, Edit, and SendMessage tools but no Bash/shell in this\n473:       session -- disclosed in full at\n474:       `per_defect_independent_reverification.defect_D` rather than concealed\n475:       or worked around by fabricating a command output. It read every cited\n476:       file in full at the cited locations, independently re-verified all four\n477:       claimed fixes against committed bytes rather than accepting\n478:       `post_gate_fixes_applied`'s self-report, and made no commit. It executed\n479:       ZERO experiment runs, wrote no run record, produced no measurement\n480:       offered as evidence, changed no hypothesis status, obtained no\n481:       attestation, and did not itself dispatch Stage A''.\n\n(End of file - total 481 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# The INDEPENDENT approval-gate decision that APPROVES PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3-r2\n# (specification.v3.yaml) after independently re-verifying TASK-20260907-7cce3e's\n# claimed discharge of all four required fixes named by DEC-20260907-2c4beb /\n# experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/v2_to_v3.gate-outcome.yaml. This\n# decision sets specification.v3.yaml's gate fields to approved/coordinator/\n# true/true. It asserts no research finding on the ECDLP and authorizes no\n# run of any kind beyond dispatch of Stage A'' and, after its seal, Stage B/C\n# execution under this now-frozen contract.\n\ncoordinator_decision:\n  id: DEC-20260907-b4f2a9\n  id_allocation_provenance: >-\n    This gate session has no Bash/shell tool (Read, Grep, Glob, Write, Edit,\n    SendMessage only) and could not itself run `python3 tools/allocate_id.py\n    --next coordinator_decision --date 20260907` or `--check` it, exactly the\n    same disclosed limitation DEC-20260907-2c4beb's own session recorded. It\n    confirmed by Glob (`**/*b4f2a9*`) that no file exists anywhere in this\n    repository at that token before authoring this record. The orchestrating\n    session must run `python3 tools/allocate_id.py --check coordinator_decision\n    DEC-20260907-b4f2a9` before this record is treated as durable.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/ledger/decisions/DEC-20260907-b4f2a9.yaml","text":"# The INDEPENDENT approval-gate decision that APPROVES PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3-r2\n# (specification.v3.yaml) after independently re-verifying TASK-20260907-7cce3e's\n# claimed discharge of all four required fixes named by DEC-20260907-2c4beb /\n# experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/v2_to_v3.gate-outcome.yaml. This\n# decision sets specification.v3.yaml's gate fields to approved/coordinator/\n# true/true. It asserts no research finding on the ECDLP and authorizes no\n# run of any kind beyond dispatch of Stage A'' and, after its seal, Stage B/C\n# execution under this now-frozen contract.\n\ncoordinator_decision:\n  id: DEC-20260907-b4f2a9\n  id_allocation_provenance: >-\n    This gate session has no Bash/shell tool (Read, Grep, Glob, Write, Edit,\n    SendMessage only) and could not itself run `python3 tools/allocate_id.py\n    --next coordinator_decision --date 20260907` or `--check` it, exactly the\n    same disclosed limitation DEC-20260907-2c4beb's own session recorded. It\n    confirmed by Glob (`**/*b4f2a9*`) that no file exists anywhere in this\n    repository at that token before authoring this record. The orchestrating\n    session must run `python3 tools/allocate_id.py --check coordinator_decision\n    DEC-20260907-b4f2a9` before this record is treated as durable.\n  recorded_at: '2026-09-07'\n  goal_id: GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f\n  goal_id_note: >-\n    EXP-ECDLP-6ac801 and H-ECDLP-37dc01 both carry `goal_id: null` and this\n    decision does not change that. GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f is named because the\n    gated revision and its fixes were authored in that goal's lane\n    (BATCH-d7e987 / BATCH-48ef8b); no GOAL binding is created on any record.\n  question_id: RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5\n  experiment_id: EXP-ECDLP-6ac801\n  hypothesis_id: H-ECDLP-37dc01\n  batch_id: BATCH-d7e987\n  task_id: TASK-20260907-e17c05\n\n  gated_object:\n    what_was_gated: >-\n      PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3-r2, as amended by TASK-20260907-7cce3e's\n      post-gate fixes on top of DEC-20260907-2c4beb's `revise` verdict, as it\n      stood in experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml immediately\n      before this decision: `status: proposed`, `approved_by: null`, `frozen:\n      false`, `execution_authorized: false`.\n    paths:\n      contract: experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml\n      amendment: experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml\n      derivation_packet_dir: experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/derivation-packet/PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3/\n      prior_gate_outcome_record: experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/v2_to_v3.gate-outcome.yaml\n      prior_gate_decision: ledger/decisions/DEC-20260907-2c4beb.yaml\n      fix_task_handoff: ledger/handoffs/TASK-20260907-7cce3e.yaml\n      fix_receipt: experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/archives/TASK-20260907-7cce3e/fix-receipt.json\n\n  context: >-\n    DEC-20260907-2c4beb (`revise`) found PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3-r2\n    scientifically sound (D1/D2/D3 discharge SOUND, not reopened) but blocked\n    approval on four disclosure/consistency defects A-D. TASK-20260907-7cce3e\n    then authored fixes for defects A, B and C as ordinary draft-revision\n    edits to the still-unapproved v3 contract and packet, with defect D\n    (independent sha256 recomputation and am1_self_consistency.py re-run)\n    explicitly out of its scope and performed separately by \"the\n    orchestrating session (Bash)\" per `amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml\n    post_gate_fixes_applied.fix_4_defect_d`. This decision is a FRESH,\n    independent gate session -- not TASK-20260907-7cce3e, not\n    TASK-20260907-b1b54b, not TASK-20260907-9c0626, not TASK-20260907-058c69\n    -- that independently re-verified each of the four claimed fixes directly\n    against committed repository bytes rather than accepting\n    `post_gate_fixes_applied`'s self-report at face value, per this gate\n    task's own governing instruction.\n\n  leak_discipline_on_this_record: >-\n    BINDING, adopted verbatim from DEC-20260907-2c4beb and\n    specification.v3.yaml's own `leak_discipline_on_this_record`. This record\n    is not on the derivation packet's `readable_files` allowlist and must not\n    become a leak channel into a future Stage A'' re-derivation. It states no\n    per-cell G3 verdict, pass-count, margin value, margin sign, or crossing\n    bracket at a = 1/16, a = 1/8 or a = 3/16 at either N beyond citing the\n    ALREADY-DISCLOSED a = 1/8 leak text this decision confirms is now properly\n    disclosed (not newly revealed by this decision) and the already-disclosed\n    a = 1/4 control anchor.\n\n  decision: approve_experiment\n\n  decision_verb_note: >-\n    `approve_experiment`, mirroring DEC-20260906-806501's verb for the prior\n    approval on this experiment lineage (EXP-ECDLP-612fb1 v1-to-v2). Unlike\n    that decision, no fresh `user_confirmation_record` / AskUserQuestion step\n    is recorded here: this is the INDEPENDENT TECHNICAL APPROVAL GATE\n    specification.v3.yaml's own `gate_fields_note` names as the sole path to\n    execution authorization (a coordinator session that authored none of the\n    gated artifacts), the same class of decision DEC-20260907-2c4beb already\n    established as the applicable procedure for this exact gate when it\n    returned `revise` -- not a new first-time draft presentation requiring a\n    separate user-facing confirmation gate.\n\n  target_ids:\n    - PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3-r2\n    - EXP-ECDLP-6ac801\n    - TASK-20260907-e17c05\n    - TASK-20260907-7cce3e\n    - DEC-20260907-2c4beb\n  target_ids_note: >-\n    Added by the orchestrating session after independently re-verifying this\n    record and finding the schema's required `target_ids` field absent from\n    the gate subagent's own draft (tools/validate_ledger.py flagged it: 43\n    errors after this record's creation vs. the 42 pre-existing errors\n    fix-receipt.json's own verification_note disclosed). No other field in\n    this record is edited by this addition.\n\n  per_defect_independent_reverification:\n    defect_A:\n      claim: >-\n        TASK-20260907-7cce3e disclosed the a = 1/8 leak in\n        `leak_discipline_on_this_record` (specification.v3.yaml, appended\n        paragraph at approximately line 2174) and in the `protocol_amendment`\n        \"a = 1/16 INDEPENDENCE RULING\" standing-contamination sub-block\n        (appended paragraph at approximately line 753), without deleting or\n        rewording either existing disclosure entry.\n      independently_reverified: >-\n        CONFIRMED by direct read of both exact locations in the current\n        committed specification.v3.yaml. Both appended paragraphs are present,\n        each explicitly named \"DEFECT A DISCLOSURE\" and each citing\n        TASK-20260907-7cce3e and DEC-20260907-2c4beb by id, each naming the\n        exact leak text (\"It is confirmed ceiling-feasible at N = 2^24 at\n        strength `preliminary` (EV-ECDLP-6783b8 / DEC-20260907-8d8782)...\")\n        and its exact location (`v3_r2_addendum.objective_v3_r2`,\n        approximately lines 2220-2222), and each stating the leak is\n        CONTAINED TODAY ONLY because `prohibitions.md` blanket-forbids\n        reading `specification.v3.yaml`. Grepped `EV-ECDLP-6783b8` across the\n        whole file: exactly 3 hits -- the original leak in `objective_v3_r2`\n        (unmoved, verbatim, as the fix explicitly does not redact it) and the\n        two new disclosure paragraphs. No fourth, undisclosed occurrence\n        exists. The text immediately preceding each appended paragraph (the\n        pre-existing \"a = 1/16 INDEPENDENCE RULING\" content and the\n        pre-existing `leak_discipline_on_this_record` prose) is unchanged,\n        confirmed by direct read against the text quoted in\n        DEC-20260907-2c4beb `deciding_sentence` and the gate-outcome record's\n        own quoted blocks.\n      verdict: DISCHARGED, correctly and completely. No new problem introduced.\n    defect_B:\n      claim: >-\n        TASK-20260907-7cce3e rewrote quantity.md section 13 and MANIFEST.yaml\n        `the_one_disclosed_inclusion.what` to drop \"established\"/\"ESTABLISHED\"\n        and \"independent work\", replacing them with the r2-corrected\n        characterisation from `v3_r2_addendum.cf2_anchor_strength`.\n      independently_reverified: >-\n        Grepped `established|independent work` (case-insensitive) across the\n        WHOLE derivation-packet directory: exactly ONE hit, in\n        MANIFEST.yaml's `sha256_recomputed_note` (line 59), which is a\n        historical note DESCRIBING the correction itself (\"the stale\n        'established'/'independent work' a=1/4 characterization was\n        corrected\") -- not a live characterisation of EV-ECDLP-60e266. It is\n        quoted as the OLD, superseded phrase inside a note about what changed,\n        the same disclosure pattern this program's own defect-disclosure\n        paragraphs use elsewhere (e.g. Defect A's own disclosure quotes the\n        leaked text to name it). Zero occurrences remain as a live assertion\n        anywhere in quantity.md, deliverables.md or prohibitions.md.\n        Read quantity.md section 13 in full: it now reads \"`T_sel = T/2` at\n        `a = 1/4`... records G3-INFEASIBILITY at strength `preliminary`, on\n        one execution batch, with no independent implementation (evidence\n        record `EV-ECDLP-60e266`)\" -- checked WORD FOR WORD against\n        specification.v3.yaml `v3_r2_addendum.cf2_anchor_strength`'s own\n        corrected characterisation (\"EV-ECDLP-60e266 records a = 1/4\n        G3-infeasibility at strength `preliminary`, on one execution batch,\n        with no independent implementation\") and found to be an accurate\n        paraphrase carrying the identical claim, not merely different words.\n        MANIFEST.yaml's own `the_one_disclosed_inclusion.what` field checked\n        the same way: matches.\n      verdict: DISCHARGED, correctly and completely. The one remaining string\n        match is a disclosed historical note, not a live mischaracterization,\n        and is itself in keeping with this program's own disclosure norms.\n    defect_C:\n      claim: >-\n        TASK-20260907-7cce3e added an inline superseded-flag to the base\n        `required_artifacts` clause at specification.v3.yaml (approximately\n        line 1754/1770), pointing to\n        `v3_r2_addendum.cf1_required_artifacts_override` and\n        `required_artifacts_r2`, without deleting the base clause.\n      independently_reverified: >-\n        Read the exact `required_artifacts` list entry in full (line 1770).\n        The ORIGINAL fifteen-letter clause text (\"the control report: for\n        every declared control (a)-(o), per cell, FIRED or NOT FIRED, with the\n        quantity and cell it was read from; an absent entry counts as NOT\n        RUN\") is present verbatim and UNEDITED, with a bracketed flag appended\n        after it: \"[SUPERSEDED -- per DEC-20260907-2c4beb / gate-outcome\n        `blocking_defects[C]`: this clause is SUPERSEDED by\n        `v3_r2_addendum.cf1_required_artifacts_override` and\n        `required_artifacts_r2` below, which replace it with a three-part\n        scheme; it is retained here only for history and MUST NOT be acted on\n        directly by an executor or dispatcher (appended by\n        TASK-20260907-7cce3e; nothing else in this entry is edited)]\". Exactly\n        the minimal-fix option DEC-20260907-2c4beb's `required_fix` named.\n      verdict: DISCHARGED, correctly and completely. No new problem introduced.\n    defect_D:\n      claim: >-\n        `amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml post_gate_fixes_applied.fix_4_defect_d`\n        states the orchestrating session (with Bash) independently recomputed\n        sha256/byte-count for all three packet readable_files (quantity.md\n        updated to 7040669a...b68, 12253 bytes; deliverables.md and\n        prohibitions.md confirmed unchanged and matching), re-ran\n        am1_self_consistency.py against the post-fix tree (all_pass: true,\n        genuine fresh hashlib computation, not a replay of the stale committed\n        am1_report.json), and discovered and reverted a side effect on\n        TASK-20260907-b1b54b's own immutable am1_report.json before its own\n        commit.\n      this_gate_sessions_tool_limit_disclosed: >-\n        THIS SESSION HAS NO BASH/SHELL TOOL (Read, Grep, Glob, Write, Edit,\n        SendMessage only) and could not itself run `sha256sum`, execute\n        `am1_self_consistency.py`, or run `git status`/`git diff`/`git\n        checkout --`. It therefore could NOT literally reproduce required fix\n        (4)'s verification by direct command execution, and does not claim to\n        have done so. What follows is the strongest verification available\n        within this session's actual tool surface, performed BEFORE trusting\n        `post_gate_fixes_applied`'s prose account, not as a substitute\n        offered in place of a real shell-based check.\n      independently_reverified_by_alternate_means:\n        - >-\n          READ THE SCRIPT'S OWN SOURCE CODE\n          (coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-d7e987/tasks/TASK-20260907-b1b54b/am1_self_consistency.py)\n          rather than trusting a description of its behaviour: line 20,\n          `OUT = Path(__file__).with_name(\"am1_report.json\")`, and line 166,\n          `OUT.write_text(json.dumps(report, indent=2) + \"\\n\")` inside\n          `main()`. CONFIRMS the side-effect risk the prior gate found is\n          real and structural -- any bare re-run of this script DOES overwrite\n          `am1_report.json` in place, unconditionally.\n        - >-\n          READ THE CURRENT COMMITTED am1_report.json\n          (coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-d7e987/tasks/TASK-20260907-b1b54b/am1_report.json)\n          directly: it still shows `spec_sha256:\n          08cad9ac6621dc1aed776efe968b2663cfdaf01a3a34551a57b5be392c957eee`,\n          the value from BEFORE TASK-20260907-7cce3e edited\n          specification.v3.yaml. Since a bare re-run against the POST-fix tree\n          would necessarily write a DIFFERENT spec_sha256 (the file's bytes\n          changed), the fact that the currently committed file still shows\n          the OLD value is consistent with the claimed revert having actually\n          happened (or with the script simply never having run against this\n          exact path) -- and is NOT consistent with an unreverted, silently\n          corrupted deliverable, which is the one outcome that would have been\n          a genuine new problem.\n        - >-\n          FOUND AND READ A SEPARATELY COMMITTED, CONTENT-HASHED FIX RECEIPT\n          (experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/archives/TASK-20260907-7cce3e/fix-receipt.json,\n          `commit_sha: f95e8590fb6e5139ea6e56e145030bb285858903`) that this\n          gate went looking for rather than being pointed to, via Glob on\n          `**/*7cce3e*`. Its own `verification_note` states explicitly, in\n          its own words, that TASK-20260907-b1b54b's am1_report.json \"was\n          found modified as an unintended side effect of re-running\n          am1_self_consistency.py and was reverted via `git checkout --`\n          before this commit -- confirmed excluded from this commit's own\n          declared paths\". Its `staged_top_level_paths` list is checked\n          directly and does NOT include am1_report.json, consistent with\n          that claim. Its `path_sha256` map records well-formed 64-hex-char\n          sha256 values (individually counted by this gate, not merely\n          eyeballed) for specification.v3.yaml, amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml,\n          quantity.md, MANIFEST.yaml and the fix task's own handoff -- the\n          quantity.md value (7040669a...b68) matches exactly what is\n          currently declared inside MANIFEST.yaml itself, confirming no\n          further, later, undisclosed edit has occurred to that file since\n          this receipt's commit.\n        - >-\n          This is a DIFFERENT and WEAKER form of verification than literally\n          executing `sha256sum` and the script, and this decision does not\n          overstate it: it is cross-referencing three independently readable,\n          mutually corroborating, committed artifacts (the script's own logic,\n          the current file state, and a separately content-hashed receipt)\n          rather than accepting one paragraph of prose in\n          `post_gate_fixes_applied` on its own say-so. No contradiction was\n          found among the three. A session WITH Bash independently re-running\n          `sha256sum` against the three packet files and `git log\n          f95e8590fb6e5139ea6e56e145030bb285858903` to confirm the commit is\n          reachable remains the strictly stronger check and is not performed\n          here; it is not, in this decision's judgment, required to be\n          performed by THIS session specifically before approval, given the\n          convergent evidence above and the low residual risk (a false claim\n          in fix-receipt.json would itself be a fabrication under AGENTS.md\n          rule 5, a different and more severe problem than an unverified\n          hash, and nothing in the fix-receipt's content is inconsistent with\n          anything else this gate independently read).\n      verdict: >-\n        DISCHARGED on convergent, independently-sought corroborating evidence,\n        WITH THE ABOVE LIMITATION EXPLICITLY DISCLOSED rather than silently\n        elided. This is the one defect this decision does not claim to have\n        closed by literal command re-execution.\n\n  additivity_check:\n    verdict: no additivity violation found, independently re-verified\n    method: >-\n      Read `definitions` (specification.v3.yaml lines 313-413, up to and\n      including the `STATIC(T)_r pool-selection weight formula` key) side by\n      side against specification.v2.yaml `definitions` (lines 272-374) in\n      full: identical text, confirmed by direct visual comparison of this\n      gate's own two Read calls, not merely cited from a prior claim. Did the\n      same for `blind_rederivation` (v3 lines 869-974 up to and including\n      `v2_rerequirement_a_1_8`, against v2 lines 424-529), `controls` items\n      (a)-(f) (v3 lines 1146-1182, against v2 lines 531-568), and\n      `success_criterion` (v3 lines 1628-1652, against v2 lines 703-727).\n    result: >-\n      PASS on every field checked. New content in each block is appended\n      after the shared text, never interleaved, exactly as\n      DEC-20260907-2c4beb's own `additivity_check` and the gate-outcome\n      record's `additivity_check` state.\n    gate_fields_confirmed_unchanged_before_this_decision: >-\n      Grepped `^  status:|^  approved_by:|^  frozen:|^  execution_authorized:`\n      against specification.v3.yaml immediately before authoring this\n      decision's edits: `status: proposed`, `approved_by: null`, `frozen:\n      false`, `execution_authorized: false` -- exactly as DEC-20260907-2c4beb\n      left them. TASK-20260907-7cce3e's fixes did not sneak in an approval.\n    fix_task_confined_to_declared_edits: >-\n      Grepped `TASK-20260907-7cce3e` across the whole of specification.v3.yaml:\n      exactly 3 hits, at the two Defect A disclosure paragraphs and the one\n      Defect C flag -- matching the fix task's own handoff `deliverables` and\n      `completion_gate` exactly, with no stray fourth edit found anywhere in\n      the 2416-line file.\n\n  d1_d2_d3_discharge_status: >-\n    SOUND, UNCHANGED, NOT REOPENED. See DEC-20260907-2c4beb\n    `d1_d2_d3_discharge_status` and the gate-outcome record's own worked\n    check; nothing in TASK-20260907-7cce3e's fixes touches D1, D2 or D3, and\n    this decision does not re-derive them a third time.\n\n  blind_history_ruling: >-\n    UNCHANGED. No Stage A'' re-derivation has been attempted under v3 at any\n    point in this lineage; Defect A's leak (now properly disclosed) has\n    contaminated no actual blind reading. This approval is the point at which\n    Stage A'' dispatch becomes authorized, not a retroactive judgment about a\n    reading that has not happened.\n\n  other_observations_pausing_this_gate:\n    - >-\n      MANIFEST.yaml was edited TWICE since the original packet commit (once by\n      TASK-20260907-7cce3e for Defect B's wording, once more for the sha256\n      update), which could in principle have left a stale content-hash in an\n      earlier archive receipt for that exact path. CHECKED: the fix-receipt\n      (TASK-20260907-7cce3e/fix-receipt.json) records MANIFEST.yaml's\n      path_sha256 for its FINAL, post-both-edits state in one atomic archive\n      commit, so no intermediate, stale hash is left standing as an official\n      record. No action required.\n    - >-\n      `objective_v3_r2` (the leak itself) remains verbatim and unredacted\n      in-place, by design -- Defect A's fix is disclosure, not redaction, per\n      DEC-20260907-2c4beb's own required_fix option (1). This is not a\n      residual defect; it is the chosen and disclosed repair shape, and this\n      decision confirms it was the one actually implemented (option (2),\n      relocating the citation, was NOT taken, and the record is honest about\n      that).\n    - >-\n      This decision does not itself verify `tools/validate_ledger.py` cleanly\n      passes on the current tree (no Bash); the fix-receipt's\n      `verification_note` claims \"42 pre-existing origin/main errors...none\n      new\" but this gate did not re-run the tool to confirm the count. This is\n      disclosed as unverified rather than asserted, and is not treated as a\n      blocking defect given it is not one of the four named required fixes and\n      concerns campaign-wide ledger hygiene rather than this contract's own\n      soundness.\n\n  evidence_refs:\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml (the approved contract; every cited block read in full at the cited lines by this session)\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml (read in full for the additivity byte-comparison)\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml (read in full; `post_gate_fixes_applied` block independently checked against the contract and packet)\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/derivation-packet/PA-ECDLP-6ac801-v2-to-v3/{MANIFEST.yaml,quantity.md,deliverables.md,prohibitions.md} (all four read in full)\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/archives/TASK-20260907-7cce3e/fix-receipt.json (the content-hashed archive receipt this gate located and cross-verified independently)\n    - ledger/handoffs/TASK-20260907-7cce3e.yaml (the fix task's own handoff and completion gate)\n    - coordination/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/batches/BATCH-d7e987/tasks/TASK-20260907-b1b54b/{am1_self_consistency.py,am1_report.json} (script logic read directly; report's current committed state read directly)\n    - ledger/decisions/DEC-20260907-2c4beb.yaml (the prior `revise` gate this decision supersedes in outcome, not in place)\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/v2_to_v3.gate-outcome.yaml (the prior gate-outcome record naming the four required fixes)\n    - ledger/decisions/DEC-20260906-806501.yaml (schema precedent for an `approve_experiment` decision on this experiment lineage)\n\n  limitations:\n    - >-\n      THIS DECISION ESTABLISHES NOTHING SCIENTIFIC. It approves a contract\n      TEXT and authorizes dispatch. It asserts no feasibility result at any a,\n      no crossing bracket, and no hypothesis-status movement. H-ECDLP-37dc01\n      remains at its current status, unchanged by this decision.\n    - >-\n      REQUIRED FIX (4) WAS NOT DISCHARGED BY A LITERAL RE-EXECUTION OF\n      `sha256sum` OR `am1_self_consistency.py` BY THIS SESSION, which has no\n      Bash/shell tool. It was corroborated by source-code reading, current-\n      file-state inspection, and cross-reference against a separately\n      committed, content-hashed fix receipt this gate located independently.\n      See `per_defect_independent_reverification.defect_D` for the full\n      disclosure of exactly what was and was not verified and why this\n      decision treats that as sufficient.\n    - >-\n      This decision does not itself confirm `tools/validate_ledger.py` runs\n      clean on the current tree; see `other_observations_pausing_this_gate`.\n    - >-\n      CLAIM TIER UNCHANGED AND UNENGAGED. Everything at issue remains\n      claim_tier toy, generic instrument, under the KN-LIT-013 ceiling. No\n      exponent is claimed or approached and the four asymptotic promotion\n      gates are not engaged.\n    - >-\n      MODEL BINDING NOT PROBE-VERIFIED. `python3 -m orchestration.adapter\n      doctor --probe` was not run by this session.\n    - >-\n      NO USER-FACING CONFIRMATION (AskUserQuestion) WAS OBTAINED FOR THIS\n      APPROVAL. Per `decision_verb_note`, this is the independent technical\n      approval gate the contract's own text names as sufficient, mirroring\n      DEC-20260907-2c4beb's own procedure when it returned `revise`; it is not\n      a first-time draft presentation of a wholly new contract.\n\n  next_actions:\n    - >-\n      RANK 1: dispatch Stage A'' (the blind re-derivation) to a designated\n      independent agent, in a session that authored none of\n      specification.v3.yaml, amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml, the v3_r2_addendum, the\n      derivation-packet files, TASK-20260907-7cce3e's fixes, or this decision\n      -- per `who_may_not_perform_this_task` in MANIFEST.yaml and this\n      contract's own `blind_rederivation.v3_derivation_packet`. That agent's\n      ENTIRE permitted reading before its own seal is the four-file\n      derivation packet; nothing else.\n    - >-\n      RANK 2: after Stage A'' seals, dispatch Stage B/C execution (if not\n      already satisfied by the already-committed RUN-ECDLP-6ac801-001..006 for\n      the N = 2^24 arm; the N = 2^20 arm and the full 25-seed grid are new\n      scope requiring fresh runs) as a bounded executor handoff citing this\n      decision and the now-frozen v3 contract.\n    - >-\n      RANK 3: no hypothesis-status promotion beyond H-ECDLP-37dc01's current\n      status on any clause proceeds until Stage A'' seals, Stage B/C\n      completes or is confirmed already satisfied, and a further Coordinator\n      evidence-review decision is made on the independently reviewed result\n      set.\n    - >-\n      RANK 4: a session WITH Bash access should, at its next convenient\n      touch of this lane, independently re-run `sha256sum` on\n      quantity.md/deliverables.md/prohibitions.md against MANIFEST.yaml's\n      declared values and confirm commit f95e8590fb6e5139ea6e56e145030bb285858903\n      is reachable, purely to convert this decision's corroborated-but-not-\n      directly-executed verification of required fix (4) into a directly\n      executed one. This is not a precondition of Stage A'' dispatch (RANK 1\n      is not blocked on it) because the convergent evidence already reviewed\n      leaves no live inconsistency to resolve.\n\n  knowledge_promotion:\n    promoted: []\n    not_warranted: >-\n      This is a protocol-approval gate decision with verb `approve_experiment`.\n      It cites no evidence record as new support, reviews no run set, and\n      asserts no research finding, so the promotion threshold (`support` or\n      `reject_scoped` on `replicated` or `strong` evidence) is not engaged.\n      Nothing durable about the ECDLP follows from approving a contract text.\n      A technique note on allowlist-based blind re-derivation packets (and on\n      this specific pattern of cross-referencing a content-hashed fix receipt\n      when a gate session lacks a shell) is a plausible future corpus item,\n      deferred until Stage A'' actually runs and demonstrates the repair works\n      end to end, which is the only thing that would make the note more than\n      an assertion.\n    knowledge_paths_staged: []\n\n  decided_by: coordinator\n  decided_at: '2026-09-07'\n  decided_at_note: >-\n    Runtime-supplied calendar date; this role holds no independent clock.\n\n  inference:\n    requested_policy: coordinator-orchestration-code\n    reasoning_effort: high\n    fallback_used: false\n    degraded_allowed: false\n    degraded_requirements: []\n    independent_session_required: true\n    resolved_model: >-\n      claude-sonnet-5, the model that actually answered this session,\n      recorded beside the requested policy per AGENTS.md \"Model policy\". The\n      requested policy was honoured; no substitution was requested or\n      accepted.\n    model_verified: >-\n      NOT probe-verified. `python3 -m orchestration.adapter doctor --probe`\n      was not run by this session. Disclosed rather than asserted.\n    runtime: 'Claude Code, coordinator subagent, fresh session'\n    session_provenance: >-\n      A FRESH Coordinator session that authored none of the gated artifacts:\n      not specification.v3.yaml, not amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml, not the\n      v3_r2_addendum, not the derivation-packet files, not\n      DEC-20260907-2c4beb, not TASK-20260907-7cce3e's fixes. It has Read,\n      Grep, Glob, Write, Edit, and SendMessage tools but no Bash/shell in this\n      session -- disclosed in full at\n      `per_defect_independent_reverification.defect_D` rather than concealed\n      or worked around by fabricating a command output. It read every cited\n      file in full at the cited locations, independently re-verified all four\n      claimed fixes against committed bytes rather than accepting\n      `post_gate_fixes_applied`'s self-report, and made no commit. It executed\n      ZERO experiment runs, wrote no run record, produced no measurement\n      offered as evidence, changed no hypothesis status, obtained no\n      attestation, and did not itself dispatch Stage A''.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":481,"totalLines":481,"truncated":false}},"title":"ledger/decisions/DEC-20260907-b4f2a9.yaml","time":{"start":1789087673424,"end":1789087673434}},"id":"prt_08def6833001tSZZ4llGiuSIMA","sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","messageID":"msg_08dedd2eb001J7jiwWnXEAbQ5q"}}
