d\n1115:    a, or about the online re-selection mechanism originates here.\n","metadata":{"output":"267:        online RESEL-L arm (the goal's largest genuine gap, zero arms ever run)\n397:        ceiling-feasibility confirmation, and records its own RANK 1 -- the v2\n588:      EV-ECDLP-6783b8 and EV-ECDLP-6a4ebc both record ceiling-feasibility at\n604:      its campaign budget carries no batch or wall-clock ceiling\n669:      ONLINE RESEL-L ARM is the goal's largest genuine gap and moves UP to\n671:      ceiling, and the ceiling's definitional gap is LIVE in the approved v2\n673:      it), so an online arm run today would be read against a definition a\n807:      basin-law measurements (survival slope, cutoff), its oracle-ceiling\n826:      `preliminary` strength, only at N = 2^24, and ZERO ONLINE RESEL-L ARMS\n828:      the online lower-bracket mechanism reaches the measured ceiling at any\n903:      RANK 2 -- THE ONLINE RESEL-L ARM. PROMOTED from RANK 3 on new facts.\n904:      Design and approve an online-mechanism batch at the confirmed-feasible a\n905:      values, mirroring EXP-ECDLP-612fb1's online-arm design, with a\n908:      online arm AT -- now exists at TWO a values rather than one\n911:      RANK 2 says exactly this. WHY IT IS STILL SECOND: every ceiling result\n912:      this goal holds is SILENT on whether the online lower-bracket mechanism\n913:      reaches that ceiling at any achievable batch size U, and ZERO online arms\n916:      ceiling-feasibility may be considered. But its comparison target is the\n917:      ceiling, and the ceiling's definitional gap is LIVE in the approved v2\n933:      only then V2-V5 / M1-M5, and compose the basin-law, oracle-ceiling and\n1115:    a, or about the online re-selection mechanism originates here.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -n \"online\\|ONLINE\\|RESEL-L\\|ceiling\" ledger/decisions/DEC-20260907-de6b71.yaml | head -60","time":{"start":1789087793308,"end":1789087793310}},"id":"prt_08df13837001