{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789087908686,"sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-92a23de1ea52d23a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/ledger/decisions/DEC-20260907-de6b71.yaml","offset":560,"limit":140},"output":"<path>/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/ledger/decisions/DEC-20260907-de6b71.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n560:           `value: null`, `measured_by: []`, `scope: null`, and its own\n561:           `obstruction_note` reads \"NOT APPLICABLE ... No obstruction quantity\n562:           is claimed here\", because its `direction` is `neutral` and it closes\n563:           no lane. So the honest answer is not \"no theory takes it up\" but \"no\n564:           obstruction was ever asserted\": there is no quantity, value, scope or\n565:           run set for any theory to re-read as an asset.\n566:         spawned_ids: []\n567:         acted_on: >-\n568:           NOTHING. EV-AES-abf3dc is a GOAL-AES-002 record, immutable, non-ECC by\n569:           declaration, and outside this lane's write scope and authority. Its\n570:           `resource_check` is not edited. Recorded so the next rerank does not\n571:           re-ask it blind -- which is the second time this reading has had to be\n572:           recorded, and is itself the small transferable finding: THE REGISTRY\n573:           CANNOT DISTINGUISH AN UNEXAMINED OBSTRUCTION FROM AN INAPPLICABLE\n574:           ONE, so a `neutral` evidence record with a wholly null obstruction\n575:           block will sit in `--unexamined` forever and will be re-read by every\n576:           rerank on every goal. The fix belongs to whoever owns\n577:           tools/obstruction_registry.py: treat a block whose every substantive\n578:           field is null and whose note declares inapplicability as OUT OF THE\n579:           STANDING SET rather than as unexamined.\n580:     consequence_for_this_rerank: >-\n581:       NONE OF THE STANDING OBSTRUCTIONS BEARS ON THIS GOAL'S RANKING. This\n582:       goal's own live obstruction -- EV-ECDLP-60e266's T_sel = T/2 disjointness\n583:       at a = 1/4, which completion criterion C3 rests on -- is already\n584:       resource-checked and is not in the unexamined set. Its resource reading is\n585:       what the small-a lane has been pursuing all along: the quantity that\n586:       bounds the gain at a = 1/4 is the hypothesis that a smaller a escapes the\n587:       bound. That reversal is now PARTLY ANSWERED rather than merely posed --\n588:       EV-ECDLP-6783b8 and EV-ECDLP-6a4ebc both record ceiling-feasibility at\n589:       a = 1/8 at `preliminary` strength, and EV-ECDLP-2e9680 records a = 1/16 --\n590:       which is a genuine advance on the obstruction's own resource_check and is\n591:       recorded here because the obstruction registry has no way to see it.\n592: \n593:   # ===================================================================\n594:   # 7. ECC PRIORITY\n595:   # ===================================================================\n596:   ecc_priority_check:\n597:     command: python3 tools/ecc_priority.py --classify GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f\n598:     output: 'GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f        area=ECDLP      ECC'\n599:     holds: true\n600:     consequence: >-\n601:       ECC by declaration in orchestration/research-priority.yaml, read through\n602:       tools/ecc_priority.py and never inferred from the identifier prefix. This\n603:       goal is considered before every non-ECC goal at every selection point and\n604:       its campaign budget carries no batch or wall-clock ceiling\n605:       (maximum_batches null, total_wall_clock_seconds null, enforced by\n606:       check_ecc_budget_is_unlimited). UNLIMITED REMOVES THE CEILING, NOT THE\n607:       DUTY TO RANK, which is why the ranking below gives reasons rather than a\n608:       list and why this close cancels a task it cannot rank ahead of doing\n609:       nothing rather than offering it.\n610:     open_ecc_ideas_note: >-\n611:       `python3 tools/ecc_priority.py --open-ideas` reports 417 open ECC ideas,\n612:       84 of them in area ECDLP. They are ranked work under instruction 3, not\n613:       backlog. This goal's own four named ideas (IDEA-20260906-a3d6ae,\n614:       -05ffb8, -cf3b76, -ac100b) are carried at RANK 5 below; the wider open-idea\n615:       set is not this lane's to rank and is not ranked here.\n616: \n617:   # ===================================================================\n618:   # 8. RATIONALE FOR THE RANKING\n619:   # ===================================================================\n620:   rationale:\n621:     - >-\n622:       THE LANE'S OUTCOME IS A REFUSAL, AND A REFUSAL ENDS THIS TASK, NOT THE\n623:       CAMPAIGN. BATCH-48ef8b authored a contract and had it gated by an\n624:       independent session that returned `revise`. That is the lane's\n625:       disposition. It executed nothing, so no evidence record exists, no\n626:       hypothesis status moves, and nothing in this close asserts anything about\n627:       the ECDLP. What the lane produced that is worth carrying: a discharged\n628:       predecessor defect list, a contract whose mathematics and mechanism are\n629:       now independently verified, a leak discipline that held under audit\n630:       including in four immutable commit messages, an enumerated ten-item\n631:       remedy list, an overturned prior, finding CF-3 against an approved\n632:       contract, and finding TG-1 about how these contracts are being written.\n633:     - >-\n634:       RANK 1 IS THE v3 REPAIR, AND THE REASON IS NOT THAT IT IS THIS LANE'S\n635:       SUCCESSOR. Three things put it first. FIRST, its work is fully specified\n636:       and bounded: the gate wrote ten per-item remedies and an explicit list of\n637:       what must NOT be reopened, so the successor authorship is a closed task\n638:       rather than another open-ended pass, and the gate's own ruling is that\n639:       the repair cost is at its minimum NOW and rises monotonically -- an\n640:       amendment to an approved contract after approval, and after execution an\n641:       amendment to a contract that runs already depend on, with\n642:       `invalidation_rules` item 7 forbidding re-scoring what has executed.\n643:       SECOND, its purpose is now BETTER motivated than when the lane opened,\n644:       not worse: a = 1/8 is confirmed feasible at N = 2^24 by two records from\n645:       two lanes, and what those records jointly show is a borderline cell\n646:       measured twice at five draws with exactly one opposite-sign draw each\n647:       time and a review joint recorded BREAKS on that disagreement -- which is\n648:       the canonical case for v3's 25-seed arm, its interval routing and the SU\n649:       label it introduced for a straddling interval. THIRD, it is the\n650:       cheapest of the five candidates by a wide margin and it unblocks the\n651:       other four rather than competing with them.\n652:     - >-\n653:       WHAT RANK 1 WAS RANKED AGAINST, AND WHY EACH LOST. (i) THE v2\n654:       SELF-CONTRADICTION CF-3 is arguably more URGENT -- v2 is\n655:       execution_authorized today and its owning lane has closed, so the remedy\n656:       is unowned -- but it is a documentation correction that reduces ZERO\n657:       research uncertainty, the one run set already executed under v2 shows no\n658:       sign of having been affected by it, and the lane that must open anyway\n659:       can carry it for approximately nothing. Urgency is not the ranking\n660:       criterion; uncertainty reduced is. It is therefore a REQUIRED CARRIED\n661:       ITEM of RANK 1, not a rank. (ii) COMPLETION CRITERION C2 is the goal's\n662:       ONLY OPEN criterion, which is the strongest argument any candidate here\n663:       has, and it still loses: its blocker is instrumental rather than\n664:       scientific (the O(theta) correction gating `fixture_gate_v2`), its next\n665:       step is ALSO an amendment authorship so it gains nothing in immediacy,\n666:       and closing the criterion tally while the central clause sits at\n667:       `preliminary` on five-draw samples would optimise the wrong quantity. C1\n668:       and C3 being MET makes that more tempting, not more justified. (iii) THE\n669:       ONLINE RESEL-L ARM is the goal's largest genuine gap and moves UP to\n670:       RANK 2 on the new facts, but not to RANK 1: its comparison target is the\n671:       ceiling, and the ceiling's definitional gap is LIVE in the approved v2\n672:       (CR-1a: cap, CAP_MULT, cycle_mass and capped_mass appear zero times in\n673:       it), so an online arm run today would be read against a definition a\n674:       from-scratch re-deriver cannot recover. Fix the definition, then measure\n675:       against it. That ordering is a reason, not a deferral. (iv)\n676:       IDEA-20260906-a3d6ae AND THE CHEAP CLOSURES are last for the reason they\n677:       have always been last: none bears on the borderline cell or on C2, and\n678:       none is blocked, so nothing is lost by their position.\n679:     - >-\n680:       THE RANKING IS WRITTEN AGAINST A MOVED FACT BASE, AND SAYS SO. Two\n681:       premises this lane opened under are false as of the origin/main merge at\n682:       4e737c70e: a = 1/8 is no longer open, and the lane the gate named as\n683:       CF-3's owner has closed. Both are recorded in\n684:       `fact_base_changed_since_this_lane_opened` with the commits that settle\n685:       them. This is the SECOND recorded recurrence of HB-1, and its concrete\n686:       cost this time is that this lane's own RANK 1 was authored against a\n687:       premise that had already been overtaken on main -- which is why the\n688:       successor's objective statement is a binding condition below rather than\n689:       an inheritance.\n690:     - >-\n691:       NOTHING IN THIS CLOSE RE-SCORES, REINTERPRETS OR RETRACTS ANY COMMITTED\n692:       FINDING, and no measurement originates in it. EV-ECDLP-6783b8,\n693:       EV-ECDLP-6a4ebc, EV-ECDLP-2e9680, EV-ECDLP-60e266, EV-ECDLP-f6b3f5,\n694:       DEC-20260907-8d8782, DEC-20260907-6d9427 and DEC-20260907-9b1b02 are\n695:       cited at their own stated scope and are untouched. The gate's\n696:       recomputations are cited as THE GATE'S; this close performed none of\n697:       them.\n698: \n699:   # ===================================================================\n\n(Showing lines 560-699 of 1115. Use offset=700 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"          `value: null`, `measured_by: []`, `scope: null`, and its own\n          `obstruction_note` reads \"NOT APPLICABLE ... No obstruction quantity\n          is claimed here\", because its `direction` is `neutral` and it closes\n          no lane. So the honest answer is not \"no theory takes it up\" but \"no\n          obstruction was ever asserted\": there is no quantity, value, scope or\n          run set for any theory to re-read as an asset.\n        spawned_ids: []\n        acted_on: >-\n          NOTHING. EV-AES-abf3dc is a GOAL-AES-002 record, immutable, non-ECC by\n          declaration, and outside this lane's write scope and authority. Its\n          `resource_check` is not edited. Recorded so the next rerank does not\n          re-ask it blind -- which is the second time this reading has had to be\n          recorded, and is itself the small transferable finding: THE REGISTRY\n          CANNOT DISTINGUISH AN UNEXAMINED OBSTRUCTION FROM AN INAPPLICABLE\n          ONE, so a `neutral` evidence record with a wholly null obstruction\n          block will sit in `--unexamined` forever and will be re-read by every\n          rerank on every goal. The fix belongs to whoever owns\n          tools/obstruction_registry.py: treat a block whose every substantive\n          field is null and whose note declares inapplicability as OUT OF THE\n          STANDING SET rather than as unexamined.","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/ledger/decisions/DEC-20260907-de6b71.yaml","text":"          `value: null`, `measured_by: []`, `scope: null`, and its own\n          `obstruction_note` reads \"NOT APPLICABLE ... No obstruction quantity\n          is claimed here\", because its `direction` is `neutral` and it closes\n          no lane. So the honest answer is not \"no theory takes it up\" but \"no\n          obstruction was ever asserted\": there is no quantity, value, scope or\n          run set for any theory to re-read as an asset.\n        spawned_ids: []\n        acted_on: >-\n          NOTHING. EV-AES-abf3dc is a GOAL-AES-002 record, immutable, non-ECC by\n          declaration, and outside this lane's write scope and authority. Its\n          `resource_check` is not edited. Recorded so the next rerank does not\n          re-ask it blind -- which is the second time this reading has had to be\n          recorded, and is itself the small transferable finding: THE REGISTRY\n          CANNOT DISTINGUISH AN UNEXAMINED OBSTRUCTION FROM AN INAPPLICABLE\n          ONE, so a `neutral` evidence record with a wholly null obstruction\n          block will sit in `--unexamined` forever and will be re-read by every\n          rerank on every goal. The fix belongs to whoever owns\n          tools/obstruction_registry.py: treat a block whose every substantive\n          field is null and whose note declares inapplicability as OUT OF THE\n          STANDING SET rather than as unexamined.\n    consequence_for_this_rerank: >-\n      NONE OF THE STANDING OBSTRUCTIONS BEARS ON THIS GOAL'S RANKING. This\n      goal's own live obstruction -- EV-ECDLP-60e266's T_sel = T/2 disjointness\n      at a = 1/4, which completion criterion C3 rests on -- is already\n      resource-checked and is not in the unexamined set. Its resource reading is\n      what the small-a lane has been pursuing all along: the quantity that\n      bounds the gain at a = 1/4 is the hypothesis that a smaller a escapes the\n      bound. That reversal is now PARTLY ANSWERED rather than merely posed --\n      EV-ECDLP-6783b8 and EV-ECDLP-6a4ebc both record ceiling-feasibility at\n      a = 1/8 at `preliminary` strength, and EV-ECDLP-2e9680 records a = 1/16 --\n      which is a genuine advance on the obstruction's own resource_check and is\n      recorded here because the obstruction registry has no way to see it.\n\n  # ===================================================================\n  # 7. ECC PRIORITY\n  # ===================================================================\n  ecc_priority_check:\n    command: python3 tools/ecc_priority.py --classify GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f\n    output: 'GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f        area=ECDLP      ECC'\n    holds: true\n    consequence: >-\n      ECC by declaration in orchestration/research-priority.yaml, read through\n      tools/ecc_priority.py and never inferred from the identifier prefix. This\n      goal is considered before every non-ECC goal at every selection point and\n      its campaign budget carries no batch or wall-clock ceiling\n      (maximum_batches null, total_wall_clock_seconds null, enforced by\n      check_ecc_budget_is_unlimited). UNLIMITED REMOVES THE CEILING, NOT THE\n      DUTY TO RANK, which is why the ranking below gives reasons rather than a\n      list and why this close cancels a task it cannot rank ahead of doing\n      nothing rather than offering it.\n    open_ecc_ideas_note: >-\n      `python3 tools/ecc_priority.py --open-ideas` reports 417 open ECC ideas,\n      84 of them in area ECDLP. They are ranked work under instruction 3, not\n      backlog. This goal's own four named ideas (IDEA-20260906-a3d6ae,\n      -05ffb8, -cf3b76, -ac100b) are carried at RANK 5 below; the wider open-idea\n      set is not this lane's to rank and is not ranked here.\n\n  # ===================================================================\n  # 8. RATIONALE FOR THE RANKING\n  # ===================================================================\n  rationale:\n    - >-\n      THE LANE'S OUTCOME IS A REFUSAL, AND A REFUSAL ENDS THIS TASK, NOT THE\n      CAMPAIGN. BATCH-48ef8b authored a contract and had it gated by an\n      independent session that returned `revise`. That is the lane's\n      disposition. It executed nothing, so no evidence record exists, no\n      hypothesis status moves, and nothing in this close asserts anything about\n      the ECDLP. What the lane produced that is worth carrying: a discharged\n      predecessor defect list, a contract whose mathematics and mechanism are\n      now independently verified, a leak discipline that held under audit\n      including in four immutable commit messages, an enumerated ten-item\n      remedy list, an overturned prior, finding CF-3 against an approved\n      contract, and finding TG-1 about how these contracts are being written.\n    - >-\n      RANK 1 IS THE v3 REPAIR, AND THE REASON IS NOT THAT IT IS THIS LANE'S\n      SUCCESSOR. Three things put it first. FIRST, its work is fully specified\n      and bounded: the gate wrote ten per-item remedies and an explicit list of\n      what must NOT be reopened, so the successor authorship is a closed task\n      rather than another open-ended pass, and the gate's own ruling is that\n      the repair cost is at its minimum NOW and rises monotonically -- an\n      amendment to an approved contract after approval, and after execution an\n      amendment to a contract that runs already depend on, with\n      `invalidation_rules` item 7 forbidding re-scoring what has executed.\n      SECOND, its purpose is now BETTER motivated than when the lane opened,\n      not worse: a = 1/8 is confirmed feasible at N = 2^24 by two records from\n      two lanes, and what those records jointly show is a borderline cell\n      measured twice at five draws with exactly one opposite-sign draw each\n      time and a review joint recorded BREAKS on that disagreement -- which is\n      the canonical case for v3's 25-seed arm, its interval routing and the SU\n      label it introduced for a straddling interval. THIRD, it is the\n      cheapest of the five candidates by a wide margin and it unblocks the\n      other four rather than competing with them.\n    - >-\n      WHAT RANK 1 WAS RANKED AGAINST, AND WHY EACH LOST. (i) THE v2\n      SELF-CONTRADICTION CF-3 is arguably more URGENT -- v2 is\n      execution_authorized today and its owning lane has closed, so the remedy\n      is unowned -- but it is a documentation correction that reduces ZERO\n      research uncertainty, the one run set already executed under v2 shows no\n      sign of having been affected by it, and the lane that must open anyway\n      can carry it for approximately nothing. Urgency is not the ranking\n      criterion; uncertainty reduced is. It is therefore a REQUIRED CARRIED\n      ITEM of RANK 1, not a rank. (ii) COMPLETION CRITERION C2 is the goal's\n      ONLY OPEN criterion, which is the strongest argument any candidate here\n      has, and it still loses: its blocker is instrumental rather than\n      scientific (the O(theta) correction gating `fixture_gate_v2`), its next\n      step is ALSO an amendment authorship so it gains nothing in immediacy,\n      and closing the criterion tally while the central clause sits at\n      `preliminary` on five-draw samples would optimise the wrong quantity. C1\n      and C3 being MET makes that more tempting, not more justified. (iii) THE\n      ONLINE RESEL-L ARM is the goal's largest genuine gap and moves UP to\n      RANK 2 on the new facts, but not to RANK 1: its comparison target is the\n      ceiling, and the ceiling's definitional gap is LIVE in the approved v2\n      (CR-1a: cap, CAP_MULT, cycle_mass and capped_mass appear zero times in\n      it), so an online arm run today would be read against a definition a\n      from-scratch re-deriver cannot recover. Fix the definition, then measure\n      against it. That ordering is a reason, not a deferral. (iv)\n      IDEA-20260906-a3d6ae AND THE CHEAP CLOSURES are last for the reason they\n      have always been last: none bears on the borderline cell or on C2, and\n      none is blocked, so nothing is lost by their position.\n    - >-\n      THE RANKING IS WRITTEN AGAINST A MOVED FACT BASE, AND SAYS SO. Two\n      premises this lane opened under are false as of the origin/main merge at\n      4e737c70e: a = 1/8 is no longer open, and the lane the gate named as\n      CF-3's owner has closed. Both are recorded in\n      `fact_base_changed_since_this_lane_opened` with the commits that settle\n      them. This is the SECOND recorded recurrence of HB-1, and its concrete\n      cost this time is that this lane's own RANK 1 was authored against a\n      premise that had already been overtaken on main -- which is why the\n      successor's objective statement is a binding condition below rather than\n      an inheritance.\n    - >-\n      NOTHING IN THIS CLOSE RE-SCORES, REINTERPRETS OR RETRACTS ANY COMMITTED\n      FINDING, and no measurement originates in it. EV-ECDLP-6783b8,\n      EV-ECDLP-6a4ebc, EV-ECDLP-2e9680, EV-ECDLP-60e266, EV-ECDLP-f6b3f5,\n      DEC-20260907-8d8782, DEC-20260907-6d9427 and DEC-20260907-9b1b02 are\n      cited at their own stated scope and are untouched. The gate's\n      recomputations are cited as THE GATE'S; this close performed none of\n      them.\n\n  # ===================================================================","lineStart":560,"lineEnd":699,"totalLines":1115,"truncated":true}},"title":"ledger/decisions/DEC-20260907-de6b71.yaml","time":{"start":1789087908656,"end":1789087908683}},"id":"prt_08df2fc98001YX60mXb3IaZ004","sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","messageID":"msg_08df14a85001H3t9mi3efFLcBZ"}}
