of 5\"), applied at 25 seeds\n1702:       as k >= 20 of 25. The seeds 1..5 SUBGROUP is additionally scored by the\n1703:       rule above verbatim (>= 4 of 5), reported SEPARATELY, and NEVER\n1704:       composited with the 25-seed reading (control (g)). WHERE THE TWO\n1705:       READINGS DISAGREE ON A CELL'S VERDICT, BOTH ARE REPORTED AND NEITHER IS\n1706:       PREFERRED: that disagreement is itself a finding about the power of a\n1707:       5-seed reading, and resolving it by picking the more convenient one\n1708:       would be the analysis mistake control (g) exists to catch.\n1709:     SU_routing_rule: >-\n1710:       SU (CONFIRMED UNRESOLVED) is assigned to a cell when BOTH readings\n1711:       agree on the verdict AND the percentile bootstrap interval of the mean\n1712:       margin (per `definitions` item 8) STRADDLES ZERO in either reading.\n1713:       PRECEDENCE, STATED EXPLICITLY BECAUSE IT IS THE ONE WAY SU COULD DO\n1714:       HARM: S3 TAKES PRECEDENCE OVER SU. If the two readings disagree on the\n1715:       pass-count-derived verdict or on the sign of the mean margin, the cell\n1716:       is S3, FULL STOP -- SU never masks a disagreement by absorbing it into\n1717:       an \"unresolved\" label. SU is reachable only from an AGREEING pair.\n1718:       WHAT SU ASSERTS: that at this cell, this seed set, this scale and this\n1719:       budget, the measurement does not separate feasible from infeasible. It\n1720:       is a statement about instrument resolution, not about the world; it\n1721:       supports NO hypothesis-status movement in either direction and closes\n1722:       no lane. A cell routed to SU is reported with its pass-count, its mean\n1723:       margin and its interval (tail check), so the routing is auditable.\n1724:     agreement_is_judged_on: >-\n1725:       EXACTLY TWO QUANTITIES, both resampling-free: (1) the pass-count k out\n1726:       of 25, and (2) the SIGN of the mean margin. AGREEMENT means both match\n1727:       in the two readings' verdicts derived from k, and the signs match.\n1728:       NOTHING ELSE ENTERS: not an interval endpoint, not a per-seed\n1729:       coincidence (the two readings implement different mix functions and\n1730:       different tie-break key streams, so per-seed coincidence is not\n1731:       expected and its absence is not a disagreement), and not a\n1732:       tie-break-induced difference in the Sel_static sets.\n1733:       A ROUTING DIFFERENCE (one reading's interval straddles zero, the other's\n1734:       does not) IS REPORTED AS INTERVAL-METHOD SENSITIVITY, never as S3.\n1735:     independence_weighting: >-\n1736:       At a = 1/16, AGREEMENT carries ZERO independence weight and\n1737:       DISAGREEMENT carries FULL weight, per `definitions` item 10 -- fixed in\n1738:       this contract, not routed to a review joint. At every other a,\n1739:       agreement carries its ordinary weight subject to the blindness\n1740:       requirement.\n1741:     crossing_bracket_at_two_scales: >-\n1742:       The crossing bracket is reported PER SCALE, independently, by the rule\n1743:       above. A cross-scale comparison of the two brackets is reported as a\n1744:       CONSISTENCY READ and is explicitly NOT A CONTROL: there is no committed\n1745:       N = 2^20 cell of this experiment to pass or fail against (see control\n1746:       (h) and `contradiction_disclosure`). If a bracket is not confirmed at a\n1747:       scale, that is reported plainly as \"crossing not confirmed at this N\",\n1748:       never filled in from the other scale.\n1749: \n1750:   falsification_criterion: >-\n1751:     F1: the a = 1/4 replication control fails to reproduce\n1752:     G3-INFEASIBLE -- see `invalidation_rules` (instrument mismatch, not a\n1753:     result about clause (C1)). F2: at a = 1/16 or a = 1/8, the CONFIRMED\n1754:     (blind-and-production-agreeing) verdict is G3-INFEASIBLE, reversing the\n1755:     N = 2^20 Stage 0 reading -- this falsifies the N-independence of the\n1756:     Stage 0 discrepancy specifically at N = 2^24 (reported as a genuine,\n1757:     scale-dependent finding, not an error) and is exactly outcome (b)'s\n1758:     \"NOT confirmed\" branch if it stems from a real N-dependence rather than\n1759:     a units/definition artifact. F3: Stage A's blind result and Stage B/C's\n1760:     production result disagree beyond seed-to-seed noise at any a without a\n1761:     demonstrable units/definition explanation -- this is a MEASUREMENT\n1762:     ARTIFACT finding about the ORIGINAL Stage 0 discrepancy's own validity,\n1763:     reported as a correction to EV-ECDLP-f6b3f5's `unresolved_confounds`\n1764:     (a new evidence record superseding, never editing, that entry), not\n1765:     treated as resolving feasibility either way at N = 2^24.\n1766:   falsification_criterion_v3_additions: >-\n1767:     F1, F2 and F3 above are retained verbatim from the approved v2 and are\n1768:     unchanged in meaning. v3 ADDS:\n1769:       F4 (CAP SENSITIVITY): a cell whose CONFIRMED verdict differs from the\n\n(Showing lines 1680-1769 of 2473. Use offset=1770 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"    the CONFIRMED (blind-and-production-agreeing) verdict changes from\n    FEASIBLE to INFEASIBLE; if no clean crossing is confirmed (e.g.\n    disagreement occurs inside the bracket), that is reported plainly as\n    \"crossing not confirmed at this N,\" not papered over with the N = 2^20\n    reading.\n  success_criterion_verbatim_attestation: >-\n    THE FIELD ABOVE IS REPRODUCED BYTE-IDENTICALLY FROM THE APPROVED\n    experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml `success_criterion`,\n    per CR-1 COND-3. S1 = CONFIRMED FEASIBLE, S2 = CONFIRMED INFEASIBLE,\n    S3 = DISAGREEMENT, with the approved meanings and no re-wording. NO\n    OUTCOME OF THIS CONTRACT IS LABELLED S4 (see `definitions` item 9 for the\n    only places that string occurs, none of them a label). Everything v3 adds is in\n    `success_criterion_v3_additions` below.\n  success_criterion_v3_additions:\n    scope_of_the_additions: >-\n      The criterion above is applied UNCHANGED at each (N, a) cell, once per\n      reading. The additions below (i) state how the >= 4/5 rule reads at 25\n      seeds, (ii) define the SU routing and its precedence, and (iii) fix\n      what agreement is judged on. They add an outcome and a threshold\n      reading; they change no meaning of S1, S2 or S3.","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml","text":"    the CONFIRMED (blind-and-production-agreeing) verdict changes from\n    FEASIBLE to INFEASIBLE; if no clean crossing is confirmed (e.g.\n    disagreement occurs inside the bracket), that is reported plainly as\n    \"crossing not confirmed at this N,\" not papered over with the N = 2^20\n    reading.\n  success_criterion_verbatim_attestation: >-\n    THE FIELD ABOVE IS REPRODUCED BYTE-IDENTICALLY FROM THE APPROVED\n    experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v2.yaml `success_criterion`,\n    per CR-1 COND-3. S1 = CONFIRMED FEASIBLE, S2 = CONFIRMED INFEASIBLE,\n    S3 = DISAGREEMENT, with the approved meanings and no re-wording. NO\n    OUTCOME OF THIS CONTRACT IS LABELLED S4 (see `definitions` item 9 for the\n    only places that string occurs, none of them a label). Everything v3 adds is in\n    `success_criterion_v3_additions` below.\n  success_criterion_v3_additions:\n    scope_of_the_additions: >-\n      The criterion above is applied UNCHANGED at each (N, a) cell, once per\n      reading. The additions below (i) state how the >= 4/5 rule reads at 25\n      seeds, (ii) define the SU routing and its precedence, and (iii) fix\n      what agreement is judged on. They add an outcome and a threshold\n      reading; they change no meaning of S1, S2 or S3.\n    pass_count_rule_at_25_seeds: >-\n      The rule above is a PROPORTIONAL one (\">= 4 of 5\"), applied at 25 seeds\n      as k >= 20 of 25. The seeds 1..5 SUBGROUP is additionally scored by the\n      rule above verbatim (>= 4 of 5), reported SEPARATELY, and NEVER\n      composited with the 25-seed reading (control (g)). WHERE THE TWO\n      READINGS DISAGREE ON A CELL'S VERDICT, BOTH ARE REPORTED AND NEITHER IS\n      PREFERRED: that disagreement is itself a finding about the power of a\n      5-seed reading, and resolving it by picking the more convenient one\n      would be the analysis mistake control (g) exists to catch.\n    SU_routing_rule: >-\n      SU (CONFIRMED UNRESOLVED) is assigned to a cell when BOTH readings\n      agree on the verdict AND the percentile bootstrap interval of the mean\n      margin (per `definitions` item 8) STRADDLES ZERO in either reading.\n      PRECEDENCE, STATED EXPLICITLY BECAUSE IT IS THE ONE WAY SU COULD DO\n      HARM: S3 TAKES PRECEDENCE OVER SU. If the two readings disagree on the\n      pass-count-derived verdict or on the sign of the mean margin, the cell\n      is S3, FULL STOP -- SU never masks a disagreement by absorbing it into\n      an \"unresolved\" label. SU is reachable only from an AGREEING pair.\n      WHAT SU ASSERTS: that at this cell, this seed set, this scale and this\n      budget, the measurement does not separate feasible from infeasible. It\n      is a statement about instrument resolution, not about the world; it\n      supports NO hypothesis-status movement in either direction and closes\n      no lane. A cell routed to SU is reported with its pass-count, its mean\n      margin and its interval (tail check), so the routing is auditable.\n    agreement_is_judged_on: >-\n      EXACTLY TWO QUANTITIES, both resampling-free: (1) the pass-count k out\n      of 25, and (2) the SIGN of the mean margin. AGREEMENT means both match\n      in the two readings' verdicts derived from k, and the signs match.\n      NOTHING ELSE ENTERS: not an interval endpoint, not a per-seed\n      coincidence (the two readings implement different mix functions and\n      different tie-break key streams, so per-seed coincidence is not\n      expected and its absence is not a disagreement), and not a\n      tie-break-induced difference in the Sel_static sets.\n      A ROUTING DIFFERENCE (one reading's interval straddles zero, the other's\n      does not) IS REPORTED AS INTERVAL-METHOD SENSITIVITY, never as S3.\n    independence_weighting: >-\n      At a = 1/16, AGREEMENT carries ZERO independence weight and\n      DISAGREEMENT carries FULL weight, per `definitions` item 10 -- fixed in\n      this contract, not routed to a review joint. At every other a,\n      agreement carries its ordinary weight subject to the blindness\n      requirement.\n    crossing_bracket_at_two_scales: >-\n      The crossing bracket is reported PER SCALE, independently, by the rule\n      above. A cross-scale comparison of the two brackets is reported as a\n      CONSISTENCY READ and is explicitly NOT A CONTROL: there is no committed\n      N = 2^20 cell of this experiment to pass or fail against (see control\n      (h) and `contradiction_disclosure`). If a bracket is not confirmed at a\n      scale, that is reported plainly as \"crossing not confirmed at this N\",\n      never filled in from the other scale.\n\n  falsification_criterion: >-\n    F1: the a = 1/4 replication control fails to reproduce\n    G3-INFEASIBLE -- see `invalidation_rules` (instrument mismatch, not a\n    result about clause (C1)). F2: at a = 1/16 or a = 1/8, the CONFIRMED\n    (blind-and-production-agreeing) verdict is G3-INFEASIBLE, reversing the\n    N = 2^20 Stage 0 reading -- this falsifies the N-independence of the\n    Stage 0 discrepancy specifically at N = 2^24 (reported as a genuine,\n    scale-dependent finding, not an error) and is exactly outcome (b)'s\n    \"NOT confirmed\" branch if it stems from a real N-dependence rather than\n    a units/definition artifact. F3: Stage A's blind result and Stage B/C's\n    production result disagree beyond seed-to-seed noise at any a without a\n    demonstrable units/definition explanation -- this is a MEASUREMENT\n    ARTIFACT finding about the ORIGINAL Stage 0 discrepancy's own validity,\n    reported as a correction to EV-ECDLP-f6b3f5's `unresolved_confounds`\n    (a new evidence record superseding, never editing, that entry), not\n    treated as resolving feasibility either way at N = 2^24.\n  falsification_criterion_v3_additions: >-\n    F1, F2 and F3 above are retained verbatim from the approved v2 and are\n    unchanged in meaning. v3 ADDS:\n      F4 (CAP SENSITIVITY): a cell whose CONFIRMED verdict differs from the","lineStart":1680,"lineEnd":1769,"totalLines":2473,"truncated":true}},"title":"experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml","time":{"start":1789090435007,"end":1789090435052}},"id":"prt_08e1985af0014ImUeukWKybvkF","sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","messageID":"msg_08e17f347001Ta7lsHMRgMA4qi"}}
