ceiling at any\n829:       achievable batch size U, which is the question RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5 actually\n830:       asks. A goal whose central question has never been measured on its own\n831:       terms is not a goal that has met its purpose, whatever its criterion\n832:       tally reads.\n833:     why_the_suspended_quorum_makes_this_decision_carry_full_weight: >-\n834:       AGENTS.md \"Goal closure quorum\" is SUSPENDED, so a met criterion plus a\n835:       committed Coordinator decision would suffice to close. There is no\n836:       three-model check standing between this decision and `completed`. That is\n837:       exactly why this one declines, and why it states its two reasons rather\n838:       than gesturing at them. No `completion_quorum` block is present, none is\n839:       claimed, and NO ATTESTATION IS RECORDED BECAUSE NONE WAS OBTAINED.\n840:     why_neither_closed_at_budget_nor_cancelled: >-\n841:       Neither would be honest. `closed_at_budget` requires the exceptional\n842:       months-long stagnation policy, which is not met and not invoked -- this\n843:       is an ECC goal whose campaign budget is UNLIMITED by declared policy and\n844:       which produced two committed evidence records dated today in adjacent\n845:       lanes. `cancelled` asserts abandonment, and the campaign is not\n846:       abandoned. Retiring a goal that DID meet a criterion under either status,\n847:       to understate it, is a contract violation in its own right.\n848:     the_goal_stays_active_and_is_not_parked: >-\n849:       `status: active`, and `paused` and `blocked` are refused statuses by name\n850:       (AGENTS.md \"Goals are never paused\"; tools/validate_ledger.py refuses\n851:       both). `impediments` stays EMPTY: nothing is blocked. The gate's refusal\n852:       names exactly what to author next, the reassigned CF-3 remedy has a\n853:       concrete owner, and every one of the five ranked actions is runnable now.\n854:       An approval refusal ends a TASK; it does not impede a campaign.\n855: \n856:   # ===================================================================\n857:   # 12. NEXT ACTIONS\n858:   # ===================================================================\n859:   next_actions:\n860:     - >-\n861:       RANK 1 -- THE SUPERSEDING v3 REVISION, WITH THREE REQUIRED CARRIED ITEMS.\n862:       Author a superseding revision of experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml\n863:       and experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml AT A NEW\n864:       SNAPSHOT, discharging the seven blocking findings (CF-1, CF-2, CF-4,\n865:       CF-5, LO-1, XR-1, XR-2) and the three non-blocking ones (XR-3, J1-CITE,\n866:       CT2-CHAR), per the per-item remedies in approval_review.yaml\n867:       `verdict_block.what_a_revision_must_contain`. NOT ONE BYTE of the\n868:       TASK-20260907-6077f2 snapshot may be rewritten and no approved or frozen\n869:       record may be touched; every item sits in v3-appended text or in the\n870:       amendment, so none of them requires it. DO NOT REOPEN what the gate\n871:       checked and passed: the cap convention, the three-term accounting\n872:       identity, the allowlist mechanism, the two-scale scope, and every block\n873:       CR-1 pins byte-identical. THEN a FRESH independent gate on the revision,\n874:       in a session that is neither the author nor TASK-20260907-9c0626, with a\n875:       narrower scope: confirm the ten remedies landed, confirm the two\n876:       normative documents now agree letter for letter on the identity and count\n877:       of the controls, confirm nothing frozen moved. A new committed decision\n878:       must set v3's four gate fields before any executor runs; until then\n879:       specification.v3.yaml stays UNAPPROVED and NOT execution-authorized and\n\n(Showing lines 810-879 of 1115. Use offset=880 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"      as a function of N/T), AND their N-independence verdict across\