aluated`, and V2-V5 / M1-M5 are explicitly not to be scored until\n      that gate is evaluated. So no N-independence verdict exists at any scale,\n      let alone across 2^20..2^30, and no CI-bearing measurement set has been\n      composed. C2 names a DIFFERENT OBJECT from the one C1 and C3 rest on, so\n      C1 and C3 being met says nothing about it.\n    the_ranked_work_left: 'RANK 1 through RANK 5 of `next_actions` below, each with its reason.'\n    why_this_close_does_not_reach_for_completed: >-\n      Two independent reasons, either sufficient. FIRST, the criterion set is\n      not satisfied and the goal head declares no rule under which two of three\n      criteria suffice. SECOND and more decisive on the merits: the goal's\n      central hypothesis clause is confirmed only at CEILING level, only at\n      `preliminary` strength, only at N = 2^24, and ZERO ONLINE RESEL-L ARMS\n      HAVE EVER BEEN RUN -- so nothing in this campaign yet bears on whether\n      the online lower-bracket mechanism reaches the measured ceiling at any\n      achievable batch size U, which is the question RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5 actually\n      asks. A goal whose central question has never been measured on its own\n      terms is not a goal that has met its purpose, whatever its criterion\n      tally reads.\n    why_the_suspended_quorum_makes_this_decision_carry_full_weight: >-\n      AGENTS.md \"Goal closure quorum\" is SUSPENDED, so a met criterion plus a\n      committed Coordinator decision would suffice to close. There is no\n      three-model check standing between this decision and `completed`. That is\n      exactly why this one declines, and why it states its two reasons rather\n      than gesturing at them. No `completion_quorum` block is present, none is\n      claimed, and NO ATTESTATION IS RECORDED BECAUSE NONE WAS OBTAINED.\n    why_neither_closed_at_budget_nor_cancelled: >-\n      Neither would be honest. `closed_at_budget` requires the exceptional\n      months-long stagnation policy, which is not met and not invoked -- this\n      is an ECC goal whose campaign budget is UNLIMITED by declared policy and\n      which produced two committed evidence records dated today in adjacent\n      lanes. `cancelled` asserts abandonment, and the campaign is not\n      abandoned. Retiring a goal that DID meet a criterion under either status,\n      to understate it, is a contract violation in its own right.\n    the_goal_stays_active_and_is_not_parked: >-\n      `status: active`, and `paused` and `blocked` are refused statuses by name\n      (AGENTS.md \"Goals are never paused\"; tools/validate_ledger.py refuses\n      both). `impediments` stays EMPTY: nothing is blocked. The gate's refusal\n      names exactly what to author next, the reassigned CF-3 remedy has a\n      concrete owner, and every one of the five ranked actions is runnable now.\n      An approval refusal ends a TASK; it does not impede a campaign.\n\n  # ===================================================================\n  # 12. NEXT ACTIONS\n  # ===================================================================\n  next_actions:\n    - >-\n      RANK 1 -- THE SUPERSEDING v3 REVISION, WITH THREE REQUIRED CARRIED ITEMS.\n      Author a superseding revision of experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/specification.v3.yaml\n      and experiments/EXP-ECDLP-6ac801/amendments/v2_to_v3.yaml AT A NEW\n      SNAPSHOT, discharging the seven blocking findings (CF-1, CF-2, CF-4,\n      CF-5, LO-1, XR-1, XR-2) and the three non-blocking ones (XR-3, J1-CITE,\n      CT2-CHAR), per the per-item remedies in approval_review.yaml\n      `verdict_block.what_a_revision_must_contain`. NOT ONE BYTE of the\n      TASK-20260907-6077f2 snapshot may be rewritten and no approved or frozen\n      record may be touched; every item sits in v3-appended text or in the\n      amendment, so none of them requires it. DO NOT REOPEN what the gate\n      checked and passed: the cap convention, the three-term accounting\n      identity, the allowlist mechanism, the two-scale scope, and every block\n      CR-1 pins byte-identical. THEN a FRESH independent gate on the revision,\n      in a session that is neither the author nor TASK-20260907-9c0626, with a\n      narrower scope: confirm the ten remedies landed, confirm the two\n      normative documents now agree letter for letter on the identity and count\n      of the controls, confirm nothing frozen moved. A new committed decision\n      must set v3's four gate fields before any executor runs; until then\n      specification.v3.yaml stays UNAPPROVED and NOT execution-authorized and","lineStart":810,"lineEnd":879,"totalLines":1115,"truncated":true}},"title":"ledger/decisions/DEC-20260907-de6b71.yaml","time":{"start":1789092984453,"end":1789092984479}},"id":"prt_08e406da6001I2S311xKqMt8e7","sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","messageID":"msg_08e31cfed001Y9mOF1zD06cunX"}}
