6e9a.yaml\n27:     - ledger/evidence/EV-ENDO-10109d.yaml\n28:     - ledger/evidence/            # corpus-wide grep sweep over all 538 EV-*.yaml for `strength:` labels and independence phrasing\n29:     - knowledge/findings/         # corpus-wide grep sweep over all 81 KN-FIND-*.md for `confidence:` values\n30:   read_sibling_reports: false\n31:   blind_from_respected: true\n32: \n33:   attestation_notes:\n34:     - >-\n35:       NOT READ, deliberately: the J1 output directory\n36:       coordination/experiments/EXP-ECDLP-c373eb/batches/BATCH-e8a3a7/reviews/TASK-20260903-6048dc/\n37:       (verified empty at the time of this review, and not opened), and every\n38:       artifact of RUN-ECDLP-c373eb-1 and RUN-ECDLP-c373eb-2 other than the two\n39:       paths listed above. RUN-1's values are taken from EV-ECDLP-f5c698, not\n40:       from its raw-result.json.\n41:     - >-\n42:       DISCLOSURE ON `blind_from`, so a mechanical checker is not misled. The\n43:       plan's `blind_rederivation.blind_from` list binds TASK-20260903-6048dc,\n44:       the assigned re-deriver. I am NOT the re-deriver. My own attack plan\n45:       (J2 clause (a)) directs me in terms to read both implementation scripts;\n46:       three paths in my `sources_read` therefore intersect the OTHER task's\n47:       `blind_from` set, lawfully and by instruction:\n48:       implementation/rc1_tabulation.py, implementation/rc1_tabulation_run2.py,\n49:       and runs/RUN-ECDLP-c373eb-2/manifest.yaml. No seal applies to me.\n50:     - >-\n51:       CLAUDE.md and the task card were supplied as injected session context\n52:       rather than opened with a read tool; they are not listed as sources_read.\n53:     - >-\n54:       ZERO COMPUTE WAS RUN. `experiment_maximum_runs: 0` was honoured: neither\n55:       tabulation script was executed, no measurement was produced, and every\n56:       number in this report is either read off a committed artifact or derived\n57:       by argument and labelled as such. `diff`, `grep` and `wc` over committed\n58:       files are reading, not measuring.\n59: \n60: red_team_report:\n61:   id: RT-20260903-d02517\n62:   task_id: TASK-20260903-d02517\n63:   batch_id: BATCH-e8a3a7\n64:   goal_id: GOAL-ECDLP-001\n65:   experiment_id: EXP-ECDLP-c373eb\n66:   joint: J2\n67:   recorded_at: '2026-09-03'\n68:   reviewed_snapshot:\n69:     run_2_commit: f7a52cbad          # \"runs(EXP-ECDLP-c373eb): RUN-ECDLP-c373eb-2 replication run archived\"\n70:     run_1_impl_commit: 5d7cf2888     # \"snapshot(GOAL-ECDLP-001): TASK-20260901-400254 RC-1 run bytes\"\n71:     note: >-\n72:       Both reviewed artifacts are Coordinator-committed, so this review rests on\n73:       durable snapshots and not on working-tree bytes, per red-team.md\n74:       responsibility 6.\n75: \n76:   claim_under_review: >-\n77:     That two agreeing toy instances -- RUN-ECDLP-c373eb-1 (p=1009, y^2=x^3+x+1,\n78:     S=(286,680), n=47) and RUN-ECDLP-c373eb-2 (p=1013, y^2=x^3+2x+2,\n79:     S=(393,263), n=41) -- are SUFFICIENT to upgrade KN-FIND-1ba0fe's recorded\n80:     confidence from `preliminary` to `replicated`, given that RUN-2's script was\n81:     adapted from RUN-1's by the same agent lineage under the same brief.\n82: \n83:   verdict: breaks\n84: \n85:   verdict_summary: >-\n86:     The upgrade is NOT warranted on this evidence. RUN-2 supplies a second\n87:     INSTANCE; `replicated` in this program's operative practice counts\n88:     IMPLEMENTATIONS. The two runs share 266 of RUN-1's 270 non-comment\n89:     executable lines verbatim -- every function definition without exception --\n90:     so their agreement is guaranteed conditional on a shared error and carries a\n91:     likelihood ratio of essentially 1 between \"the mathematics is right\" and\n92:     \"the shared arithmetic core is wrong\". The order-n certificate that both\n93:     runs advertise as independent is computed by the same `scalar_mult` it\n94:     certifies. The null-lift control varies the INPUT, not the CODE PATH, and is\n95:     itself common-mode across the two runs: running a shared control twice does\n96:     not make it a cross-run control. Separately, the measured outcome is forced\n97:     by the already-derived Lemmas 1-2 once the order-n certificate passes, so\n98:     the experiment's residual information content is about the implementation,\n99:     which is precisely the axis on which the two runs are not independent.\n100:     This verdict is INSUFFICIENT-FOR-UPGRADE, not a contradiction: RUN-2's\n101:     reported values agree with RUN-1's and with Proposition E, and nothing here\n102:     is evidence against the finding.\n103: \n104:   escalation:\n105:     fires: false\n106:     reason: >-\n107:       The plan's escalation_condition fires only on a genuine CONTRADICTION of\n108:       RUN-1 or of prior validated evidence. RUN-2 confirms RUN-1 (canonical\n109:       {0,8}, null {0,1}, Vandermonde {0,8}, non-rigid {0} in both). My objection\n110:       is that confirmation from a near-clone implementation is weak, not that it\n111:       is contrary. The plan states explicitly that an insufficient-for-upgrade\n112:       verdict does not fire escalation. No review-breakthrough re-run is\n113:       requested on my joint.\n114: \n115:   # =====================================================================\n116:   # OBJECTIONS\n117:   # =====================================================================\n118:   objections:\n119: \n120:     - id: OBJ-1\n\n(Showing lines 1-120 of 961. Use offset=121 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"schema: crypto.autoresearch.red_team_report.v1\n\nreview_attestation:\n  task_id: TASK-20260903-d02517\n  joints_owned:\n    - \"J2: Two agreeing toy instances (RUN-1 and RUN-2) are sufficient to upgrade KN-FIND-1ba0fe from `preliminary` to `replicated` confidence, given that RUN-2's implementation was adapted from RUN-1's by the same agent lineage under the same brief.\"\n  verdict: breaks\n  sources_read:\n    - AGENTS.md\n    - agents/red-team.md\n    - coordination/experiments/EXP-ECDLP-c373eb/batches/BATCH-e8a3a7/review-plan.yaml\n    - knowledge/findings/KN-FIND-1ba0fe.md\n    - ledger/hypotheses/H-ECDLP-a40416.yaml\n    - ledger/evidence/EV-ECDLP-f5c698.yaml\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-c373eb/specification.yaml\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-c373eb/implementation/rc1_tabulation.py\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-c373eb/implementation/rc1_tabulation_run2.py\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-c373eb/runs/RUN-ECDLP-c373eb-2/manifest.yaml\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-c373eb/runs/RUN-ECDLP-c373eb-2/execution-report.yaml\n    - docs/evidence-and-reproducibility.md","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Volumes/SSD990/llm/tmp/opencode/ecdlp-20260910/coordination/experiments/EXP-ECDLP-c373eb/batches/BATCH-e8a3a7/reviews/TASK-20260903-d02517/red-team-report.yaml","text":"schema: crypto.autoresearch.red_team_report.v1\n\nreview_attestation:\n  task_id: TASK-20260903-d02517\n  joints_owned:\n    - \"J2: Two agreeing toy instances (RUN-1 and RUN-2) are sufficient to upgrade KN-FIND-1ba0fe from `preliminary` to `replicated` confidence, given that RUN-2's implementation was adapted from RUN-1's by the same agent lineage under the same brief.\"\n  verdict: breaks\n  sources_read:\n    - AGENTS.md\n    - agents/red-team.md\n    - coordination/experiments/EXP-ECDLP-c373eb/batches/BATCH-e8a3a7/review-plan.yaml\n    - knowledge/findings/KN-FIND-1ba0fe.md\n    - ledger/hypotheses/H-ECDLP-a40416.yaml\n    - ledger/evidence/EV-ECDLP-f5c698.yaml\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-c373eb/specification.yaml\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-c373eb/implementation/rc1_tabulation.py\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-c373eb/implementation/rc1_tabulation_run2.py\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-c373eb/runs/RUN-ECDLP-c373eb-2/manifest.yaml\n    - experiments/EXP-ECDLP-c373eb/runs/RUN-ECDLP-c373eb-2/execution-report.yaml\n    - docs/evidence-and-reproducibility.md\n    - docs/claims-and-verification.md\n    - docs/task-lifecycle.md\n    - templates/research-records.md\n    - ledger/evidence/EV-ECQ-5c2c0a.yaml\n    - ledger/evidence/EV-DIFFP-1e08cc.yaml\n    - ledger/evidence/EV-MCE-3d6e9a.yaml\n    - ledger/evidence/EV-ENDO-10109d.yaml\n    - ledger/evidence/            # corpus-wide grep sweep over all 538 EV-*.yaml for `strength:` labels and independence phrasing\n    - knowledge/findings/         # corpus-wide grep sweep over all 81 KN-FIND-*.md for `confidence:` values\n  read_sibling_reports: false\n  blind_from_respected: true\n\n  attestation_notes:\n    - >-\n      NOT READ, deliberately: the J1 output directory\n      coordination/experiments/EXP-ECDLP-c373eb/batches/BATCH-e8a3a7/reviews/TASK-20260903-6048dc/\n      (verified empty at the time of this review, and not opened), and every\n      artifact of RUN-ECDLP-c373eb-1 and RUN-ECDLP-c373eb-2 other than the two\n      paths listed above. RUN-1's values are taken from EV-ECDLP-f5c698, not\n      from its raw-result.json.\n    - >-\n      DISCLOSURE ON `blind_from`, so a mechanical checker is not misled. The\n      plan's `blind_rederivation.blind_from` list binds TASK-20260903-6048dc,\n      the assigned re-deriver. I am NOT the re-deriver. My own attack plan\n      (J2 clause (a)) directs me in terms to read both implementation scripts;\n      three paths in my `sources_read` therefore intersect the OTHER task's\n      `blind_from` set, lawfully and by instruction:\n      implementation/rc1_tabulation.py, implementation/rc1_tabulation_run2.py,\n      and runs/RUN-ECDLP-c373eb-2/manifest.yaml. No seal applies to me.\n    - >-\n      CLAUDE.md and the task card were supplied as injected session context\n      rather than opened with a read tool; they are not listed as sources_read.\n    - >-\n      ZERO COMPUTE WAS RUN. `experiment_maximum_runs: 0` was honoured: neither\n      tabulation script was executed, no measurement was produced, and every\n      number in this report is either read off a committed artifact or derived\n      by argument and labelled as such. `diff`, `grep` and `wc` over committed\n      files are reading, not measuring.\n\nred_team_report:\n  id: RT-20260903-d02517\n  task_id: TASK-20260903-d02517\n  batch_id: BATCH-e8a3a7\n  goal_id: GOAL-ECDLP-001\n  experiment_id: EXP-ECDLP-c373eb\n  joint: J2\n  recorded_at: '2026-09-03'\n  reviewed_snapshot:\n    run_2_commit: f7a52cbad          # \"runs(EXP-ECDLP-c373eb): RUN-ECDLP-c373eb-2 replication run archived\"\n    run_1_impl_commit: 5d7cf2888     # \"snapshot(GOAL-ECDLP-001): TASK-20260901-400254 RC-1 run bytes\"\n    note: >-\n      Both reviewed artifacts are Coordinator-committed, so this review rests on\n      durable snapshots and not on working-tree bytes, per red-team.md\n      responsibility 6.\n\n  claim_under_review: >-\n    That two agreeing toy instances -- RUN-ECDLP-c373eb-1 (p=1009, y^2=x^3+x+1,\n    S=(286,680), n=47) and RUN-ECDLP-c373eb-2 (p=1013, y^2=x^3+2x+2,\n    S=(393,263), n=41) -- are SUFFICIENT to upgrade KN-FIND-1ba0fe's recorded\n    confidence from `preliminary` to `replicated`, given that RUN-2's script was\n    adapted from RUN-1's by the same agent lineage under the same brief.\n\n  verdict: breaks\n\n  verdict_summary: >-\n    The upgrade is NOT warranted on this evidence. RUN-2 supplies a second\n    INSTANCE; `replicated` in this program's operative practice counts\n    IMPLEMENTATIONS. The two runs share 266 of RUN-1's 270 non-comment\n    executable lines verbatim -- every function definition without exception --\n    so their agreement is guaranteed conditional on a shared error and carries a\n    likelihood ratio of essentially 1 between \"the mathematics is right\" and\n    \"the shared arithmetic core is wrong\". The order-n certificate that both\n    runs advertise as independent is computed by the same `scalar_mult` it\n    certifies. The null-lift control varies the INPUT, not the CODE PATH, and is\n    itself common-mode across the two runs: running a shared control twice does\n    not make it a cross-run control. Separately, the measured outcome is forced\n    by the already-derived Lemmas 1-2 once the order-n certificate passes, so\n    the experiment's residual information content is about the implementation,\n    which is precisely the axis on which the two runs are not independent.\n    This verdict is INSUFFICIENT-FOR-UPGRADE, not a contradiction: RUN-2's\n    reported values agree with RUN-1's and with Proposition E, and nothing here\n    is evidence against the finding.\n\n  escalation:\n    fires: false\n    reason: >-\n      The plan's escalation_condition fires only on a genuine CONTRADICTION of\n      RUN-1 or of prior validated evidence. RUN-2 confirms RUN-1 (canonical\n      {0,8}, null {0,1}, Vandermonde {0,8}, non-rigid {0} in both). My objection\n      is that confirmation from a near-clone implementation is weak, not that it\n      is contrary. The plan states explicitly that an insufficient-for-upgrade\n      verdict does not fire escalation. No review-breakthrough re-run is\n      requested on my joint.\n\n  # =====================================================================\n  # OBJECTIONS\n  # =====================================================================\n  objections:\n\n    - id: OBJ-1","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":120,"totalLines":961,"truncated":true}},"title":"coordination/experiments/EXP-ECDLP-c373eb/batches/BATCH-e8a3a7/reviews/TASK-20260903-d02517/red-team-report.yaml","time":{"start":1789093945021,"end":1789093945028}},"id":"prt_08e4f162a001TdRgV3hobTDfnq","sessionID":"ses_f72344e8bffef224SU4Jqwq9zP","messageID":"msg_08e4d234b001ugh2f9iQJ7D8GR"}}
