seed_used\\n        20282157, B=10000, log2(N) convention; a=3/16: k_25=11, G3-INFEASIBLE,\\n        mean −0.006495399475097656, CI [−0.012656432151794433,\\n        −0.0003270072937011728]. N=2^24 — a=1/4: k_25=2, G3-INFEASIBLE, mean\\n        −0.01933633327484131, CI [−0.023274486124515534, −0.01499074494838715];\\n        a=1/16: k_25=25, G3-FEASIBLE, mean +0.021622254848480224, CI\\n        [+0.01982123154401779, +0.0233601616024971]; a=1/8: k_25=20,\\n        G3-FEASIBLE, mean +0.008110418319702148, CI [+0.004968686401844024,\\n        +0.011464009404182431], no straddle; a=3/16: k_25=9, G3-INFEASIBLE,\\n        mean −0.003705017566680908, CI [−0.00608834832906723, −0.0012291942834854158].\\n        Verdict rule as implemented (run_full.py lines 206-210): k_25 =\\n        count(margin >= 0); verdict_25 = G3-FEASIBLE iff k_25 >= 20.\\n        Recomputed from cells.jsonl: all eight summaries internally consistent\\n        (k_25, k_5, mean, all 200 accounting_identity_holds true) —\\n        recomputed (j3_aggregate.py).\\n    - id: F2\\n      statement: >-\\n        Stage B'' recomputation over the 200 production cells (recomputed,\\n        j3_aggregate.py): per-(N,a) mean margin and k_geq-0 count — N=2^20:\\n        a=1/16 +0.016803474426269532 (24/25); a=1/8 +0.006927833557128906\\n        (17/25); a=3/16 −0.00860198974609375 (8/25); a=1/4 −0.022809906005859373\\n        (2/25). N=2^24: a=1/16 +0.020187950134277342 (25/25); a=1/8\\n        +0.010225589275360108 (24/25); a=3/16 −0.0054317331314086914 (5/25);\\n        a=1/4 −0.018461544513702393 (0/25). These match, value for value, the\\n        Coordinator's independent recomputation recorded in the review plan's\\n        coordinator_prior (e.g. \\\"+0.0168 k=24/25 at 2^20 ... max residual\\n        fraction 0.0232\\\"). Production negatives at a=1/8: N=2^20 seeds\\n        {2,6,7,8,15,21,24,25} with margins from −0.0019960403442382812 to\\n        −0.017505645751953125; N=2^24 seed {8} only, margin\\n        −0.004464387893676758.\\n    - id: F3\\n      statement: >-\\n        Stage B'' identities, recomputed on all 200 cells (j3_aggregate.py):\\n        margin == exact_top_T_sel_share − static_T_r2_exact_coverage with\\n        ZERO float residual in 200/200 cells (max |residual| = 0.0);\\n        basin_mass_accounting_sum == N exactly in 200/200; residual_fraction ==\\n        (cycle_mass + capped_mass)/N exactly in 200/200; self_check_o1_basin_\\n        mass_accounting / o2_exact_coverage_nesting / o3_margin_nesting all\\n        SATISFIED in 200/200; exceedance=false in 200/200.\\n    - id: F4\\n      statement: >-\\n        Cap and W: the v3 frozen table (specification.v3.yaml `definitions`\\n        item 6) gives cap 256/363/444/512 at N=2^20 and 512/725/887/1024 at\\n        N=2^24 for a=1/16,1/8,3/16,1/4. Stage A'' records the table's cap in\\n        all 200 cells.jsonl lines and Stage B'' in all 200 summary cells —\\n        zero mismatches in either (recomputed, j3_aggregate.py). W values\\n        agree to full float64 precision between the two packages at all eight\\n        (N,a) (e.g. 45.254833995939045 at (2^20, 1/8) in both; A'' carries\\n        the Decimal-80 string, B'' the float64).\\n    - id: F5\\n      statement: >-\\n        Eight-frozen-cell triangulation (J1 results.json vs Stage A''\\n        cells.jsonl vs Stage B'' summaries; recomputed, j3_aggregate.py).\\n        PARTITION-LEVEL fields are bit-identical across all three\\n        implementations at all eight frozen cells: share_top_Tsel\\n        (e.g. (2^20,1/8,seed1): J1 exact 195351/1048576 == A'' 0.18630123138427734\\n        == B'' 0.18630123138427734; likewise all seven other cells), n_dps\\n        (23104/22809/23106 at 2^20 a=1/8 seeds 1/7/13; 185418/185849/185684\\n        at 2^24; 32725 at (2^20,1/16,5); 261938 at (2^24,1/16,17)),\\n        cycle_mass (1104/1908/2468; 1576/4895/5299; 2130; 1467), capped_mass\\n        (0/0/43; 14917/4594/6630; 0; 318), residual_fraction (69/65536,\\n        477/262144, 2511/1048576; 16493/16777216, 9489/16777216,\\n        11929/16777216; 1065/524288; 1785/16777216). POOL-DEPENDENT fields\\n        differ: cov_static/cov (e.g. (2^20,1/8,1): J1 25483/131072=0.1944198608\\n        vs A'' 0.20221042633056641 vs B'' 0.18311786651611328), margin\\n        (−0.0081186 / −0.0159092 / +0.0031834 at that cell), rho_ORACLE\\n        (35/64 / 0.578125 / 0.5), tie counts and capped_walks. Margin signs\\n        differ across implementations at 4 of the 6 frozen a=1/8 cells:\\n        (2^20,seed1) J1−/A''−/B''+; (2^20,seed7) J1+/A''+/B''−;\\n        (2^24,seed3) J1+/A''−/B''+; (2^24,seed11) J1−/A''+/B''+. Both frozen\\n        a=1/16 cells agree +/+/+.\\n    - id: F6\\n      statement: >-\\n        a=1/8 per-seed sign sequences, seeds 1..25 (recomputed,\\n        j3_aggregate.py): Stage A'' N=2^20 k=16/25\\n        (\\\"- + + + + + + + + + - - + - + + - - + + + - - - +\\\"); Stage B''\\n        N=2^20 k=17/25 (\\\"+ - + + + - - - + + + + + + - + + + + + - + + - -\\\");\\n        Stage A'' N=2^24 k=20/25; Stage B'' N=2^24 k=24/25. J1's 3-seed\\n        samples at a=1/8: 2^20 signs (s1,s7,s13) = −,+,+; 2^24 (s3,s11,s25)\\n        = +,−,+. Other cells, k_geq0 A''/B'' (2^20 then 2^24): a=1/16:\\n        25/24, 25/25; a=3/16: 11/8, 9/5; a=1/4: 3/2, 2/0.\\n    - id: F7\\n      statement: >-\\n        a=1/4 known-false control: Stage A'' verdicts G3-INFEASIBLE at both\\n        scales (k_25=3 at 2^20, k_25=2 at 2^24; means −0.017541961669921877 /\\n        −0.01933633327484131; CIs excluding zero); Stage B'' k_geq0 = 2/25\\n        (2^20), 0/25 (2^24), means −0.022809906005859373 / −0.018461544513702393;\\n        J1 control (frozen report control_a_quarter): k_25=3 (2^20), k_25=1\\n        (2^24), means −526979/26214400 ≈ −0.0201026535 and −8359221/419430400\\n        ≈ −0.0199299359, CIs [−0.0255774, −0.0143420] and [−0.0230591,\\n        −0.0165219] excluding zero. All six readings reproduce\\n        G3-INFEASIBLE; the three per-seed k counts at 2^24 are 1 (J1), 2\\n        (A''), 0 (B'').\\n    - id: F8\\n      statement: >-\\n        Contract text (specification.v3.yaml), cited by line in the current\\n        tree: G3-style feasibility criterion (line ~372-379, \\\"G3-FEASIBLE iff\\n        exact top-T_sel basin share >= STATIC(T)_r exact coverage in >= 4 of\\n        the 5 seeds\\\"; the 25-seed reading is the proportional k >= 20 of 25\\n        per success_criterion_v3_additions.pass_count_rule_at_25_seeds, lines\\n        1700-1708); INTERVAL ESTIMATOR (lines ~678-725: \\\"NO VERDICT, NO\\n        CONTROL CLAUSE AND NO AGREEMENT TEST IN THIS CONTRACT DEPENDS ON A\\n        BOOTSTRAP\\\"; \\\"a cell whose interval straddles zero is routed to SU\\n        rather than called either way\\\"); SU (lines ~727-750: \\\"the measurement\\n        DOES NOT SEPARATE FEASIBLE FROM INFEASIBLE. It is a statement about\\n        the resolution of the instrument, not about the world\\\");\\n        success_criterion_v3_additions.SU_routing_rule (lines 1709-1723: SU\\n        \\\"when BOTH readings agree on the verdict AND the percentile bootstrap\\n        interval ... STRADDLES ZERO in either reading\\\"; \\\"S3 TAKES PRECEDENCE\\n        OVER SU\\\"); agreement_is_judged_on (lines 1724-1734: \\\"EXACTLY TWO\\n        QUANTITIES, both resampling-free: (1) the pass-count k out of 25, and\\n        (2) the SIGN of the mean margin\\\"; \\\"NOT ... a per-seed coincidence ...\\n        its absence is not a disagreement\\\"); control (o) structural\\n        self-checks (lines ~1398-1424: \\\"CANNOT FAIL on a correct\\n        implementation, so its passing means nothing beyond 'no defect of\\n        this kind'\\\"); accounting identity (line ~552-566: \\\"an identity of the\\n        object exact_basins computes, NOT an empirical claim ... carried as a\\n        STRUCTURAL SELF-CHECK ... and NOT as a control\\\"); crossing point\\n        (line ~380-386: \\\"the (open) interval between the largest a at which\\n        T_sel = T/2 is G3-feasible and the smallest a at which it is not, as\\n        bracketed by this contract's own a_grid\\\"); crossing_bracket_at_two_\\n        scales (lines 1741-1748: \\\"reported PER SCALE, independently\\\"; \\\"If a\\n        bracket is not confirmed at a scale, that is reported plainly as\\n        'crossing not confirmed at this N'\\\"); a = 1/16 INDEPENDENCE RULING\\n        (lines ~752-800: \\\"AGREEMENT ... at a = 1/16 carries ZERO independence\\n        weight, from the outset, at both scales\\\"); stage plan STAGE B''\\n        (line ~852-862: \\\"Zero online re-selected (RESEL-L) arms -- this is an\\n        exact-enumeration measurement only, as in v1\\\"); arms (line ~875-881:\\n        \\\"No ORACLE, RESEL-L, ... arm is run; those test the re-selection\\n        MECHANISM ... and remain out of scope for this narrow\\n        ceiling-feasibility check\\\"); objective_v3 (line ~320-343, the\\n        two-readings comparison \\\"on the PASS-COUNT and the SIGN OF THE MEAN\\n        MARGIN ... never on an interval endpoint\\\").\\n    - id: F9\\n      statement: >-\\n        Goal-head standing record (ledger/goals/GOAL-ECDLP-bbc21f/goal.yaml,\\n        current next_action): RANK 2 — \\\"the ONLINE RESEL-L arm at the\\n        confirmed-feasible a values ... Every ceiling result this goal holds\\n        is SILENT on whether the online lower-bracket mechanism REACHES that\\n        ceiling at any achievable batch size U, and ZERO online arms have\\n        ever been run, so no hypothesis-status promotion beyond\\n        ceiling-feasibility may be considered before it does.\\\" GOAL STATUS —\\n        \\\"the central hypothesis clause is confirmed only at CEILING level,\\n        only at `preliminary` strength, and ZERO ONLINE RESEL-L ARMS HAVE\\n        EVER BEEN RUN, so nothing yet bears on the question RQ-ECDLP-78dbc5\\n        actually asks.\\\" DEC-20260907-de6b71 goal_closure_assessment\\n        (lines 821-832) carries the same record; its RANK 2 (lines 903-926)\\n        names the online arm as \\\"the goal's largest genuine gap\\\".\\n        DEC-20260907-b4f2a9 RANK 3 (lines 414-418): \\\"no hypothesis-status\\n        promotion ... proceeds until Stage A'' seals, Stage B/C completes ...\\n        and a further Coordinator evidence-review decision is made on the\\n        independently reviewed result set.\\\"\\n    - id: F10\\n      statement: >-\\n        Stage B'' certificate note, identical in all 50 summaries: kind\\n        \\\"none\\\", note \\\"Stage B'': exact-basin closed form, zero re-selected\\n        arms\\\" (verified per file, j3_aggregate.py).\\n\\n  # =====================================================================\\n  # PROVES-TOO-MUCH OBJECTS\\n  # Each entry: the candidate inference, its verdict, and the EXACT step\\n  # where it breaks or survives. Failure signature per the plan: an\\n  # inference that still goes through where its conclusion is known false,\\n  # or that voids or validates what the recorded numbers and the frozen\\n  # contract text do not, is wrong somewhere nobody has read closely enough.\\n  # =====================================================================\\n  proves_too_much:\\n\\n    - id: PTM-1\\n      declared: true\\n      candidate_inference: >-\\n        \\\"a=1/8 at N=2^24 with margin CI [+0.0050,+0.0115] is a confirmed\\n        feasible operating point for an online RESEL-L arm.\\\"\\n      verdict: breaks\\n      exact_step_where_it_breaks: >-\\n        The step from \\\"ceiling-level G3-feasibility at (N=2^24, a=1/8)\\\" to\\n        \\\"operating point for an online RESEL-L arm\\\". (Step 1) Neither package\\n        under review contains any online arm: Stage B'''s certificate note in\\n        all 50 summaries says \\\"exact-basin closed form, zero re-selected arms\\\"\\n        (F10); v3's stage plan STAGE B'' says \\\"Zero online re-selected\\n        (RESEL-L) arms -- this is an exact-enumeration measurement only\\\" (F8);\\n        v3's arms text keeps RESEL-L out of scope because it \\\"test[s] the\\n        re-selection MECHANISM\\\" (F8); Stage A'''s run_full.py computes only\\n        ceiling-level quantities (share_top, cov_static, margin, null arms).\\n        (Step 2) The quantity the inference names — whether the online\\n        lower-bracket mechanism reaches the static-T ceiling at any\\n        achievable batch size U — is not measured anywhere in the record\\n        under review, and the goal head's standing record (F9) says every\\n        ceiling result this goal holds is SILENT on exactly that question,\\n        with ZERO online arms ever run and no promotion beyond\\n        ceiling-feasibility permitted before one does. The CI in the\\n        inference's premise is the Stage A'' reading's percentile bootstrap\\n        on the 25-seed mean of the CEILING margin (F1: [0.004968686401844024,\\n        0.011464009404182431]); it is a single-reading interval over\\n        ceiling-level seed noise (Stage B'' records no interval) and the\\n        contract gates nothing on it (F8).\\n      exact_step_where_it_survives: >-\\n        The scoped reading \\\"T_sel=T/2 at (N=2^24, a=1/8, r=2, T=256, seeds\\n        1..25) is G3-feasible at CEILING level under the frozen v3 rule in\\n        both readings\\\" survives, and is exactly what the packages record:\\n        Stage A'' k_25=20/25, verdict_25=G3-FEASIBLE, mean\\n        +0.008110418319702148, CI excluding zero (F1); Stage B'' 24/25\\n        margin>=0 (the single negative is seed 8, margin\\n        −0.004464387893676758), mean +0.010225589275360108 (F2, recomputed).\\n        The two readings agree on the verdict derived from k and on the sign\\n        of the mean margin (F6, F8). Scope of the surviving reading:\\n        ceiling-level, exact-basin, the tested N, claim_tier toy; it supports\\n        nothing beyond ceiling-feasibility and no online-arm claim (F9).\\n\\n    - id: PTM-2\\n      declared: true\\n      candidate_inference: >-\\n        Two inferences on the straddled cell (N=2^20, a=1/8), recorded CI\\n        [−0.00018343830108642574, +0.008746505737304686], k_25=16/25:\\n        (i) \\\"a=1/8 at N=2^20 is G3-INFEASIBLE\\\" read as a strict\\n        infeasibility claim; (ii) \\\"the straddle means the cell is really\\n        feasible\\\" read as a feasibility claim.\\n      verdict: breaks (both directions)\\n      exact_step_where_it_breaks: >-\\n        Inference (i) breaks at two steps. (Step A) The G3-INFEASIBLE label\\n        is a pass-count rule output, not a sign claim: the contract's\\n        operative rule makes the verdict a function of k alone, and the 25-\\n        seed reading is the proportional k >= 20 (F8); k=16 < 20, so the\\n        label is recorded — but 16 of 25 seeds (64%) had margin >= 0 and the\\n        cell's recorded mean margin is POSITIVE, +0.004251747131347656 (F1).\\n        Reading the label as \\\"the margin is negative\\\" is the first broken\\n        step. (Step B) The contract's own interval routing sends this exact\\n        cell to SU: the Stage A'' interval straddles zero, and the two\\n        readings agree on the verdict derived from k (both k < 20: 16 A'',\\n        17 B'', F1/F2) and on the sign of the mean margin (both +:\\n        +0.0042517, +0.0069278). SU_routing_rule assigns SU \\\"when BOTH\\n        readings agree on the verdict AND the percentile bootstrap interval\\n        ... STRADDLES ZERO in either reading\\\" (F8), and the INTERVAL\\n        ESTIMATOR definition says \\\"a cell whose interval straddles zero is\\n        routed to SU rather than called either way\\\" (F8). The frozen contract\\n        text routes this cell to \\\"the measurement DOES NOT SEPARATE FEASIBLE\\n        FROM INFEASIBLE ... a statement about the resolution of the\\n        instrument, not about the world\\\" (F8); the strict-infeasibility\\n        reading overrides that routing. Inference (ii) breaks at the\\n        symmetric step: the straddle is not evidence of positivity — the CI\\n        contains negative values, the pass counts are below the frozen\\n        threshold in BOTH readings (16/25 and 17/25 < 20), so the\\n        verdict-derived reading is INFEASIBLE in both, and nothing in the\\n        recorded numbers establishes margin >= 0. The straddle means the data\\n        does not decide; it does not decide in favor of feasibility.\\n      exact_step_where_it_survives: >-\\n        The scoped reading \\\"(N=2^20, a=1/8) is an unresolved borderline cell:\\n        INFEASIBLE by the frozen k-rule in both readings (k=16, k=17),\\n        positive mean margin in both readings, interval straddling zero in\\n        the Stage A'' reading — therefore SU under the contract's own\\n        routing\\\" survives, and is the only reading the recorded numbers\\n        support. It licenses neither a strict infeasibility claim nor a\\n        feasibility claim (F1, F2, F8).\\n\\n    - id: PTM-3\\n      declared: true\\n      candidate_inference: >-\\n        \\\"the margin identity holding exactly on all 200 cells validates the\\n        walk-based estimator\\\" — including its companion reading that per-seed\\n        margin agreement between independently seeded implementations is\\n        required.\\n      verdict: breaks\\n      exact_step_where_it_breaks: >-\\n        (Step A — identity read as validation) In the production summaries,\\n        margin is the recorded difference of two recorded fields\\n        (exact_top_T_sel_share, static_T_r2_exact_coverage); I verified\\n        margin == exact_top_T_sel_share − static_T_r2_exact_coverage with\\n        ZERO float residual in 200/200 cells (F3) — it holds because it is\\n        definitional over the recorded triple, not because it measured the\\n        pool. The contract itself classifies exactly this check: control (o)\\n        \\\"STRUCTURAL SELF-CHECKS -- NOT CONTROLS ... Each item below CANNOT\\n        FAIL on a correct implementation, so its passing means nothing beyond\\n        'no defect of this kind'. Calling any of them a control would repeat\\n        exactly the vacuity the independent gate correctly removed\\\" (F8), and\\n        the accounting identity is \\\"an identity of the object exact_basins\\n        computes, NOT an empirical claim ... carried as a STRUCTURAL\\n        SELF-CHECK ... and NOT as a control\\\" (F8). The walk-based part of\\n        Stage B'' — the uniform-restart pool that produces S_d, h_d, hence\\n        weight_d = S_d + 4*W*h_d, hence the T selected, hence\\n        static_T_r2_exact_coverage — is an INPUT to the difference, and the\\n        identity does not exercise it: a pool-construction defect (wrong cap\\n        credit, wrong weight, wrong selection) would pass the identity\\n        untouched. The broken step is reading identity-of-identity as\\n        inter-method or intra-method validation of the walk mechanism.\\n        (Step B — per-seed agreement read as required) The contract's own\\n        agreement standard excludes it: \\\"NOT ... a per-seed coincidence (the\\n        two readings implement different mix functions and different tie-\\n        break key streams, so per-seed coincidence is not expected and its\\n        absence is not a disagreement)\\\" (F8). My triangulation shows the\\n        expected pattern is exactly what the packages carry: bit-identical\\n        partition-level fields at all 8 frozen cells (same K/K_dp derivation\\n        in all three packages — J1 declared_conventions.mix64, Stage A''\\n        instrument.py derive_keys lines 36-39, production quoted in v3\\n        definitions item 3), but per-seed pool outputs differing — margin\\n        signs differ across the three implementations at 4 of the 6 frozen\\n        a=1/8 cells (F5), tie counts at 6 of 8, capped_walks at 4 of 8, and\\n        the per-(N,a) k counts differ between Stage A'' and Stage B'' at 7 of\\n        the 8 cells (only (2^24, 1/16) agrees, 25=25; F6). Even the known-\\n        false a=1/4 control disagrees at the per-seed level across the three\\n        implementations (k = 1, 2, 0 at 2^24; means −0.0199299 / −0.0193363 /\\n        −0.0184615) while agreeing on the verdict (F7).\\n      exact_step_where_it_survives: >-\\n        Two scoped readings survive. (1) \\\"The structural self-checks pass on\\n        200/200 production cells\\\" — margin identity zero-residual,\\n        basin_mass_accounting_sum == N exactly, residual_fraction ==\\n        (cycle+capped)/N exactly, self_check_o1/o2/o3 SATISFIED, exceedance\\n        false (F3) — which, per the contract's own label, means \\\"no defect of\\n        this kind\\\" and nothing more. (2) \\\"The two readings agree, under the\\n        contract's own standard, at all 8 of 8 (N,a) cells\\\": verdicts\\n        derived from k match 8/8 and mean-margin signs match 8/8 (F1, F2,\\n        F6) — no S3 anywhere; the k counts themselves match only 1/8, which\\n        the standard does not require to match cell-by-cell beyond the\\n        verdict they derive.\\n\\n    - id: PTM-4\\n      declared: true\\n      candidate_inference: >-\\n        \\\"the crossing bracket is N-stable\\\" — and, as the plan requires, its\\n        converse \\\"the bracket moves with N\\\".\\n      verdict: breaks (as stated); the scoped reading survives\\n      exact_step_where_it_breaks: >-\\n        (N-stability) Breaks at the step that treats the bracket as a\\n        cross-scale object. The contract defines the bracket PER SCALE:\\n        \\\"the (open) interval between the largest a at which T_sel = T/2 is\\n        G3-feasible and the smallest a at which it is not, as bracketed by\\n        this contract's own a_grid\\\" and \\\"reported PER SCALE, independently\\\"\\n        (F8). From the recorded verdicts: at N=2^20 the largest feasible a is\\n        1/16 (A'' 25/25, B'' 24/25) and the smallest infeasible a is 1/8 (A''\\n        16/25, B'' 17/25) — bracket (1/16, 1/8); at N=2^24 the largest\\n        feasible a is 1/8 (A'' 20/25, B'' 24/25) and the smallest infeasible\\n        a is 3/16 (A'' 9/25, B'' 5/25) — bracket (1/8, 3/16) (F1, F2). The\\n        bracket's location moves by exactly one grid step between scales,\\n        driven by the a=1/8 verdict flip (k 16→20 A''; 17→24 B''). An N-\\n        stability claim that survives that flip is the failure signature.\\n        (Converse) \\\"The bracket moves with N\\\" (a wholesale shift of the\\n        ordering) breaks at the step that ignores the stable cells: the\\n        a=1/16 verdict is FEASIBLE at both scales in both readings (25/25,\\n        24/25, 25/25, 25/25) and the a=3/16 verdict is INFEASIBLE at both\\n        scales in both readings (11/25, 8/25, 9/25, 5/25, with negative mean\\n        margin in all four: −0.0064954/−0.0086020 at 2^20, −0.0037050/\\n        −0.0054317 at 2^24); a=1/4 is INFEASIBLE in all six readings\\n        (3/25, 2/25, 2/25, 0/25, and J1 3/25, 1/25) (F1, F2, F7). The ONLY\\n        N-dependent verdict in the whole grid is at a=1/8; the ordering does\\n        not shift wholesale, so the converse over-reads too.\\n      exact_step_where_it_survives: >-\\n        The scoped reading \\\"the crossing is located within (1/16, 3/16) at\\n        both scales, in both readings (the stable part), and the N-dependence\\n        is concentrated exactly at the borderline cell a=1/8 — verdict\\n        INFEASIBLE→FEASIBLE from 2^20 to 2^24, k 16→20 (A'') and 17→24\\n        (B''), A'' CI straddling→excluding zero\\\" survives, and is exactly the\\n        robustness-and-N-dependence reading v3's rewritten objective exists\\n        to measure (F1, F2, F6).\\n\\n    - id: PTM-5\\n      declared: false\\n      mine: true\\n      plan_hook: >-\\n        The plan's attack_plan asks whether \\\"robustness of the crossing\\n        bracket\\\" is even well-defined when one bracket edge (a=1/8 at 2^20)\\n        is underpowered.\\n      candidate_inference: >-\\n        \\\"The crossing bracket is robust across N in the strong sense: the\\n        per-scale bracket intervals are identical (both (1/16, 3/16), or\\n        both (1/8, 3/16)) at N=2^20 and N=2^24.\\\"\\n      verdict: breaks (strong sense); well-defined only per scale and in the weak cross-scale sense\\n      exact_step_where_it_breaks: >-\\n        The step of comparing the per-scale bracket at N=2^20 — (1/16, 1/8),\\n        whose upper edge sits on the a=1/8 cell — with the per-scale bracket\\n        at N=2^24 — (1/8, 3/16) (F1, F2, PTM-4). They differ, and the\\n        difference is one cell's verdict: at 2^20 that cell's measurement is\\n        the underpowered one (k=16/25 and 17/25 vs the 20/25 threshold — 4\\n        and 3 seeds short in the two readings — with the A'' mean-margin CI\\n        straddling zero at ci_lo = −0.00018343830108642574, F1). The 2^20\\n        bracket is exactly four non-negative seeds away from becoming the\\n        2^24 bracket (16+4 = 20). The contract's own text names this\\n        situation: the 2^20 a=1/8 cell is routed to SU (PTM-2), and\\n        \\\"If a bracket is not confirmed at a scale, that is reported plainly\\n        as 'crossing not confirmed at this N'\\\" (F8). A strong cross-scale\\n        robustness claim requires resolving a cell the contract itself\\n        labels unresolved.\\n      exact_step_where_it_survives: >-\\n        The weak-sense reading survives and is well-defined: \\\"the crossing is\\n        bracketed within the union (1/16, 3/16) at both scales, in both\\n        readings; a=1/8 is the cell whose resolution determines which sub-\\n        interval the crossing occupies at each scale.\\\" That is the only\\n        cross-scale robustness statement the recorded numbers support (F1,\\n        F2, F6).\\n\\n    - id: PTM-6\\n      declared: false\\n      mine: true\\n      plan_hook: >-\\n        The plan's attack_plan asks whether the two-scale comparison supports\\n        any N-extrapolation beyond 2^24.\\n      candidate_inference: >-\\n        Any N-extrapolation in either direction — e.g. \\\"a=1/8 will be\\n        robustly feasible at all larger N\\\" (from the rising means), or \\\"a=3/16\\n        will become feasible at larger N\\\" (from its drift toward zero).\\n      verdict: breaks\\n      exact_step_where_it_breaks: >-\\n        The step where a two-point sequence is read as a trend with a\\n        direction. The recorded N-sequences have exactly two points each:\\n        a=1/8 mean +0.0042517→+0.0081104 (A'') and +0.0069278→+0.0102256\\n        (B''); a=3/16 mean −0.0064954→−0.0037050 (A'') and −0.0086020→\\n        −0.0054317 (B'') — the infeasible cell drifting toward zero as N\\n        grows, recorded as an observation (F1, F2); a=1/4 mean −0.0175420→\\n        −0.0193363 (A'') and −0.0228099→−0.0184615 (B'') (F1, F2, F7). Two\\n        points establish no trend, and the contract's operative grid is\\n        N in {2^20, 2^24} (F8, independent_variables_v3); the frozen W/cap\\n        table's T(2^30)=1024 row is a future-scale parameter, not a\\n        measurement of this batch. No extrapolation beyond 2^24 is licensed\\n        by the record.\\n      exact_step_where_it_survives: >-\\n        The two-scale comparison supports exactly one cross-scale statement,\\n        stated per scale: the verdict pattern of F1/F2 at each N, with the\\n        a=1/8 N-dependence recorded (PTM-4/PTM-5). Nothing further.\\n\\n    - id: PTM-7\\n      declared: false\\n      mine: true\\n      plan_hook: >-\\n        The plan's attack_plan asks for exact algebra on the cap convention\\n        and the exact-basin closed form: is \\\"exact ceiling\\\" exact by\\n        construction or by computation?\\n      candidate_inference: >-\\n        Question, answered by the record: the \\\"exact ceiling\\\"\\n        (exact_top_T_sel_share / share_top_Tsel) is exact BY COMPUTATION\\n     